hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10336","(10331) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās, that is, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — Muḥammad, that is, al-Ṣaghānī, narrated to us — ʿAffān narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salama narrated to us — Qatāda narrated from — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr al-Khuldī narrated to us — al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāma narrated to us — al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Salama narrated from Qatāda — from ʿIkrima — from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prohibited drinking from the mouth of a waterskin, riding the animal that feeds on filith, and [eating] the animal that is stoned to death. And that was also narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, in a marfūʿ hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Abū Dāwūd narrated it: 3719; al-Tirmidhī: 1835]"
"10337","(10332) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī informed us: Ayyūb narrated from Abū Qilābah from Abū al-Muhallab from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was on a journey, a woman of the Anṣār was upon her she-camel. She grew impatient with it and cursed it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Unload her and set her apart"","" for she is cursed.\"" He said: \""So no one would give her shelter.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb.\n\nḤammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Ayyūb"","" who said in the hadith: \""Unload from her"","" for she is cursed.\"" So they unloaded from her. ʿImrān said: \""It is as though I can still see her—a greyish she-camel.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2595]"""""
"10338","(10333) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Wāsiṭī informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sulaymān al-Taymī informed us: from Abū ʿUthmān from Abū Barzah al-Aslamī, who said: A young girl was upon a riding camel or a camel upon which was some of the people's belongings, between two mountains. The mountain pass became narrow for her. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came and she saw him, and she began saying: \Move on"","" O Allah"","" curse it! Move on"","" O Allah"","" curse it!\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Who is the owner of this young girl? Who is the owner of this young girl? No riding camel or camel upon which a curse has been invoked should accompany us.\"" Or as he said.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various routes from al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2596]"""""
"10339","(10334) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī informed us: Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿwar al-Maṣīṣī said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited branding on the face and striking the face.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn al-Ḥammāl from Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2116]"
"10340","(10335) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Najdah informed us: Ibn ʿAyyāsh informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Saybānī from Abū Maryam from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Beware of making the backs of your beasts of burden into pulpits"","" for Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has subjected them to you only so that they may convey you to a land you could not reach except with great hardship to yourselves. And He has made the earth for you"","" so upon it fulfill your needs.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 2567]"""""
"10341","(10336) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥāfiẓ in Hamadhān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Shabābah ibn Sawwār informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Sahl ibn Muʿādh ibn Anas from his father, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Ride these beasts while they are healthy"","" and return them while they are healthy"","" and do not make them into chairs.\""\n\nThus I found it in the Mustadrak"","" and I think it is Ādam ibn Abī Iyās in place of Shabābah ibn Sawwār"","" and Allah knows best. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 3/440]"""""
"10342","(10337) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: al-Layth informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī informed us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us. He mentioned it with its chain, similar to it."
"10343","(10338) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sarakhṣī al-Daghūlī in Bukhārā informed us: my grandfather informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Quhdhādh informed us: Abū al-Wazīr Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan informed us: ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed Fajr during a journey, he would walk a little. Others added in it: he would walk a little, and his she-camel would be led by its halter. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah 8/180]"
"10344","(10339) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us: Ibn Abī Fudayk informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Yaḥyā informed me from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hind, who said: Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There are camels belonging to the devils and houses belonging to the devils. As for the camels of the devils"","" I have seen them: one of you goes out with fine camels that he has fattened"","" yet he will not let anyone ride any of them. He passes by his brother whose camel has collapsed"","" yet he will not carry him. As for the houses of the devils"","" I have not seen them.\"" Saʿīd used to say: \""I do not see them except as these cages with which people cover themselves with silk brocade.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 2568]"""""
"10345","(10340) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us orally: Abū Ḥāmad ibn al-Sharqī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me: my father informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān informed us from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you travel in a time of abundance"","" give the camels their due from the earth (i.e."","" let them graze). When you travel in a year of drought or famine"","" hasten their pace. And when you encamp at night"","" avoid the road"","" for it is the refuge of harmful creatures at night.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1926]"""""
"10346","(10341) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us: Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us: Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ informed us. He mentioned it similarly, except that he did not say \or in a year of drought.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10347","(10342) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us that ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī narrated to us that Khālid ibn Yazīd al-ʿUmarī narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Travel by night"","" for the earth is folded up during the night.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it from ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī from Khālid ibn Yazīd. [Ḥasan for other than its source. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2571. Al-Ḥākim"","" 2/124.]"""""
"10348","(10343) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Tamtām informed us that Ruwaym, meaning Ibn Yazīd, narrated to me that al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me that Anas ibn Mālik informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the land becomes fertile and lush"","" dismount from your riding animals and give it its due of grazing. And when the land becomes barren"","" then traverse it quickly"","" and travel by night"","" for the earth is folded up during the night.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than its source. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"","" 2555. Al-Ḥākim"","" 1/613.]"""""
"10349","(10344) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Rabḥ al-Sammāk narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥumayd from Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh from ʿAbdillāh ibn Rabāḥ from Abū Qatādah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped to rest at night, he would lie on his right side, and when he stopped to rest close to dawn, he would prop up his forearm upright and place his head upon his palm. — This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh.\n\nAnd in the narration of Ibn Bishrān, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stopped to rest and it was still night, he would use his right side as a pillow, and when he stopped to rest near dawn, he would place his head upon his right palm and remain upright for a while.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Ḥammād ibn Salamah with the first wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 683.]"
"10350","(10345) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Abū Khaythamah narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not let your livestock and your children out when the sun sets until the darkness of the evening has passed"","" for the devils are dispatched when the sun sets until the darkness of the evening has passed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 3/30.]"""""
"10351","(10346) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father from Jābir, who said: People complained to the Prophet ﷺ about the difficulty of walking, so he summoned them and said: \Adopt a brisk"","" flowing gait (nasalān).\"" So we adopted it and found it to be lighter upon us.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"","" 2537.]"""""
"10352","(10347) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥīrī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Sālim and Mālik ibn Anas narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥarmalah from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, that a man arrived from a journey and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Who accompanied you?\"" He said: \""I did not accompany anyone.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""A lone rider is a devil"","" two riders are two devils"","" and three are a caravan (rakb).\""\n\nIbn Ḥarmalah said: And I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"","" the devil concerns himself with the one and concerns himself with the two"","" but when they are three"","" he does not concern himself with them.\"" However"","" Mālik did not mention in the ḥadīth that a man arrived from a journey; he only mentioned the statement of the Prophet ﷺ in its entirety.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2607.]"""""
"10353","(10348) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that al-Asfāṭī, meaning ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl, narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us that Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from his father from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If people knew what is in solitude (al-waḥdah)"","" no rider would ever travel alone at night.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym. And in the narration of Abū al-Walīd"","" he said: From the Prophet ﷺ"","" who said: \""If you knew what is in solitude"","" no rider would ever travel alone at night.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd and Abū Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 2836.]"""""
"10354","(10349) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Baḥr narrated to us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Abū Jaʿfar ibn Musāwir and Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Jābir said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us that Ḥātim narrated to us that Ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Nāfiʿ from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When there are three on a journey"","" let them appoint one of them as leader (amīr).\""\n\nNāfiʿ said: So I said to Abū Salamah: \""You are our amīr.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2609.]"""""
"10355","(10350) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Baḥr narrated to us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated with the same meaning, except that he said: \When they are three.\"""""""
"10356","(10351) He said: And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Baḥr ibn Barrī narrated to us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Nāfiʿ from Abū Salamah from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When three people set out on a journey"","" let them appoint one of them as leader (amīr).\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2608.]"""""
"10357","(10352) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī ʿUthmān narrated from Abī al-Zubayr that Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to them, saying: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would lag behind during the journey"","" assisting the weak"","" giving them rides"","" and supplicating for them.\"" And it has been narrated to us from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to do the same. [Hasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2639.]"""""
"10358","(10353) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us; Abū Muslim and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Yūnus; from Thābit; from Anas, who said: \I accompanied Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh"","" and he used to serve me"","" although he was older than Anas.\"" Jarīr said: \""I saw the Anṣār treating the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a manner that I saw no one among them but that I honoured him.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Naṣr ibn ʿAlī and others from Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah."""""
"10359","(10354) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Naṣrābādhī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to me; ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to me; my father narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah narrated to me: \I heard my father Buraydah say: 'While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was walking"","" a man came to him with a donkey and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" ride"","" and I shall take the rear.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""No"","" you are more entitled to the front of your mount than I am—do you see fit to give it to me?\"" He said: \""Then I have given it to you.\""' Another narrator transmitted it from ʿAbd Allāh. [Hasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2572.]"""""
"10360","(10355) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us. (H) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; both said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us; Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buraydah that Muʿādh ibn Jabal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with a mount for him to ride. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The owner of the mount is more entitled to its front.\"" Muʿādh said: \""It is for you"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) rode and seated Muʿādh behind him. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 25477.]"""""
"10361","(10356) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Jawharī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Kurayb al-Hamdānī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Hishām; from his father; from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), regarding the story of the Prophet's (peace and blessings be upon him) migration and his departure from Makkah with Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, she said: \When they set out"","" ʿĀmir ibn Fuhayrah accompanied them"","" supporting them"","" until they reached Madīnah.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 3866.]"""""
"10362","(10357) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah; from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh; from ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \On the day of Badr"","" we were two upon a camel and three upon a camel. The two companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were ʿAlī and Abū Lubābah al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with them both). When their turn came"","" they would say: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" ride"","" and we shall walk on your behalf.' He said: 'You are not stronger in walking than I am"","" nor am I more desirous of reward than you.'\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Aḥmad"","" 1/411.]"""""
"10363","(10358) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated from Burayd; from Abī Burdah; from Abū Mūsá (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on a military expedition"","" and we were six men sharing one camel"","" taking turns riding it.\"" He mentioned the hadith. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 3899.]"""""
"10364","(10359) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb in Hamadhān informed us; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Waḥshī ibn Ḥarb ibn Waḥshī; from his father; from his grandfather Waḥshī ibn Ḥarb, that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" we eat but are not satisfied.\"" He said: \""Perhaps you eat separately from your food. Gather together over it and mention the name of Allah"","" the Most High"","" and He will bless it for you.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 3764.]"""""
"10365","(10360) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Yaḥyá ibn Ādam narrated to us; Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib; from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr; from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When the verse was revealed: {And do not approach the orphan's property except in the best way} (al-Anʿām: 152)"","" they separated their wealth from the wealth of the orphans. Food would spoil and meat would rot. They complained of this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" so Allah"","" the Blessed and Most High"","" revealed: {Say: 'Setting things right for them is better"","" and if you mix with them"","" they are your brothers'} (al-Baqarah: 220). So they mixed with them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2871.]"""""
"10366","(10361) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá narrated to us. He said: I said to Mālik ibn Anas: \Did Sumayy narrate to you from Abī Ṣāliḥ"","" from Abī Hurayrah"","" that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Travel is a piece of punishment; it prevents one of you from his sleep"","" his food"","" and his drink. When one of you has fulfilled the purpose of his journey"","" let him hasten back to his family'?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 1710.]"""""
"10367","(10362) And 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq informed us, al-Qa'nabī informed us, Mālik from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr, and he narrated it similarly, except that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qa'nabī and others, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, al-Qa'nabī, and others."
"10368","(10363) Abū 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Dhuhlī informed us, Ja'far ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Marwān Muḥammad ibn 'Uthmān al-'Uthmānī informed us, Abū Ḍamrah al-Laythī informed us from Hishām ibn 'Urwah, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you has fulfilled his Hajj"","" let him hasten the journey back to his family"","" for it is greater in reward for him.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. al-Ḥākim narrated it"","" 1/650.]"""""
"10369","(10364) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī from his original copy said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, 'Umar ibn Muḥammad, 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar, Mālik ibn Anas, and others informed me that Nāfi' narrated to them from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he returned from a military expedition, or Hajj, or 'Umrah, would pronounce takbīr (say \Allāhu Akbar\"") upon every elevated point of the land three times"","" and then say: \""Lā ilāha illā Allāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lahu"","" lahu al-mulku wa lahu al-ḥamdu wa huwa 'alā kulli shay'in qadīr. Ā'ibūnā tā'ibūnā 'ābidūnā sājidūna li-Rabbinā ḥāmidūn. Ṣadaqa Allāhu wa'dahu wa naṣara 'abdahu wa hazama al-aḥzāba waḥdahu.\"" (\""There is no deity except Allah alone"","" without partner. To Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise"","" and He is over all things competent. We are returning"","" repenting"","" worshipping"","" prostrating"","" and praising our Lord. Allah has fulfilled His promise"","" aided His servant"","" and defeated the confederates alone.\"")\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik ibn Anas. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1703.]"""""
"10370","(10365) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-'Alawī informed us by dictation and recitation, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr informed us, Sufyān informed us from 'Ubayd Allāh, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar. And Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān from Sālim from Ibn 'Umar. And 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr informed us, Sufyān informed us on one occasion, Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān informed us from Sālim from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he returned from Hajj, or 'Umrah, or a military expedition, and came upon an elevated tract of land, would say: \Tā'ibūnā in shā'a Allāh"","" 'ābidūnā ḥāmidūn. Ṣadaqa Allāhu wa'dahu wa naṣara 'abdahu wa hazama al-aḥzāba waḥdahu.\"" (\""We are returning"","" if Allah wills"","" worshipping"","" praising. Allah has fulfilled His promise"","" aided His servant"","" and defeated the confederates alone.\"")\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ṣāliḥ"","" and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Umar"","" more complete than that"","" similar to the narration of Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2833.]"""""
"10371","(10366) Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī informed us, 'Imrān and al-Wazzān said: Bin Dār informed us, Ibn Abī 'Adī informed us from Shu'bah, from Ḥuṣayn, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Ja'd, from Jābir, who said: \When we ascended"","" we would pronounce takbīr"","" and when we descended"","" we would pronounce tasbīḥ.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Bindār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2831.]"""""
"10372","(10367) Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hāni' informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed me, Hārūn al-Farwī informed us, Abū Ḍamrah informed us from 'Ubayd Allāh, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he set out for Makkah, would pray in the Mosque of al-Shajarah, and when he returned, he would pray at Dhū al-Ḥulayfah in the bottom of the valley, and he would spend the night there until morning.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir and others, from Abī Ḍamrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1460.]"
"10373","(10368) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Abū al-Bakhtarī 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Hammām ibn Yaḥyā informed us from Isḥāq ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not come to his family at night. He would arrive in the early morning or in the evening.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"","" from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl"","" from Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1706.]"""""
"10374","(10369) And Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn 'Alī al-Warrāq informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Hammām informed us, Isḥāq ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah informed us from Anas, that the Prophet ﷺ would not come to his family at night. He would not arrive except in the early morning or in the evening.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"10375","(10370) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-'Askarī in al-Baṣrah informed us, Ja'far ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us, Shu'bah informed us, Muḥārib ibn Dithār informed us. He said: I heard Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that a man should come to his family at night (ṭuruqan).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"","" and Muslim narrated it from two other routes from Shu'bah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 1704.]"""""
"10376","(10371) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shu'bah from Sayyār, who heard al-Sha'bī from Jābir, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade a man to come to his family at night, until the dishevelled woman has combed her hair and the woman whose husband has been absent has shaved her pubic hair.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Shu'bah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 4791.]"
"10377","(10372) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Musaddad and al-Muqaddamī — meaning Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — both said: Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Khālid narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived, and young girls from Banī ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib came out to meet him. He placed one of them in front of him and another behind him.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1704]"
"10378","(10373) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad — that is, ibn al-Minhāl — narrated to us; Yazīd narrated it with the same wording, except that he said: \He arrived at Makkah in the year of the Conquest (al-Fath).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Muʿallā ibn Asad"","" from Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ. [Sahih. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10379","(10374) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Muwarriq al-ʿIjlī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he returned from a journey, would be met by the young children of his household. He returned from a journey and I was brought to him ahead of the others, so he placed me in front of him. Then one of the two sons of Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her) was brought, and he seated him behind him. He said: \We entered Madīnah — the three of us — on a single mount.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahīh from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Sahih. Muslim 2428]"""""
"10380","(10375) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥātim al-Muzakkī narrated to us in Marw; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rūḥ al-Madāʾinī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: We arrived from Makkah during a Hajj or ʿUmrah, and Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr was riding in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Young boys from the Anṣār came out to meet us — they used to come out to meet their families when they returned.\n\n[Improvable]"
"10381","(10376) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Ḥumayd narrated to me that he heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he returned from a journey and saw the walls of Madīnah, would urge his she-camel to go faster, and if he was on another mount, he would spur it on.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam. Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar added therein, from Ḥumayd: \out of love for it (Madīnah).\""\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1708]"""""
"10382","(10377) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan — that is, al-Hisinjānī — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl narrated from Ḥumayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (ﷺ), when he returned from a journey and looked upon the walls of Madīnah, would urge his mount to go faster, and if he was on another riding animal, he would spur it on out of love for it (Madīnah).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd, from Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar. [Sahih. Bukhari 1787]"
"10383","(10378) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj; Ibn Shihāb narrated to me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik informed him from his father and his uncle ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from Kaʿb ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would only return from a journey during the day. When he arrived, he would begin with the mosque and pray two rakʿahs therein, and then he would sit down.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Abū ʿĀṣim, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Mūsā, from Abū ʿĀṣim.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 2922]"
"10384","(10379) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bisṭāmī al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed us; Abū Isḥāq informed us; he said: I heard al-Barāʾ say: The Anṣār, when they returned from Hajj, would not enter their houses through their doors, but rather from behind them. A man from the Anṣār came and entered through his door, and it was as if he was reproached for that. Then this verse was revealed: \And it is not righteousness that you enter houses from their backs"","" but righteousness is [found in] the one who fears Allah. And enter houses from their doors.\"" (Al-Baqarah: 189)\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Abū al-Walīd"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah.\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1709]"""""
"10385","(10380) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Wakīʿ narrated from Shuʿbah, from Muḥārib ibn Dithār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Madīnah, he sacrificed a camel or a cow.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Muḥammad, from Wakīʿ."
"10386","(10381) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us in Marw; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Marwarrūdhī narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Manṣūr, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah"","" forgive the pilgrim (al-ḥājj)"","" and forgive the one for whom the pilgrim asks forgiveness.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Ḥākim: 1/609]"""""
"10387","(10382) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh — al-Qaʿnabī — from Mālik, from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \An ʿUmrah performed after another ʿUmrah is an expiation for whatever sins occur between them"","" and the accepted Ḥajj has no reward except Paradise.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read before Mālik"","" and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1183]"""""
"10388","(10383) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī Sakhtawayh ibn Māziyār narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Masʿadah narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAjlān, from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr, and he mentioned it with the same meaning."
"10389","(10384) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnqazī narrated to us, from Misʿar and Sufyān, from Manṣūr.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated it to us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Misʿar narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever performs Ḥajj and does not engage in sexual indecency nor commit sin will return as on the day his mother bore him.\"" In the narration of al-Faqīh"","" he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" and he said: \""Then he will return — he will return as his mother bore him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Misʿar and Sufyān"","" and al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1723]"""""
"10390","(10385) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in Baghdad: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Manṣūr, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever performs Ḥajj to this House and does not engage in sexual indecency nor commit sin will return as on the day his mother bore him.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"","" and Muslim extracted it from another route from Shuʿbah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous one.]"""""
"10391","(10386) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭaḥmān narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Hilāl ibn Yasāf, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever comes to this House — meaning the Kaʿbah — and does not engage in sexual indecency nor commit sin will return as on the day his mother bore him.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous one.]"""""
"10392","(10387) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khawlānī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to me: Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, who said: I heard Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ say: I heard my father say: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The delegations of Allah are three: the warrior (al-ghāzī)"","" the pilgrim performing Ḥajj (al-ḥājj)"","" and the pilgrim performing ʿUmrah (al-muʿtamir).\"" Thus I found it"","" and thus it was narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Suhayl.\n\nAnd Wuhayb narrated it from Suhayl"","" from his father"","" from Mirdās"","" from Kaʿb"","" who said: \""The delegations are three: the warrior in the path of Allah is a delegate to Allah; the pilgrim to the House of Allah; and the performer of ʿUmrah is a delegate to Allah. No one raises the talbiyah except that it is said to him: 'Receive glad tidings!'\"" Mirdās said: \""With what?\"" He said: \""With Paradise.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to me: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ narrated to me: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Munkar al-isnād]"""""
"10393","(10388) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us by dictation in Baghdad: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Daybulī narrated to us in the Sacred Mosque: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿAbd Allāh, a freedman of Banī ʿĀmir ibn Luʾayy, narrated to me: Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The Ḥājj and the ʿUmmār (those performing ʿUmrah) are delegates of Allah. If they supplicate to Him"","" He answers them"","" and if they seek His forgiveness"","" He forgives them.\"" Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿAbd Allāh is munkar al-ḥadīth.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Mājah extracted it"","" 2892]"""""
"10394","(10389) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: A man asked the Prophet (ﷺ): \Which deed is the best?\"" He said: \""Faith in Allah.\"" He said: \""Then what?\"" He said: \""Then jihād in the path of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then what?\"" He said: \""Then an accepted Ḥajj (ḥajj mabrūr).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and ʿAbd"","" from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" and al-Bukhārī extracted it from another route from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 26]"""""
"10395","(10390) The Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān — may Allah have mercy on him — narrated to us by dictation, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mahrānī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ al-Adīb, and Abū al-Qāsim al-Sarrāj — by recitation — said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Umawī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Ayyūb ibn Suwayd narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \What constitutes the righteousness of Ḥajj (birr al-ḥajj)?\"" He said: \""Feeding food and speaking kindly (ṭīb al-kalām).\"" Ayyūb ibn Suwayd is alone in narrating it.\n\nAnd Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn and Muḥammad ibn Thābit narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir"","" likewise"","" as a connected narration.\n\n[Munkar. al-Ḥākim extracted it"","" 1/658]"""""
"10396","(10391) And al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awzāʿī, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, as a mursal narration. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed it to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Ibrāhīh ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, from his father, from al-Walīd."
"10397","(10392) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us: al-Faḍl — meaning Ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī — informed us: Saʿīd — meaning Ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Khalīfah narrated to us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Musayyab narrated from his father, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, a hadith which he attributed (marfūʿan), saying: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \Indeed"","" a servant whose body I have made healthy and upon whom I have bestowed abundance in livelihood — five years pass over him and he does not come to Me. He is indeed deprived.\""\n\nOthers narrated it from Khalaf"","" and it was said: from the Prophet ﷺ. And it was said: from al-ʿAlāʾ"","" from Yūnus ibn Khabbāb"","" from Abū Saʿīd. And it was also narrated as mawqūf (stopped at the Companion) and as mursal (with a missing link in the chain).\n\nIt was also narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah"","" but its chain is weak. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān 3703; Abū Yaʿlā 1031.]"""""
"10398","(10393) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us: Abū Marwān Hishām ibn Khālid al-Azraq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Anmāṭī narrated to us: Hishām al-Dimashqī informed us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ṣadaqah ibn Yazīd, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: \Indeed"","" a servant whose body I have made healthy and upon whom I have expanded provision — he does not come to Me once every five years — he is indeed deprived.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Qaṭṭān.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-ʿUqaylī in al-Ḍuʿafāʾ 188.]"""""
"10399","(10394) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us: Shabbābah narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, from Mujāhid, regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {Eat of the good things which We have provided for you} [al-Baqarah: 172]. He said: It means trade (al-tijārah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"10400","(10395) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from Mujāhid, that he said regarding this verse: {O you who believe, spend of the good things that you have earned} [al-Baqarah: 267]. He said: It means from trade (al-tijārah).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"10401","(10396) And through this chain of narration, he said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah regarding this verse: {O you who believe, do not consume your wealth among yourselves unjustly, except it be trade by mutual consent among you} [al-Nisāʾ: 29]. He said: Trade is a provision from the provisions of Allah, and it is lawful from the lawful things of Allah, for whoever seeks it through its honesty and righteousness.\n\n[Ḥasan.]"
"10402","(10397) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī narrated to us: al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from Wāʾil ibn Dāwūd, from Jumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr, from his maternal uncle Abū Burdah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \Which earning is the purest"","" or the best?\"" He said: \""A man's work with his own hand"","" and every blessed transaction (bayʿ mabrūr).\""\n\nThis is how Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Qāḍī narrated it"","" and he erred in it in two respects. The first is his saying \""Jumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr\"" — when in fact it is Saʿīd ibn ʿUmayr. The second is in connecting it (waṣl). Others narrated it from Wāʾil as mursal.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by al-Ḥākim 2/12.]"""""
"10403","(10398) As Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Wāʾil ibn Dāwūd narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿUmayr, the maternal uncle of al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked: \Which earning of a man is the purest?\"" He said: \""A man's work with his own hand"","" and every blessed transaction.\""\n\nThis is the preserved narration"","" mursal.\n\nAnd it is also said from him: from Saʿīd"","" from his paternal uncle"","" who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \""Which earning is the best?\"" He said: \""A blessed earning (kasb mabrūr).\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. See the preceding.]"""""
"10404","(10399) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us: al-Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Wāʾil ibn Dāwūd, from Saʿīd ibn ʿUmayr, from his paternal uncle, and he mentioned it.\n\nOthers narrated it from Sufyān as mursal. And Sharīk said: from Wāʾil ibn Dāwūd, from Jumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr, from his maternal uncle Abū Burdah — and Jumayʿ is an error. And al-Masʿūdī said: from Wāʾil ibn Dāwūd, from ʿAbāyah ibn Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, from his father — and this is also an error.\n\nThe correct narration is that of Wāʾil from Saʿīd ibn ʿUmayr from the Prophet ﷺ, mursal. Al-Bukhārī said: some of them narrated it with a complete chain (asnadahu), and it is an error."
"10405","(10400) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī in Kūfah informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd and al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn both said: Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us orally: Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād and ʿAmr ibn Tamīm al-Ṭabarī both said: Abū Nuʿaym said: Zakariyyā narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \The lawful (al-ḥalāl) is clear and the unlawful (al-ḥarām) is clear"","" and between them are doubtful matters that many people do not know. Whoever guards against the doubtful matters has safeguarded his honour and his religion"","" and whoever falls into the doubtful matters falls into the unlawful — like a shepherd who grazes his flock near a sanctuary"","" all but grazing therein. Indeed"","" every king has a sanctuary"","" and indeed the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions. Indeed"","" in the body there is a morsel of flesh: if it is sound"","" the whole body is sound"","" and if it is corrupt"","" the whole body is corrupt. Indeed"","" it is the heart.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn"","" and Muslim narrated it through other routes from Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 52.]"""""
"10406","(10401) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us: Sufyān narrated from Abū Farwah, from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear"","" and between them are doubtful matters. Whoever leaves what is doubtful to him"","" he has left what is clear for him"","" and whoever ventures into what he is uncertain about"","" he is likely to fall into what is clear. And sins are the sanctuary of Allah"","" and whoever grazes around a sanctuary is likely to fall into it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"","" and Muslim narrated it through another route from Abū Farwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1946.]"""""
"10407","Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shadhyakhi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakim informed us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to me: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There will come upon the people a time when a person will not care whether he acquires his wealth through lawful means or unlawful means.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam ibn Abi Iyas from Ibn Abi Dhi'b. [Sahih. Bukhari 1954]"""""
"10408","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us — it was recited to them — and Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Qushayri narrated to us verbatim, saying: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me: Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Suwayd from Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Be gentle and moderate in your pursuit of the worldly life"","" for each one will be facilitated that which has been decreed for him from it.\""\n\n[Sahih. Ibn Khuzaymah 2142]"""""
"10409","Imam Abu al-Tayyib Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us by dictation: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Shashi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Bunan al-Anmati narrated to us: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not be slow in seeking provision"","" for no servant dies until the last portion of his provision reaches him. So fear Allah and be moderate in your seeking — from the lawful and by abandoning the unlawful.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Hibban 3239]"""""
"10410","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi 'Isa al-Halali narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \O people"","" none of you will die until he has received his full provision. So do not be slow in seeking provision"","" and fear Allah"","" O people"","" and be moderate in your seeking: take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. [Sahih in other chains. Narrated by Ibn Majah 2144]"""""
"10411","Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us: Yahya narrated: al-Layth narrated from Yunus from Ibn Shihab, who said: Ibn al-Musayyab said that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Oath-selling promotes the sale but erases the profit.\""\n\n[Sahih. Bukhari 1981]"""""
"10412","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated it with a similar wording, except that he said: from Ibn al-Musayyab, and he said: \it erases the blessing.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr"","" and he said: \""for the blessing.\"" [Sahih. As previously mentioned]"""""
"10413","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn 'Amr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yunus narrated it with a similar wording and said: \it erases the earnings.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Tahir. [Sahih. As previously mentioned]"""""
"10414","Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from al-'Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub al-Juhani from his father from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), narrating marfu' to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \A false oath promotes the sale but erases the earnings.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Nasa'i 441]"""""
"10415","Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami from his original, and others narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abu Ja'far Ahmad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us: Abu Usamah informed me: al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated from Ma'bad ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from Abu Qatadah al-Ansari that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Beware of excessive oaths in trade"","" for they promote the sale but then erase it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr and others from Abu Usamah. [Sahih. Muslim 1607]"""""
"10416","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Ali ibn Mudrik, who said: I heard Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There are three to whom Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection"","" nor will He speak to them"","" and for them is a painful punishment.\"" He said: I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" who are they? They have indeed failed and are lost.\"" He said: \""The one who reminds others of his favors"","" the one who trails his garment out of pride"","" and the one who promotes his merchandise by means of false oaths.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Ghundar from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Muslim 106]"""""
"10417","(10412) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Ibn ʿAffān narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir from his original, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from his original, all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, from Qays ibn Abī Gharazah, who said: \In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" we used to trade in the markets and call ourselves brokers (al-samasirah). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and named us with a name better than that"","" saying: 'O company of traders! Indeed"","" this transaction is attended by falsehood and idle talk"","" so mix it with charity.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3326]"""""
"10418","(10413) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; al-Ramādī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥakīm narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us. (Ḥ) He said: And Abū Saʿīd informed us; ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; Shabbābah narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Abū Wāʾil, from Qays ibn Abī Gharazah, who said: \We used to sell in the market and we were called brokers (al-samasirah). The Prophet ﷺ said: 'O company of traders! Indeed"","" these markets of yours are mixed with oaths"","" so mix them with charity"","" or with something of charity.'\"" The wording of Sufyān is close to it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it]"""""
"10419","(10414) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Zakarīyāʾ informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ al-Zuraqī, from his father, from his grandfather, that he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the place of prayer (al-muṣallā) in al-Madīnah and found the people trading. He said: \O company of traders!\"" They responded to him and raised their gazes and their necks toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \""Indeed"","" the traders will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as wicked"","" except the one who feared Allah"","" was righteous"","" and was truthful.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 1210]"""""
"10420","(10415) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Zayd ibn Salām, from Abū Salām, from Abū Rāshid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl, a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed"","" the traders are the wicked (al-fujjār).' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" did not Allah permit trade?' He said: 'Yes"","" but they swear oaths and thereby sin.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 3/444]"""""
"10421","(10416) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakarīyāʾ Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Shādhān al-Ṣaydalānī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us; Kathīr ibn Hishām narrated to us; Kulthūm ibn Jawshan narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The truthful"","" trustworthy Muslim trader will be with the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection.\"" And that has been narrated from al-Ḥasan"","" from Abū Saʿīd"","" from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2139]"""""
"10422","(10417) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of uncertainty (al-gharar) and the sale of pebbles (al-ḥaṣāh). Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1513]"
"10423","(10418) And Abū Zayd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs, Abū Usāmah, and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, with the same meaning, except that they said: \And the sale of pebbles (al-ḥaṣā).\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it]"""""
"10424","(10419) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is not permissible to combine a loan and a sale"","" nor two conditions in a sale"","" nor profit from that which is not guaranteed"","" nor the sale of what is not in your possession.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3504]"""""
"10425","(10420) Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated it from Ayyūb, who said: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me; he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, until he mentioned ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us, and he mentioned it."
"10426","(10421) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ forbade me from selling what is not with me"","" or selling a commodity that is not in my possession.\"" [Ḥasan for other than it. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3503]"""""
"10427","(10422) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak — informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar — informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Iyās — informed us, who said: I heard Yūsuf ibn Māḥak narrating from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" a man asks me for a sale (i.e."","" goods) and I do not have them with me — should I sell them to him?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not sell what is not with you.\"" [Ḥasan for something else. It was mentioned before.]"""""
"10428","(10423) Abū al-Qāsim — Hibbatullāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭabarī al-Faqīh, may Allah have mercy on him — in Baghdad, informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Aḥmad al-Fārisī — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq — informed us; Maʿmar — from al-Zuhrī — from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \We wished that ʿUthmān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf would transact a sale between themselves so that we might see which of them was more fortunate in trade.\"" So ʿAbd al-Raḥmān purchased from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them both) a horse located in another land for forty thousand dirhams or thereabouts"","" with the condition that the transaction would be valid if the item was found intact. Then he went a short distance and returned and said: \""I will increase it by six thousand dirhams if my messenger finds it intact.\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" But ʿAbd al-Raḥmān's messenger found that it had perished"","" so he was released from the second condition. Others narrated it and added therein: \""I do not think ʿAbd al-Raḥmān would have done so unless he had recognized it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 14240.]"""""
"10429","(10424) Abū al-Qāsim — Hibbatullāh ibn al-Ḥasan — informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad — informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad — narrated to us; Abū Qilābah — narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd — narrated to us; Rabbāh ibn Abī Maʿrūf — from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, that ʿUthmān purchased from Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh a piece of land in Madīnah in exchange for a piece of land he had in Kūfah. When they concluded the transaction, ʿUthmān became anxious and then said: \I sold you something I have not seen.\"" Ṭalḥah said: \""The right to inspect was mine"","" for I purchased something absent. As for you"","" you saw what you purchased.\"" So they appointed an arbitrator between them"","" and they appointed Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim. He ruled against ʿUthmān that the sale was valid"","" and that the right of inspection belonged to Ṭalḥah"","" because he had purchased something absent. It has also been narrated in this regard from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" but it is not authentic. [Ḥasan.]"""""
"10430","(10425) Abū Ḥāzim — ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī — informed us; Abū al-Faḍl — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīrūyah — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh — from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Maryam — from Makhūl, who raised the hadith to the Prophet (ﷺ), saying: \Whoever purchases something he has not seen"","" he has the option when he sees it — if he wishes"","" he may take it"","" and if he wishes"","" he may leave it.\"" This is a mursal hadith. Abū Bakr ibn Abī Maryam is weak (ḍaʿīf). Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith and others said this to me regarding ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar"","" Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī"","" the ḥāfiẓ"","" may Allah have mercy on him. It has also been narrated through another chain from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" but it is not authentic. [Very weak (ḍaʿīf jiddan). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"","" 3/4.]"""""
"10431","(10426) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — both said: Abū ʿAbdullāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Abī Yaʿqūb al-Aṣbahānī al-Muʿaddil — narrated to us; Dāhir ibn Nūḥ — narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Khālid — from Wahb al-Yashkurī — from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn — from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases something he has not seen"","" he has the option when he sees it.\"" Likewise"","" ʿAbdān narrated it from Dāhir ibn Nūḥ from ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and from him from ʿUmar from Fuḍayl ibn ʿIyāḍ from Hishām from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah. And from ʿUmar from al-Qāsim ibn al-Ḥakam from Abū Ḥanīfah from al-Haytham from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah"","" likewise"","" as a marfūʿ narration. [Bāṭil (false). Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"","" 413.]"""""
"10432","(10427) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh — informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūd ibn Khurrāzād al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā ʿAbdān — narrated it. Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ said: ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm, called al-Kurdī, fabricates hadith, and this is false and not authentic. No one else narrated it. It is only narrated from Ibn Sīrīn as his own statement. [Bāṭil (false).]"
"10433","(10428) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū al-Faḍl — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Khamīrūyah — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd — from Ayyūb, who said: I heard al-Ḥasan say: \Whoever purchases something he has not seen"","" he has the option when he sees it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 19974.]"""""
"10434","(10429) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us from Hushaym, who said: Yūnus and Ibn ʿAwn informed us from Ibn Sīrīn that he used to say: \If it is as he described it to him"","" then it is binding upon him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 19974.]"""""
"10435","(10430) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī, and others — by recitation; and Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — by dictation — all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Mālik — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh — narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī — narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī — from what he read to Mālik — (ḥ) He said: And Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh — informed me; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — narrated to us, who said: I read to Mālik — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The two parties to a sale each have the option over their counterpart as long as they have not separated"","" except a sale of option (bayʿ al-khiyār).\"" And in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \""over his counterpart"","" the option.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 2005.]"""""
"10436","(10431) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān — informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar — narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān — narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī — (ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib — narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar — both said: Sufyān — narrated to us, and the wording is that of al-Ḥumaydī, who said: Ibn Jurayj — narrated to us, who said: I came to Nāfiʿ and he placed a bag for me, so I sat upon it, and he dictated to me on my tablets. He said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When two parties transact a sale"","" each one of them has the option regarding his sale as long as they have not separated"","" or their sale is based on option.\"" He said: So when Ibn ʿUmar would transact a sale and wished for it to become binding"","" he would walk a short distance and then return. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 1531.]"""""
"10437","(10432) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā both said — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us — he said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say — he heard Nāfiʿ narrate from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] in their transaction so long as they have not separated"","" unless the sale is a sale by option (bayʿ al-khiyār).\"" Nāfiʿ said: \""And when ʿAbdullāh [ibn ʿUmar] purchased something that pleased him"","" he would part from his companion.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ṣadaqah"","" from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and others.\n\nAl-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān also narrated it from Nāfiʿ with the same meaning"","" regarding the action of ʿAbdullāh and the narration in its entirety. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See before it.]"""""
"10438","(10433) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Aḥmad ibn Salamaḥ narrated to us — Qutayba ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \When two men enter into a sale"","" each of them has the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated and are still together"","" or one of them grants the option to his companion. If they then transact upon that"","" the sale becomes binding. And if they separate after having transacted and neither of them abandons the sale"","" the sale becomes binding.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutayba"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutayba and Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ."""""
"10439","(10434) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — Jaʿfar al-Firyābī informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ḥisāb and Abū Kāmil narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ said — they all said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us — Ayyūb narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated"","" or one of them says to his companion: 'Choose [whether to proceed or annul].'\"" He [the narrator] said: And sometimes he would say: \""Or it is a sale by option (khiyār).\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Muqriʾ. And in the narration of al-Adīb: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated"","" unless it is a sale by option"","" or he says to his companion: \""Choose.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān"","" from Ḥammād"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Rabīʿ and Abī Kāmil. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2003.]"""""
"10440","(10435) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us — Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar — (ḥ) and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed me — Muḥammad ibn Ḥajjāj narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār that he heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Every two parties to a sale — there is no sale between them until they separate"","" except a sale by option (bayʿ al-khiyār).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Firyābī"","" from Sufyān"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2007.]"""""
"10441","(10436) The jurist Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ṭūsī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — (ḥ) and Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Abū ʿUmar narrated to us — they both said: Shuʿba narrated from Qatāda, from Ṣāliḥ Abī al-Khalīl — and in the narration of al-Ṭayālisī, he said: \I heard Abā al-Khalīl narrate — from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith"","" from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām"","" who said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated. If they are truthful and transparent"","" a blessing is placed in their transaction. And if they lie and conceal"","" the blessing of their transaction is obliterated.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥs through various chains from Shuʿba ibn al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 1973.]"""""
"10442","(10437) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān narrated to us — Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī narrated to us — Hammām narrated from Qatāda, from Abī al-Khalīl, from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated.\"" Hammām said: \""And I found in my book: 'And he may exercise the option three times. If they are truthful and transparent"","" a blessing is placed in their transaction. And if they lie and conceal"","" perhaps they may gain a profit"","" but the blessing of their transaction will be obliterated.'\"" Hammām said: \""I narrated this ḥadīth to Abā al-Ṭayyāḥ"","" and he said: 'I was with Abī al-Khalīl when ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated this ḥadīth to us.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīths from the ḥadīth of Hammām. Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūba and Ḥammād ibn Salama narrated it from Qatāda without the additional wording that Hammām found in his book. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See before it.]"""""
"10443","(10438) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Jamīl ibn Murra, from Abī al-Waḍīʾ, who said: \We went on a military expedition and encamped at a certain place. A companion of ours sold a horse for a slave"","" and then remained [with the buyer] for the rest of that day and night. When we set out the next morning"","" the time for departure arrived"","" and he went to his horse to saddle it"","" whereupon he regretted [the sale]. He came to the man and took him by [the agreement of] the sale"","" but the man refused to hand it over to him. He said: 'Between me and you is Abū Barza"","" a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So we came to Abū Barza in a corner of the camp and told him the story. He said: 'Are you two content that I judge between you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated.'\""\n\nHishām ibn Ḥassān narrated that Jamīl said: \""I do not think the two of you had separated.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3457.]"""""
"10444","(10439) Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdad informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us — Abū al-Ashʿath narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Jamīl ibn Murra, from Abī al-Waḍīʾ, from Abī Barza al-Aslamī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The two parties to a sale have the option [of annulment] so long as they have not separated.'\"" [Ḥasan. See before it.]"""""
"10445","(10440) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Lakhmī narrated to us — ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamaḥ narrated to us — Abū Muʿīd Ḥafṣ ibn Ghaylān narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Mūsā narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar; and from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās — that both of them used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Whoever purchases something and it becomes binding upon him"","" he retains the option so long as his companion has not separated from him. If he wishes"","" he may take it. And if he separates from him"","" he has no further option.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 3/5.]"""""
"10446","(10441) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Muʿādh al-Ḍabbī narrated from Simāk, from ʿIkrima, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ concluded a sale with a man. When he had concluded the sale with him, he said: \You have the option.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Thus is the sale [to be conducted].\"" [Ḥasan in other than this chain. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 2675.]"""""
"10447","(10442) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿāwiya narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, that he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) purchased from a Bedouin — I think Abū al-Zubayr said, from Banī ʿĀmir ibn Ṣaʿṣaʿa — a load of fodder. When the sale was concluded, the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \You have the choice (to confirm or annul).\"" The Bedouin said to him: \""I have never seen a buyer more judicious than you. From which people are you?\"" He said: \""From Quraysh.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" Ibn Wahb narrated it from Ibn Jurayj.\n[Ḥasan in view of other chains. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (1249).]"""""
"10448","(10443) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us; Mawhab ibn Yazīd ibn Mawhab narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed us that Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī narrated to him from Jābir: that the Prophet (ﷺ) purchased from a Bedouin a load of fodder. When the sale was concluded, the Prophet (Ḥasan) said to him: \You have the choice.\"" The Bedouin said to him: \""May Allah grant you long life — the sale stands.\""\n\nAnd similarly"","" Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb narrated it from his uncle Ibn Wahb. And Ibn ʿUyayna narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"","" from Abū al-Zubayr"","" from Ṭāwūs"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration. And similarly"","" ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs narrated it from his father.\n[Ḥasan in view of other chains. See the preceding narration.]"""""
"10449","(10444) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyayna narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a man the option after the sale. The man said: \May Allah grant you long life — from which people are you?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""A man from Quraysh.\"" He (Ṭāwūs) said: \""My father used to swear that the option (of annulment) is only after the sale.\"""""""
"10450","(10445) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkari informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) purchased, before prophethood, a camel — or something else — from a Bedouin. When the sale was concluded, the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \You have the choice.\"" The Bedouin looked at him and said: \""May Allah grant you long life — who are you?\"" He said: \""When Islam came"","" the Prophet (ﷺ) established the option (of annulment) after the sale.\""\n[Ḥasan in view of other chains.]"""""
"10451","(10446) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Jarjarāʾī narrated — Marwān al-Fazārī informed us — from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb, who said: Abū Zurʿa, when he concluded a sale with a man, would give him the option. Then he would say: \Give me the option as well.\"" And he would say: \""I heard Abū Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Let not two persons (in a sale) separate except by mutual consent.'\""\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3458).]"""""
"10452","(10447) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us; Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ narrated from Abū Qilāba; Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by the people of al-Baqīʿ and said: \O people of al-Baqīʿ!\"" They responded attentively. He said: \""O people of al-Baqīʿ"","" let not two parties to a sale separate except by mutual consent.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in view of other chains.]"""""
"10453","(10448) Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī and Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh both informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us; Abū ʿUbayd Allāh Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb informed us; my uncle narrated to me; Makhrama ibn Bukayr narrated from his father, who said: I heard ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb say: I heard Shuʿayb say: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whenever a man makes a purchase from another man"","" each of them has the option (to confirm or annul) until they separate from their place"","" unless it is a sale with a stipulated option. And it is not permissible for either of them to part from his companion for fear that he might rescind the transaction.\""\n\nHis statement \""that he might rescind\"" — he meant thereby"","" and Allah knows best"","" that he might annul it. He expressed annulment (fasakh) through the term \""iqāla\"" (rescission).\n\nAnd we have narrated something similar from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"","" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"","" and Jarīr ibn ʿAbd Allāh"","" and then from Sharīḥ"","" Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"","" and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said in al-Ṣaḥīḥ: And al-Layth narrated to me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Shihāb"","" from Sālim"","" from Ibn ʿUmar"","" who said: \""I sold to the Commander of the Faithful ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — property in the valley in exchange for his property in Khaybar. When we completed the sale"","" I turned on my heels until I left his house"","" fearing that he might reverse the sale. And the established practice was that the two parties to a sale had the option until they separated.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""When my sale and his sale became binding"","" I realized that I had cheated him"","" for I had driven him to the land of Thamūd — a journey of three nights — while he brought me to the land of Madīna — a journey of three nights.\""\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""""
"10454","(10449) Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani al-Faqih both said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abu 'Ubayd Allah Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to me: My uncle said: Makhrah ibn Bukayr narrated to me from his father, who said: I heard 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb saying: I heard Shu'ayb saying: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \When any one of you enters into a sale with another person"","" each of them has the option until they part from one another's place"","" unless it be a sale of option (bay' al-khiyar)"","" and it is not permissible for either of them to part from his companion for fear that he may annul the transaction.\""\n\nHis statement \""that he may annul it\"" — meaning thereby the rescission (faskh) — he expressed rescission through the term al-iqalah.\n\nAnd we have been narrated regarding that from 'Uthman ibn 'Affan"","" 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar"","" and Jarir ibn 'Abd Allah"","" and then from Shurayh"","" Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab"","" and 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah.\n\nAl-Bukhari said in Kitab al-Sahih: And al-Layth narrated to me: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to me from Ibn Shihab"","" from Salim"","" from Ibn 'Umar"","" who said: \""I sold some property in al-Wadi to the Commander of the Faithful"","" 'Uthman — may Allah be pleased with him — for property he had in Khaybar. When we completed the transaction"","" I turned on my heels until I left his house"","" fearing that he might rescind the sale. And the established practice was that the two parties to a sale have the option until they part.\"" 'Abd Allah said: \""When my sale and his sale became binding"","" I realized that I had cheated him"","" for I had driven him to the land of Thamud in three nights"","" and he had driven me to al-Madinah in three nights.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"10455","(10450) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; Abū ʿImrān narrated to us; al-Ramādī narrated — Abū Bakr said — and al-Ḥasan informed me; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated — and Abū al-Qāsim informed us; Ibn Zanjawayh narrated — they all said: Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; al-Layth narrated with this (chain).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Abū Ṣāliḥ also narrated it, as did Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, from al-Layth, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd, from Ibn Shihāb, with the same meaning."
"10456","(10451) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, from ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Zurʿa, who said: Jarīr said: \I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) upon hearing and obedience"","" and upon giving sincere counsel to every Muslim.\"" He said: \""Whenever Jarīr concluded a sale with a person"","" he would say: 'Indeed"","" what we have taken from you is more beloved to us than what we have given you — so exercise your choice.' He intended by this the completion of his pledge of allegiance.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4945).]"""""
"10457","(10452) And Ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad informed us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Yūnus narrated it with a similar chain, except that he did not say: \intending thereby the completion of his pledge of allegiance.\"" [Sahih. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10458","(10453) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī said: I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī say: I heard Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī say: I heard Sufyān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik say: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak say: \The hadith regarding 'the two parties to a sale have the option (of annulment) so long as they have not separated' is more firmly established than these pillars.\"" He said: And I heard ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd say: I heard ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī say"","" from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"","" that he narrated to the Kūfans the hadith of Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ regarding \""the two parties to a sale have the option so long as they have not separated.\"" He said: So they narrated it to Abū Ḥanīfah"","" and Abū Ḥanīfah said: \""This is nothing. What if they are both on a ship?\"" ʿAlī said: \""Allah will question him for what he said.\"" [Sahih.]"""""
"10459","(10454) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: al-Ḥākim Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muʿaddil in Ḥalab narrated to us: Ibrāhīm, meaning ibn Saʿīd al-Jawharī, narrated to us: Ḥusayn, meaning ibn Muḥammad al-Marwarrūdhī, narrated to us: Shaybān narrated from Manṣūr, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When two men make a sale"","" they both have the option (of annulment) so long as they have not separated"","" or their sale is one with an option (of annulment).\""\n\nAnd ʿUmar"","" or Ibn ʿUmar"","" used to call out: \""A sale is either a binding transaction (ṣafqah) or one with an option (khiyār).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Muṭarrif ibn Ṭarīf"","" on one occasion from al-Shaʿbī on the authority of ʿUmar"","" and on another occasion from ʬāṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ on the authority of ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — (the statement): \""A sale is either a binding transaction or one with an option.\"" Both of these narrations are weak due to the discontinuity (inqiṭāʿ) of that chain. If it is authentic"","" then what is meant by it — and Allah knows best — is a sale in which there is a stipulation to terminate the option"","" so that after the transaction they have no option; or a sale in which there is no stipulation to terminate the option"","" so that they both have the option so long as they have not separated. Many of the people of knowledge have deemed the narration from ʿUmar to be weak"","" and they hold that it is not permissible in a sale to stipulate the termination of the option. What is meant by \""a sale with an option\"" is either the option after the sale"","" or a sale with a stipulation of a three-day option"","" in which case their option is not terminated by separation due to the stipulation. The correct view is that what is meant by it — and Allah knows best — is the option after the sale"","" except that Nāfiʿ sometimes expressed it as \""a sale with an option\"" and sometimes explained it. That which clarifies this is:"""""
"10460","(10455) What Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us. And Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us. Both said: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The two parties to a sale have the option (of annulment) until they separate"","" or it is a sale with an option.\"" Nāfiʿ said: \""Or one of them says to the other: 'Choose (what you will).'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr."""""
"10461","(10456) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Fāmī, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever purchases a muṣarrāh (an animal whose milk has been retained)"","" he has the option (of annulment) for three days. If he returns it"","" he returns it along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Qurrah from Ibn Sīrīn."""""
"10462","(10457) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik. And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥajjāj and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us. All of them narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, that he heard Ibn ʿUmar say: A man mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he was being cheated in sales. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \When you make a sale"","" say: 'No deception (lā khalābah).'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym"","" and in another place from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. And Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. It was also narrated from the ḥadīth of Ghundar from Shuʿbah"","" and it was narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar with additional wording. [Sahih. Muslim 1524.]"""""
"10463","(10458) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us. He said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to me from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: Ḥabbān ibn Munqidh was a man who was weak, and he had been struck on his head leaving a scar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him the option (of annulment) for three days in whatever he purchased. His tongue had become heavy (he had a speech impediment). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Sell and say: 'No deception (lā khalābah).'\"" I used to hear him say: \""No deception"","" no deception"",""\"" and he would purchase something and bring it to his family"","" and they would say: \""This is expensive.\"" He would say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the option in my sale.\"" [Hasan. al-Ḥākim narrated it (2/26).]"""""
"10464","(10459) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Nāfiʿ narrated to me, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I heard a man from the Anṣār — and there was an impediment in his tongue — complaining to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he was always being cheated in sales. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \When you make a sale"","" say: 'No deception (lā khalābah).' Then you have the option in every commodity you purchase for three nights. If you are pleased"","" keep it"","" and if you are displeased"","" return it.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: It is as though I can still hear him"","" whenever he made a sale"","" saying: \""No deception"",""\"" his tongue faltering.\n\nIbn Isḥāq said: I narrated this hadith to Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān"","" and he said: My grandfather was Munqidh ibn ʿAmr. He was a man who had been struck on his head by a severe wound"","" which impaired his tongue and diminished his intellect. He was being cheated in sales"","" but he would not abandon trade. He complained of that to the Prophet ﷺ"","" and the Prophet ﷺ said: \""When you sell"","" say: 'No deception.' Then you have the option in every sale you make for three nights. If you are pleased"","" keep it"","" and if you are displeased"","" return it.\""\n\nHe lived on until the time of ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — and he was a hundred and thirty years old. The people had become numerous in the time of ʿUthmān. When he purchased something and brought it back"","" they would say to him: \""You should not have bought this.\"" He would say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the option for three days in whatever I purchase.\"" They would say: \""Return it"","" for you have been cheated\"" — or he said: \""deceived.\"" So he would go back to his transaction and say: \""Take your commodity and return my dirhams.\"" The seller would say: \""I will not do so; you were pleased (with the sale).\"" He would persist until a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pass by and say: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has given him the option for three days in whatever he purchases.\"" Then the seller would return his dirhams to him and take back his commodity. [Hasan. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10465","(10460) And Abū Bakr narrated to us: Abū al-Shaykh narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Jamīl narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlá narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated something similar to it."
"10466","(10461) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — Abū al-Shaykh — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid, meaning ibn Yazīd al-Rāsibī al-Nīlī, narrated to us: Abū Maysarah Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Maysarah narrated to us: Abū ʿAlqamah al-Farwī narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The option (of annulment) is for three days.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: This is an abridged version of the hadith of Ibn Isḥāq. [Munkar.]"""""
"10467","(10462) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, by way of ijāzah, he said: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Lahīʿah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Asad ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to us, Ḥabbān ibn Wāsiʿ narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah: that he spoke to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding sales transactions, and ʿUmar said: \I cannot find for you anything more expansive than what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted to Ḥabbān ibn Munḏhir. He was weak of eyesight"","" so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted him a respite of three days: if he was pleased"","" he would keep it"","" and if he was displeased"","" he would return it.\""\n\nAnd ʿUbayd ibn Abī Qurrah narrated it from Ibn Lahīʿah"","" from Ḥabbān ibn Wāsiʿ"","" from his father"","" from his grandfather"","" from ʿUmar"","" in an abbreviated form"","" and he did not mention \""weak of eyesight.\"" This narration is reported uniquely by Ibn Lahīʿah"","" and Allah knows best. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 3/54]"""""
"10468","(10463) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Asadī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, Sayyār Abū al-Ḥakam narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy took a horse from a man at an agreed price. He mounted a man upon it, and it was injured while in its care. The man disputed with him, so ʿUmar said: \Appoint a man between you and me.\"" The man said: \""I am satisfied with Shurayḥ al-ʿIrāqī.\"" So they came to Shurayḥ"","" and Shurayḥ said to ʿUmar: \""You took it sound and healthy"","" and you are responsible for it until you return it sound and healthy.\"" This pleased ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāy"","" so he appointed him as a judge"","" and he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn ʿAsākir in his Tārīkh 34/18]"""""
"10469","(10464) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, my father narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Zurārah narrated to us, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, regarding the Ḥajj of the Prophet (ﷺ) and his sermon at ʿArafah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"","" your blood and your wealth are sacred to you"","" as sacred as this day of yours"","" in this month of yours"","" in this land of yours. Behold"","" indeed all matters of the Jāhiliyyah are placed beneath my two feet"","" and the bloodshed of the Jāhiliyyah is annulled. The first blood I annul is the blood of Rabīʿah ibn al-Ḥārith"","" who was being nursed among Banī Saʿd"","" and Hudhayl killed him during the time of the Jāhiliyyah. And the usury of the Jāhiliyyah is annulled. The first usury I annul is the usury of al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"","" for it is entirely annulled.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1218]"""""
"10470","(10465) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, Shabīb ibn Gharqadah narrated from Sulaymān ibn ʿAmr, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \Behold"","" all usury of the Jāhiliyyah is annulled. You are entitled to the principal of your wealth; you shall neither commit injustice nor shall injustice be committed against you. Behold"","" all bloodshed of the Jāhiliyyah is annulled. The first blood I annul thereof is the blood of al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"","" who was being nursed among Banī Layth"","" and Hudhayl killed him. O Allah"","" have I conveyed?\"" They said: \""Yes"",""\"" three times. He said: \""O Allah"","" bear witness"",""\"" three times. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than the previous chain. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3334]"""""
"10471","(10466) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding His statement {And leave what remains of usury} (al-Baqarah 2:278), he said: \A man would have a debt owed to him by another man"","" and he would say: 'You owe me such-and-such an increase"","" and you may defer it for me.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10472","(10467) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: \Usury in the Jāhiliyyah was that a man would have a debt owed to him by another man for a fixed term. When the term expired"","" he would say: 'Will you pay"","" or will you increase it?' If he paid"","" he would take it; otherwise"","" he would increase his debt"","" and the other would extend the term.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 1353]"""""
"10473","(10468) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us, my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Bakr ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī informed us, ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us, they both said: Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated to us, Abū al-Zubayr informed us, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the consumer of usury, the one who pays it, its scribe, and its two witnesses, and he said: \They are all equal.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Ṣāliḥ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1598]"""""
"10474","(10469) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah and Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, who said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, from his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) cursed the consumer of usury, the one who pays it, and its two witnesses—or he said, its witness and its scribe. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2277]"
"10475","(10470) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, Abū Rajāʾ informed us, from Samurah ibn Jundab, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished praying, he would turn his face toward us and say: \Has anyone among you seen a dream tonight?\""\n\nThe ḥadīth: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""I saw two men who came to me"","" took me by the hand"","" and brought me out to a flat land or an open space.\""\n\nThe ḥadīth"","" and he said in it: \""We proceeded until we came to a river of blood"","" in which men were standing"","" and a man was standing on the bank of the river with stones before him. The one in the river would come forward"","" and when he tried to get out"","" the man would throw a stone into his mouth and send him back to where he was. Every time he came to get out"","" the man would throw a stone into his mouth and send him back to where he was. I said to the two men: 'What is this?' He said: 'The one you saw in the river is the consumer of usury.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1320]"""""
"10476","(10471) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī informed us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū Muḥammad Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad ibn Daʿlaj informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us, they both said: Qabīṣah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The last verse that Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" revealed to His Messenger (ﷺ) was the verse of usury.\"" And al-Wāsiṭī said: \""It was revealed.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4270]"""""
"10477","(10472) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — ʿAbbād ibn Rāshid informed us. He said: I heard Saʿīd ibn Abī Khayrah narrating to Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, who narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, from approximately forty years ago or thereabouts, from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There will come upon the people a time in which they will consume ribā (usury/interest) — or he said: all of them will consume it. Whoever does not consume it will be afflicted by its dust.\"" [Weak. Abū Dāwūd (3331)]"""""
"10478","(10473) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us — Khālid informed us, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Khayrah, from al-Ḥasan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There will most certainly come upon the people a time in which no one will remain except that he consumes ribā. Whoever does not consume it will be struck by its vapour.\"" [Weak. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10479","(10474) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāh al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and others said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh, meaning al-Qaʿnabī, and Abū Muṣʿab narrated to us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān, who informed him that he sought a currency exchange for one hundred dinars. He said: Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydullāh, may Allah be pleased with him, called me, and we negotiated until he purchased from me. He took the gold and was turning it over in his hand, then said: \Wait until my treasurer comes from al-Ghābah.\"" And ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" was listening. ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""By Allah"","" do not leave him until you take your payment from him.\"" Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Gold for gold is ribā"","" except hand to hand (on the spot); silver for silver is ribā"","" except hand to hand; wheat for wheat is ribā"","" except hand to hand; dates for dates is ribā"","" except hand to hand; and barley for barley is ribā"","" except hand to hand.\"" The wording of their hadith is the same"","" except that in the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī it reads: \""Wait until my treasurer comes"","" or until my servant girl comes from al-Ghābah.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: I read it to Mālik correctly"","" without any doubt. Then a long time passed and I did not memorise it precisely"","" so I became uncertain whether it was 'my servant girl' or 'my treasurer"",""' while others narrate 'my treasurer' from him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and he said: \""Until my treasurer comes.\"" And Muslim and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Layth ibn Saʿd and others from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī (2065)]"""""
"10480","(10475) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others said — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Qutbiyyah informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not sell gold for gold except equal for equal"","" and do not make some of it exceed others. Do not sell silver for silver except equal for equal"","" and do not make some of it exceed others. And do not sell any of it that is absent (ghāʾib) for that is present (nājiz).\"" In the narration of Abī Naṣr: \""And do not sell any of it as absent for that which is present.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And ʿUbādah"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" mentioned from the Prophet ﷺ something of similar meaning and clarified it"","" then he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī (2068)]"""""
"10481","(10476) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and others said — Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us — from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah — from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn — from Muslim ibn Yasār and another man — from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not sell gold for gold"","" nor silver for silver"","" nor wheat for wheat"","" nor barley for barley"","" nor dates for dates"","" nor salt for salt"","" except equal for equal"","" like for like"","" of the same kind"","" hand to hand. But sell gold for silver"","" and silver for gold"","" and wheat for barley"","" and barley for wheat"","" and dates for salt"","" and salt for dates"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish.\"" One of the two (narrators) omitted salt or dates"","" and the other added: \""Whoever gives more or takes more has indeed committed ribā.\"" The other man is said to be ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. (1587)]"""""
"10482","(10477) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us — Salamah ibn ʿAlqamah narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn informed us that Muslim ibn Yasār and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd both narrated to him, saying: The place brought together ʿUbādah and Muʿāwiyah, either in a transaction or in a church. He said: And he mentioned the hadith regarding currency exchange in its full length.\n\nThis ḥadīth was not heard by Muslim ibn Yasār from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit; rather, he heard it from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī from ʿUbādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"10483","(10478) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-Munādī narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us — Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah informed us — from Qatādah — from Muslim ibn Yasār — from Abī al-Ashʿath — from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that he stood and said: \O people"","" you have indeed introduced transactions of which I know not what they are. Indeed"","" gold for gold — its raw form and its minted form — weight for weight"","" hand to hand; and silver for silver — hand to hand"","" its raw form and its minted form. There is no harm in selling gold for silver"","" and silver for gold"","" the greater of the two in weight for weight"","" hand to hand. But deferred payment (nasīʾah) is not permissible. And wheat for wheat — mudd for mudd"","" hand to hand; and barley for barley — muddayn for muddayn"","" hand to hand. There is no harm in selling barley for wheat"","" and barley being the greater of the two"","" hand to hand. But deferred payment is not permissible. And dates for dates —\"" until he counted \""— salt for salt"","" like for like"","" hand to hand. Whoever gives more or takes more has indeed committed ribā.\"" Qatādah said: And ʿUbādah was a Badrī"","" an ʿAqbī"","" one of the leaders of the Anṣār"","" and he had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he would not fear"","" regarding Allah"","" the blame of any blamer. Thus narrated Ibn Abī ʿArūbah.\n\nAnd Hammām ibn Yaḥyā"","" who is among the trustworthy narrators"","" narrated it from Qatādah"","" from Abī al-Khalīl"","" from Muslim"","" connected and marfūʿ"","" reaching the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""""
"10484","(10479) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Hishām ibn ʿAlī ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us — Hammām narrated to us — from Qatādah — from Abī al-Khalīl — from Muslim al-Makkī — from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī, that he witnessed the sermon of ʿUbādah and heard him narrate from the Prophet ﷺ: \Gold for gold — its raw form and its minted form — weight for weight; and silver for silver — its raw form and its minted form — weight for weight; and wheat for wheat; and barley for barley; and dates for dates; and salt for salt — whoever gives more or takes more has indeed committed ribā. And there is no harm in selling barley for wheat"","" hand to hand"","" and barley being the greater of the two.\"" This is the correct version.\n\nAnd the established ḥadīth is ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Qilābah"","" from Abī al-Ashʿath"","" from ʿUbādah"","" marfūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim (1587)]"""""
"10485","(10480) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr and ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawarīrī both narrated to us. They said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abī Qilābah, who said: I was in Shām in a gathering in which Muslim ibn Yasār was present. Then Abī al-Ashʿath came. They said: \Abī al-Ashʿath! Abī al-Ashʿath!\"" So he sat down. I said to him: \""Narrate to us the ḥadīth of ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit.\"" He said: \""Yes. We went on an expedition"","" and over the people was Muʿāwiyah. We acquired abundant spoils"","" and among what we acquired were vessels of silver. Muʿāwiyah ordered a man to sell them as stipends to the people"","" so the people rushed to purchase them. This reached ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" so he stood and said: 'Indeed"","" I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid the sale of gold for gold"","" silver for silver"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" dates for dates"","" and salt for salt"","" except equal for equal"","" like for like"","" hand to hand. Whoever gives more or takes more has indeed committed ribā.' So the people returned what they had taken. This reached Muʿāwiyah"","" so he stood as an orator and said: 'What is the matter with men who narrate ḥadīths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — we used to witness him and accompany him"","" yet we did not hear these from him?' So ʿUbādah"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" stood and repeated the story"","" then said: 'We shall narrate what we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" even if Muʿāwiyah dislikes it' — or he said: 'even if Muʿāwiyah is angered.' I care not if I do not accompany him in his army on a dark night.'\"" Ḥammād said: \""This or something similar.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawarīrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. (1587)]"""""
"10486","(10481) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us. Isḥāq said: \He informed us"",""\"" and Ibn Bashshār said: \""He narrated to us\"" — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us — Ayyūb narrated to us"","" from Abī Qilābah"","" from Abī al-Ashʿath"","" who said: We were on an expedition"","" and over us was Muʿāwiyah. We acquired gold and silver as spoils. Muʿāwiyah ordered a man to sell them to the people as their stipends"","" so the people rushed to purchase them. ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" stood and forbade them"","" so they returned them. The man went to Muʿāwiyah and complained to him"","" so Muʿāwiyah stood as an orator and said: \""What is the matter with men who narrate ḥadīths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" attributing lies to him"","" which we did not hear from him?\"" So ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit stood and said: \""By Allah"","" we shall narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" even if Muʿāwiyah dislikes it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do not sell gold for gold"","" nor silver for silver"","" nor wheat for wheat"","" nor barley for barley"","" nor salt for salt"","" nor dates for dates"","" except equal for equal"","" like for like"","" hand to hand.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""""
"10487","(10482) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥad al-Miṣrī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: al-Firyābī narrated to us: Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Abū al-Ashʿath, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Gold for gold"","" equal in weight and equal in measure; silver for silver"","" equal in weight and equal in measure; salt for salt"","" like for like; barley for barley"","" like for like; wheat for wheat"","" like for like; and dates for dates"","" like for like. Whoever gives more or asks for more has engaged in usury (ribā). So sell gold for silver"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish; and dates for salt"","" hand to hand; and barley for wheat"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See before it.]"""""
"10488","""The one who takes gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, dates for dates, and a hand for a hand, if these categories differ, then sell as you wish, for a hand is for a hand."""","" silver for silver"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" dates for dates"","" and salt for salt"","" like for like"","" equal for equal"","" hand to hand. If these categories differ"","" then sell however you wish"","" provided it is hand to hand.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed it: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Wakīʿ —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān — and he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See before it.]"""""
"10489","(10484) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsá narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Ḥakīm ibn Jābir, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Gold by the handful for gold by the handful"","" and silver by the handful for silver by the handful\"" — until he specified and said: \""Salt for salt.\"" Muʿāwiyah said: \""This says nothing.\"" ʿUbādah"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"","" 4566.]"""""
"10490","(10485) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsá —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Khālid ibn Mawhab al-Ramlī — both of them said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhrah ibn Bukayr narrated to me from his father, that he heard Sulaymān ibn Yasār narrating that he heard Mālik ibn Abī ʿĀmir narrating from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not sell one dīnār for two dīnārs"","" nor one dirham for two dirhams.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsá and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1585.]"""""
"10491","(10486) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Mūsá ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Mūsá ibn Abī Tamīm —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik narrated from Mūsá ibn Abī Tamīm, from Saʿīd ibn Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A dīnār for a dīnār"","" with no excess between them; and a dirham for a dirham"","" with no excess between them.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"","" and it was also narrated from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1588.]"""""
"10492","(10487) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abū al-Mutawakkil al-Nājī narrated to us: from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Gold for gold"","" silver for silver"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" dates for dates"","" and salt for salt"","" like for like"","" hand to hand. Whoever gives more or takes more has committed usury — the taker and the giver are equal in it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1584.]"""""
"10493","(10488) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us: Ibn ʿAwn informed us from Nāfiʿ, who said: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar and narrated to him a ḥadīth from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī. Then Abū Saʿīd arrived and came down to this house. He (Nāfiʿ) took my hand until we came to him. He (Ibn ʿUmar) said: \What does this man narrate from you?\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""My eye saw and my ear heard\"" — he did not forget his saying"","" pointing with his finger — \""the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling gold for gold and silver for silver"","" except equal for equal"","" like for like; and that you should not make one of them exceed the other; and that you should not sell absent (commodities) for present (ones).\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn"","" and al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2176.]"""""
"10494","(10489) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Saʿīd narrated from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAmr ibn Thābit al-ʿAtawārī narrated to Ibn ʿUmar that he heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrating from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \A dīnār for a dīnār and a dirham for a dirham"","" with no excess between them.\"" ʿAbd Allāh (ibn ʿUmar) walked"","" and Nāfiʿ was with him"","" until they entered upon Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī. He asked him"","" and he said: \""My eye saw and my ear heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'A dīnār for a dīnār and a dirham for a dirham"","" weight for weight"","" with no excess between them"","" and a present (commodity) shall not be sold for an absent one.'\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyá ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1584.]"""""
"10495","(10490) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Shaybān ibn Farūkh narrated to us — both of them said: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us. He said: I heard Nāfiʿ saying: Ibn ʿUmar used to narrate from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding currency exchange (al-ṣarf), and he had not heard anything in that from the Prophet ￺. He (ʿUmar) said: \Do not sell gold for gold"","" nor silver for gold"","" except like for like"","" equal for equal; and do not make some of it exceed some. I fear for you al-ramāʾ.\"" I said to Nāfiʿ: \""And what is al-ramāʾ?\"" He said: \""Al-ribā (usury).\"" Then a man from the Anṣār narrated to him a ḥadīth from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī. Nāfiʿ said: He took the hand of the Anṣārī"","" and I was with them"","" until we entered upon Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī. He said: \""O Abū Saʿīd"","" this man narrated from you such-and-such a ḥadīth.\"" He said: \""What is it?\"" He mentioned it. He said: \""Yes"","" my two ears heard and my two eyes saw\"" — he said it three times"","" gesturing with his two fingers toward his two eyes — \""the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Do not sell gold for gold"","" and do not sell silver for gold"","" except like for like"","" equal for equal; and do not sell any of it"","" absent for present; and do not make some of it exceed some.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān ibn Farūkh"","" without the statement of ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1584.]"""""
"10496","(10491) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Sammāk informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays al-Makkī, from Mujāhid, who said: I was with Ibn ʿUmar when a goldsmith came and said to him: \O ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" I refine gold and then sell from it something for more than its weight"","" taking the excess as the wage for my labor.\"" Ibn ʿUmar forbade him from that. The goldsmith kept repeating the question to him"","" and Ibn ʿUmar kept forbidding him"","" until they reached the door of the mosque"","" at the mount he was to ride. Ibn ʿUmar said: \""A dīnār for a dīnār and a dirham for a dirham"","" with no excess between them. This is the covenant of our Prophet ﷺ to us"","" and our covenant to you.\""\n\nIn the narration of Sālim and Nāfiʿ there is an indication that Ibn ʿUmar had not heard anything in that from the Prophet ﷺ"","" but rather heard it from his father"","" and then from Abū Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1300.]"""""
"10497","(10492) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿUmar that he said: \Dīnār for dīnār and dirham for dirham"","" there is no excess between them. This is the covenant of our Prophet ﷺ to us"","" and our covenant to you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10498","(10493) Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in the transmission of al-Muzanī from him in full, in the story of the goldsmith. Then he said: \This is an error.\"" Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from Wardān al-Rūmī that he asked Ibn ʿUmar"","" saying: \""I am a man who fashions jewellery and then sells it"","" taking in it the equivalent of my wage or the work of my hands.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: \""Gold for gold"","" there is no excess between them. This is the covenant of our Companion to us"","" and our covenant to you.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""By 'our Companion' he means ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.\""\n\nAbū Isḥāq al-Uramwī narrated to us: Shāfiʿ ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Salamah narrated to us: al-Muzanī narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10499","(10494) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and others narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh, meaning al-Qaʿnabī, narrated from Mālik from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār that Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān sold a vessel of gold or silver for more than its weight. Abū al-Dardāʾ said to him: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid such a thing"","" except like for like.\"" Muʿāwiyah said: \""I see no harm in it.\"" Abū al-Dardāʾ said to him: \""Who will excuse me before Muʿāwiyah? I inform him of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he informs me of his own opinion. I shall not reside with you in a land in which you are.\"" Then Abū al-Dardāʾ came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" and mentioned that to him. So ʿUmar wrote to Muʿāwiyah: \""Do not sell it except like for like"","" weight for weight.\"" Al-Rabīʿ did not mention from al-Shāfiʿī in this report the coming of Abū al-Dardāʾ to ʿUmar"","" though al-Shāfiʿī mentioned it in the transmission of al-Muzanī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1302.]"""""
"10500","(10495) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us that he heard ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd say: \I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: 'Usāmah ibn Zayd informed me that the Prophet ￠ said: \""Indeed"","" ribā (usury) is in al-nasīʾah (deferred payment).\""'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and a group"","" from Ibn ʿUyaynah. Likewise"","" Ṭāwūs"","" ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ"","" and others narrated it from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 1596.]"""""
"10501","(10496) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān narrated to us, saying: \I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī relate that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Dirham for dirham and dīnār for dīnār"","" like for like; there is no excess between them.'\""\n\nI said to Abū Saʿīd: \""Ibn ʿAbbās used to see no harm in it.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""I met Ibn ʿAbbās and said to him: 'Tell me about what you say — is it something you found in the Book of Allah"","" or something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'I did not find it in the Book of Allah"","" nor did I hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. But you are more knowledgeable about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than I. However"","" Usāmah ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"","" ribā is in al-nasīʾah (deferred payment).\""'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād and others"","" from Sufyān. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj"","" from ʿAmr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 2069.]"""""
"10502","(10497) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār and ʿĀmir ibn Muṣʿab narrated to us that they both heard Abū al-Minhāl say: \I asked al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib and Zayd ibn Arqam about al-ṣarf (exchange)"","" and they both said: 'We were merchants in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" so we asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about al-ṣarf. He said: \""Whatever is hand to hand (on the spot)"","" there is no harm in it; and whatever is on credit (deferred)"","" it is not permissible.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim"","" without mentioning ʿĀmir ibn Muṣʿab. He also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad"","" from Ibn Jurayj"","" with the mention of ʿĀmir ibn Muṣʿab. Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim ibn Maymūn"","" from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"","" from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from Abū al-Minhāl"","" who said: \""A partner of mine sold silver on credit until the season or the Ḥajj"","" and he mentioned it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated something similar from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"","" from Sufyān.\n\n{T} Likewise"","" Aḥmad ibn Rawḥ narrated it from Sufyān.\n\nIt was also narrated from al-Ḥumaydī"","" from Sufyān"","" from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"","" from Abū al-Minhāl"","" who said: \""A partner of mine sold dirhams for dirhams in Kūfah"","" with an excess between them.\"" I consider this to be an error"","" and the correct narration is what ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī and Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim narrated. This is what is intended by what was stated without qualification in the transmission of Ibn Jurayj. Thus the ḥadīth pertains to the sale of one genus for another of a different genus. He said: \""Whatever is hand to hand"","" there is no harm; and whatever is deferred"","" it is not permissible.\"" This is what is intended by the ḥadīth of Usāmah"","" and Allah knows best. That which indicates this is also: [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 1955.]"""""
"10503","(10498) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Birtī narrated to us: Abū ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Ḥabīb, who is Ibn Abī Thābit, narrated to us, saying: \I heard Abū al-Minhāl say: 'I asked al-Barāʾ and Zayd ibn Arqam about al-ṣarf"","" and both of them said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of silver for gold on credit (as deferred payment).\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿUmar Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar. Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 2070.]"""""
"10504","(10499) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from Abū Naḍrah, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās about al-ṣarf"","" and they saw no harm in it. While I was sitting with Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" I asked him about al-ṣarf. He said: 'Whatever exceeds is ribā (usury).' I rejected that because of their statement. He said: 'I will only narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The owner of date-palms came with a ṣāʿ of fine dates"","" while the dates of the Prophet ﷺ were of an inferior quality. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \""How did you come by this?\"" He said: \""I took my ṣāʿ and bought this ṣāʿ with it"","" for the market price of this is such-and-such and the market price of that is such-and-such.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \""You have engaged in ribā when you intended that. Sell your dates for a commodity"","" and then buy with your commodity whatever dates you wish.\""' Abū Saʿīd said: 'So dates for dates are more deserving of being considered ribā"","" or silver for silver.' He said: 'Then I came to Ibn ʿUmar afterwards"","" and he forbade me. I did not go to Ibn ʿAbbās.' He said: 'Abū al-Ṣahbāʾ narrated to me that he asked Ibn ʿAbbās about it"","" and he disapproved of it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and he said: \""The dates of the Prophet ﷺ were of this colour.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 1594.]"""""
"10505","(10500) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn, Abū ʿAlī al-Māsarjisī, narrated to us: My grandfather, Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad — and he was the son of the daughter of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā — narrated to us: My grandfather al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Abī al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated from Maʿrūf ibn Saʿd that he heard Abū al-Jawzāʾ say: \I served Ibn ʿAbbās for nine years. A man came to him and asked about one dirham for two dirhams. Ibn ʿAbbās raised his voice and said: 'This one commands me to feed him ribā!' The people around him said: 'We used to act upon your ruling (fatwā).' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'I used to give that ruling until Abū Saʿīd and Ibn ʿUmar narrated to me that the Prophet ﷺ forbade it. So I forbid you from it.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn ʿAsākir in Tārīkh"","" 14/292.]"""""
"10506","(10501) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated from Isrāʾīl, from Abī Isḥāq, from Saʿd ibn Iyās, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, that a man from Banū Shamkh ibn Fazārah asked him about a man who married a woman, then saw her mother and was attracted to her, so he divorced his wife — could he marry her mother? He said: \There is no harm.\"" So the man married her. ʿAbdullāh was in charge of the bayt al-māl (public treasury)"","" and he used to sell the surplus of the bayt al-māl"","" giving much and taking little. Then he came to Madīnah and asked the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ. They said: \""This woman is not lawful for this man"","" and silver is not permissible except weight for weight.\"" When ʿAbdullāh arrived"","" he went to the man but did not find him; he found his people and said: \""That which I gave as a ruling (fatwā) to your companion is not lawful.\"" They said: \""She has already conceived by him.\"" He said: \""Even so.\"" Then he came to the money-changers (al-ṣayārifah) and said: \""O company of money-changers! Indeed"","" that which I used to transact with you is not lawful. Silver for silver is not permissible except weight for weight.\"" [Narrated by al-Fasawī in al-Maʿrifah"","" 1/88.]"""""
"10507","(10502) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah narrated from his father that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of silver for silver and gold for gold except in equal measure for equal measure, and he commanded us to purchase silver for gold and gold for silver however we wished. He (the narrator) said: A man asked him, saying, \Hand to hand?\"" He replied"","" \""Thus I heard.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿImrān ibn Maisarah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ"","" both from ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2071]"""""
"10508","(10503) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us; Abū Kurayb informed us; Ibn Fuḍayl informed us, from his father, from Abū Zurʿah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Dates for dates"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" and salt for salt — like for like"","" hand to hand. Whoever increases or seeks an increase has indeed engaged in ribā (usury)"","" except when the types differ.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1588]"""""
"10509","(10504) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh informed us; Yazīd ibn al-Haytham informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth informed us; al-Ashjaʿī informed us, from Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī, from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that he witnessed the people trading vessels of gold and silver until the time of the gifts (al-aʿṭiyah). ʿUbadah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Sell gold for gold"","" silver for silver"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" dates for dates"","" and salt for salt — equal for equal"","" like for like. Whoever increases or seeks an increase has indeed engaged in ribā. When these categories differ"","" then sell them hand to hand however you wish"","" there is no harm in it — gold for silver"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish; wheat for barley"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish; and salt for dates"","" hand to hand"","" however you wish.\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ from Sufyān al-Thawrī as mentioned above"","" and this is a sound"","" explanatory narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1587]"""""
"10510","(10505) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us; ʿAffān informed us; Hammām informed us; Qatādah informed us, from Abī al-Khalīl, from Muslim, from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī, that he witnessed a sermon of ʿUbadah in which he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it is: \And there is no harm in selling barley for wheat"","" even if the barley is greater in quantity.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10511","(10506) Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated it from Hammām, and he said in the ḥadīth: \And there is no harm in selling gold for silver"","" even if the silver is greater in quantity"","" hand to hand; as for deferred payment (nasīʾah)"","" no. And there is no harm in selling wheat for barley"","" even if the barley is greater in quantity"","" hand to hand; as for deferred payment"","" no.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī informed us; Bishr ibn ʿUmar informed us"","" and he mentioned it. As for the ḥadīth which… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd 3349]"""""
"10512","(10507) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf ibn Khālid informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that Abū al-Naḍr informed him that Busr ibn Saʿīd informed him from Maʿmar ibn ʿAbdillāh, that he sent his slave with a ṣāʿ of wheat. He said: \Sell it"","" then buy barley with it.\"" The slave went and took a ṣāʿ and some additional amount. When Maʿmar came"","" the slave informed him of that. Maʿmar said to him: \""Why did you do that? Go and return it"","" and do not take anything except like for like"","" for I used to hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Food for food"","" like for like.'\"" And our food at that time that was barley. It was said: \""But it is not its equivalent.\"" He said: \""Then I fear that it may resemble (ribā).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir and others.\n\nWhat Maʿmar ibn ʿAbdillāh disliked was out of caution against falling into ribā"","" on his own initiative"","" not based on a narration. The narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) is general and encompasses both possibilities — that he intended a single category (jins) alone"","" or both categories together. When ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit came with a text that specified one of the two possibilities"","" it became obligatory to refer to it. And with Allah lies success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1592]"""""
"10513","(10508) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Khalīfah informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Layth informed us. And Abū Bakr informed us; al-Fāryābī informed us; and al-Ḥasan informed me. They both said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us; al-Layth informed us, from Ibn Shihāb — and this is the ḥadīth of Abū al-Walīd — from Mālik ibn Aws, who said: I came saying, \Who will exchange the dirhams?\"" Ṭalḥah said: \""Show us the gold until the treasurer comes"","" then come and take your silver.\"" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""No"","" by the One in whose Hand is my soul"","" you must return his gold to him or pay him his silver"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Gold for silver is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ (hand to hand); wheat for wheat is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; barley for barley is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; and dates for dates is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ.'\"" Qutaybah said: \""Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh said this while he was in the presence of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab (may Allah be pleased with them both)"","" and he said: 'Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said it.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2062]"""""
"10514","(10509) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān informed us; ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed us first, before we met al-Zuhrī, from Ibn Shihāb, from Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān, who said: I came with a hundred dinars seeking an exchange. Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh said to me: \We have an exchange; wait until our treasurer comes from the forest (al-ghābah).\"" He took the hundred dinars from me. I asked ʿUmar"","" and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: \""Do not part from him"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Gold for silver is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; wheat for wheat is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; barley for barley is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; and dates for dates is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ.'\"" Sufyān said: \""When al-Zuhrī came to us"","" I checked him"","" but he did not mention this wording.\"" He said: \""I heard al-Zuhrī say: 'I heard Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān al-Naṣrī say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Gold for silver is ribā…\""'\"" He mentioned something similar in full. Sufyān said: \""And this is the most authentic ḥadīth narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding this matter"","" i.e."","" the exchange (ṣarf).\"" And sometimes Sufyān would say in it: \""Al-Zuhrī narrated to us; he said: Mālik informed me.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān"","" in abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Extracted by al-Fasawī in al-Maʿrifah 1/355]"""""
"10515","(10510) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū ʿUtbah informed us; Ibn Abī Fudayk informed me; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Mālik ibn Aws ibn al-Ḥadathān, that he said: \I wanted an exchange (ṣarf).\"" Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbaydillāh said: \""I will exchange for you until my treasurer comes from the forest.\"" He said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Silver for silver is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; gold for gold is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; wheat for wheat is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ; and barley for barley is ribā"","" except haʾ wa-haʾ.'\"" Thus it is in this narration: \""silver for silver and gold for gold.\"" And the narration of the majority (al-jamāʿah) in the marfūʿ ḥadīth is as mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10516","(10511) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ informed us in Baghdād; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Najjād informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qāḍī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Kathīr informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab said: \Do not sell gold for gold except like for like"","" and do not sell silver for silver except like for like"","" and do not sell silver for gold with one of them being deferred and the other being immediate. And if he asks you to wait until he enters his house"","" do not wait for him — except hand to hand"","" give (and take). And this is because I fear ribā for you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Extracted by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭā 812]"""""
"10517","(10512) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad Abū al-Qāsim al-Ṭabarānī informed us, ʿAbbād al-ʿAdanī informed us, Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥakīm informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Sulaymān informed us, Ibn Ḥanbal informed us, my father informed us, Wakīʿ — all of them — from Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Abī al-Ashʿath, from ʿUbadah ibn al-Ṣāmit, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Gold for gold"","" silver for silver"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" dates for dates"","" and salt for salt — like for like. If these categories differ"","" then sell however you wish"","" provided it is hand to hand (on the spot).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" from Wakīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1584]"""""
"10518","(10513) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Ḥamzah ibn al-ʿAbbās al-ʿAqabī in Baghdād informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I used to sell camels in al-Baqīʿ"","" selling for dinars and taking dirhams"","" and selling for dirhams and taking dinars. This troubled my soul"","" so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Ḥafṣah — or he said: when he came out of the house of Ḥafṣah — and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" allow me to ask you: I sell camels in al-Baqīʿ; I sell for dinars and take dirhams"","" and I sell for dirhams and take dinars.' He said: 'There is no harm in taking it at the price of the day"","" so long as you do not separate and something remains between you (i.e."","" an outstanding obligation).'\""\n\nIsrāʾīl narrated something to this effect from Simāk. [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3354]"""""
"10519","(10514) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-Jawwāb informed us, ʿAmmār ibn Ruzayq informed us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I used to sell camels in al-Baqīʿ. Dirhams would accumulate with me"","" so I would sell them to a man for dinars"","" and he would give them to me the next day. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. He said: 'When you transact with a man in gold and silver"","" do not part from him while there is any ambiguity between you.'\""\n\nSomething close to its meaning was narrated in one of the two narrations from Isrāʾīl"","" from Simāk"","" and from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ"","" from Simāk. The hadith is singular in its being raised (marfūʿ) by Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"","" among the companions of Ibn ʿUmar. [Munkar. See the preceding]"""""
"10520","(10515) By way of corroboration: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us that Abū al-Naḍr informed him that Busr ibn Saʿīd informed him from Maʿmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who mentioned the hadith, and in it Maʿmar said: \I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Food for food"","" like for like.'\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ"","" as has been mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 10507]"""""
"10521","(10516) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāʾinī informed us there, Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥadhāʾ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us, from Mughīrah. Shibāk mentioned that Ibrāhīm said: \ʿAlqamah informed us"","" from ʿAbd Allāh"","" who said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the consumer of ribā and the one who feeds it to others.' He said: 'I said: And its two witnesses and its scribe?' He said: 'We only narrate what we have heard.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" from Jarīr. Al-Bukhārī extracted it from the hadith of Abī Juḥayfah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1597]"""""
"10522","(10517) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥīrī informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, Ibn Abī Zāʾidah informed us, from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the sale of the fruit of date palms for dates by measure, raisins for grapes by measure, and crops for wheat by measure.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1542]"
"10523","(10518) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā and Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq both said: al-Qaʿnabī informed us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us, from ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn Suhayl ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab narrate that Abū Hurayrah and Abū Saʿīd informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent the brother of Banī al-ʿAdī al-Anṣārī and appointed him over Khaybar. He came with excellent dates (janīb). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Is all the dates of Khaybar like this?\"" He said: \""No"","" by Allah"","" O Messenger of Allah. We merely buy one ṣāʿ for two ṣāʿs of mixed dates.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do not do so. Rather"","" sell like for like"","" or sell this and buy with its price from that. And likewise with the balance (mīzān).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"","" from his brother"","" from Sulaymān.\n\nLikewise"","" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Dārawardī narrated it from ʿAbd al-Majīd. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it from the hadith of Mālik"","" from ʿAbd al-Majīd"","" without his words \""And likewise with the balance.\"" Qatādah narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd without this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 6918]"""""
"10524","(10519) Abū al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī informed us, Yūnus ibn Muḥammad informed us, Ḥayyān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿAdawī Abū Zuhayr said: Lāḥiq ibn Ḥumayd, Abū Mijlaz, was asked about al-ṣarf (exchange) while I was present. He said: \Ibn ʿAbbās used to see no harm in it for a period of his life"","" until he met Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" who said to him: 'O Ibn ʿAbbās"","" do you not fear Allah? How long will you feed the people ribā? Has it not reached you that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day while he was with his wife Umm Salamah: \""I desire dates of ʿajwah.\"" She sent two ṣāʿs of old dates to the house of a man of the Anṣār"","" and in exchange she was given one ṣāʿ of ʿajwah dates. She presented them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and he was pleased with them. He took a date and then held back and said: \""Where did you get this from?\"" She said: \""I sent two ṣāʿs of old dates to the house of so-and-so"","" and in exchange we received this one ṣāʿ.\"" He threw the date from his hand and said: \""Return it"","" return it! I have no need of it. Dates for dates"","" wheat for wheat"","" barley for barley"","" gold for gold"","" silver for silver — hand to hand"","" like for like"","" with no increase or decrease. Whoever increases or decreases has committed ribā. And likewise everything that is measured or weighed.\""' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'You have reminded me"","" O Abū Saʿīd"","" of a matter I had forgotten. I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him.' And after that he prohibited it with the sternest prohibition.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Extracted by al-Ḥākim 2/49]"""""
"10525","(10520) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Yaʿlā informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj informed us, Ḥayyān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh Abū Zuhayr said: Abū Mijlaz Lāḥiq ibn Ḥumayd was asked about al-ṣarf while I was present. He said: \Ibn ʿAbbās used to say for a period of his life: 'There is no harm in it when it is hand to hand.' And he used to say: 'Ribā is only in al-nasīʾah (deferred payment).' Until he met Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" who narrated the hadith in a similar manner"","" except that he said: 'Coin for coin"","" like for like. Whoever increases"","" that is ribā. And likewise everything that is measured or weighed.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'May Allah reward you for me"","" O Abū Saʿīd"","" with Paradise"","" for you have reminded me of a matter I had forgotten. I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him.' And after that he prohibited it with the sternest prohibition.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""This hadith"","" from the hadith of Abū Mijlaz"","" is singular in being narrated by Ḥayyān.\"" I say: Ḥayyān has been spoken about critically. And it is said regarding his words \""And likewise with the balance\"" in the first hadith that it is on the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" and likewise this wording"","" if it is authentic. It is corroborated by the narration of Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind"","" from Abū Naḍrah"","" from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"","" in his argument against Ibn ʿAbbās with the story of the dates. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""You have committed ribā if you intended that. So sell your dates for a commodity"","" and then buy with your commodity whatever dates you wish.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""Then dates are more deserving of being considered ribā than silver is for silver.\"" This was a qiyās (analogical reasoning) made by Abū Saʿīd regarding silver based on the dates in which the story was narrated"","" except that some of the narrators narrated it in an elaborated"","" detailed form"","" while others narrated it in a summarized"","" connected form. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf. See the preceding]"""""
"10526","(10521) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us, Abū al-Yamān informed us, Shuʿayb informed us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab said: \Ribā is only in gold and silver"","" and in that which is measured or weighed among things that are eaten and drunk.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Extracted by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 14139]"""""
"10527","(10522) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir, who said: A slave came and gave his pledge of allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ upon emigration, and the Prophet ﷺ did not realize that he was a slave. Then his master came seeking him, so the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \Sell him to me.\"" So he purchased him with two black slaves. Thereafter"","" he ﷺ did not accept anyone's pledge of allegiance until he asked: \""Is he a slave?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and others. [Sahih. Muslim 1602]"""""
"10528","(10523) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi and 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Shadhan al-Jawhari narrated to us; Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us. They both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thabit from Anas: that the Prophet ﷺ purchased Safiyyah from Dihyah al-Kalbi for seven heads (i.e., seven slaves).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from 'Affan, within a lengthy hadith. [Sahih. Muslim 1365]"
"10529","(10524) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, along with others; they said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us; al-Rabi' narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyyaynah narrated to us from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn 'Abbas: that he was asked about (exchanging) one camel for two camels. He said: \A single camel may be better than two camels.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Rafi' ibn Khadij: that he purchased one camel for two camels. He gave one of them (immediately) and said: \""I will bring you the other tomorrow"","" insha'Allah ta'ala"","" at ease.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq 141402]"""""
"10530","(10525) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; al-Rabi' narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Malik narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: \There is no usury (riba) in livestock. Rather"","" what has been prohibited regarding livestock are: al-madamin (the unborn in the womb of its mother)"","" al-malaqih (the offspring of a she-camel that has been covered)"","" and habal al-habalah (the offspring of a she-camel that has been impregnated"","" then gives birth"","" and is then impregnated again and gives birth).\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik 1334]"""""
"10531","(10526) Abu Sa'id narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; al-Rabi' narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Ibn 'Ulayyah narrated to us — insha'Allah — (al-Rabi' expressed doubt) from Salamah ibn 'Alqamah from Muhammad ibn Sirin: that he was asked about (exchanging) iron for iron. He said: \Allah knows best. However"","" they used to trade armor for armor.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Shafi'i in al-Umm 3/43]"""""
"10532","(10527) Abu Sa'id narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; al-Rabi' narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; al-Qaddah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Aban from Hammad from Ibrahim, who said: \There is no harm in giving a loan (salam) in al-fulus (copper coins).\"" Sa'id al-Qaddah said: \""There is no harm in giving a loan in al-fulus.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"10533","(10528) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghayyath narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Muslim ibn Jubayr from Abu Sufyan from 'Amr ibn Harish, who said: I said to 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As: \We are in a land where there is neither gold nor silver. Should we sell one cow for two cows"","" one camel for two camels"","" and one sheep for two sheep?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to equip an army. The camels ran out"","" so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" the camels have run out.' He said: 'Take from the camels of charity (sadaqah).'\"" He said: \""So I began taking one camel for two camels from the camels of charity.\"" The Sheikh said: \""They differed regarding its chain of narration upon Muhammad ibn Ishaq"","" and Hammad ibn Salamah was the best of them in its narration. And it has a sound witness (shahid).\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawud 3357]"""""
"10534","(10529) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated to us; Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me that 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed him from his father from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to equip an army. 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr said: \We had no mounts available.\"" So the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to purchase mounts until the arrival of the collector of charity (al-musaddiq). So 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr purchased one camel for two camels"","" and for several camels"","" until the arrival of the collector of charity"","" by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" [Hasan. Narrated by al-Daraqutni 3/69]"""""
"10535","(10530) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and others narrated to us; they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Malik narrated to us from Salih ibn Kaysan from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib: that he sold a camel of his called 'Usayfir for twenty camels, to be delivered at a fixed term. [Da'if. Narrated by Malik 1330]"
"10536","(10531) Abu Zakariyya narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; al-Rabi' narrated to us; al-Shafi'i narrated to us; he narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar: that he purchased a riding camel for four camels, guaranteed upon him, to be delivered by its owner at al-Rabadhah.\ [Sahih. Narrated by Malik 13312]"""""
"10537","(10532) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd — Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prohibited the exchange of animal for animal on credit.\n\nAnd Ḥammād ibn Salamah likewise narrated it from Qatādah.\n\nHowever, most of the ḥuffāẓ do not affirm that al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī heard directly from Samurah except in the hadith of the ʿAqīqah.\n\nSome of the fuqahāʾ interpreted it as the exchange of one for the other on credit from both sides, making it a debt for a debt, which is not permissible — and Allah knows best. And it has been narrated through another chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by others. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3356]"
"10538","(10533) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed him: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān informed me, from Maʿmar, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the exchange of animal for animal on credit.\""\n\nAnd Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAṭṭār likewise narrated it from Maʿmar"","" connected (mawṣūlan). And it was likewise narrated from Abī Aḥmad al-Zubayrī and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dhimārī"","" from al-Thawrī"","" from Maʿmar — and all of that is an error (wahm). And the correct version is [as above].\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ"","" narrated by others. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān 5028]"""""
"10539","(10534) From Maʿmar, from Yaḥyā, from ʿIkrimah, from the Prophet ﷺ, as a mursal narration. Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed him: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us: al-Firyābī informed us: Sufyān narrated from Maʿmar, and he mentioned it as mursal.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Razzāq and ʿAbd al-Aʿlā likewise narrated it from Maʿmar. And ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak likewise narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿIkrimah, from the Prophet ﷺ, as mursal. And it has been narrated to us from al-Bukhārī that he weakened the narration of the one who connected it."
"10540","(10535) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū ʿAmr ibn Ismāʿīl informed me. I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah say: \The correct view"","" according to the people of hadith knowledge"","" is that this report is mursal.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān mentioned"","" on the authority of al-Shāfiʿī"","" that he said: \""As for his statement that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the exchange of animal for animal on credit"","" this is not established from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10541","(10536) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Khaṣīb ibn Nāṣiḥ informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Sulaymān ibn Shuʿb al-Kaysānī informed us: al-Khaṣīb informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī informed us, from Mūsā, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the exchange of al-kāliʾ bi-l-kāliʾ (debt for debt).\n\nThis Mūsā is Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah al-Rabadhī. And our shaykh Abū ʿAbd Allāh said in his narration: \from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah\"" — and that is an error. And the remarkable thing is that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī"","" the shaykh of his era"","" narrated this hadith in his book al-Sunan from Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī"","" and he said: \""from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah.\""\n\nAnd our shaykh Abū al-Ḥusayn narrated it to us from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī in the third part of the Sunan of al-Miṣrī"","" and he said: \""from Mūsā\"" without identifying him"","" and then al-Miṣrī followed it up with [the rest of the chain]. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ḥākim 2/65]"""""
"10542","(10537) Abū al-Ḥusayn informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan informed us: Aḥmad ibn Dāwūd informed us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad informed us, from Abī ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Rabadhī, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the exchange of al-kāliʾ bi-l-kāliʾ.\n\nAbū ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Rabadhī is Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"10543","(10538) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Qāsim ibn Mahdī informed us: Abū Muṣʿab informed us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Dārawardī, from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nMūsā said: Nāfiʿ said: \That is the exchange of debt for debt.\"" Abū Aḥmad said: \""This is known from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah"","" from Nāfiʿ.\""\n\nThe shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: And ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā"","" Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb"","" and others narrated it from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah"","" from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār"","" from Ibn ʿUmar."""""
"10544","(10539) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-ʿAdl informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Khazzāz informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah al-Rabadhī informed us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-kāliʾ bi-l-kāliʾ — debt for debt.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. See the previous]"""""
"10545","(10540) ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī al-Mu'adhdhin informed us: Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Wāqidī informed us: Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us: Abū ʿUbayd informed us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us, from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Miqdām ibn Dāwūd informed us: Dhuʾayb ibn ʿImāmah informed us: Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us, from Mūsā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he prohibited the exchange of al-kāliʾ bi-l-kāliʾ.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Abū ʿUbaydah said: \It is said: it is al-nasīʾah bi-l-nasīʾah (credit for credit)"",""\"" with a hamzah.\n\nThe shaykh said: In Zayd's narration"","" the word \""exchange (al-bayʿ)\"" does not appear. And our shaykh Abū al-Ḥusayn did not identify Mūsā when narrating from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī — and he is Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah"","" without doubt.\n\nAnd the shaykh Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī — may Allah have mercy on him — narrated it from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī and said: \""from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah.\"" And our shaykh Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated it through another chain from Miqdām ibn Dāwūd al-Ruʿaynī and said: \""from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah\"" — and that is an error (wahm). And the hadith is well-known from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah"","" once from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar"","" and once from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn ʿUmar. And in Allah is the granting of success. [Ḍaʿīf. See the previous]"""""
"10546","(10541) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us: ʿAffān informed us: Hammām informed us: Qatādah informed us, from Abī al-Khalīl, from Muslim, from Abī al-Ashʿath al-Ṣanʿānī, that he witnessed the sermon of ʿUbaydah, who was narrating from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Gold for gold"","" weight for weight; silver for silver"","" weight for weight; wheat for wheat"","" measure for measure; barley for barley"","" measure for measure; dates for dates; and salt for salt. Whoever gives more or asks for more has indeed engaged in ribā (usury).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated under no. 10505]"""""
"10547","(10542) Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us from Qatada, with his chain of narration, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Gold for gold"","" its nuggets and its minted coins; silver for silver"","" its nuggets and its minted coins; wheat for wheat"","" a mudd for a mudd; barley for barley"","" a mudd for a mudd; dates for dates"","" a mudd for a mudd; and salt for salt"","" a mudd for a mudd. Whoever gives more or demands more has indeed dealt in riba (usury).\"" Abu ʿAli al-Rudhbari informed us"","" Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us"","" Abu Dawud informed us"","" al-Hasan ibn ʿAli informed us"","" Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated it and said it was from ʿUbadah ibn al-Samit. [Sahih. See the hadith before it.]"""""
"10548","(10543) Abu ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu ʿAbd Allah Muhammad ibn Yaʿqub informed us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Marwazi both said: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, he said: I read to Malik from ʿAbd al-Majid ibn Suhayl ibn ʿAbd al-Rahman ibn ʿAwf from Saʿid ibn al-Musayyib from Abu Saʿid al-Khudri and from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) appointed a man over Khaybar, and he brought him dates of the janiʿb variety. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Are all the dates of Khaybar like this?\"" He said: \""No"","" by Allah"","" O Messenger of Allah. We take one saʿ of this in exchange for two saʿs"","" and two saʿs in exchange for three.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Do not do so. Sell the mixed dates for dirhams"","" then use the dirhams to buy the janiʿb dates.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ismaʿil ibn Abi Uways and others from Malik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Bukhari 4001.]"""""
"10549","(10544) Muhammad ibn ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ʿIsa al-Qadi informed us, Abu Nuʿaym informed us, Shayban narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Salama from Abu Saʿid who said: \We used to be given the jamʿ dates as provision during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and they were mixed varieties of dates. We would sell two saʿs for one saʿ.\"" He (i.e."","" the Prophet ﷺ) said: \""No"","" and not two dirhams for one dirham.\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 1974.]"""""
"10550","(10545) Abu ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu ʿAmr ibn Abi Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAbd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us, Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, ʿUbayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us from Shayban, mentioning something similar, except that he said: \This reached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and he said: 'Not two saʿs of dates for one saʿ"","" and not two saʿs of wheat for one saʿ"","" and not two dirhams for one dirham.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Nuʿaym"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur. [Sahih. See the hadith before it.]"""""
"10551","(10546) Abu ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-ʿAbbas Muhammad ibn Yaʿqub informed us, Muhammad ibn ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿAbd al-Hakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Ibn Jurayj informed me that al-Zubayr narrated to him. He (Ibn Jurayj) said: \I heard Jabir ibn ʿAbd Allah say: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the sale of a bulk heap (subra) of dates whose measure is not known by a specified measure of dates.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Muslim 1530.]"""""
"10552","(10547) Abu ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu ʿAmr ibn Abi Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAbd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us, Abu Kurayb informed us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us from his father from Ibn Abi Nuʿm from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Gold for gold"","" weight for weight"","" like for like; and silver for silver"","" weight for weight"","" like for like. Whoever gives more or demands more has indeed dealt in riba (usury).\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Kurayb. [Sahih. Muslim 1588.]"""""
"10553","(10548) Abu Ahmad ʿAbd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-ʿAdl informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-ʿAbdi informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Malik narrated to us from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki from Mujahid that he said: \I was circumambulating with ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar when a goldsmith came to him and said: 'O Abu ʿAbd al-Rahman"","" I fashion gold and then sell the item for more than its weight"","" taking the difference as compensation for the work of my hands.' ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar forbade him from doing so. The goldsmith kept repeating the question to him"","" and ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar kept forbidding him"","" until he reached the door of the mosque or his mount"","" intending to ride it. Then ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar said: 'A dinar for a dinar and a dirham for a dirham"","" with no excess between them. This is the covenant of our Prophet (ﷺ) to us"","" and our covenant to you.'\"" The hadith of Muʿawiya has already passed"","" in which he sold a drinking vessel of gold or silver for more than its weight"","" and Abu al-Dardaʾ forbade him from that"","" as well as what has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the prohibition of that. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik 1300.]"""""
"10554","(10549) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us, Ismaʿil ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us, Yahya ibn Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhab, i.e., ibn ʿAtaʾ, informed us, Saʿid, i.e., ibn Abi ʿAruba, narrated to us from Dinar, Abu Fatima, from Abu Rafiʿ who said: \ʿUmar ibn al-Khattab used to sit with me and teach me a verse"","" and I would forget it. I would call out to him: 'O Commander of the Faithful"","" I have forgotten it.' He would return and teach it to me. I said to him: 'I fashion gold and sell it by its weight. May I take compensation for the work of my hands?' He said: 'Do not sell gold for gold except weight for weight"","" and silver for silver except weight for weight"","" and do not take any excess.'\"" [Daʿif.]"""""
"10555","(10550) Muhammad ibn ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, ʿAbd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Kaʿbi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Ahmad ibn ʿIsa al-Misri informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Abu Haniʾ al-Khawlani informed me that he heard ʿAli ibn Rabbah al-Lakhmi say: \I heard Fadalah ibn ʿUbayd al-Ansari say: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought"","" while he was in Khaybar"","" necklaces containing beads and gold"","" which were from the war spoils being sold. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered that the gold in the necklaces be removed. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them: \""Gold for gold"","" weight for weight.\""'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Muslim 1591.]"""""
"10556","(10551) Abu ʿAbd Allah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed us, ʿAbd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Isfaraʾini informed us, Yunus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿla informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Qurra ibn ʿAbd al-Rahman al-Maʿafiri and ʿAmr ibn al-Harith informed me that ʿAmir ibn Yahya al-Maʿafiri informed them from Hanash, who said: \We were with Fadalah ibn ʿUbayd on a military expedition"","" and necklaces containing gold"","" silver"","" and jewels came to me—or he said"","" 'to me and my companions.' I wanted to purchase them"","" so I asked Fadalah ibn ʿUbayd"","" and he said: 'Remove their gold and place it in one pan of the scale"","" and place your gold in the other pan"","" then take only like for like"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"","" let him take only like for like.\""'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Muslim 1591.]"""""
"10557","(10552) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī in Naysābūr, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān al-Ghazzāl, and Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān and others in Baghdād reported to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Yazīd, who said: Khālid ibn Abī ʿImrān narrated to me from Ḥanash from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd, who said: A necklace containing beads strung with gold was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year of Khaybar. A man had purchased it for seven or nine dinārs. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Not until the distinction is made between it and it.\"" He said: \""I only intended the stones.\"" He said: \""Not until the distinction is made between the two.\"" He said: He returned it until the distinction was made between the two.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Ibn al-Mubārak. The narration of Ibn al-Mubārak is consistent with the two preceding narrations in its ruling"","" although some of these narrations contain additional wording beyond others. Al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Saʿīd"","" but he contradicted Ibn al-Mubārak in its text. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1591]"""""
"10558","(10553) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Abī Shujaʿ Saʿīd ibn Yazīd from Khālid ibn Abī ʿImrān from Ḥanash al-Ṣanʿānī from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd, who said: I purchased a necklace on the day of Khaybar containing twelve dinārs of gold and beads. I separated them and found therein more than twelve dinārs. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \It shall not be sold until it is separated.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb. In the narration of Abū Dāwūd"","" it reads: \""A necklace for twelve dinārs containing gold and beads.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah according to the wording of the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb. Abū al-Walīd narrated it from al-Layth in a manner similar to the narration of Abū Dāwūd. Al-Layth has another chain of narration with a different wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1591]"""""
"10559","(10554) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to me; ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn Abī Jaʿfar, narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us from Ibn Abī Jaʿfar from al-Julāḥ Abī Kathīr; Ḥanash al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to me from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Khaybar, trading with the Jews one ūqiyyah of gold for two or three dinārs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sell gold for gold except weight for weight.\""\n\nThe context of these aḥādīth"","" along with the integrity of their narrators"","" indicates that they were all transactions witnessed by Faḍālah"","" and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited them"","" and he reported them all. Ḥanash al-Ṣanʿānī reported them separately. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1591]"""""
"10560","(10555) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to us from his father from the jurists whose opinions are relied upon among the people of Madīnah, who used to say regarding fruit that belongs to two men: There is nothing wrong with them dividing it while still on the palm trees by estimation (kharṣ), so that each one of them takes a portion of the palm trees. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"10561","(10556) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and others reported to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us in the Muwaṭṭaʾ, and Abū Muṣʿab narrated to us from Mālik from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd that Zayd Abū ʿAyyāsh informed him that he asked Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ about selling al-bayḍāʾ (fine wheat) for al-sult (inferior wheat). Saʿd said to him: \Which of the two is better?\"" He said: \""Al-bayḍāʾ.\"" So he prohibited him from that and said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) being asked about purchasing dates with fresh dates. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Does the fresh date diminish when it dries?' They said: 'Yes.' So he prohibited it.\""\n\nYaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Mālik"","" saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to me. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Mālik 1293]"""""
"10562","(10557) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Mālik narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to me from Zayd Abī ʿAyyāsh from Saʿd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about purchasing fresh dates with dates, or dates with fresh dates. He said to those around him: \Does it diminish when it dries?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So he prohibited it.\n\nʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd likewise narrated it from Mālik"","" saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to me. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Madanī narrated it from Mālik from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd. [Ḥasan. See the one before it]"""""
"10563","(10558) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed him; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, saying: My father narrated to me from Mālik ibn Anas, who narrated to him from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, the mawlā of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, and he mentioned it in full. ʿAlī said: My father's hearing from Mālik was an old hearing, before these others heard from him. I think that Mālik had initially suspended it (ʿallaqahu) from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, then he heard it directly from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, so he narrated it in the old narration from Dāwūd, then he examined it and corrected it as being from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, and he abandoned Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn. And Allah knows best."
"10564","(10559) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Marwān narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd from Zayd Abī ʿAyyāsh from Saʿd ibn Mālik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about fresh dates for dates. He said: \Does it diminish when it dries?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So he prohibited it. We also narrated it from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah in a manner similar to the narration of al-Thawrī. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī 4546. Aḥmad 1/179]"""""
"10565","(10560) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ Abū Tawbah narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr; ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū ʿAyyāsh informed him that he heard Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fresh dates for dates on credit (nasīʾah). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3360. Al-Ḥākim 2/45]"
"10566","(10561) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; Ḥarb narrated to us from Yaḥyā; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us, and he mentioned it in a similar manner. Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Mālik, Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān, and Usāmah ibn Zayd contradicted him. They narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd and did not say in it \nasīʾah\"" (on credit). The agreement of these four against what Yaḥyā narrated indicates their precision in preserving the ḥadīth"","" and among them is an imām and ḥāfiẓ"","" namely Mālik ibn Anas.\n\nThe Sheikh said: The ʿillah (defect) transmitted in this report indicates the error of this wording. ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas narrated it from Abī ʿAyyāsh in a manner similar to the narration of the group. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned by al-Dāraquṭnī 3/49]"""""
"10567","(10562) Malik, Isma'il ibn Umayyah, Dâhâk ibn Uthman, and Usamah ibn Zaid — all of them narrate from 'Abdullah ibn Zaid, and he does not mention the word 'borrowing'."
"10568","(10563) Abu ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb — informed me Makhramah ibn Bukayr, from his father, from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas, who said: I heard Abū ʿAyyāsh saying: I asked Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the sale of fresh dates (ruṭab) in exchange for dried dates (tamr). Saʿd said: \Do they have an excess (faḍl) over one another?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then it is not permissible.\"" Saʿd said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the sale of fresh dates in exchange for dried dates"","" and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Do they have an excess over one another?' They said: 'Yes"","" the fresh dates diminish (when they dry).' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Then it is not permissible.'\"" [Ḥasan. See what preceded.]"""""
"10569","(10564) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Ṣayrafī — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl — Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about (selling) fresh dates for dried dates, so he said: \Does the fresh date diminish when it dries?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then fresh dates shall not be sold for dried ones.\"" And this is a good mursal (narration) serving as a witness for what preceded it. [Ḥasan.]"""""
"10570","(10565) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl — Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm, he is Ibn Milḥān — Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr — al-Layth — ʿUqayl — Ibn Shihāb, who said: Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: \Do not sell fruit until its soundness (ṣalāḥ) becomes apparent"","" and do not sell fruit in exchange for dried dates.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from Ḥujayn ibn al-Muthannā from al-Layth"","" with an irsāl (disconnection) in this portion of the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2072.]"""""
"10571","(10566) Abū al-Qāsim Hibatullāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭabarī al-Faqīh al-Ḥāfiẓ (may Allah have mercy on him) in Baghdad — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Fārisī — Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī — Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī — Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd — his father — Ibn Shihāb — Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh — ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sell fruit in exchange for dried dates"","" nor the fruit of date-palms in exchange for the fruit of date-palms"","" and do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes apparent.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what preceded.]"""""
"10572","(10567) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī — Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham — Saʿīd ibn Ḥafṣ, who said: We read to Maʿqil ibn ʿUbaydullāh, from Abī Qazʿah, from Abī Naḍrah, from Abī Saʿīd, who said: Some dates were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \Are these from our dates?\"" A man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" sell us two ṣāʿ of our dates for one ṣāʿ of these.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""That is ribā (usury). Return them. Then sell our dates"","" and buy these for us.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1594.]"""""
"10573","(10568) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn Abī Khāld al-Aṣbahānī — Salamah ibn Shabīb — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Aʿyan — Maʿqil ibn ʿUbaydullāh, who mentioned something similar to it. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb."
"10574","(10569) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī saying: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, meaning Ibn Khuzaymah, and he was asked about the sale of a slaughtered sheep (maslūkh) in exchange for a live one (shāh). He said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sulamī narrated to us — my father narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān — al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj — Qatādah — al-Ḥasan — Samurah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a sheep be sold in exchange for meat.\n\nThis isnād is sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Whoever affirms that al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī heard from Samurah ibn Jundub considers it connected (mawṣūl), and whoever does not affirm it, then it is a good mursal (narration) which joins with the mursal of Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and al-Qāsim ibn Abī Bazʿah, and the statement of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ḥasan for other reasons. Al-Ḥākim narrated it 2/41.]"
"10575","(10570) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — al-Shāfiʿī — Mālik — Zayd ibn Aslam — Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of meat in exchange for an animal (alive). This is the correct version.\n\nAnd Yazīd ibn Marwān al-Khallāl narrated it from Mālik from al-Zuhrī from Sahl ibn Saʿd from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and erred in it. [Ḥasan for other reasons. Mālik narrated it 1335. Al-Ḥākim 2/141.]"
"10576","(10571) And Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī — Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Khamīruwayh — Aḥmad ibn Najdah — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad and Ḥafṣ ibn Maysarah — Zayd ibn Aslam — Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade the sale of meat in exchange for an animal (alive). [Ḥasan for other reasons. See what preceded.]"
"10577","(10572) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazza, who said: I came to Madinah and found that a camel had been slaughtered and divided into four parts, each part being sold for the price of a young goat. I intended to purchase one of its parts, whereupon a man from the people of Madinah said to me: \Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade selling a living animal in exchange for a slaughtered one.\"" He said: \""I then inquired about that man"","" and I was informed of his goodness.\""\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Shafi'i"","" 1226]"""""
"10578","(10573) Abu Zakariyya narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: al-Rabi' narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Ibn Abi Yahya narrated from Salih, the freed slave of al-Taw'amah, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), that he disliked the sale of livestock in exchange for meat.\n[Very weak. Narrated by al-Shafi'i, 1227]"
"10579","(10574) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajanī narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to us: Abu 'Amr Isma'il ibn Nujayd al-Sulami said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bushanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated from Abu al-Zinad from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that he used to say: \The sale of livestock in exchange for meat has been prohibited.\""\n[Sahih]"""""
"10580","(10575) Abu al-Zinad said: \And those of the people whom I met used to forbid the sale of livestock in exchange for meat.\""\nAbu al-Zinad said: \""And that used to be written in the covenants of the governors during the time of Aban ibn 'Uthman and Hisham ibn Isma'il"","" forbidding it.\""\nHe said: And Malik narrated from Dawud ibn al-Husayn that he heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say: \""Among the forms of gambling (maysir) of the people of the Jahiliyyah was the sale of meat in exchange for one sheep or two sheep.\""\n[Sahih]"""""
"10581","(10576) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl narrated to us in Baghdad: Abu al-Husayn 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: Yahya ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Ibn Shihab from Salim from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever sells a date-palm tree after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya and others"","" all from al-Layth.\n[Sahih. Bukhari"","" 2250]"""""
"10582","(10577) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī narrated to us among others, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a date-palm tree after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and others from Sufyan.\n[Sahih. Muslim"","" 1543]"""""
"10583","(10578) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us among others, who said: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: al-Rabi' narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Malik narrated to us.\nAnd Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Ali ibn 'Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Hiri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Amr and Ibrahim ibn 'Ali and Musa ibn Muhammad said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us. He said: I read to Malik from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a date-palm tree that has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" In the narration of al-Shafi'i"","" it is: \""its fruit.\""\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n[Sahih. Bukhari"","" 2250]"""""
"10584","(10579) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us.\nAnd Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Adib narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us: al-Fariyabi, that is Ja'far ibn Muhammad, narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us. They said: al-Layth, that is ibn Sa'd, narrated from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Any man who pollinates a date-palm tree and then sells its trunk"","" the fruit of the date-palm belongs to the one who pollinated it"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn Rumh. And Muslim also narrated it from the hadith of Ayyub and 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar.\n[Sahih. See the previous]"""""
"10585","(10580) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Shakir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to me. He said: Ibrahim narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us. He said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating from Nafi', the freed slave of Ibn 'Umar: \Any date-palm that is sold after having been pollinated"","" and the fruit is not mentioned"","" then the fruit belongs to the one who pollinated it. And likewise the slave and the crop.\"" Nafi' named these three.\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his book. And Nafi' narrates the hadith of the date-palm from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and the hadith of the slave from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him).\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari after hadith 2089]"""""
"10586","(10581) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ja'far narrated to us.\nAnd Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us. They said: 'Abd al-Wahhab, that is ibn 'Ata', narrated to us: Sa'id narrated from Ayyub from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he said: \Any man who sells a date-palm tree that has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to its first owner"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\nHe said: And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled: \""Any man who sells a slave of his who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to his first owner"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\nAnd Salim ibn 'Abd Allah narrated it from his father from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding both the date-palm and the slave together. And that will be mentioned in its proper place"","" if Allah the Most High wills.\n[Sahih. See the previous]"""""
"10587","(10582) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ṭāʾī, Isḥāq ibn Wahb, and Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Yūnus said: ʿUmar ibn Yūnus narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah narrated from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited al-mukhāḍarah, al-muḥāqalah, and al-muzābanah. Ibn ʿUmar ibn Yūnus added: and al-munābadhah and al-mulāmasah.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Wahb in its entirety. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2093]"
"10588","(10583) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd narrated to me; ʿUmar ibn Yūnus ibn al-Qāsim al-Yamāmī narrated it with his chain of narration, except that he said: concerning al-muḥāqalah, al-mukhāḍarah, al-mulāmasah, al-munābadhah, and al-muzābanah.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Al-mukhāḍarah is that fruits be sold before their soundness becomes apparent, while they are still unripe. Also included in al-mukhāḍarah is the sale of fresh dates, vegetables, and the like. For this reason, whoever considered it disliked to sell fresh dates in excess of a single portion. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"
"10589","(10584) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Burayd ibn Abī Burdah, who said: I asked ʿAṭāʾ about selling two portions of fresh dates. He said: No, only one portion.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 20050]"
"10590","(10585) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Aṣbagh informed me; Ibn Wahb narrated from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes apparent"","" and do not exchange fruit for dates.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: And Sālim narrated to me from his father"","" from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"","" from Ibn Wahb"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar from the ḥadīth of al-Layth from Yūnus ibn Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2072]"""""
"10591","(10586) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓufar ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī in Kūfah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent, and He prohibited the exchange of fruit for dates.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others, from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1534]"
"10592","(10587) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said — and the last narrators said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Muḥammad ibn Ḥajjāj said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent, prohibiting both the seller and the buyer.\n\nIn the narration of al-Shāfiʿī, it is \the sale of fruits\"" and he said \""the purchaser\"" instead of \""the buyer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"","" from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2082]"""""
"10593","(10588) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Jarīr narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes apparent and affliction departs from it.\"" He said: \""Its soundness becoming apparent means its redness and yellowness.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"","" from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1534]"""""
"10594","(10589) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥajjāj said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated that he heard Ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes apparent.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1534]"""""
"10595","(10590) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of date-palm fruit until its soundness becomes apparent. Ibn ʿUmar said: \Its soundness is that it becomes edible from it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what preceded]"""""
"10596","(10591) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated it, except that he said: It was said to Ibn ʿUmar: \What is its soundness?\"" He said: \""Its affliction departs.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1534]"""""
"10597","(10592) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Ghurzah informed us — Ubayd Allah, meaning ibn Musa, informed us — Ibn Abi Dhubyan informed us from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Suraqah from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruits until they were safe from affliction. It was asked: \And when is that"","" O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?\"" He replied: \""When the Pleiades (al-Thurayya) rise.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"10598","(10593) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us in his last narrations — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik informed us from Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruits until they ripened. It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" and what does their ripening mean?\"" He replied: \""Until they turn red.\"" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruit"","" what would any of you take of his brother's wealth?\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik"","" and Muslim transmitted it from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb from Malik"","" except that these two did not include the phrase \""O Messenger of Allah\"" nor the phrase \""And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said\"" — rather"","" both of them said: \""Tell me"",""\"" and one of them said: \""It was said to him"",""\"" and the other said: \""They said.\"" And a group has narrated it from Malik just as al-Shafi'i narrated it. [Sahih. Bukhari 2086]"""""
"10599","(10594) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us — (and in another chain:) Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Adban informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Makki narrated to us — al-Darawardi narrated to us from Humayd from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If Allah does not cause them to bear fruit"","" why would any of you consider lawful the wealth of his brother?\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abbad. [Sahih. Muslim 1555]"""""
"10600","(10595) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Muqri', known as Ibn al-Hamami, informed us in Baghdad — Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Faqih narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of the fruit of date-palms until they ripened. We said to Anas: \What is their ripening?\"" He replied: \""They turn red.\"" He said: \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruit"","" how can you consider the wealth of your brother lawful?\"" [Sahih. Bukhari 2094]"""""
"10601","(10596) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — al-Sufi narrated to us — Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ja'far informed us — Humayd informed us from Anas that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the sale of the fruit of date-palms until they ripened. I said to Anas: \And what is their ripening?\"" He replied: \""They turn red and yellow.\"" He said: \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruit"","" how can you consider the wealth of your brother lawful?\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah from Isma'il"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Ayyub and Qutaybah and others. [Sahih. See the preceding]"""""
"10602","(10597) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu al-Fadl 'Ubaydus ibn al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Simsar narrated to us — Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to me — Humayd al-Tawil said: Anas ibn Malik was asked regarding the sale of fruits. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruits until they ripened. It was said: \O Abu Hamzah"","" and what is their ripening?\"" He replied: \""Until they turn red and yellow.\"" He said: \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruits"","" how can you consider the wealth of your brother lawful?\"" And similarly a group narrated it from Humayd. And in some of the narrations from Isma'il ibn Ja'far from Humayd"","" Anas said: \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruit"","" how can you consider the wealth of your brother lawful?\"" And Sufyan al-Thawri said similarly from Humayd"","" making the answer regarding the interpretation of ripening and the statement \""Tell me"","" if Allah withholds the fruit\"" to be from the words of Anas ibn Malik. And Malik ibn Anas made it to be from the words of the Prophet ﷺ"","" and al-Darawardi followed him upon that in the narration of Muhammad ibn 'Abbad from him. And Allah knows best. [Sahih. See the preceding]"""""
"10603","(10598) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hurdi informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Miqsim al-Muqri' narrated to us — Musa ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — 'Affan ibn Muslim al-Saffar narrated to us — Hammad ibn Salamah informed us — Humayd al-Tawil informed us from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruits until they ripened, and the sale of grain until it becomes firm, and the sale of grapes until they turn black. [Sahih. Abu Dawud 3371]"
"10604","(10599) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us — Rawh narrated to us — Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Dinar informed us that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruits until their soundness becomes apparent. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Hatim from Rawh ibn 'Ubadah. [Sahih. Muslim 1536]"
"10605","(10600) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi informed us — Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us — Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to me — Sa'id ibn Mina' said: I heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited that fruits be sold until they become mushqah. It was asked: \And what is mushqah?\"" He replied: \""They turn red or yellow"","" and can be eaten from.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musaddad from Yahya. [Sahih. Muslim 2084]"""""
"10606","(10601) Abu al-Hasan al-'Alawi informed us — Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hafiz, who is al-Sharqi, narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir ibn al-Hakam al-'Abdi narrated to us — Bahz ibn Asad narrated to me — Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Mina' from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muzabanah, al-muhaqalah, al-mukhabarah, and the sale of fruits until they become mushqah. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Hashim from Bahz ibn Asad. [Sahih. Muslim 1536]"
"10607","(10602) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī informed us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, from Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah, from Abū al-Walīd al-Makkī — Zayd said: he narrated to us while he was sitting with ʿAṭāʾ — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he prohibited *al-muḥāqalah*, *al-muzābanah*, *al-mukhābarah*, and the sale of dates until they are *tushaqqah*. He said: *al-ishqāh* is that they turn red, or turn yellow, or something is eaten from them. And *al-muḥāqalah* is that a field is sold for a known measure of food. Zayd said: I said to ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ: \Did you hear Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh mention that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1536]"""""
"10608","(10603) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Zuhayr said: he narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿIṣmah ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAdl narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit until it becomes good (ripe).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1536]"
"10609","(10604) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to us. He said: I heard Abū al-Bakhtarī al-Ṭāʾī say —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb both said: Shuʿbah narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to me, from Abū al-Bakhtarī, who said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about *al-salam* (forward sale) in palm trees. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of palm trees until something is eaten from them and until they are weighed. I said: \What is weighed?\"" A man from the people said: \""Until they are estimated (*yuḥzar*).\"" In the narration of Ādam"","" a man said: \""And what thing is weighed?\"" A man beside him said: \""Until it is estimated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Ādam and from Abū al-Walīd"","" and he and Muslim both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar"","" from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1537]"""""
"10610","(10605) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, all saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Abū Zurʿah Wahb Allāh ibn Rāshid narrated to us, from Yūnus, who said: Abū al-Zinād said — and ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr used to narrate from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah — that he informed him that Zayd ibn Thābit used to say: In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, people used to sell fruits. When the people harvested and the time of settlement arrived, the buyer would say: \The fruit has been afflicted by decay (*al-ʿafan*)"","" by *al-dumān*"","" by *murāq*"","" by *quṣām*\"" — various afflictions by which they would seek to justify their claims. *Al-quṣām* is something that afflicts the fruit so that it does not ripen. Zayd said: When disputes regarding this became frequent before him"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Then do not sell until the soundness of the fruit becomes apparent.\"" This was by way of counsel (*al-mashūrah*)"","" given on account of the frequency of their disputes.\n\nAbū al-Zinād said: And Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit informed me that Zayd ibn Thābit would not sell the fruits of his properties until the Pleiades (al-Thurayyā) rose"","" so that the red could be distinguished from the yellow.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ*"","" saying: And al-Layth said"","" from Abū al-Zinād"","" and he mentioned it"","" using *murāḍ* instead of *murāq*.\n\nAl-Aṣmaʿī said: *Al-dumān* is that the palm tree splits open at the first appearance of its heart"","" due to decay and blackness. And *al-quṣām* is that the fruit of the palm tree diminishes before it becomes *balah* (unripe dates). And *al-murāḍ* is a term for types of diseases. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 2087]"""""
"10611","(10606) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr, from Ṭāwūs, who heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \Fruit is not to be sold until its soundness becomes apparent.\"" He said: \""And we heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: 'Fruit is not to be sold until it yields food (*yuṭʿam*).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī 695]"""""
"10612","(10607) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr, from Abū Maʿbad, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, that Ibn ʿAbbās used to sell the fruit from his slave before its soundness became apparent, and he would say: \There is no usury (*ribā*) between a slave and his master.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah 2004]"""""
"10613","(10608) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj, from Sulaymān ibn ʿAtīq, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit for years (i.e., advance sale for multiple years).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and others, from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1536]"
"10614","(10609) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥumayd al-Ushnānī and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAṭṭār al-Ḥīrī both said: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Bisṭām narrated to us: al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, from his father, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of *al-gharar* (uncertainty/deception). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10615","(10610) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, along with others, all saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Abū al-Zinād, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of *al-gharar* (uncertainty/deception) and the sale of *al-ḥaṣā* (the sale by casting pebbles).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, as has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1513]"
"10616","(10611) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us. He said: We said to al-Shāfiʿī: \ʿAlī ibn Maʿbad informed us"","" with an isnād"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" that he permitted the sale of wheat in its ears once it has turned white.\"" He said: \""As for this"","" it is *gharar* (deception)"","" because it is obstructed and cannot be seen. However"","" if the report is established from the Prophet ﷺ"","" we would follow it"","" and this would be a specific ruling extracted from a general one"","" because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of *al-gharar* and yet permitted this.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned by al-Shāfiʿī in *al-Umm* 3/81]"""""
"10617","(10612) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us regarding the hadith that was narrated concerning that; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī narrated to us, Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of date-palms until the fruit becomes ripe (yazhuwa), and the sale of grain (sunbul) until it whitens and is safe from blight. He prohibited it for both the seller and the buyer.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1535]\n\nThe Shaykh said: The mention of grain (sunbul) in this hadith is something unique to Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Nāʿif among the companions of Nāʿif. Ayyūb is trustworthy and authoritative (thiqatun ḥujjatun), and an addition from one such as him is acceptable. This hadith is among those over which al-Bukhārī and Muslim differed regarding its inclusion in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections; Muslim included it, while al-Bukhārī omitted it. For the hadith of the prohibition of selling fruit until its soundness becomes apparent, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī, Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, Mālik ibn Anas, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān, and others narrated it from Nāʿif, and not one of them mentioned in it the prohibition of selling grain (sunbul) until it whitens, other than Ayyūb.\n\nSālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, and others narrated it from Ibn ʿUmar, and not one of them mentioned in it what Ayyūb mentioned.\n\nJābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī, Zayd ibn Thābit, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās, Abū Hurayrah, and others narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and not one of them mentioned in it what Ayyūb mentioned, except what… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1535]"
"10618","(10613) Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of grain until it hardens (yashtadda), the sale of grapes until they turn black (yaswadda), and the sale of fruit until it ripens (yazhuwa).\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nThe mention of grain until it hardens and grapes until they turn black in this hadith is something unique to Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Ḥumayd among the companions of Ḥumayd. For Mālik ibn Anas, Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar, Hushaym ibn Bashīr, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak, and a large group whose number is too many to enumerate narrated it from Ḥumayd, from Anas, regarding the fruit only, without that. There was also a difference regarding the wording of Ḥammād; ʿAffān ibn Muslim, Abū al-Walīd, Ḥibbān ibn Hilāl, and others narrated from him as has been previously mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See no. 10598]"
"10619","(10614) Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣāliḥīnī and Ḥasan ibn Mūsā al-Ashyab narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from Ḥumayd, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent — it turns yellow (taṣfarra) or red (taḥmarra) — and the sale of grapes until they turn black, and the sale of grain until it can be rubbed out (yufraka).\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣāliḥīnī and Ḥasan ibn Mūsā al-Ashyab both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nHis statement \until it can be rubbed out (yufraka)\"": if the rāʾ is in the genitive (khafḍ)"","" attributing the rubbing (ifrāk) to the grain"","" it agrees with the narration of the one who said \""until it hardens (yashtadda).\"" But if the rāʾ is in the nominative (fatḥ) and the yāʾ is in the nominative"","" attributing the rubbing (fark) to an unnamed agent"","" it contradicts the narration of the one who said \""until it hardens"",""\"" and it would imply the cleansing of the grain from the husk until its sale becomes permissible. I have not seen any of the muḥaddithūn of our time clarify that. It is more likely that yufraka has the rāʾ in the genitive"","" in agreement with the meaning of the one who said \""until it hardens.\"" And Allah knows best.\n\nAbān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh also narrated it"","" but no proof is established by his narration from Anas according to the second wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10620","(10615) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed me, Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to us, al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Sufyān, from Abān, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of grain until it can be rubbed out, the sale of date-palms until the fruit ripens, and the sale of fruits until they become edible (tuṭʿima).\n\nIt was narrated from Abū Shaybah, from Anas ibn Mālik, but it is nothing (i.e., not strong). Jābir al-Juʿfī narrated from Umm Thawr: that her husband, Bishr, asked Ibn ʿAbbās: \When may date-palms be sold?\"" He said: \""Until the fruit ripens (yazhuwa).\"" He said: \""And I asked him about the sale of crops"","" i.e."","" grain (sunbul).\"" He said: \""Until it turns yellow (yaṣfarra).\""\n\nIts chain of narration is weak. The authentic narration in this topic is the narration of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"","" followed by the narration of Ḥammād ibn Salamah"","" as we have mentioned regarding its wording. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10621","(10616) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah al-Mājishūn narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent (yabdū ṣalāḥuhu).\n\nAl-Zuhrī said: The scholars say that its soundness becoming apparent means that it ripens (yazhuwa), and the soundness of crops is that the grain can be rubbed out (yufraka). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Meaning is abundant]"
"10622","(10617) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik informed us that it reached him that Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn used to say: \Do not sell grain in its ears until it whitens (yabyaḍḍa).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik: 1325]"""""
"10623","(10618) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Ayyūb narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd ibn Mīnāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited al-muḥāqalah, al-muzābanah, al-mukhābarah, and al-muʿāwamah — one of them said — and the sale of years (al-sinīn), and al-thunyyā, and he granted concession regarding al-ʿarāyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1536]"
"10624","(10619) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh al-Qawārīrī narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawārīrī and others."
"10625","(10620) Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited… and he mentioned it, and he said \al-muʿāwamah\"" but did not mention \""al-sinīn.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"","" al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us"","" Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us"","" Ismāʿīl narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others.\n\nIf one excludes from it a quarter"","" a half"","" or specific date-palms that he points to by their individual identities"","" then we have narrated from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"","" ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ"","" and ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that which indicates the permissibility of that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10626","(10621) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Yazīd al-Sayyārī Abū Ḥafṣ narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn, from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, from ʬāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited al-muzābanah, al-muḥāqalah, and al-thunyyā, unless it is made known (tuʿlama). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3405] [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"
"10627","(10622) Sufyan ibn Husayn said: He narrated to us and added the mention of al-Mukhabarah."
"10628","(10623) Abu Ahmad — Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihranjani al-Mu'adl — informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Humayd al-Tawīl from Anas ibn Mālik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of fruits until they showed signs of ripening. It was said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" what is their ripening?\"" He said: \""When they turn red.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""What do you think if Allah withholds the fruit"","" on what basis would one of you take the wealth of his brother?\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Sahīh"","" as has been mentioned. [Sahīh. Meaning is close.]"""""
"10629","(10624) Abu Sa'id ibn Abī 'Amr narrated to us; al-'Abbās informed us; al-Rabī' informed us; al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Malik narrated it with the same wording.\n\nAl-Shāfi'ī said, during his discussion on the question of al-jā'ihah (blight/damage): If the owner of the fruit were not liable for the price of what was blighted of his fruit, there would be no meaning in preventing him from selling it, when its sale is permissible at the stage of ṭal' (spathe) or balah (unripe dates), which are picked and cut — except that he was commanded to sell it at the time when it is most likely to be safe from calamity. If the price of what was afflicted by blight were not binding upon him, that would not harm the seller or the buyer. He said: If the hadith on waḍ' al-jā'ihah (removal of blight damage) is established, there is no proof in this, and I apply the hadith according to its apparent meaning. [Sahīh. See what preceded it.]"
"10630","(10625) Abu Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabī' informed us; al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Malik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Abī al-Rijāl — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān — from his mother 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Raḥmān that she heard her say: A man purchased the fruit of a garden during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He tended it and maintained it, but loss became evident to him. He asked the owner of the garden to reduce the price for him or to annul the sale. The owner swore that he would not do so. The mother of the buyer went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \He has sworn not to do good.\"" The owner of the garden heard of this and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \""It is for him (i.e."","" I give it to him).\""\n\nThe wording is that of Ibn Bukayr. In the narration of al-Shāfi'ī"","" the phrase \""or to annul the sale\"" is not present"","" and he said: \""He tended it and maintained it.\""\n\nAbū Sa'id added to me"","" from Abī al-'Abbās"","" from al-Rabī'"","" from al-Shāfi'ī"","" who said: The hadith of 'Amrah is mursal"","" and the scholars of hadith — and we — do not accept the mursal. Were the hadith of 'Amrah to be established"","" there would be in it"","" and Allah knows best"","" an indication that al-jā'ihah (blight damage) should not be waived"","" due to her statement: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'He has sworn not to do good.'\"" If the ruling upon him were to waive the blight damage"","" it would be more appropriate for him to say: \""That is binding upon him"","" whether he swore or not.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Al-Hārithah ibn Abī al-Rijāl narrated it with a complete chain"","" reporting it from his father"","" from 'Amrah"","" from 'Ā'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"","" except that al-Hārithah is weak and cannot be used as evidence.\n\nAnd Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated it from Abī al-Rijāl"","" except that it is abridged and does not mention the fruit. [Da'īf. Mālik narrated it"","" 1286.]"""""
"10631","(10626) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us orally; al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī and al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn Ziyād said: Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us; my brother narrated to us from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd from Abī al-Rijāl — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān — from his mother 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard 'Ā'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) heard the voices of disputants at the door, their voices raised, and one of them was asking the other for a reduction and seeking leniency in something, while he was saying: \By Allah"","" I will not do it.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went out to them and said: \""Where is the one who swears by Allah that he will not do a good deed?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" it is me. Whatever of it he wishes (it is for him).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Sahīh from Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways"","" and Muslim narrated it from some of his companions from Ismā'īl. [Sahīh. Bukhārī"","" 2558.]"""""
"10632","(10627) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbās — Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb — narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī narrated to us; 'Abd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; 'Amr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj from 'Iyāḍ ibn 'Abd Allāh from Abī Sa'īd al-Khudrī, who said: A man was afflicted during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in fruits he had purchased, and his debt increased. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Give charity on his behalf.\"" They gave charity on his behalf"","" but it did not cover his debt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Take what you find"","" and you are entitled to nothing beyond that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahīh from Yūnus ibn 'Abd al-A'lā from Ibn Wahb. [Sahīh. Muslim"","" 1556.]"""""
"10633","(10628) Abu Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbās — Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb — informed us; al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays from Sulaymān ibn 'Atīq from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of al-sinīn (two-year sale) and commanded the waḍ' (removal/remission) of al-jawā'ih (blights/calamities).\n\nMuslim narrated it in a fragmented manner: he narrated the hadith of the prohibition from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān, and he narrated the hadith of al-jawā'ih from Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam and others from Sufyān. Al-Bukhārī did not narrate it. [Sahīh. Muslim, 1554.]"
"10634","(10629) Abu Zakariyyā narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbās informed us; al-Rabī' said: Al-Shāfi'ī said: I heard Sufyān narrating this hadith frequently throughout the duration of my companionship with him — I cannot count how many times I heard him narrate it — due to its frequency, he did not mention in it the command to waive al-jawā'ih (blight damage), and he added nothing beyond: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of al-sinīn.\"" Then he added afterwards: \""And he commanded the waḍ' (removal) of al-jawā'ih.\""\n\nSufyān said: Ḥumayd used to mention"","" after the sale of al-sinīn"","" some words before the waḍ' of al-jawā'ih"","" which I do not remember. So I refrained from mentioning the waḍ' of al-jawā'ih because I did not know how the wording was"","" even though the hadith contains the command to waive al-jawā'ih.\n\nAbū Sa'id ibn Abī 'Amr added to me"","" from Abī al-'Abbās"","" from al-Rabī'"","" from al-Shāfi'ī"","" who said: It is possible that the wording which Sufyān did not remember from the hadith of Ḥumayd indicates that his command to waive it was like his command to settle for half"","" or like his command to give charity voluntarily — as an encouragement to do good"","" not as an obligation. And whatever resembles that is also permissible. When the hadith carries both meanings together"","" and there is no indication as to which of the two is more appropriate"","" it is not permissible for us — and Allah knows best — to rule over people in their wealth by waiving what is due to them without a firmly established report that mandates its waiver.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has also been narrated in this regard from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir. [Sahīh. See what preceded it.]"""""
"10635","(10630) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Aḥmad ibn Muhammad al-'Anazī narrated to us; 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī narrated to us; 'Alī ibn 'Abd Allāh narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays from Sulaymān ibn 'Atīq from Jābir that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) waived al-jawā'ih (blight damage). 'Alī said: Sufyān had narrated to us from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he waived al-jawā'ih. This is how Sufyān brought it.\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj narrated it from Abī al-Zubayr. [Sahīh. See what has passed.]"
"10636","(10631) As Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abu Aḥmad — Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw — narrated to us; Abu Qalābah al-Raqāshī narrated to us; Abū 'Āṣim informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Alī al-Rūdbārī informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Mahrī and Aḥmad ibn Sa'īd al-Hamdānī said: Ibn Wahb informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) He said: And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Abū 'Āṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, with the same meaning, that Abū al-Zubayr al-Makkī informed him from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \If you sell fruit to your brother and it is afflicted by a blight (jā'ihah)"","" it is not permissible for you to take anything from it. How can you take the wealth of your brother without right?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Sahīh from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb"","" and from al-Ḥasan al-Ḥulwānī from Abū 'Āṣim. [Sahīh. Muslim"","" 1554.]"""""
"10637","(10632) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; Abū al-Ṭāhir ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ al-Miṣrī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us, and he mentioned it with its like, except that he said: \It is not permissible for you to take anything from its price.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10638","(10633) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ṣanʿānī in Makkah informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī in Makkah narrated to us; Zayd ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣanʿānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Thawr narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \How can any of you make lawful the wealth of his brother if a calamity from the heavens befalls it?\""\n\nThe hadith of Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir"","" even if it is not explicitly recorded regarding the sale of fruits before the appearance of their soundness—as in the hadith of Mālik from Ḥumayd from Anas—it is explicit in prohibiting the taking of their price if they are destroyed by a calamity. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10639","(10634) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Mahrī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; ʿUthmān ibn al-Ḥakam narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \Al-Jawāʾiḥ (calamities) are every manifest destructive occurrence from rain"","" cold"","" locusts"","" wind"","" or fire.\"" [Jayyid. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 3471.]"""""
"10640","(10635) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Among the last of them, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited al-Muzābanah. And al-Muzābanah is that a man sells the fresh dates of his palm trees by measure and his grapes by measure for raisins by measure.\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. And in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him): \And al-Muzābanah is the sale of fresh fruit for dried dates by measure"","" and the sale of grapes for raisins by measure.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā with the wording of the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 2073.]"""""
"10641","(10636) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq al-Baṣrī in Egypt narrated to us; ʿĀrim Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū al-Fayyāḍ narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited al-Muzābanah. And al-Muzābanah is that a man sells his fruit by measure—if it increases, it is for me, and if it falls short, it is upon me.\n\nAnd in the narration of ʿĀrim: \That he sells the fruit by measure.\"" And Abū al-Rabīʿ added in his narration through this chain from Ibn ʿUmar"","" from Zayd ibn Thābit"","" that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted a concession in the sale of al-ʿArāyā by estimate.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 2064.]"""""
"10642","(10637) And Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated from Ḥammād, and he added in it: Nāfiʿ said: \And al-Muḥāqalah in crops is equivalent in status to al-Muzābanah in date palms.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed me; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10643","(10638) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited al-Muzābanah. And al-Muzābanah is that a man sells the fruit of his garden—if it is date palms, he sells it for dried dates by measure; if it is grapes, he sells it for raisins by measure; and if it is crops, he sells it for a measure of food. He prohibited all of that.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 2091.]"
"10644","(10639) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibit al-Muḥāqalah, al-Mukhābarah, and al-Muzābanah, and he granted a concession in the sale of al-ʿArāyā. And al-Mukhābarah is the leasing of land for one-third or one-quarter of its produce; and al-Muḥāqalah is the purchase of grain in its ears for wheat; and al-Muzābanah is the sale of fresh fruit for dried dates.\n\nI said to Sufyān: \Is this explanation in the hadith of Ibn Jurayj?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān"","" without the explanation. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 2252.]"""""
"10645","(10640) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyyaynah narrated from Ibn Jurayj, and he mentioned it with its meaning, except that they both said in the hadith: \And al-Muḥāqalah is that a man sells the crop for one hundred faraqs of wheat; and al-Muzābanah is that he sells the fruit on the heads of the date palms for one hundred faraqs of dried dates; and al-Mukhābarah is the leasing of land for one-third or one-quarter [of its produce].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10646","(10641) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, that he said to ʿAṭāʾ: \What is al-Muḥāqalah?\"" He said: \""Al-Muḥāqalah in crops is of the same nature as al-Muzābanah in date palms—that is"","" the sale of the crop for wheat.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: \""I said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'Did Jābir explain al-Muḥāqalah to you as I have informed you?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" [Ḥasan.]"""""
"10647","(10642) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAbdullāh — he is al-Qaʿnabī — from Mālik, from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from Abū Sufyān, the freedman of Ibn Abī Aḥmad, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muzābanah and al-muḥāqalah. Al-muzābanah is the purchase of fresh fruit (on the tree) in exchange for dried dates, and al-muḥāqalah is the leasing out of land.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1546]"
"10648","(10643) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed us: Saʿdān informed us: Abū Muʿāwiyah Muḥammad ibn Khāzim informed us, from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muḥāqalah and al-muzābanah. And ʿIkrimah used to disapprove of the sale of al-qaṣīl (fresh produce on the stalk).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Abū Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2075]"
"10649","(10644) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym and Aḥmad ibn Salamah both said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us: Yaʿqūb — he is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Iskandarānī — from Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muḥāqalah and al-muzābanah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1545]"
"10650","(10645) Sharīk al-Nakhaʿī narrated it from Suhayl, adding therein: As for al-muzābanah, it is that you purchase the fruit (on the palm trees) in exchange for dried dates; and as for al-muḥāqalah, it is that you purchase the wheat (still) in the ears in exchange for wheat.\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sharīk informed us, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10651","(10646) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us: Abū al-Azhar informed us: Makkī informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Saʿdī informed us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of a ṣubrah of dates — whose measure is not known by the specified measure — in exchange for dates.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1530]"
"10652","(10647) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said among the last of those who narrated: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father: that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness (ṣalāḥ) becomes apparent, and the sale of fruit in exchange for dried dates.\n\nʿAbdullāh said: And Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to us: that the Prophet ﷺ granted a concession (arrakhaṣa) in the sale of al-ʿarāyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1539]"
"10653","(10648) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me: Abū Yaʿlā informed us: Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb informed us: Sufyān informed us, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others."
"10654","(10649) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr said: al-Layth informed me, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh informed me, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: \Do not sell fruit until its soundness becomes apparent"","" and do not sell fruit in exchange for dried dates.\""\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan informed us: Aḥmad informed us: Ibn Milḥān informed us: Yaḥyā informed me: al-Layth informed me"","" from ʿUqayl"","" from Ibn Shihāb"","" from Sālim"","" who said: And ʿAbdullāh informed me"","" from Zayd ibn Thābit"","" from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: that he thereafter granted a concession in the sale of the ʿariyah"","" (allowing it to be sold) with an estimated measure of dried dates"","" and he did not grant a concession in anything other than that.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated both in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated both from another route from al-Layth"","" with an irsāl (broken chain) in the first. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2072]"""""
"10655","(10650) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah informed us, from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī, and Mūsā ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd ibn Thābit: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted the owner of an ʿariyah the concession to sell it by its estimated measure of dried dates.\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā. And in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī and al-Qaʿnabī: \He granted the owner of an ʿariyah the concession to sell it by its estimated measure.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh al-Qaʿnabī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2076]"""""
"10656","(10651) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī both said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted the concession that al-ʿarāyā be sold by their estimated measure of dried dates.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, and Muslim narrated it from other routes from Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"
"10657","(10652) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd ibn Thābit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession regarding the sale of al-ʿarāyā by estimating its measure in dry dates. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from two routes from ʿUbayd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what preceded.]"
"10658","(10653) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muḥāqalah, al-muzābanah, and al-mukhābarah, and the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent, and nothing should be sold except with dinars or dirhams, except al-ʿarāyā.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shayyah, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2252.]"
"10659","(10654) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan, who is Ibn Sufyān, informed me; Ḥarmalah informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Jurayj informed me from ʿAṭāʾ and Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit until it ripens, and nothing from it should be sold except with dinars and dirhams, except al-ʿarāyā.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān from Ibn Wahb, and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abū ʿĀṣim from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what preceded.]"
"10660","(10655) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-ʿAnazī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Usāmah narrated to us from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr, who said: Bushayr ibn Yasār informed me that Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj and Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muzābanah — the exchange of fresh dates for dried dates — except for the owners of al-ʿarāyā, for he granted them permission.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah and others, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2254.]"
"10661","(10656) Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, who said: I heard Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit for dried dates, except that he granted a concession in the sale of al-ʿariyyah, that it may be sold by its estimate in dried dates, so that its people may eat it as fresh dates.\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī, and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others, all from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2079.]"
"10662","(10657) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us from Yaḥyā, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, from some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from among the people of his household, among them Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit for dried dates and said: \That is ribā; that is al-muzābanah.\"" Except that he granted a concession in the sale of al-ʿariyyah — a palm tree or two palm trees — that the people of the household may take them by their estimate in dried dates"","" eating them as fresh dates.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1540.]"""""
"10663","(10658) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; al-Thaqafī said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd say: Bushayr ibn Yasār informed me from some of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit for dried dates. He said: \And that is al-zabn; that is al-muzābanah.\"" Then al-Bāriqī mentioned something similar to it.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what preceded.]"""""
"10664","(10659) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, who said: Nāfiʿ informed me that he heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrate that Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession in al-ʿariyyah, that the people of the household may take it by its estimate in dried dates, eating it as fresh dates.\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Passed above.]"
"10665","(10660) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Hushaym informed us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent, and he granted a concession in al-ʿarāyā. He said: \And al-ʿariyyah is a palm tree that is given to a people"","" and they sell it by its estimate in dried dates.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Passed above.]"""""
"10666","(10661) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us from Yaḥyā, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession in the sale of al-ʿariyyah by its estimate. And Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd said: \Al-ʿariyyah is that a man purchases the fruit of palm trees for the sustenance of his household as fresh dates"","" by their estimate in dried dates.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2080.]"""""
"10667","(10662) Abu 'Amr al-Adib narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to me: al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Sufyan, narrated to us: Habban narrated to us: 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave concession regarding al-'ara'iyyah, that they may be sold by estimation by weight (kayl). Musa said: \And al-'ara'iyyah are known palm-trees that one comes to and purchases.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari recorded it in al-Sahih from Muhammad from 'Abd Allah. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 2080]"""""
"10668","(10663) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me from 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, who said: \Al-'ariyyah is when a man gives a man a palm-tree as a gift"","" or when a man excludes from his property one or two palm-trees so that he may eat from them"","" and then he sells them in exchange for dried dates.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 3365]"""""
"10669","(10664) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated to us: 'Abadah narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, who said: \Al-'ara'iyyah is when a man gives a man palm-trees as a gift"","" and it becomes burdensome for him to tend to them"","" so he sells them in exchange for the equivalent of their estimated yield.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud 3366]"""""
"10670","(10665) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya — and others with him — all said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Malik narrated to us.\n\nAnd Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Faqih narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Nasr and Ja'far ibn Muhammad both said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, who said: I said to Malik, \Did Dawud ibn al-Husayn narrate to you from Abu Sufyan"","" the mawla of Ibn Abi Ahmad"","" from Abu Hurayrah"","" that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave concession regarding the sale of al-'ara'iyyah by estimation"","" for less than five awsuq — or five?\"" — and Dawud was uncertain — He said"","" \""Five or less than five?\"" He said"","" \""Yes.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1541]"""""
"10671","(10666) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, 'Abdullāh, meaning al-Qa'nabī, narrated from Mālik from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \He permitted it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qa'nabī and Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10672","(10667) Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī informed us, Abū Khalīfah informed me, 'Abdullāh al-Ḥajabī said: I heard Mālik, and 'Ubaydullāh, meaning Ibn al-Rabī', asked him: \Did Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrate to you from Abū Sufyān from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of al-'arāyā by estimation up to five awsuq or less than five awsuq?\"" Mālik said: \""Yes.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2078.]"""""
"10673","(10668) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Abū Zur'ah 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Amr al-Dimashqī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān from his uncle Wāsi' ibn Ḥabbān from Jābir ibn 'Abdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-muḥāqalah and al-muzābanah, and he permitted the owners of al-'arāyā to sell it by its estimated measure, then he said: \One wasq"","" two"","" three"","" and four.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 3/360.]"""""
"10674","(10669) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn 'Alī al-Faqīh narrated to us, Abū 'Abdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who said: And Sālim ibn 'Abdillāh informed me, who said: 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar informed me from Zayd ibn Thābit from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he permitted the sale of al-'ariyyah with al-ruṭab (fresh dates) or al-tamr (dried dates) and did not permit it otherwise. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr as mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Proceeded previously.]"
"10675","(10670) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated from al-Awzā'ī, who said: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me from Sālim ibn 'Abdillāh from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar from Zayd ibn Thābit that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of al-'arāyā with al-tamr (dried dates) and al-ruṭab (fresh dates) and did not permit it otherwise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Proceeded previously.]"
"10676","(10671) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit informed me from his father that the Prophet ﷺ permitted the sale of al-'arāyā with al-tamr (dried dates) and al-ruṭab (fresh dates). Similarly, al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Faḍālah narrated it from Yūnus ibn Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3362.]"
"10677","(10672) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and others said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us, al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfi'ī informed us, Mālik informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd ibn Sulaymān informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Ismā'īl ibn Abī Uways said: Mālik narrated to me. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik. (Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, 'Alī ibn 'Īsā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Ḥarashī, Ibrāhīm ibn 'Alī, and Mūsā ibn Muḥammad said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken full possession of it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abdullāh al-Qa'nabī"","" and Muslim narrated it from al-Qa'nabī and Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. Al-Bukhārī said: Ismā'īl added: \""Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken possession of it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2029.]"""""
"10678","(10673) Muḥammad ibn 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated from 'Abdullāh ibn Dīnār from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken possession of it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding hadith.]"""""
"10679","(10674) And Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī' informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb informed us, Abū al-Rabī' informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Ja'far narrated from 'Abdullāh ibn Dīnār, and he mentioned it similarly. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Ismā'īl."
"10680","(10675) Abū 'Abdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzzakī, Abū 'Uthmān Sa'īd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdān, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris all said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn 'Affān narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, Wuhaib ibn Khālid narrated to us. (Ḥ) And 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Mūsā narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated to us. Ibn Ṭāwūs narrated from his father from Ibn 'Abbās that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from selling food until he has taken full possession of it. Ṭāwūs said: I said to Ibn 'Abbās, \How is that?\"" He said: \""That is dirhams for dirhams"","" and the food is deferred.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl"","" and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ma'mar and al-Thawrī from Ibn Ṭāwūs. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2025.]"""""
"10681","(10676) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Dārabujardī narrated to us; Abū ʀāṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken full possession of it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1529]"""""
"10682","(10677) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah and Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad both said: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \When you purchase food"","" do not sell it until you have taken full possession of it.\""\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it]"""""
"10683","(10678) Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū ʀāṣim narrated — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Abū ʀāṣim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʀāʾ informed me from Ṣafwān ibn Mawhab, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣayfī, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, that the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \Shall I not inform you — or shall I not give you news — or has it not reached you — or as Allah wills — that you sell food?\"" He said: \""Yes indeed.\"" He said: \""When you purchase food"","" do not sell it until you have taken full possession of it.\"" The meaning of both is the same.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī 4601. Aḥmad 3/ no. 3096]"""""
"10684","(10679) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām sold food before taking possession of it, so ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — rescinded the sale and said: \When you purchase food"","" do not sell it until you have taken possession of it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10685","(10680) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr — (ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated; ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from whom we preserved it — said: He heard Ṭāwūs saying: \I heard Ibn ʿAbbās saying: 'As for that which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade"","" it is that food should not be sold until it is taken into possession.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""And I do not think that everything is except like it.\""\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿAlī. al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2028]"""""
"10686","(10681) Abū al-Qāsim Hibbat Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Faqīh al-Ṭabarī — may Allah have mercy on him — informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us; Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī narrated to us; my father narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from ʀāʾ, from Ṣafwān ibn Yaʿlā, from his father, who said: The Prophet ﷺ appointed ʿAttāb ibn Usayd over Makkah and said: \I have appointed you over the people of Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic"","" with taqwā of Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic. Let none of them eat from the profit of that for which he has not assumed liability. And forbid them from a loan combined with a sale"","" and from two conditions in a single sale"","" and from any one of them selling what he does not possess.\""\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"10687","(10682) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; Miqdām ibn Dāwūd narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, from ʀāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAttāb ibn Usayd: \I have sent you to the people of Allah and the people of Makkah. So forbid them from selling what they have not taken into possession"","" or profiting from that for which they have not assumed liability"","" and from a loan combined with a sale"","" and from two conditions in a sale"","" and from a sale combined with a loan.\""\nYaḥyā ibn Ṣāh al-Aylī is alone in narrating it"","" and it is munkar with this isnād. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"10688","(10683) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī both said: Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣrī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet ﷺ sent ʿAttāb ibn Usayd and forbade him from two conditions in a sale, from a loan combined with a sale, from selling what is not in one's possession, and from profiting from that for which one has not assumed liability.\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3504]"
"10689","(10684) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʀiṣmah, who narrated to him that Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām narrated to him, saying: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I am a man who purchases various commodities. What is lawful among them and what is unlawful?\"" He said: \""O my nephew"","" when you purchase a commodity"","" do not sell it until you have taken possession of it.\""\nYaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr did not hear it directly from Yūsuf; rather"","" he heard it from Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm from Yūsuf. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi]"""""
"10690","(10685) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mūsā al-Ashyab and Saʿad ibn Ḥafṣ al-Ṭalḥī — and this is the wording of al-Ashyab — both said: Shaybān narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥak, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʀiṣmah, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" I purchase these various commodities. What is lawful for me among them and what is unlawful for me?\"" He said: \""O my nephew"","" do not sell anything until you have taken possession of it.\"" This is a ḥasan"","" connected isnād.\nSimilarly"","" Hammām ibn Yaḥyā and Abān al-ʿAṭṭār narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr"","" and Abān said in the ḥadīth: \""When you purchase a commodity"","" do not sell it until you have taken possession of it.\"" And Hammām said something to the same effect. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi]"""""
"10691","(10686) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us that Waki' narrated to us that Sufyan narrated from Ibn Tawus from his father from Ibn 'Abbas from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has measured it.\"" I said to Ibn 'Abbas"","" \""Why?\"" He said"","" \""Do you not see that they are trading gold and food while it [the food] remains in its place [undelivered]?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih — Muslim 1525]"""""
"10692","(10687) Zayd ibn al-Hubab also narrated it with this wording from al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman from Bukayr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me that Abu al-Walid narrated to me that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to me that Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me that Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr."
"10693","(10688) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us that Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us that Ibn Wahb narrated to me that 'Amr narrated from al-Mundhir ibn 'Ubayd al-Madini that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade anyone to sell food that he had purchased by measure until he had taken full possession of it.\n\n[Sahih — Abu Dawud narrated it (3495)]"
"10694","(10689) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me that Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydus said: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us that al-Qa'bi narrated — having read it to Malik — and Abu 'Abd Allah narrated to me that Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam and Muhammad ibn 'Amr and Ibrahim ibn 'Ali said: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I read to Malik from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" we used to purchase food"","" and he would send someone to us commanding us to move it from the place where we had purchased it to another place before we sold it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih — Muslim 1527]"""""
"10695","(10690) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me that Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah informed us that al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us that my father narrated to us that 'Ubayd Allah narrated from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken full possession of it.\"" He said: \""And we used to purchase food from the caravans in bulk"","" and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from selling it until we moved it from its place.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Numayr"","" and al-Bukhari also narrated it from another chain from 'Ubayd Allah. [Sahih — al-Bukhari 2029]"""""
"10696","(10691) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us that 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us that Yahya narrated to me that al-Layth narrated from Yunus from Ibn Shihab from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar said: \I saw people in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" when they purchased food in bulk"","" being prevented from selling it in their places until they took it to their dwellings.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim also narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Wahb from Yunus ibn Yazid. [Sahih — al-Bukhari 2030]"""""
"10697","(10692) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-Saydalani said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us that Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Abu al-Zinad from 'Ubayd ibn Hunayn from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I purchased oil in the market"","" and when I became entitled to it"","" a man met me and offered me a good profit"","" and I wanted to strike a deal with him. Then a man took hold of my cloak from behind me"","" and I turned to him"","" and lo"","" it was Zayd ibn Thabit. He said: 'Do not sell it where you purchased it until you take it to your own dwelling"","" for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade goods to be sold where they are purchased until the merchants have taken them to their dwellings.'\""\n\n[Sahih in other than this chain — Abu Dawud narrated it (3499)]"""""
"10698","(10693) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Isfahani informed us that Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi informed us that Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us that 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us that 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated from Sufyan from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Ibn 'Umar and Zayd ibn Thabit that they both did not see any harm in selling provisions.\n\nAnd from Sufyan from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid from al-Sha'bi that he did not see any harm in selling provisions, and he said: \The one who purchased it should not sell it until he has taken possession of it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this"","" if Allah wills"","" is what is intended by what was narrated concerning that from 'Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him. [Da'if]"""""
"10699","(10694) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Mihrajani informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Malik narrated from Nafi', the mawla of 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, that Hakim ibn Hizam purchased provisions that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab had ordered for the people. Hakim sold the provisions before taking full possession of them, and 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, heard of that and returned them to him and said: \Do not sell provisions that you have purchased until you have taken full possession of them.\"" For Hakim had purchased them from his companion"","" and he was forbidden from selling them until he had taken full possession of them.\n\n[Sahih — Malik narrated it (1313)]"""""
"10700","(10695) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us that Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us that Abu Dawud narrated to us that Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I used to sell camels in al-Baqi'"","" selling for dinars and taking dirhams"","" and selling for dirhams and taking dinars. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was about to enter the house of Hafsah"","" and I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" I sell camels in al-Baqi'"","" selling for dinars and taking dirhams"","" and selling for dirhams and taking dinars.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no harm in you taking them at the price of the day"","" so long as you two have not separated and there remains any matter between you.'\""\n\n[Da'if — previously mentioned under no. 10513]"""""
"10701","(10696) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; my grandfather Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah informed us; Mūsā ibn Wardān narrated to me that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib narrating that he heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allāh be pleased with him) saying from the pulpit: \I used to purchase dates by measure and bring them to Madīnah"","" carrying them myself along with my servants"","" from a place near Madīnah at the market of Banū Qaynuqāʿ. I would profit one or two ṣāʿs"","" measure out my profit"","" and then pour the remaining dates for them.\"" This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him). Then he asked ʿUthmān (may Allāh be pleased with him). He said: \""Yes"","" O Messenger of Allāh.\"" The Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) said: \""When you purchase"","" O ʿUthmān"","" measure it yourself"","" and when you sell"","" let the buyer measure it.\""\n\nIbn al-Mubārak"","" al-Walīd ibn Muslim"","" and a group of senior scholars narrated it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Lahīʿah. Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Farwah narrated it from Saʿīd. [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations. Aḥmad reported it"","" 1/62.]"""""
"10702","(10697) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Muḥāribī informed us in Kūfah; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah narrated to us; Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl Abū Ghassān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated to us from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Farwah, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, who said: \I used to purchase bulk quantities and bring them to such-and-such a market. They would take them from me by their own measure and grant me a profit. I mentioned this to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"","" and he said: 'When you buy by measure"","" measure it yourself"","" and when you sell by measure"","" let the buyer measure it.'\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Munqidh"","" the freedman of Surāqah"","" from ʿUthmān. [Weak.]"""""
"10703","(10698) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed him; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, and Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; they said: Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me from ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Mughīrah, from Munqidh, the freedman of Surāqah, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, that the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) said to ʿUthmān: \When you buy"","" measure it yourself"","" and when you sell"","" let the buyer measure it.\""\n\nIt is also narrated through another chain as a mursal narration from ʿUthmān. [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations. Al-Dāraquṭnī reported it"","" 3/8.]"""""
"10704","(10699) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to us; Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated to us from Maṭar al-Warrāq, from one of his companions, that Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām and ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān used to bring food from the land of Qaynuqāʿ to Madīnah and sell it by its own measure. The Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) came to them and said: \What is this?\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allāh"","" we brought it from such-and-such a land and we sell it by its measure.\"" He said: \""Do not do that. When you purchase food"","" take full possession of it"","" and when you sell it"","" measure it out for the buyer.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir. [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations.]"""""
"10705","(10700) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed him; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, and Ibrāhīm ibn Hāniʾ narrated to us; they said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Ibn Abī Laylā narrated to us from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said: \The Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) prohibited the sale of food until two measures have been applied to it—the measure of the seller and the measure of the buyer.\""\n\nIt is also narrated through another chain from Abū Hurayrah. [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations. Ibn Mājah reported it"","" 2228.]"""""
"10706","(10701) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Abū Bakr al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Zayyāt narrated to us in Baghdād; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Muslim ibn Abī Muslim narrated to us; Makhlad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us from Hishām, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \The Prophet (peace be upon him) prohibited the sale of food until two measures are applied to it. Thus"","" the surplus belongs to the seller and the deficiency falls upon him.\"" [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations. Al-Abzār reported it"","" as cited in Naṣb al-Rāyah"","" 4414.]"""""
"10707","(10702) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAmr narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \We were with the Prophet (peace be upon him) on a journey"","" and I was riding a difficult camel belonging to ʿUmar. It would overtake me and go ahead of the people. ʿUmar would scold it and pull it back. Then it would go ahead again"","" and ʿUmar would scold it and pull it back. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to ʿUmar: 'Sell it to me.' He said: 'It is yours"","" O Messenger of Allāh.' He said: 'Sell it to me.' So he sold it to the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him). Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'It is yours"","" O ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar; do with it as you wish.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 2009.]"""""
"10708","(10703) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir al-Tinnīsī narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Jaʿfar ibn Musāfir narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ narrated to us from Isḥāq Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī narrated to him that Nāfiʿ narrated to him from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allāh (peace be upon him) say: 'When you engage in ʿīnah transactions"","" grasp the tails of cattle"","" are content with agriculture"","" and abandon jihād"","" Allāh will impose upon you a humiliation from which He will not remove you until you return to your religion.'\"" [Ḥasan due to supporting narrations. Abū Dāwūd reported it"","" 3462.]"""""
"10709","(10704) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Mahrī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed me from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Khurāsānī, from ʿAṭāʾ, and he mentioned it.\n\nThat is also narrated through two weak chains from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rāḥiḥ from Ibn ʿUmar. It is also narrated from Ibn ʿUmar as a mawqūf narration that he disapproved of it and prohibited a man from coming and saying: \Buy such-and-such"","" and I will purchase it from you at such-and-such a profit.\"" [Ḥasan through its routes. See the preceding.]"""""
"10710","(10705) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us from Abū Bishr, from Yūsuf ibn Māḥik, from Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"","" a man comes to me asking me to sell him something which I do not have. Should I sell it to him and then go to the market and procure it for him at my own effort?' He said: 'Do not sell what is not with you.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ due to supporting narrations. Previously reported under number 106084.]"""""
"10711","(10706) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl and Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar both narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to me, ʿAdīy ibn Thābit informed me, he said: I heard Abū Ḥāzim narrate from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited meeting trade caravans (outside the city), a Muhājir selling on behalf of a Bedouin, a woman asking for the divorce of her sister, a man bidding against the bid of his brother, taṣriyah (withholding milk from an animal's udder), and najsh (deceptive bidding).\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith and Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh from Shuʿbah, marfūʿ (attributed to the Prophet). Al-Bukhārī alluded to their narration, and Muslim narrated it. Al-Bukhārī also narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah from Shuʿbah, marfūʿ, and he said: Ghundar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \He was forbidden\"" (nuhiya)"","" and Ādam said: \""We were forbidden\"" (nuhīnā)"","" and al-Naḍr and Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl said: \""He forbade\"" (nahā). And Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar: \""He forbade\"" (nahā). And Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb likewise said it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"","" 2577.]"""""
"10712","(10707) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī and Abū Muslim both narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAdīy ibn Thābit from Abū Ḥāzim from Abū Hurayrah, who said: He forbade meeting trade caravans, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"
"10713","(10708) Abū Dāwūd narrated it from Shuʿbah, and he said: \He forbade\"" (nahā) or \""He was forbidden\"" (nuhiya).\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us"","" ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us"","" Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us"","" Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"","" Shuʿbah narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it. Abū Dāwūd said: As though he meant the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in his saying: \""He forbade\"" (nahā).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10714","(10709) Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated it from Shuʿbah. Shuʿbah said: I said: \From the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me"","" Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Mukram narrated to us"","" Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us"","" Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us"","" Shuʿbah narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10715","(10710) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not go out to meet trade caravans"","" do not withhold milk (from animals)"","" and let none of you bid against the bid of another.\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than it. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"","" 1268.]"""""
"10716","(10711) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Masʿūdī narrated from Jābir from Abū al-Ḍuḥā from Masrūq from ʿAbdullāh, who said: I bear witness to the Truthful and Believed, Abū al-Qāsim (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: \The sale of al-muḥaffalāt is deception"","" and deception is not permissible for a Muslim.\""\n\nJābir al-Juʿfī raised it with this chain of narration from Ibn Masʿūd.\n\nAnd it was narrated with a sound chain from Ibn Masʿūd as mawqūf (stopped at the Companion).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"","" 2241.]"""""
"10717","(10712) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal al-Māsarjisī informed us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baṣrī informed us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us, al-Aʿmash narrated from Khaythamah from al-Aswad, who said: ʿAbdullāh said: \Beware of al-muḥaffalāt"","" for it is deception"","" and deception is not permissible for a Muslim.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 20814.]"""""
"10718","(10713) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Akram narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad both narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not withhold the milk of camels and sheep. Whoever purchases them after that has the option of two choices after milking it: if he is pleased with it"","" he may keep it"","" and if he is displeased with it"","" he may return it along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 2043.]"""""
"10719","(10714) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb, Abū al-Muthannā, and Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn al-Sakan all narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from Mūsā ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever purchases a sheep whose milk has been withheld"","" let him take it back and milk it. If he is pleased with its milk"","" he may keep it; otherwise"","" let him return it along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"","" and al-Bukhārī alluded to it"","" saying: And it is mentioned from Abū Ṣāliḥ"","" Mujāhid"","" al-Walīd ibn Rabbāḥ"","" and Mūsā ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""A ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it.]"""""
"10720","(10715) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you purchases a she-camel or a sheep whose milk has been withheld"","" he has the option of two choices after milking it: either he keeps it"","" or he returns it along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it.]"""""
"10721","(10716) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Makhlad al-Tamīmī informed us, al-Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Ziyād informed us that Thābit, the freedman of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd, informed him that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained sheep (muṣarrāh) and milks it"","" if he is pleased with it"","" he may keep it"","" and if he is displeased with it"","" then for its milk there should be a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from al-Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm. Al-Bukhārī said: Some of them narrated from Ibn Sīrīn: \""A ṣāʿ of dates.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10722","(10717) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān both said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān informed us from Muḥammad, who is Ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained animal (muṣarrāh) and returns it"","" let him return with it a ṣāʿ of dates — not wheat (samrāʾ).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1524]"""""
"10723","(10718) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, and he mentioned it with the same meaning, except that he said: \A milk-retained sheep (shāh muṣarrāh) — he has the option. If he returns it"","" he returns with it a ṣāʿ of dates — not wheat (samrāʾ).\"" And with its meaning"","" Ayyūb narrated it from Ibn Sīrīn. Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ayyūb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10724","(10719) Abū Zakariyyā informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb, and he mentioned it with its meaning and said: \He returns it along with a ṣāʿ of dates — not wheat (samrāʾ).\"" The Shaykh said: And some of them said from Ibn Sīrīn: \""A vessel (ināʾ) of food.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10725","(10720) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, he said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us, Hawdha ibn Khalīfah informed us, ʿAwf informed us from Muḥammad from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained she-camel (liqḥah muṣarrāh) or a milk-retained sheep (shāh muṣarrāh) and milks it"","" then he is between two considerations — he has the option. If he wishes"","" he may return it along with a vessel (ināʾ) of food.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And some of them narrated from Ibn Sīrīn: \""A ṣāʿ of food"","" and he has the option for three days.\"" Al-Bukhārī (raḥimahullāh) said: And dates are more prevalent.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And what is meant by \""food\"" (ṭaʿām) in this report is dates"","" for he said: \""Not wheat (samrāʾ).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1524]"""""
"10726","(10721) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us from Ayyūb, Hishām, and Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained sheep (shāh muṣarrāh)"","" he has the option for three days. If he wishes"","" he may return it along with a ṣāʿ of food — not wheat (samrāʾ).\"" And likewise"","" Qurrah narrated it from Ibn Sīrīn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10727","(10722) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū ʿĀmir informed us, Qurrah informed us from Muḥammad, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), the same as it.\n\nMuslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Jabalah from Abū ʿĀmir."
"10728","(10723) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us, Ṣadaqah ibn Saʿīd al-Ḥanafī informed us from Jumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr al-Taymī, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar say: We were at the door of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) waiting for him, and he came out and we followed him until he came to one of the mountain passes of Madīnah and sat upon it. He said: \O people! Let none of you meet a caravan (outside the city)"","" and let no Muhājir sell on behalf of a Bedouin. And whoever sells a milk-retained animal (muḥaffalah)"","" he has the option for three days. If he returns it"","" he returns with it the equivalent of — or he said: twice — its milk in wheat.\""\n\nJumayʿ ibn ʿUmayr is alone in narrating it. Al-Bukhārī said regarding it: \""There is a consideration (naẓar) in it.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3446]"""""
"10729","(10724) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us from ʿAwf, from al-Ḥasan, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained animal (muṣarrāh) or a milk-retained she-camel (liqḥah muṣarrāh)"","" then he is between two considerations: either he returns it along with a vessel (ināʾ) of food"","" or he keeps it.\""\n\nThis is the preserved narration (maḥfūẓ)"","" and it is mursal. Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Ḥasan from Anas ibn Mālik. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10730","(10725) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, both saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim informed us from al-Ḥasan from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a milk-retained sheep (shāh muḥaffalah)"","" its owner has the right to milk it. If he is pleased with it"","" let him keep it; otherwise"","" let him return it along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\"" [Its chain is munkar]"""""
"10731","(10726) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Shu'bah reported from al-Hakim from 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he forbade meeting the incoming trade caravans, and that a townsman should not sell on behalf of a bedouin. And whoever purchases a musarrah (an animal whose milk has been retained in its udder), he has the option of two choices: if he milks it and is pleased with it, he may keep it; but if he returns it, he shall return it along with a sa' of food or a sa' of dates.\n\nThe Sheikh said: It is possible that this is a doubt on the part of one of the narrators, who said \a sa' of this or of that"",""\"" not by way of giving a choice"","" so as to accord with the established hadiths on this matter. And Allah knows best. [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad 4/314]"""""
"10732","(10727) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Musaddad narrated to us: Mu'tamir narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman reported from al-Taymi from Abu 'Uthman from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: \Whoever purchases a muhaffalah (an animal whose milk has been retained) and returns it"","" let him return with it a sa'.\"" He said: \""And the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade meeting the trade caravans (al-buyu').\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad. [Sahih. Bukhari 2042]"""""
"10733","(10728) Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra' narrated it: Mu'tamir informed us. He said: I heard my father say: Abu 'Uthman narrated to us from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: \Whoever purchases a muhaffalah sheep and returns it"","" let him return with it a sa' of dates.\""\n\nAbu 'Amr al-Adib informed us of it: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: Abu Yahya al-Ruwayani narrated to us: Ibrahim mentioned it.\n\nAl-Isma'ili said: The hadith of the muhaffalah is from the statement of 'Abdullah"","" though Abu Khalid raised it (as a marfu' hadith) from al-Taymi. [Sahih. See the one before it]"""""
"10734","(10729) Abu 'Amr informed us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: al-Qasim narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Khalid mentioned it, but he did not say \min tamr\"" (of dates).\n\nAl-Isma'ili said: And Ibn al-Mubarak"","" Yahya ibn Sa'id"","" Ibn Abi 'Adi"","" Yazid ibn Zurai'"","" Hushaym"","" Jarir"","" and others narrated the hadith of the muhaffalah as a mawquf narration from Ibn Mas'ud. [Sahih. See the one before it]"""""
"10735","(10730) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muzzi informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn 'Abdur-Rahman reported from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a musarrah (an animal whose milk has been retained in its udder)"","" he has the option for three days. If he wishes"","" he may keep it"","" and if he wishes"","" he may return it and return with it a sa' of dates.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Muslim 1524]"""""
"10736","(10731) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: al-Asfati (i.e., al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl) narrated to us: 'Ayyash narrated to us: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Qurrah reported from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever purchases a musarrah"","" he has the option for three days. If he returns it"","" he shall return it along with a sa' of food — not samra' (wheat).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the hadith of Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi from Qurrah.\n\nAnd al-Bukhari said: \""And some of them said from Ibn Sirin: 'A sa' of food"","" and he has the option for three days.'\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1524]"""""
"10737","(10732) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us: Abu Hamid ibn Bilal al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Rabi' al-Makki narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah reported from al-'Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by a man who was selling food and said: \How do you sell?\"" The man informed him"","" and revelation came to him: \""Put your hand into it.\"" So he put his hand in"","" and behold"","" it was wet. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""He who deceives is not of us.\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawud 3552"","" Ibn Majah 2224]"""""
"10738","(10733) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abdullah informed me: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah informed us: Dalaj ibn Ahmad al-Sajzi narrated to us: Musa ibn Harun narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us. Both said: Isma'il ibn Ja'far reported from al-'Ala' from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a heap of food. He put his hand into it, and his fingers touched moisture. He said: \What is this"","" O owner of the food?\"" He said: \""The rain fell upon it"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Why did you not place it on top of the food so that the people could see it? He who deceives is not of me.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Qutaybah and Yahya ibn Ayyub. [Sahih. Muslim 102]"""""
"10739","(10734) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father said: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub narrating from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from 'Abdur-Rahman ibn Shumasah from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. It is not permissible for a Muslim who sells to his brother a sale in which there is a defect that he does not disclose it to him.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Majah 2246]"""""
"10740","(10735) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Hayri both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr Hisham ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Razi reported from Yazid ibn Abi Malik. Abu Sibah informed us, saying: \I purchased a she-camel from the house of Wathilah ibn al-Asqa'. When I came out"","" Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' caught up with us"","" dragging his cloak. He said: 'O servant of Allah"","" have you purchased?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Was what is in it (i.e."","" its defects) explained to you?' I said: 'What is in it? It is fat and apparently healthy.' He said: 'Did you intend it for meat"","" or did you intend it for travel?' I said: 'Rather"","" I intend to use it for Hajj.' He said: 'Indeed"","" there is a perforation in its hoof.' Then its owner said: 'May Allah set you right! What do you want with this? You are ruining my sale.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""Whoever sells something"","" it is not permissible for him until he discloses what is in it"","" and it is not permissible for one who knows that to not disclose it.\""'\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Ahmad 3/419]"""""
"10741","(10736) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep (to deceive buyers). Whoever purchases them after that"","" then after milking them"","" he has the option: if he wishes"","" he may keep them"","" and if he wishes"","" he may return them along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it as mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Passed previously.]"""""
"10742","(10737) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to us, saying: \Ibn ʿUmar purchased from the partner of al-Nawwās camels afflicted with ḥīm (thirst disease).\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us"","" Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us"","" Abū Aḥmad ibn Ziyād narrated to us"","" Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us"","" Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that Ibn ʿUmar purchased camels afflicted with ḥiyām from a partner of a man called al-Nawwās from the people of Makkah. He informed al-Nawwās that he had sold them to a certain elder. Al-Nawwās said: \""Woe to you! That was Ibn ʿUmar!\"" So al-Nawwās came to Ibn ʿUmar and said: \""My partner sold you camels afflicted with ḥiyām and did not know you.\"" He said: \""Then drive them away.\"" When he went to drive them away"","" Ibn ʿUmar said: \""Leave them. We are pleased with the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: there is no contagion (lā ʿadwā).\"" The wording is that of Ibn Abī ʿUmar.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī from Sufyān"","" and he said: \""ḥīm.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 19993]"""""
"10743","(10738) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ, the son of the daughter of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr Kashmard informed us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us from Makhlad ibn Khufāf from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The yield (al-kharāj) is by virtue of liability (al-ḍamān).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it 3508]"""""
"10744","(10739) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī narrated to us, ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated it, except that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the yield is by virtue of liability.\""\n\nAnd likewise Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"","" and they differed over Ibn Abī Dhiʾb regarding the story of the hadith. [Ḍaʿīf. Passed in the one before it.]"""""
"10745","(10740) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us from Makhlad ibn Khufāf, who said: \Between me and my partners there was a slave"","" and we shared him among ourselves. One of them was absent"","" and he arrived and took us to Hishām for judgment. He ruled that the slave be returned along with his yield"","" and there had accumulated from his yield one thousand dirhams. So I went to ʿUrwah and informed him"","" and ʿUrwah informed me from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the yield is by virtue of liability. So I went to Hishām and informed him"","" and he reversed that and approved it.\""\n\nAnd with its meaning Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"","" except that he did not name the thousand nor Hishām"","" and he said: \""to one of the judges.\"" And Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb and named them both."""""
"10746","(10741) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us from Makhlad ibn Khufāh al-Ghifārī, who said: \I took ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz to judgment regarding a slave who had deceived us"","" and we obtained his produce. ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr was present"","" and ʿUrwah narrated to him from ʿĿʾishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the yield is by virtue of liability.\""\n\nAnd with this meaning al-Shāfiʿī narrated it from one whom he does not suspect"","" from the people of Madīnah"","" from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb. [Ḍaʿīf. Passed in the one before it.]"""""
"10747","(10742) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us among others, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, one whom I do not suspect informed me from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, who said: Makhlad ibn Khufāf informed me, saying: \I purchased a slave and derived profit from him"","" then I discovered a defect in him. I took the matter to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz for judgment. He ruled for me the return of the slave and ruled against me the return of his profit. So I went to ʿUrwah and informed him. He said: 'I will go to him this evening and inform him that ʿĀʾishah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in a similar case that the yield is by virtue of liability.' So I hastened to ʿUmar and informed me of what ʿUrwah had narrated from ʿĀʾishah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar said: 'How easy it is for me regarding a judgment I have passed—Allah knows that I intended nothing but the truth in it—when a Sunnah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reaches me regarding it. I will reverse the judgment of ʿUmar and enforce the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So ʿUrwah went to him and ruled for me that I should take the yield from the one against whom he had ruled it for him.\""\n\nAnd with this meaning Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah that a man purchased a slave during the time of the Prophet ﷺ who had a defect of which he was unaware. He derived profit from him"","" then discovered the defect and returned him. He took the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" he derived profit from him for some time.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""The profit is by virtue of liability.\""\n\nAnd likewise Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated it from Muslim ibn Khālid"","" except that he said: \""The yield is by virtue of liability.\""\n\nAnd likewise Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Kitāb al-Sunan from Ibrāhīm ibn Marwān from his father from Muslim.\n\nAnd ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī al-Muqaddamī followed Muslim ibn Khālid in his narration from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah without the story. [Ḍaʿīf. Passed in the one before it.]"""""
"10748","(10743) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed him, Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the yield is by virtue of liability. [Ḍaʿīf. al-Tirmidhī narrated it 1286]"
"10749","(10744) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, al-Shaybānī narrated to us from al-Shaʿbī that a man purchased a slave from another man and derived profit from him, then discovered a disease in him that had been present with the seller. He took the dispute to Shurayḥ, who said: \Return the disease for its disease"","" and the profit is yours by virtue of liability.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10750","(10745) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb al-Kirmānī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Abī Yaʿqūb, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to me, my father narrated to me from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn from ʿAlī regarding a man who purchased a slave girl and had intercourse with her, then found a defect in her. He said: \She is his"","" and the seller shall return the difference between soundness and the defect. And if he had not had intercourse with her"","" he would have returned her.\""\n\nAnd likewise Sufyān al-Thawrī and Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated it from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"","" and it is mursal. ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn did not meet his grandfather ʿAlī. And it has been narrated from Muslim ibn Khālid from Jaʿfar from his father from his grandfather from Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī from ʿAlī"","" but it is not preserved. [Ḍaʿīf. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it 14685]"""""
"10751","(10746) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Sharīk narrated — (ḥ) and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Jaʿfar al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Jābir from ʿĀmir from ʿUmar, who said: \If she is a previously married woman (thayyib)"","" he returns with her half of the ʿushr (one-tenth)"","" and if she is a virgin (bikr)"","" he returns the full ʿushr.\"" ʿAlī said: \""This is mursal. ʿĀmir did not meet ʿUmar.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""We do not know this to be established from ʿUmar"","" nor from ʿAlī"","" nor from either of them.\"" And likewise said some of those who were present and who were present with those who debated him on this matter from among the people of ḥadīth: \""That is not established.\"" And it is among what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him"","" from Abī al-ʿAbbās"","" from al-Rabīʿ"","" from al-Shāfiʿī"","" in the book *Ikhtilāf al-ʿIrāqiyyīn*. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"","" 3/309]"""""
"10752","(10747) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Abān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Hāshim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn ʿAjlān narrated to us; Abū Yazīd al-Madanī narrated to us; Abū Hurayrah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \The refractory one is to be returned\"" — meaning the refractory camel. ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith and Badal ibn al-Muḥabbar narrated it from ʿAbd al-Salām"","" in the case of a man who purchased a camel and kept it with him"","" then it became refractory and he brought it back to its owner"","" who accepted it. Then this was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ"","" and he said: \""Indeed"","" the refractory camel is to be returned.\"" [Weak. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"""""
"10753","(10748) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us; Sawwār ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn ʿAjlān al-ʿUjayfī narrated to us; Abū Yazīd al-Madanī narrated to us; from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. [Empty]"
"10754","(10749) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf, may Allah be pleased with him, purchased a female slave from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī and found that she had a husband, so he returned her. [Weak. Narrated by Mālik, 1278]"
"10755","(10750) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ narrated, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said: Sufyān informed us from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah: that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf purchased a slave girl from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī and was informed that she had a husband, so he returned her. [Weak. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"
"10756","(10751) The shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghaylān from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā: regarding a female slave who is sold while she has a husband, that ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, judged that it is a defect (ʿayb) by which she may be returned. [Weak]"
"10757","(10752) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us; Saʿīd — that is, Ibn Abī ʿArūbah — narrated to us; Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The ʿuhdah (warranty period) for a slave is three nights.\"" ʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: Saʿīd said: I said to Qatādah: \""How can this be?\"" He said: \""If the buyer finds a defect in the merchandise"","" then he returns it within those three days and is not asked for evidence. But when the three days have passed"","" he has no right to return it except with evidence that he purchased it and the defect was present in it; otherwise"","" the seller's oath is required that he did not sell it with any ailment.\"" And likewise narrated it Hammām ibn Yaḥyā and Abān ibn Yazīd from Qatādah. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 3556]"""""
"10758","(10753) Hishām al-Dastawāʾī contradicted them in its text (matn). Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us; Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated to us; Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \The ʿuhdah (warranty period) for a slave is four nights.\"" ʿAbd al-Wahhāb said: Hishām said: Qatādah said: \""The people of Madīnah say three.\"" And likewise narrated it Muʿādh ibn Hishām and others from Hishām. [Weak. See the one before it]"""""
"10759","(10754) Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated it from Hishām from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan from Samurah or ʿUqbah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The ʿuhdah (warranty period) for a slave is four days.\"" Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated it to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated it. And Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated it from al-Ḥasan. [Weak. See the one before it]"""""
"10760","(10755) As Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd informed us from al-Ḥasan from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ʿuhdah (warranty period) beyond four.\"" The crux of this ḥadīth rests on al-Ḥasan from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir"","" and it is mursal. [Weak. See the one before it]"""""
"10761","(10756) 'Alī ibn 'Abdullāh ibn al-Madīnī said: al-Ḥasan did not hear anything from 'Uqbah ibn 'Āmir. Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of that. He said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Barā' informed us; he said: I heard 'Alī ibn 'Abdullāh al-Madīnī, and he mentioned it. And a group of the imāms of the people of transmission said the same.\n\nAl-Shāfi'ī said: And the report that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) granted Ḥabbān ibn Munqidh a warranty of three days is specific.\n\nIt is narrated from Sa'īd ibn Sālim, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Aṭā', that he said: There was, in the past, no warranty on land — neither for [damage from] wandering [animals], nor for leprosy, nor for anything. I said to him: What about three days? He said: There is nothing [in that]. If he sold it [the slave] in sound condition, I see nothing [to the contrary] — Allah brings about from his affair what He wills — unless he brings proof of something that existed before he purchased it. And this is how we see the matter now. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10762","(10757) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-'Adl narrated to us; he said: Ismā'īl ibn Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Salām both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us. And 'Alī narrated to me; he said: Aḥmad ibn Salamah and Muḥammad ibn Nu'aym both said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'īd narrated to us; he said: al-Layth narrated, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn 'Abdullāh, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever purchases a date-palm after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the one who sold it"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise]. And whoever purchases a slave"","" his wealth belongs to the one who sold him"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise].\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from 'Abdullāh ibn Yūsuf"","" from al-Layth"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2250]"""""
"10763","(10758) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓufar ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-'Alawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us; he said: Abū Ja'far Muḥammad ibn 'Alī ibn Duḥaym informed us; he said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us; he said: 'Ubaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; he said: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever sells a date-palm after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the one who pollinated it"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise]. And whoever sells a slave who has wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the one who sold him"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it]"""""
"10764","(10759) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to me; he said: Ismā'īl ibn Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Salām both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: Sufyān narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others. Thus Sālim ibn 'Abdullāh narrated it from his father, from the Prophet (ﷺ), the story of the date-palm and the slave together. But Nāfi' contradicted him: he narrated the story of the date-palm from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ), and the story of the slave from Ibn 'Umar from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it]"
"10765","(10760) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed him; he said: Abū Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-'Abadī narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; he said: Mālik narrated, from Nāfi', from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells date-palms that have been pollinated"","" their fruit belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it]"""""
"10766","(10761) And with this chain of narration, Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfi', from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, that 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever sells a slave who has wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise].\""\n\nAnd Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī and others narrated it similarly from Nāfi'. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it]"""""
"10767","(10762) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: I heard Abū 'Alī al-Ḥusayn ibn 'Alī al-Ḥāfiẓ say: I heard Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan say: I asked Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj, may Allah have mercy on him, about the disagreement of Sālim and Nāfi' regarding the story of the slave. He said: The position is what Nāfi' said, even though Sālim is more precise (aḥfaẓ) than him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10768","(10763) Abū 'Abdullāh informed us; he said: I heard Abū 'Alī say: I asked Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Nasā'ī about the ḥadīth of Sālim and Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, regarding the story of the slave and the date-palm. He said: The position is what Nāfi' said, even though Sālim is more precise (aḥfaẓ) than him. And I saw in the Kitāb al-'Ilal of Abū 'Īsā al-Tirmidhī, from Abū 'Īsā, who said: I asked Muḥammad — meaning al-Bukhārī, may Allah have mercy on him — about it. He said: Indeed, Nāfi' contradicts Sālim in certain aḥādīth, and this is one of those aḥādīth. It is as though he considered both ḥadīths ṣaḥīḥ and that both are possible.\n\nHe said: And they narrated this ḥadīth from 'Ubaydullāh ibn Abī Ja'far and others.\n\nThe Shaykh said: As for the narration from 'Ubaydullāh ibn Abī Ja'far, it is from him, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with wording differing from this. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10769","(10764) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr informed us; he said: Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; he said: Aḥmad ibn Mahdī narrated to us; he said: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us; he said: al-Layth informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us from the original of his book and in his Fawā'id; he said: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdūs al-'Anazī informed us, by the selection of Abū 'Alī al-Ḥāfiẓ; he said: 'Uthmān ibn Sa'īd al-Dārimī narrated to us; he said: 'Abdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ and Ibn Abī Maryam both said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us; he said: 'Ubaydullāh ibn Abī Ja'far narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn 'Abdullāh, from Nāfi', from 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he said: \Whoever frees a slave"","" his wealth belongs to him"","" unless the master stipulates his wealth for himself"","" and it shall be his.\"" And in the narration of Abū Sa'īd: that the Prophet (ﷺ) [said it] — and the rest is the same.\n\nAnd Ibn Wahb narrated it from Ibn Lahī'ah and al-Layth ibn Sa'd"","" and he said in his wording: \""Whoever frees a slave who has wealth"","" the slave's wealth belongs to him"","" unless the master stipulates [otherwise].\""\n\nAnd this contradicts the narration of the group from Nāfi'. Indeed"","" the ḥuffāẓ narrated it from Nāfi'"","" from Ibn 'Umar"","" from 'Umar"","" as has preceded. And a group narrated it from Nāfi'"","" from Ibn 'Umar"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" just as Sālim narrated it from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Mājah 2529]"""""
"10770","(10765) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed us; he said: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; he said: Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; he said: Abū al-Rabī' narrated to us; he said: Abū Shihāb narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Any man who sells a slave"","" his wealth belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates [otherwise].\"" And 'Uthmān ibn Jabalah narrated it similarly"","" from Shu'bah"","" from 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'īd"","" from Nāfi'"","" from Ibn 'Umar"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its text passed shortly before]"""""
"10771","(10766) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan al-Farisi informed us; 'Abd ibn 'Uthman ibn Jabalah ibn Abi Rawwad informed me; my father informed me from Shu'bah, who said: I heard 'Abd Rabbih ibn Sa'id narrating from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a date-palm after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to its first owner; and whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to his first owner"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" Shu'bah said: \""I narrated to him the hadith of Ayyub from Nafi' that he narrated the matter of the date-palm from the Prophet (ﷺ) and the matter of the slave from 'Umar.\"" So 'Abd Rabbih said: \""I do not know them both except from the Prophet (ﷺ).\"" Then he said on another occasion"","" narrating from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" without any doubt. And it was narrated by Sulayman ibn Musa from Nafi'"","" raised [to the Prophet]. [Sahih. Previously mentioned.]"""""
"10772","(10767) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us. (H) And Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us. Both said: Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us from Sa'id from Qatadah from 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to his first owner"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever sells a date-palm whose fruit has ripened"","" its fruit belongs to its first owner"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" This chain is munqati' [disconnected]. It has also been narrated from Hisham al-Dastawa'i from Qatadah from 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid from al-Zuhri from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" as though he intended the hadith of al-Zuhri from Salim from his father. And it has been narrated from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Sahih.]"""""
"10773","(10768) Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi informed us; al-Hakam ibn Musa informed us; Yahya ibn Hamzah informed me from Abu Wahb 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Ubayd al-Kala'i from Sulayman ibn Musa from Nafi' that he narrated from Ibn 'Umar and from 'Ata' from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said. (H) And Abu Ahmad informed us, and he said: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim informed us; al-Walid informed us from Abu Mu'ayd Hafs ibn Ghaylan from Sulayman ibn Musa from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar and 'Ata' from Jabir that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to him and his debt is upon him"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and whoever pollinates a date-palm and then sells it after pollinating it"","" its fruit belongs to him"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" [Sahih.]"""""
"10774","(10769) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani informed me; Ahmad ibn Hazim ibn Abi Gharzah informed me; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed me; al-Nu'man ibn Thabit, Abu Hanifah (may Allah have mercy on him), informed me from al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \Whoever sells a pollinated date-palm or a slave who possesses wealth"","" the fruit and the wealth belong to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" And similarly"","" Hammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated it from al-Zubayr. [Sahih.]"""""
"10775","(10770) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh informed me; Yazid ibn al-Haytham informed me; Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth informed me; al-Ashja'i informed me from Sufyan from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: One who heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah narrating informed me that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" And similarly"","" Yahya al-Qattan and others narrated it from Sufyan"","" and it is a hasan mursal [disconnected]. And it has been narrated from 'Ali and 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with them) through two mursal chains"","" raised [to the Prophet]. [Sahih.]"""""
"10776","(10771) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed us; Sulayman ibn Bilal informed us from Ja'far ibn Muhammad from his father that 'Ali said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" his wealth belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise—the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged by this. And whoever sells a date-palm after it has been pollinated"","" its fruit belongs to the seller"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" [Sahih.]"""""
"10777","(10772) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr informed us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah ibn Abi 'Ayyash al-Asadi informed me; Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit informed me from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Among the judgments of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) is that the fruit of the date-palm belongs to the one who pollinated it"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise; and that the wealth of the slave belongs to the one who sold him"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\"" [Sahih.]"""""
"10778","(10773) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah, Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Ali ibn Hamdan, and Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Saffar, and others said: Abu 'Amr Isma'il ibn Najayd al-Sulami informed us; Abu Muslim informed us; al-Ansari informed us; 'Abd al-A'la ibn Abi al-Mawarin informed us; 'Imran ibn 'Umayr from his father, who was a slave of 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, said: 'Abd Allah said to him: \What wealth do you have"","" O 'Umayr? For I wish to emancipate you. Indeed"","" I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever emancipates a slave"","" his wealth belongs to the one who emancipated him.'\"" And it has been narrated from al-Qasim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman that Ibn Mas'ud said that to 'Umayr. And although it is mursal"","" it has strength due to the narration of 'Abd al-A'la. And al-Thawri narrated it from Abu Khalid from 'Imran ibn 'Umayr from his father that Ibn Mas'ud emancipated his father 'Umayr"","" then said: \""As for your wealth"","" it is mine"",""\"" and then he left it. [Sahih.]"""""
"10779","(10774) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Tahir al-Faqih, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us; Ibn Abi Fudayk informed me; Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed me from al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah that he heard him say: \Were it not for two matters"","" I would love to be a slave. That is because a slave has no power to do anything with his wealth"","" and because I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Allah has not created a slave who fulfills the right of Allah upon him and the right of his master except that Allah will grant him his reward twice.'\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad 2/448.]"""""
"10780","(10775) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; 'Abd al-Karim ibn al-Haytham informed us; Abu al-Yaman informed me; Shu'ayb informed me. Nafi' said: Ibn 'Umar used to say: \The slave and his wealth belong to his master"","" and there is no sin upon his master for what he takes from his wealth.\"" And with this chain"","" he said: Nafi' said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar used to say: \""It is not permissible for a slave to spend anything from his wealth or to give it to anyone except with the permission of his master"","" except that he may eat from it in a reasonable manner or clothe himself.\"" [Sahih.]"""""
"10781","(10776) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Abu al-Shaykh al-Isfahani informed us — Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us — Abu 'Amir narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us — Hanzalah narrated to us that he heard Tawus narrating from Ibn 'Abbas that a slave possesses nothing of his own blood or wealth. [Hasan]"
"10782","(10777) Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muhammadabadi narrated to us — al-'Abbas al-Dawri narrated to us — Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi narrated to us — Maslamah ibn 'Alqamah narrated to us — Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from Simak ibn Harb from Salamah al-'Ijli from Salman al-Farsi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with a vessel of bread and meat. He said, \What is this"","" O Salman?\"" I said"","" \""It is charity (sadaqah).\"" He did not eat it and said to his Companions"","" \""Eat.\"" Then I came to him with a vessel of bread and meat and he said"","" \""What is this"","" O Salman?\"" I said"","" \""It is a gift (hadiyyah).\"" He ate it and said"","" \""We eat the gift"","" but we do not eat charity.\"" I said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what do you say about the Christians?\"" He said"","" \""O Salman"","" there is no good in the Christians nor in those who love them"",""\"" three times"","" \""except one who is upon the religion of your companion.\"" He said: \""I then knew that my companion was upon the religion of 'Isa"","" meaning the monk who was with Salman.\"" The Shaykh said: In the hadith of Buraydah there is an addition indicating that Salman was a slave when he presented the gift to the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Da'if]"""""
"10783","(10778) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us — Ja'far ibn Awn informed us — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah and a man among our freedmen narrated to us — (and in another chain:) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar from Abu 'Alqamah, their freedman, and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ghafiqiyy — that they both heard Ibn 'Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Allah has cursed wine (khamr)"","" its drinker"","" its server"","" its seller"","" its buyer"","" its presser"","" its one who has it pressed"","" its carrier"","" and the one to whom it is carried.\"" Ja'far added in his narration: \""and its price-earner.\"" [Sahih. Abu Dawud narrated it (3674)]"""""
"10784","(10779) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi narrated to us — ibn Hammad narrated to me — 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to me: I asked Yahya ibn Ma'in about Muhammad ibn Mus'ab. He narrated to me one day from Abu al-Ash'hab from Abu Raja' from 'Imran ibn Husayn that he disliked the sale of weapons during tribulation (fitnah). [Munkar. Al-Khatib narrated it in his Tarikh (3/278)]"
"10785","(10780) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us — Abu Ahmad narrated to us — Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Yahya, the imam of the mosque of Qarqisya, narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us — Abu al-Ash'hab narrated from Abu Raja' from 'Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the sale of weapons during tribulation. Its being raised (as a marfu' hadith) is an error; the mawquf version is more correct, and that is also narrated from Abu Raja' as his own statement. [Munkar. Ibn 'Adi narrated it in al-Kamil (2/372)]"
"10786","(10781) It is known as marfu' only from the hadith of Bahr ibn Kaniz al-Saqqa' from 'Ubayd Allah al-Qibti from Abu Raja' al-'Ataridi from 'Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade the sale of weapons during tribulation. Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us — they both said: Abu al-'Abbas, that is al-Asamm, narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun informed us — Bahr al-Saqqa' narrated it. And Bahr al-Saqqa' is weak (da'if) and cannot be used as evidence. [Munkar]"
"10787","(10782) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu Qilabah narrated to us — 'Abbad ibn Layth, the owner of al-Karabis, narrated to us — 'Abd al-Majid, that is Abu Wahb, narrated from al-'Adi ibn Khalid ibn Hawdah, who said: \Shall I not recite to you a letter that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) wrote for me?\"" He then produced a letter"","" and in it was: \""This is what al-'Adi ibn Khalid ibn Hawdah purchased from Muhammad"","" the Messenger of Allah — he purchased from him a male or female slave\"" — 'Abbad was uncertain — \""there being no defect (da')"","" no deception (gha'illah)"","" and no hidden defect (khibthah). The sale of a Muslim to a Muslim.\"" The Shaykh said: This hadith is known through 'Abbad ibn al-Layth. And we have recorded it from another unreliable source. [Hasan li-ghayrihi. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it (1216)]"""""
"10788","(10783) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Fahr al-Misri in Makkah narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Rashid narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us — Qa'nab ibn Muharir narrated to us — al-Ashma'i narrated to us — 'Uthman al-Shahham narrated from Abu Raja' al-'Ataridi, who said: Al-'Adi ibn Khalid ibn Hawdah said, \Shall I not recite to you a letter that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) wrote for me?\"" We said"","" \""Yes.\"" And in it was written: \""In the name of Allah"","" the Most Gracious"","" the Most Merciful. This is what al-'Adi ibn Khalid ibn Hawdah purchased from Muhammad"","" the Messenger of Allah — he purchased from him a male or female slave\"" — 'Uthman was uncertain — \""the sale of a Muslim to a Muslim"","" there being no defect"","" no deception"","" and no hidden defect.\"" [Hasan. Al-Tabarani narrated it in al-Kabir (15)]"""""
"10789","(10784) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us — Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi al-Harawi informed us — Mu'adh ibn Najdah narrated to us — Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us — Sharik narrated from 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir from Zayd ibn Thabit, who used to hold that freedom from liability (bara'ah) from every defect was permissible. And 'Ali ibn Hujr narrated it from Sharik and said: from Zayd ibn Thabit and Ibn 'Umar. [Da'if. Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it (21099)]"
"10790","(10785) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar in Baghdad informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shafi'i narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Azhar narrated to us — al-Mufaddal ibn Ghassan al-Ghalabi said: Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ma'in said regarding the hadith of Sharik from 'Asim ibn 'Ubayd Allah from Zayd ibn Thabit — \Freedom from liability from every defect constitutes freedom from liability\"" — \""It is not established; Sharik alone narrated it"","" and it was in his book from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"10791","(10786) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Jarrāḥī in Marw narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Sāsawayh narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkari narrated to us; Wahb ibn Zamʿah informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik said: ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — was asked about the ḥadīth of Sharīk from Zayd ibn Thābit regarding sale with a declaration of freedom from defects (barāʾah). He replied: Sharīk responded contrary to what was in his book, and we could not find any basis (aṣl) for this ḥadīth.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The most authentic narration on this topic is what…"
"10792","(10787) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar sold a slave of his for eight hundred dirhams and sold him with a declaration of freedom from defects (barāʾah). The one who purchased him said to ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar: \There is a disease in the slave that you did not disclose.\"" So they disputed and brought the matter before ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān. The man said: \""He sold me a slave who had a disease"","" and he did not inform me of it.\"" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \""I sold him with a declaration of freedom from defects.\"" ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān ruled that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar must swear an oath that he sold the slave while knowing of no disease in him. ʿAbd Allāh refused to swear the oath for him"","" so the slave was returned. Thereafter"","" ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar sold the slave for one thousand five hundred dirhams.\n\nMālik said: The matter upon which there is consensus among us regarding one who sells a slave"","" a slave-girl"","" or an animal with a declaration of freedom from defects is that he is absolved of every defect"","" unless he knew of a defect and concealed it. If he knew of a defect and concealed it"","" his declaration of absolution shall not benefit him"","" and what he sold shall be returned to him.\n\nIt has been narrated to us from al-Shāfiʿī that he said regarding a man who sells a slave or any animal with a declaration of freedom from defects: The position to which we adhere — and Allāh knows best — is the ruling of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu)"","" that he is absolved of every defect he did not know of"","" but he is not absolved of a defect he knew of and the seller did not specify. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1274.]"""""
"10793","(10788) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, Hishām, and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAtīq, from Ḥumayd, that Sharīḥ would not grant absolution from a disease until he showed it to him. Yaḥyā says: \I absolve myself from such and such"","" and if a disease occurs between those two points"","" he is not absolved until he is shown that defect.\""\n\nIt has been narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī regarding a man who sells goods and declares himself free from disease: He is absolved of whatever he named.\n\nAnd from Sharīḥ al-Qāḍī: He is not absolved until he places his hand upon the disease. And from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ a similar statement. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"10794","(10789) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that when he purchased a slave-girl, he would uncover her shin and place his hand between her breasts and on her buttocks, as though he was doing so from behind the garment. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"10795","(10790) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿUmar ibn Sinān narrated to us; ʿAbbās al-Khallāl narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no harm in a man examining a slave-girl when he intends to purchase her and looking at her"","" apart from her ʿawrah. Her ʿawrah is from her knees to the place where her lower garment is tied.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is singular (tafarrada bihi) on the authority of Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar"","" the judge of Ḥalab"","" from Ṣāliḥ ibn Ḥassān.\n\nIt has also been narrated to us in the book of Ṣalāh from the ḥadīth of ʿĪsā ibn Maymūn from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"","" and both chains of narration are weak. And Allāh knows best. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"","" 10773.]"""""
"10796","(10791) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl informed us; my grandfather narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Qays ibn Wahb, from Abī al-Wadāk, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who raised it (to the Prophet), saying regarding the captives of Awṭās: \A pregnant woman shall not be approached until she gives birth"","" and one who is not pregnant shall not be approached until she has one menstrual cycle.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"","" 2157.]"""""
"10797","(10792) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah said: ʿĀmir was asked about a man who purchases a slave-girl — may he have intercourse with her before verifying the purity of her womb (istibrāʾ)? He said: \The Muslim women were captured on the day of Awṭās"","" and the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'No man shall approach a pregnant woman until she delivers her child"","" and no one who is not pregnant until she has one menstrual cycle.'\"" This mursal narration serves as a witness for what preceded.\n\nIt has been narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd that he said: A slave-girl"","" when purchased"","" is to be cleared by one menstrual cycle. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi.]"""""
"10798","(10793) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us; Abū Muslim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning Ibn Ḥammād al-Shuʿaythī, narrated to us; Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Muḥammad, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān used to purchase a caravan of camels and say: \Who will increase me in their ropes? Who will place a dīnār in my hand?\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi.]"""""
"10799","(10794) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Misʿar narrated from Abī Baḥr, from a shaykh of theirs, who said: I saw upon ʿAlī (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) a thick lower garment. He said: \I purchased it for five dirhams; whoever will give me a profit of one dīnār on it"","" I will sell it to him.\""\n\nIt has been narrated to us from Sharīḥ"","" Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"","" and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that they used to permit the sale of \""dah dahāzdah\"" (ten for eleven). [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad in Fāḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah"","" 885.]"""""
"10800","(10795) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Ziyād — or Yazīd — who heard Ibn ʿAbbās prohibiting the sale of \dah yāzdah\"" (ten for eleven) or \""dah davāzdah\"" (ten for twelve)"","" and he said: \""This is the sale of the non-Arabs (al-aʿājim).\""\n\nIt is possible that it was only prohibited when one says: \""It is yours for ten-eleven\"" or \""for ten-twelve"",""\"" without naming the principal (raʾs al-māl)"","" and then naming it at the time of payment. And similarly what has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar regarding this. And Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 15011.]"""""
"10801","(10796) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There are three persons whom Allah will not speak to"","" nor will He purify them"","" and for them is a painful punishment: a man who sells a commodity to a man after ʿAṣr"","" swearing by Allah that he purchased it for such-and-such a price"","" and the buyer believes him and takes it"","" though the matter was not so; a man who pledges allegiance to an imām only for worldly gain — if he gives him of it"","" he fulfils his pledge"","" and if he does not give him of it"","" he does not fulfil it; and a man who has surplus water in the wilderness and prevents the wayfarer from it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" from Abū Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 108]"""""
"10802","(10797) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, al-ʿAwwām narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Saksakī, from Ibn Abī Awfā, that a man set out his merchandise and swore by Allah that he had been offered for it what he had not in fact been offered. Then this verse was revealed: {Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price…} [Āl ʿImrān: 77]. Ibn Abī Awfā said: \The one who artificially inflates the price (al-nājish) is a consumer of ribā"","" a traitor.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from two other routes from al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1982]"""""
"10803","(10798) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Muḥammad al-Karābīsī narrated to us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī al-Imām narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sharīḥ al-Anṣārī narrated to us, Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, who said: My wife visited ʿĀʾishah, along with the umm walad of Zayd ibn Arqam. The umm walad of Zayd said to her: \I sold to Zayd a slave girl for eight hundred dirhams on deferred payment"","" and I bought her back from him for six hundred dirhams in cash.\"" ʿĀʾiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Convey to Zayd that he has nullified his jihād alongside the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" unless he repents. Evil is what you sold"","" and evil is what you bought.\""\n\nThis is how Shuʿbah narrated it via a mursal route. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd 451]"""""
"10804","(10799) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from al-ʿĀliyah, who said: I was sitting with ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) when Umm Muḥibbah came to her and said: \O Umm al-Muʾminīn"","" did you know Zayd ibn Arqam?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""I sold him my slave girl for eight hundred dirhams on deferred payment"","" and he wishes to sell her to me for six hundred dirhams in cash.\"" She said to her: \""Evil is what you bought"","" and evil is what he sold. Convey to Zayd that he has nullified his jihād alongside the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) unless he repents.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. See the preceding]"""""
"10805","(10800) And Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from his wife al-ʿĀliyah, that the wife of Abū al-Safar sold her slave girl to Zayd ibn Arqam for eight hundred dirhams on deferred payment. He mentioned it, except that he said: \Evil is what you sold"","" and evil is what you bought.\"" And he added: she said: \""What do you think if I only take back my capital?\"" She said: {So whoever receives an admonition from his Lord and desists"","" he shall have what has passed.} [al-Baqarah: 275]\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us"","" Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us"","" Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us"","" ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us"","" ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us"","" Sufyān narrated it.\n\nAnd thus Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from his mother al-ʿĀliyah bint Ayyaf"","" who said: I went out with Umm Muḥibbah to Makkah"","" and we entered upon ʿĀʾishah"","" and she mentioned it. [Ḍaʿīf. See the preceding]"""""
"10806","(10801) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī said: ʿĀʾishah — had this been authentically established from her — would have condemned the sale to the deferred payment (al-ʿaṭāʾ), because it involves an unspecified term, and this is something we do not permit. However, she condemned what she bought with cash when she had sold it on credit. And if some of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) differed on a matter, and one of them said one thing and another said the opposite, our principle is to take the position of the one whose view is supported by qiyās (analogical reasoning), and the one whose view is supported by qiyās is the view of Zayd ibn Arqam. The sum of this is that we do not establish such a report against ʿĀʾishah, especially since Zayd ibn Arqam would only sell what he considered ḥalāl and would only buy what he considered ḥalāl. And if a man sold or bought something that we consider ḥarām while he considers it ḥalāl, we would not claim that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, thereby nullifies any of his deeds. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mentioned by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 3/95]"
"10807","(10802) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī narrated to us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Layth narrated from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, that a man sold a saddle to another man and did not receive its price in cash. The owner of the saddle, who had bought it, wished to sell it, and the one who had sold it wished to take it back for less than the price at which he had sold it. Ibn ʿUmar was asked about this, and he saw no harm in it. Ibn ʿUmar said: \Perhaps if he sold it to someone else"","" he would sell it for that same price or less.\""\n\nAnd from Sufyān"","" Hishām narrated from Ibn Sīrīn"","" that a man sold a camel to another man and said: \""Take back your camel and thirty dirhams.\"" They asked Shurayḥ about it"","" and he saw no harm in it. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 14822]"""""
"10808","(10803) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \If people were to be granted the claims they assert"","" some people would claim the bloods and wealth of others. Rather"","" the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from Ibn Abī Mulaykah.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""When two men transact the sale of a slave"","" and the seller says"","" 'I sold it to you for one thousand"",""' and the buyer says"","" 'For five hundred"",""' each one is a claimant and the other is the one against whom the claim is made. The seller claims the excess of the price"","" and the buyer claims the commodity for less than the price. They both swear oaths"","" and the oath of the seller is taken first.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4277]"""""
"10809","(10804) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ and al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿIṣmah narrated to us, saying: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abī al-ʿUmays, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Qays ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ashʿath ibn Qays narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: Al-Ashʿath purchased slaves from the khums from ʿAbdullāh for twenty thousand. ʿAbdullāh sent to him for their price, and he said: \I only took them for ten thousand.\"" ʿAbdullāh said: \""Then choose a man to arbitrate between us.\"" Al-Ashʿath said: \""You are between me and myself.\"" ʿAbdullāh said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'When the two sellers differ and there is no proof between them"","" then it is as the owner of the commodity says"","" or they mutually cancel the transaction.'\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā"","" from ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ. This is a ḥasan"","" musnad isnād. It has also been narrated through various routes as mursal reports; when these are combined"","" the ḥadīth becomes strong by virtue of that. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 3511. Al-Ḥākim 2/52]"""""
"10810","(10805) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī al-Muḥāribī narrated to us in Kūfah, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us, Ibn ʿUyaynah and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿAwn ibn ʿAbdillāh, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the two sellers differ"","" the statement of the seller is taken"","" and the buyer has the option.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/466. Al-Tirmidhī 1270]"""""
"10811","(10806) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Ma'rūf al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarā'īnī informed us — Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'īd informed us — Ya'qūb ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān from Ibn 'Ajlān from 'Awn ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Utbah, that Ibn Mas'ūd and al-Ash'ath ibn Qays entered into a sale transaction and then disagreed over the price. Ibn Mas'ūd said: \Place between us and yourself whomever you wish as an arbitrator.\"" Al-Ash'ath replied to him: \""Then you are [the arbitrator] between me and yourself.\"" Ibn Mas'ūd said: \""Then I shall judge with what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He said: \""I heard him ﷺ saying: 'When the seller and the buyer disagree"","" the word is what the seller says"","" and the buyer has the option.'\""\n\n'Awn ibn 'Abd Allāh did not meet 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd"","" and he is a witness to what has preceded.\n\nAl-Shāfi'ī transmitted it from Ibn 'Uyaynah from Ibn 'Ajlān"","" in the narration of al-Za'farānī and al-Muzanī from him. Then al-Za'farānī said: 'Abd Allāh — meaning al-Shāfi'ī — said: \""This is a disconnected (munqaṭi') hadith; I do not know anyone who connects it to Ibn Mas'ūd"","" though it has come from another direction.\"" [Ḥasan due to corroborating chains; see before it.]"""""
"10812","(10807) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us — he said: I read to my father, he said: Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfi'ī informed me — Sa'īd ibn Sālim informed us — Ibn Jurayj informed us — Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah informed him — from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr — that he said: \I was present with Abū 'Ubaydah ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd when two men came to him who had sold merchandise"","" and one of them said: 'I bought it for such and such"",""' while the other said: 'I sold it for such and such.' Abū 'Ubaydah said: \""'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd was brought a similar case"","" and he said: 'I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a similar case was brought to him"","" and he ﷺ ordered the seller to be sworn an oath"","" and then the buyer was given the option: if he wished"","" he could take it"","" and if he wished"","" he could leave it.'\""\n\nAnother narrator added to it from 'Abd Allāh ibn Aḥmad — he said: 'Abd Allāh said: Aḥmad said: I was informed about Hishām ibn Yūsuf from Ibn Jurayj from Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Ubayd. Aḥmad said"","" and Ḥajjāj al-A'war also said: \""'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Ubaydah.\"" [Ḥasan due to corroborating chains. Transmitted by Aḥmad (1/466) and al-Nasā'ī (4649).]"""""
"10813","(10808) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed me — my father — and he mentioned it. The Shaykh said: [empty]."
"10814","(10809) Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym transmitted from Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from some of the sons of 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd, from Ibn Mas'ūd, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he ﷺ said: \When the two parties to a sale disagree and there is no witness between them"","" the seller is sworn an oath"","" and then the buyer has the option: if he wishes"","" he may take it"","" and if he wishes"","" he may leave it.\""\n\n'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us of it — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us — Aḥmad ibn 'Alī informed us — Ya'qūb ibn Ḥumayd informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym — and he mentioned it. [Ḥasan due to corroborating chains.]"""""
"10815","(10810) Sa'īd ibn Maslamah transmitted from Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah from 'Abd al-Malik from Ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd from his father, similarly.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan ibn 'Abdān informed us of it — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us — al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl informed us — al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā informed us — Sa'īd ibn Maslamah — and he mentioned it, except that he said: \The two parties to a sale"","" when there is no proof between them.\"" Another narrator transmitted it from Sa'īd — Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Ubaydah. [Ḥasan due to corroborating chains; see before it.]"""""
"10816","(10811) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣfahānī informed us of it — 'Alī ibn 'Umar informed us — Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Anṭākī informed us — Sa'īd ibn Maslamah — and he mentioned it. This hadith is also mursal [in another chain], since Abū 'Ubaydah did not meet his father. {J}"
"10817","(10812) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī informed us — they said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharzah informed us — Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us — Abū 'Umays and 'Abd al-Raḥmān, meaning al-Mas'ūdī, from al-Qāsim from 'Abd Allāh, that he said: \Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays purchased slaves from the khums for twenty thousand"","" and he sent to him regarding their prices to demand payment. He said: 'You sold me for ten thousand.' Either al-Ash'ath had forgotten or he considered the sale to be at a higher price. 'Abd Allāh said to him: 'I sold you for twenty thousand.' 'Abd Allāh said: 'Appoint a man between us.' He said: 'I choose you [to arbitrate] between me and yourself.' He said: 'I shall judge between us with a ruling I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" who said: \""When the two parties to a sale disagree and there is no proof between them"","" the word is what the owner of the merchandise says"","" or they mutually rescind the sale.\""' Al-Ash'ath said: 'Then I rescind the sale with you.' So he rescinded it.\""\n\nMa'n ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān"","" the brother of al-Qāsim"","" and Abān ibn Taghlib similarly transmitted it from al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd. And Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā transmitted it from al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān from his father. [Ḥasan due to corroborating chains. Transmitted by Aḥmad (1/466) and al-Ṭayālisī (399).]"""""
"10818","(10813) As Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī informed us — Hushaym —\n\nAnd Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us — they said: 'Alī ibn 'Umar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz informed us — 'Uthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us — Hushaym informed us — Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān from his father, he said: \'Abd Allāh ibn Mas'ūd sold to al-Ash'ath a slave from the slaves of the governorship"","" and they disagreed over the price. 'Abd Allāh said: 'I sold it to you for twenty thousand.' Al-Ash'ath said: 'I bought it from you for ten thousand.' 'Abd Allāh said: 'If you wish"","" I shall narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'Go ahead.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \""When the two parties to a sale disagree"","" the merchandise still exists in its [original] state"","" and there is no proof between them"","" the word is what the seller says"","" or they mutually rescind the sale.\""' Al-Ash'ath said: 'I see that the sale should be rescinded.'\""\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Ibn Abī Shaybah differs from Ibn Abī Laylā and the group in the transmission of this hadith"","" in that he said \""from his father\"" in the isnād"","" and in the matn he added: \""the merchandise still exists in its [original] state.\""\n\nIsmā'īl ibn 'Āsh transmitted it from Mūsā ibn 'Uqbah from Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"","" and he said in it: \""and the merchandise remains as it is in its [original] state.\""\n\nIsmā'īl"","" when he transmits from the people of the Ḥijāz"","" is not used as an authoritative proof. And Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"","" although he was great in jurisprudence"","" he is weak in narration due to his poor memory"","" his frequent errors in chains and texts"","" and his contradicting the reliable memorizers therein. May Allah forgive us and him.\n\nAl-Ḥasan ibn 'Umārah followed him in this narration from al-Qāsim"","" and he is matrūk (abandoned)"","" not used as an authoritative proof. [Ṣaḥīḥ due to corroborating chains. This chain is found in Abū Dāwūd (3512).]"""""
"10819","(10814) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Baghdādī informed us — 'Uthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bashīr informed us — Ismā'īl al-Qāḍī informed us — Ibn Abī Uways informed us — Ibn Abī al-Zinād from his father, from the jurists whose word is relied upon among the people of Madīnah, that they used to say: \When two men transact a sale and disagree over the price"","" and both are sworn an oath"","" then whichever of them refuses [to swear] the judgment is binding against him. If both swear an oath"","" the word is what the seller says"","" and the buyer is given the option: if he wishes"","" he may take it at that price"","" and if he wishes"","" he may leave it.\""\n\nAnd it has been transmitted to us from Shurayḥ that he said: \""If they both refuse to swear an oath"","" they mutually rescind the sale.\"" [Ḍa'īf.]"""""
"10820","(10815) The Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-'Umarī informed us — 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us — Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us — 'Alī ibn al-Ja'd informed us — Hushaym and Abū Mu'āwiyah informed us — from al-Shaybānī — from Muḥammad ibn 'Ubayd Allāh al-Thaqafī, that he purchased merchandise from a man and paid part of the price, with some remaining. He said: \Hand it over to me"",""\"" but the seller refused. The buyer went and hastened to pay the remainder of the price and handed it to him. He said: \""Go in and take your merchandise.\"" He found it dead. He said to him: \""Return my money to me"",""\"" but he refused. They took their dispute to Shurayḥ. Shurayḥ said: \""Return the man's money to him"","" and go back to your carcass and bury it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Transmitted by Ibn al-Ja'd (2481).]"""""
"10821","(10816) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us; Ibn ʬAwn informed us, from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)—and by Allah, I will not hear anyone after him say: \I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\""—say: \""Indeed"","" the ḥalāl is clear and indeed the ḥarām is clear"","" and between them are doubtful matters.\"" And sometimes he said: \""doubtful things.\"" And I shall strike for you a parable regarding that: Indeed"","" Allah has a protected pasture"","" and the protected pasture of Allah is that which He has forbidden. And whoever grazes around the protected pasture is likely to enter it. And sometimes he said: \""is likely to graze therein.\"" And indeed"","" whoever mingles with doubt is likely to become audacious. He (the narrator) said: And I do not know whether this is something in this hadith or something else. Al-Shaʿbī said: Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ibn ʬAwn"","" and Muslim narrated it as well. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1946]"""""
"10822","(10817) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Farwah al-Hamdānī narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī say: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr say upon the minbar: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \The ḥalāl is clear and the ḥarām is clear"","" and between them are doubtful matters. So whoever leaves that which is doubtful to him regarding sin"","" he has left that which is clear for him. And whoever is audacious regarding that which he doubts"","" he is likely to fall into the ḥarām. And indeed"","" for every king there is a protected pasture"","" and the protected pasture of Allah on earth is His disobediences.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Sufyān"","" and Muslim narrated it from another route from Abī Farwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10823","(10818) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us orally; Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I return to my family and find a date fallen upon my bed or in my house"","" so I pick it up to eat it"","" then I fear that it may be from the ṣadaqah"","" so I throw it away.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"","" and he said: And Hammām ibn Munabbih narrated it. And Muslim narrated it from Ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2300]"""""
"10824","(10819) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; Yazīd ibn Abī Maryam informed me, who said: I heard Abā al-Ḥawrāʾ say: I said to al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī: What do you remember from the Prophet (ﷺ)? He used to say: \Leave that which makes you doubt for that which does not make you doubt"","" for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 2518]"""""
"10825","(10820) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us; Abū ʿUqayl narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Dimashqī, from Rābiʿah ibn Yazīd and ʬAṭiyyah ibn Qays, from ʬAṭiyyah al-Saʿdī, who had been a companion (of the Prophet). He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The servant does not reach the rank of the muttaqīn until he leaves that which is harmless out of caution for that which is harmful.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Tirmidhī 245]"""""
"10826","(10821) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Abū Hilāl narrated to us; Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl narrated to us, from a man from his people, from the Bedouin, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was delivering a sermon, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me. And he mentioned the hadith. He said: And at the end of what I preserved, he said: \Indeed"","" you will not leave anything out of taqwā of Allah except that Allah will replace for you something better than it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10827","(10822) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Abī Ḥamzah ʿImrān ibn Abī ʬAṭāʾ. He said: I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: Indeed, my father is a trader of sheep, and he partners with the Jews and the Christians. He said: We do not partner with a Jew, nor a Christian, nor a Magian. I said: Why? He said: Because they deal in ribā, and ribā is not permissible. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 1998]"
"10828","(10823) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, who said: I found in my book from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Muzāḥim ibn Zufar, from Rābiʿ ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who heard a man ask Ibn ʿUmar: Indeed, I have a neighbor who consumes ribā—or he said: whose earnings are impure—and he sometimes invites me to his food. Should I accept? He said: Yes. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"10829","(10824) And Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Miʿsar narrated to us, from Jawwāb al-Taymī, from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd, who said: A man came to ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, and said: Indeed, I have a neighbor, and I know of nothing from him except what is impure or ḥarām, and he invites me. I feel reluctant to come to him, and I feel scrupulous about not coming to him. He said: Come to him, or accept his invitation, for his sin is upon him. The Shaykh said: Jawwāb al-Taymī is not strong (in narration). And this is when one does not know that what has been presented to him is ḥarām. But if he knows it is ḥarām, he should not eat it, just as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not eat from the sheep that was presented to him. [Ḥasan]"
"10830","(10825) In what Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us; Ibn Idrīs informed us; ʬĀṣim ibn Kulayb informed us, from his father, from a man from the Anṣār, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for a funeral, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the grave instructing the digger: \Widen it from the side of his feet; widen it from the side of his head.\"" When he returned"","" he was met by a woman's invitation. He came"","" and food was brought. He placed his hand (upon it)"","" and the people placed theirs"","" and they ate. Our fathers saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) chewing a morsel in his mouth"","" then he said: \""I find the meat of a sheep that was taken without the permission of its owners.\"" The woman sent (word): O Messenger of Allah"","" I sent to al-Baqīʿ to buy me a sheep"","" but none was found. So I sent to a neighbor of mine who had bought a sheep"","" asking him to send it to me at its price"","" but he was not found. So I sent to his wife"","" and she sent it to me. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Feed it to the captives.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 33322]"""""
"10831","(10826) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ and Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Zāhid narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Razīn al-Sulamī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī informed us, from Muṣʿab ibn Muḥammad al-Madanī, from Shuraḥbīl, the freedman of the Anṣār, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \Whoever purchases stolen property while knowing it is stolen has shared in its disgrace and its sin.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Muṣʿab ibn Muḥammad ibn Shuraḥbīl"","" from a shaykh of the people of Madīnah"","" who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Whoever buys stolen property while knowing it is stolen has shared in its disgrace and its sin.\""\n\nʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us of it: Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Sufyān narrated it. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Ḥākim 2/41]"""""
"10832","(10827) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī al-Kūfī narrated to us: Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid"","" even if it be a hundred conditions.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"","" from Wakīʿ"","" and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it through other routes from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2060]"""""
"10833","(10828) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ḥajjāj, meaning Ibn Minhāl, narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a loan combined with a sale, and two conditions in a single sale, and selling what is not in one's possession, and profiting from that for which one bears no liability. [Ḥasan. Previously referenced under number 10419]"
"10834","(10829) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd, that ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, purchased a slave woman from his wife Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, and she stipulated upon him that if he sold her, she would be hers for the price at which he sold her. So he sought a ruling on that from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, and ʿUmar said to him: \Do not approach her while there is a condition in her for someone else.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik 1275; ʿAbd al-Razzāq 14291]"""""
"10835","(10830) And with this chain of narration, Mālik narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar used to say: \A man shall not have intercourse with a slave woman unless it be a slave woman whom he may sell if he wishes"","" or gift if he wishes"","" or do with her as he wishes.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 1272]"""""
"10836","(10831) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \It is not permissible for a man to have intercourse with any private part except one which he may gift if he wishes"","" or sell if he wishes"","" or free if he wishes"","" wherein there is no condition.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10837","(10832) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd ibn Baḥr narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Abū al-Zubayr and Saʿīd ibn Mīnāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade al-muḥāqalah, al-muzābanah, al-mukhābarah, and al-muʿāwamah. And the other narrator said: and selling by years, and [he forbade] al-thuniyyā, and he granted concession in al-ʿarāyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1536]"
"10838","(10833) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rujāʾ al-Ḥanẓalī and Tamīm ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ḥisāb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, mentioning something similar to it, except that he said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived"","" he forbade.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ḥisāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding]"""""
"10839","(10834) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥurfī narrated to us in Baghdad, in the Mosque of al-Ḥarbiyyah: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Qurashī al-Kūfī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to me, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Ḍirār, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, gave a slave woman from the khums to the wife of ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, and she sold her to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd for one thousand dirhams, and she stipulated upon him her service. This reached ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and he said to him: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" you purchased your wife's slave woman and she stipulated her service upon you?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Do not buy her"","" for there is a dual share in her.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Khālid ibn Salamah"","" from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr"","" except that he said: ʿUmar said to ʿAbdullāh"","" may Allah be pleased with them both: \""Do not approach her"","" nor anyone else"","" while there is a condition in her.\""\n\nAnd al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it in a mursal form"","" and he said: ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""That in which there is a dual share for another does not belong to your wealth.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿĀʾishah that she disliked the stipulation of a condition regarding a slave who is sold or gifted with a condition. As for the hadith which… [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10840","(10835) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Shaʿbī say: Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to me: that he was traveling on a camel of his that had become exhausted, and he intended to set it free. He said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with me and struck it and supplicated for it, and it traveled a journey such as it had never traveled before. Then he said: \Sell it to me for a ūqiyyah.\"" I said: \""No.\"" Then he said: \""Sell it to me for a ūqiyyah.\"" He said: \""So I sold it"","" but I stipulated its carrying me to my family.\"" When I arrived"","" I brought him the camel"","" and he paid me its price in cash. Then I departed"","" and he sent someone after me: \""I did not haggle with you in order to take your camel. Take your camel and your dirhams; both are yours.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"","" and Muslim narrated it through two routes from Zakariyyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2569]"""""
"10841","Al-Bukhārī said: Shuʿbah narrated from Mughīrah from ʿĀmir al-Shaʿbī from Jābir: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the use of his camel's back to Madīnah.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ"","" who reported to me from Abū Aḥmad"","" who reported to us from Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"","" who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Sakan"","" who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Kathīr"","" Abū Ghassān al-ʿAnbarī"","" who narrated to us Shuʿbah"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10842","Al-Bukhārī said: Isḥāq narrated from Jarīr from Mughīrah: \I sold it on the condition that I would have the use of its back until I reached Madīnah.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"","" who reported to me from Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar"","" who narrated to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"","" who narrated to us Isḥāq"","" who informed us Jarīr"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10843","Al-Bukhārī said: ʿAṭāʾ narrated from Jābir: \Its back is yours until you reach Madīnah.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"","" who reported to me from Abū Bakr ibn Quraysh"","" who informed us al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān"","" who narrated to us Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"","" who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10844","Al-Bukhārī said: Ibn al-Munkadir narrated from Jābir: \And he stipulated the use of its back to Madīnah.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ"","" who reported to me from Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh"","" who narrated to us Tamīm ibn Muḥammad"","" who narrated to us Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Qawwās"","" who narrated to us al-Munkadir ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from his father from Jābir"","" and he mentioned it. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""""
"10845","Al-Bukhārī said: From Zayd ibn Aslam from Jābir: \Its back is yours until you return.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"","" who narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ"","" who narrated to us al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah"","" who narrated to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"","" who narrated to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father from Jābir"","" and he mentioned it."""""
"10846","Al-Bukhārī said: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir: \We grant you the use of its back to Madīnah.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"","" who informed us Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā"","" who narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad"","" who narrated to us al-Ḥajabī"","" who narrated to us Ḥammād ibn Zayd"","" who narrated to us Ayyūb from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"10847","Al-Bukhārī said: al-Aʿmash narrated from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Jābir: \Use it to reach your family.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"","" who narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb"","" who narrated to us al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī"","" who narrated to us Ibn Numayr from al-Aʿmash from Sālim from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"","" and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated the ḥadīth of ʿAṭāʾ and Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from Jābir with this wording"","" and he also narrated the ḥadīth of Abū al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 715.]"""""
"10848","As Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, who informed us al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who narrated to us Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us Abū al-Rabīʿ, who narrated to us Ḥammād ibn Zayd, who narrated to us Ayyūb from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ came to me when my camel had become exhausted. He struck it"","" and it leapt forward. After that"","" I used to hold back its bridle"","" but I could not control it. The Prophet ﷺ caught up with me and said: 'Sell it to me.' So I sold it to him for five awaq"","" and I said: 'On the condition that I have the use of its back to Madīnah.' He said: 'You have the use of its back to Madīnah.' When I arrived in Madīnah"","" I brought it to him"","" and he added a wiqiyyah for me"","" then he gifted it to me.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ.\n\nSome of these wordings indicate that this was a condition stipulated in the sale"","" and some of them indicate that it was from him ﷺ an act of generosity"","" benevolence"","" and kindness after the sale. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 715.]"""""
"10849","Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh narrated to us, who narrated to us Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn Naṣr, who both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, who said: I read to Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, who narrated to us Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh, who informed us Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī, who informed us Ibn Abī Uways and al-Qaʿnabī from Mālik ibn Anas from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar: \That ʿĀʾishah wished to purchase a slave-girl in order to set her free. Her owners said: 'We will sell you her on the condition that her walāʾ (clientage) belongs to us.' She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and he said: 'Do not let that prevent you"","" for walāʾ belongs only to the one who sets free.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. And in the narration of Abū Naṣr from Ibn ʿUmar from ʿĀʾishah: \""That she wished to purchase a slave-girl in order to set her free"",""\"" and the remainder is the same.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2579.]"""""
"10850","Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, who reported to me from Abū al-Walīd, who narrated to us Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib, who narrated to us Abū Kurayb, who narrated to us Abū Usāmah, who narrated to us Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, who said: My father informed me from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \Barīrah came to me and said: 'My family have contracted me for nine awaq over nine years"","" one wiqiyyah per year. Help me.' I said to her: 'If your family wish"","" I will pay them the entire sum in one payment and set you free"","" and the walāʾ will be mine.' She mentioned that to her family"","" but they refused unless the walāʾ would be theirs. She came to me and mentioned that"","" and I rebuked her. She said: 'No"","" by Allah"","" not then.' She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of it"","" and I informed him. He said: 'Buy her and set her free"","" and stipulate the walāʾ for them"","" for walāʾ belongs only to the one who sets free.' I did so. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon in the evening. He praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves"","" then he said: 'To proceed: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Any condition that is not in the Book of Allah is invalid"","" even if it be a hundred conditions. The Book of Allah is more deserving"","" and the conditions of Allah are more binding. What is the matter with men among you who say: \""Free so-and-so"","" and the walāʾ is mine\""? Walāʾ belongs only to the one who sets free.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl"","" and Muslim narrated it from Abū Kurayb from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2424.]"""""
"10851","(10846) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik and others informed us, on the authority of Abū Ḥāzim, who reported it from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of *al-gharar* (uncertainty/risk in transactions). This is a *mursal* hadith.\n\nWe have also narrated it in a connected (*mawṣūl*) form from the hadith of al-Aʿraj, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, and from the hadith of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik, 1345.]"
"10852","(10847) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, on the authority of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, on the authority of Abū al-Zinād, on the authority of al-Aʿraj, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us; Qabīṣah said: Sufyān informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abī Laylā, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of *al-gharar* (uncertainty/risk in transactions). The hadith of Abū Hurayrah was narrated by Muslim in *al-Ṣaḥīḥ* as previously mentioned.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1513.]"
"10853","(10848) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʔUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Tamtām informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sinān informed us; Jaḥḍam ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Yamāmī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn Zayd al-ʿAbdī, on the authority of Shahr ibn Ḥawshab, on the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of what is in the wombs of livestock until they give birth, and the sale of what is in their udders except by measure; the purchase of war spoils (*al-ghanāʾim*) until they are divided; the purchase of charitable alms (*al-ṣadaqāt*) until they are taken into possession; the purchase of a slave who has fled (*ābiq*); and the sale of the diver's dive (*ḍarbat al-ghāʾiṣ*).\n\nAlthough these prohibitions are narrated in this hadith through a chain that is not strong, they fall under the category of the sale of *al-gharar* (uncertainty/risk), which was prohibited in the authentic hadith established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 14375; Ibn Mājah, 2196.]"
"10854","(10849) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us in Marw; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Shaybān informed us, on the authority of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Mujāhid, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited every predatory animal with a fang, the killing of children, and the purchase of war spoils (*al-maghnam*) until they are divided. It was also narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, on the authority of Mujāhid, regarding war spoils (*al-maghānim*).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim, 2/47.]"
"10855","(10850) Abū ʿAbdullāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Baghdādī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb al-ʿAllāf informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād informed me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abī Najīḥ, on the authority of Mujāhid, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited, on the day of Khaybar, the sale of war spoils (*al-maghānim*) before they are divided.\n\nAl-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and others followed him in narrating from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith. It was also narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, on the authority of Mujāhid, regarding war spoils (*al-maghānim*).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim, 2/43.]"
"10856","(10851) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Musaddad informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, on the authority of ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the hiring of the stud male (*ʿasb al-faḥl*).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in *al-Ṣaḥīḥ* from Musaddad.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 2164.]"
"10857","(10852) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me, saying: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the sale of the camel's stud service (*ḍirāb al-jamal*), the sale of water, and the sale of land to be cultivated — regarding all of that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in *al-Ṣaḥīḥ* from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm."
"10858","(10853) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Kāmil al-Zāhid al-Bukhārī — who came to us as a pilgrim — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazdād al-Rāzī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Māhān al-Abulī informed us; ʿAbadah ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥumayd al-Ruʾāsī informed us, on the authority of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, on the authority of Anas ibn Mālik, that a man from Banū Kilāb asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the stud fee of the male (*ʿasb al-faḥl*), so he prohibited him from that. The man said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" we offer it as a gesture of generosity and honor.\"" So he granted permission in the case of generosity (*al-karāmah*).\n\nAbū ʿĪsā narrated it from ʿAbadah"","" and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿArʿarah followed him in narrating from Yaḥyā ibn Ādam.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"","" 4672.]"""""
"10859","(10854) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Zayyāt informed us; Yūsuf ibn Mūsā informed us; Wakīʿ and ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā both said: Sufyān informed us, on the authority of Hishām Abī Kulayb, on the authority of Ibn Abī Nuʿm al-Bajalī, on the authority of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: He (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the stud fee of the male (*ʿasb al-faḥl*). ʿUbaydullāh added: \and the *qafīz* (a specific measure) of the miller.\""\n\nIbn al-Mubārak narrated it from Sufyān as ʿUbaydullāh narrated it"","" and he said: \""He prohibited.\"" Likewise"","" Isḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī said it on the authority of Wakīʿ: \""He prohibited the stud fee of the male (*ʿasb al-faḥl*).\""\n\nʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿm"","" who said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited"",""\"" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Qawī. Narrated by al-Nasāʾī"","" 4674.]"""""
"10860","(10855) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥajjāj informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us, on the authority of Ayyūb —\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī informed us; Aḥmad informed us; Tamtām informed us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl Abū Salamah informed us; Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, on the authority of Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, on the authority of Ayyūb, on the authority of Yūsuf ibn Māhak, on the authority of Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited me from selling what I do not possess.\n\nIn the narration of Ḥammād: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \Do not sell what you do not possess.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"10861","(10856) Abū ʿAbdullāh — Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī — both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazyad informed us: my father narrated to me: al-Awzāʿī narrated to me: ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent ʿAttāb ibn Usayd to the people of Makkah, saying: \Convey to them from me four matters: Indeed"","" two conditions in a single sale are not permissible; nor a sale combined with a loan; nor the sale of that which one does not possess; nor profit from that for which one bears no liability.\""\n\n[Hasan. Previously cited under number 10828.]"""""
"10862","(10857) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan — both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Farrūkh narrated to us: from Ḥabīb ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the sale of fruit until its soundness becomes apparent"","" or the sale of wool upon the back"","" or ghee mixed within milk"","" or milk within the udder.\""\n\nOnly ʿUmar ibn Farrūkh narrated it in this raised (marfūʿ) form"","" and he is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). Wakīʿ narrated it from him in a mursal form"","" and others narrated it as a mawqūf (stopped) narration.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"","" 11935.]"""""
"10863","(10858) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to us: ʿAmmār ibn Khālid narrated to us: Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us: from Sufyān, from Abū Isḥāq, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \We do not purchase milk within the udders"","" nor wool upon the backs.\""\n\nThis is the preserved version"","" narrated as a mawqūf (stopped report). Likewise"","" Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated it from Abū Isḥāq"","" and likewise it was narrated from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Ibn ʿAbbās as a mawqūf report.\n\n[Weak. See the preceding narration.]"""""
"10864","(10859) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ibn Ḥanbal —\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Bālawayh narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: my father narrated to me, saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from al-Musayyib ibn Rāfiʿ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not purchase fish in water"","" for it is gharar (uncertainty/deception).\""\n\nThus it was narrated as a marfūʿ (raised) report"","" but there is an irsāl (disconnection) between al-Musayyib and Ibn Masʿūd. The correct version is what Hushaym narrated from Yazīd"","" as a mawqūf report attributed to ʿAbdullāh. And Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated it from Yazīd as a mawqūf report attributed to ʿAbdullāh"","" that he disliked the sale of fish in water.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Aḥmad"","" 1/288.]"""""
"10865","(10860) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from what he read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the sale of ḥabal al-ḥabalah, and it was a transaction practiced by the people of Jāhiliyyah, whereby one would purchase a camel until the she-camel gives birth, and then the one in her womb gives birth.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 2036.]"
"10866","(10861) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Yaʿqūb — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Barhawayh al-Nuʿmānī, in Nuʿmāniyyah, narrated to us: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us: Abū al-Naḍr Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to me: Nāfiʿ narrated to me —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: al-Layth informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he prohibited the sale of ḥabal al-ḥabalah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim, 1514.]"
"10867","(10862) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, dictating: Abū al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb — and the narration is from Abū al-Muthannā — narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh, who informed me: Nāfiʿ informed me, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The people of Jāhiliyyah used to sell a camel for ḥabal al-ḥabalah. And ḥabal al-ḥabalah is that the she-camel gives birth to what is in her womb"","" and then the one that was born becomes pregnant. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited them from that.\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us"","" mentioning something similar to it"","" except that he said: \""They used to sell the meat of the camel.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"","" and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"","" 3630.]"""""
"10868","(10863) Abū Aḥmad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl — narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he used to say: \There is no ribā (usury) in animals. However"","" three things were prohibited regarding animals: al-maḍāmīn"","" al-malāqiḥ"","" and ḥabal al-ḥabalah. Al-maḍāmīn refers to what is in the wombs of female camels"","" and al-malāqiḥ refers to what is upon the backs of male camels.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in the narration of al-Muzanī from al-Shāfiʿī"","" he said: \""Al-maḍāmīn is what is upon the backs of male camels"","" and al-malāqiḥ is what is in the wombs of female camels.\"" And Abū ʿUbayd explained it thus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1334.]"""""
"10869","(10864) As for what has been narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding his prohibition of al-majr, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū ʿUbayd narrated to me: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to me: from Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), to that effect.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Abū Zayd said: \Al-majr is that a camel or other animal is sold for what is in the womb of a she-camel.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this hadith in this wording was narrated solely by Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah. Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn said"","" and this was one of the reasons for his being declared weak.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Bazzār"","" as cited in Majmaʿ al-Zawāʾid"","" 3/16.]"""""
"10870","(10865) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkārī informed us: Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān narrated to us: from Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn, mentioning it.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), that he heard him prohibiting the sale of al-majr. Thus the hadith returns to the narration of Nāfiʿ, and it is as though Ibn Isḥāq conveyed it according to the meaning. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"10871","(10866) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us in his latter narrations — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik informed us from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban and from Abu al-Zinad from al-A'raj.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abd Allah informed us: Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed me: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Salam informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us, he said: I read to Malik from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-mulamasah and al-munabadhah.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways from Malik from both of them, and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya. He also recorded it additionally from the hadith of Hafs ibn 'Asim from Abu Hurayrah in this manner, and Muslim recorded it from the hadith of Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih. Bukhari 2039]"
"10872","(10867) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far informed me: 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us: Muhammad ibn Rafi' informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me from 'Ata' ibn Mina', that he heard him narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that he (the Prophet ﷺ) was prohibited from two types of sale: al-mulamasah and al-munabadhah. As for al-mulamasah, it is that each one of them touches the garment of his companion without careful inspection, and al-munabadhah is that each one of them throws his garment to the other, and neither of them looks at the garment of his companion.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi'. [Sahih. Muslim 1511]"
"10873","(10868) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: Ibn Milhan informed us: Yahya informed us: al-Layth informed me: Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab, he said: 'Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas informed me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two types of garments and two types of sale. He prohibited al-mulamasah and al-munabadhah in sale. Al-mulamasah is a man touching the garment of another with his hand, by night or by day, without turning it over except merely that. Al-munabadhah is that a man throws his garment to another man, and the other throws his garment, and that becomes their sale without inspection or mutual consent. And the two garments are al-shi'mal (al-shi'm al-samma') and al-samma' — that a man places his garment upon one of his shoulders, exposing one side of it, with no garment upon it; and the other garment is his wrapping himself with his garment, such that nothing covers his nakedness.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Bukayr. [Sahih. Muslim 1511]"
"10874","(10869) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq, and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yunus informed me from Ibn Shihab, from 'Amr ibn Sa'd, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-mulamasah and al-munabadhah in sale, then he explained this same explanation that has preceded in the hadith of al-Layth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Harmalah and others from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Muslim 1512]"
"10875","(10870) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us: Bishr ibn Musa informed us: al-Humaydi informed us: Sufyan informed us: al-Zuhri informed us: 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi informed us from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two types of sale and two types of garments. As for the two types of sale, they are al-mulamasah and al-munabadhah. And as for the two types of garments, they are al-shi'm al-samma' and a man wrapping himself in a single garment such that nothing covers his nakedness.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah from Sufyan. Al-Bukhari said: Ma'mar followed him in this. [Sahih. Bukhari 5927]"
"10876","(10871) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed me: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abu Dawud informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from 'Ata' ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet ﷺ with this hadith. He added: Al-shi'm al-samma' is that a man wraps himself in a single garment, placing the two ends of the garment upon his left shoulder and exposing his right side. And al-munabadhah is that he says, \When I throw this garment"","" the sale is binding.\"" And al-mulamasah is that he touches it with his hand and does not spread it out nor turn it over; when he touches it"","" the sale becomes binding. [Sahih. See the preceding]"""""
"10877","(10872) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri' and others informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd informed us from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Abu al-Zinad from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of gharar (deceptive uncertainty) and the sale of al-hasah (pebble-based sale). [Sahih. Muslim 1513]"
"10878","(10873) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Balwayh informed us: Musa ibn Harun informed me: Zuhayr ibn Harb informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us from 'Ubayd Allah, he said: Abu al-Zinad informed me, mentioning it in a similar narration. Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb."
"10879","(10874) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Malik ibn Anas informed me, he said: It reached me from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father from his grandfather, that he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of al-'urbān (earnest money deposit). Ibn Wahb said: Malik said to me, \And that"","" as we see — and Allah knows best — is that a man purchases a slave or a female slave"","" or hires a mount"","" and then says to the one from whom he purchased or hired"","" 'I will give you a dinar or a dirham or more than that"","" or less"","" on the condition that if I take the goods or ride what I hired from you"","" then what I gave you is part of the price of the goods or the hire of the beast; and if I abandon the sale or the hire"","" then what I gave you is void and without anything in return.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Malik ibn Anas narrated this hadith in al-Muwatta' in this manner"","" but he did not name the narrator from whom he transmitted it. [Da'if. Transmitted by Malik 1271]"""""
"10880","(10875) And Habib ibn Abi Habib narrated it from Malik, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amir al-Aslami informed me from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, and he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Faqih, meaning al-Masarisji, informed us: Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn al-Qasim al-Saddafi in Egypt informed us: al-Miqdam ibn Dawud ibn Talid al-Ru'ayni informed us: Habib ibn Abi Habib informed us, and he mentioned it. And it is said: \Nay"","" rather Malik took it from Ibn Lahi'ah.\"" [Da'if. See the preceding]"""""
"10881","(10876) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Qāsim ibn Mahdī narrated to us; Abū Muṣʿab narrated to us; Mālik narrated from al-Thiqah from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, and he mentioned it.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: Thus Abū Muṣʿab mentioned it, from Mālik, from al-Thiqah, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb. And it is said that Mālik heard this ḥadīth from Ibn Lahīʿah from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, and the ḥadīth from Ibn Lahīʿah from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is well-known. Abū Aḥmad said: Muḥammad ibn Ḥafṣ informed us; Qutaybah narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This ḥadīth has also been narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Dhubāb from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb."
"10882","(10877) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed him; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, i.e. Abū al-Shaykh, informed us; Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; Abū Mūsā al-Anṣārī narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Dhubāb narrated, and he mentioned it.\n\nʿĀṣim ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Ashjaʿī is subject to scrutiny [in his narration], and Ḥabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb is weak, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir and Ibn Lahīʿah are not used as proof. The original [source] of this ḥadīth is the mursal of Mālik."
"10883","(10878) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited two sales in one sale.\n\nAnd in the narration of Yaḥyā, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited two sales in one sale. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb said, meaning he says: \It is for you in cash for ten"","" and on credit for twenty.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar"","" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawārdī"","" and Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr. [Weak. See the preceding.]"""""
"10884","(10879) And Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever makes two sales in one sale"","" then for him is the lesser of the two"","" or it is ribā (usury).\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī informed me; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā narrated"","" and he mentioned it. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the book of Sunan from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nThe Shaykh"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: I read in the book of Abū Sulaymān"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" in the explanation of this ḥadīth"","" that it is as though this is a ruling regarding a specific thing"","" as though he advanced a dīnār in exchange for a qafīz of wheat for a month. When the time came and he demanded the wheat"","" he said to him: \""Sell me the qafīz that is owed to you for two qafīzes for two months.\"" This is a second sale that has entered upon the first sale"","" thus becoming two sales in one sale. They are both returned to the lesser of the two"","" which is the original. If they transact the second sale before annulling the first sale"","" then both are engaging in ribā. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 20461.]"""""
"10885","(10880) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Dāwūd ibn Qays and others from among the people of knowledge informed me that ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb informed them from his father from his grandfather ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a sale combined with a loan (bayʿ wa salaf), and two sales in a single transaction, and selling what is not in one's possession. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \It is forbidden (ḥarām) to profit from that for which one bears no liability.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad"","" 2/174.]"""""
"10886","(10881) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq said, and among others they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us by dictation; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq and ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, and the ḥadīth is from Ismāʿīl; ʿAbd Allāh, i.e. Ibn Maslamah, narrated from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated; he said: I read to Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited al-najsh (artificial bidding).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, 6862.]"
"10887","(10882) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Do not practise najsh upon one another.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"","" 831.]"""""
"10888","(10883) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it."
"10889","(10884) He said: And al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān and Mālik narrated from Abū al-Zinād from Ayyūb from Ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it."
"10890","(10885) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī said: \Al-najsh is that a man attends merchandise being sold and bids for it with something"","" while he does not intend to purchase it"","" so that the bidders follow his lead and offer more than they would have offered had they not heard his bidding. Whoever practises najsh is a sinner thereby"","" if he is aware of the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He said: \""The sale is valid; it is not invalidated by the sin of a man who practised najsh upon it.\"" He said: \""And selling by bidding was practised during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and the sale was valid. And it may be that the one who increased the bid did not intend to purchase.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"10891","(10886) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us, saying: Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us. Abū Muslim informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah, Abū Manṣūr al-Faqīh, and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān, and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us. Abū Muslim informed us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us. Akhḍar ibn ʿAjlān narrated to me. Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to me from Anas ibn Mālik that the Prophet ﷺ called for bids on a ḥils (a type of garment or cloth) and a qadḥ (a vessel). A man offered one dirham, and another offered two dirham, so he sold it to him.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 3/114; Abū Dāwūd 1641.]"
"10892","(10887) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us. Ibn Wahb informed me. ʿAmr ibn Mālik narrated to me from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar from Zayd ibn Aslam. He said: I heard a man called Shahr, who was a merchant, asking ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar about the sale by public auction (bayʿ al-muzāyadah). He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that any one of you should sell over the sale of his brother, unless it be the spoils of war (al-ghanāʾim) and inheritances (al-mawārīth).\n\nIbn Lahīʿah also narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar. And Yūnus ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated it from Ibn Wahb, and he said in the hadith: \And he was asking ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"","" so he sent him.\"" {Q}\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāḥ that he said: I found the people not considering any harm in the sale of the spoils of war (al-maghānim) by bidding up the price.\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn al-Jārūd 570; al-Dāraquṭnī 3/11.]"""""
"10893","(10888) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us. al-Rabīʿ informed us. al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Let not some of you sell over the sale of others.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Abū Zakariyyā: \""Let he not sell…\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ibn Abī Uways from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2032.]"""""
"10894","(10889) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān, and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let none of you sell over the sale of his brother"","" nor propose marriage over the proposal of his brother"","" except with his permission.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of ʿAlī ibn Mushhir and Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān from ʿUbayd Allāh.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1412.]"""""
"10895","(10890) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us. Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us. Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us. ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us. Sufyān narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Do not artificially inflate prices (lā tanājashū)"","" nor should a townsman sell on behalf of a bedouin"","" nor should a man sell over the sale of his brother"","" nor propose over the proposal of his brother"","" nor should a woman ask for the divorce of her sister so as to deprive her of what is in her vessel (i.e."","" to take what belongs to her).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2033.]"""""
"10896","(10891) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me. Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me. Abū Yaʿlā informed us. ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-Nāqid narrated to us. Sufyān narrated it with its chain, similar to it, except that he said: \It reached the Prophet ﷺ"",""\"" and he added: \""Nor should a man bid over the bid of his brother (wa-lā yasūmu al-rajulu ʿalā sawm akhīh).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others from Sufyān. And he also narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid with the addition.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous reference.]"""""
"10897","(10892) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us. al-Rabīʿ informed us. al-Shāfiʿī informed us. Mālik and Sufyān informed us from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let not some of you sell over the sale of others.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik.\n\nAnd al-Shāfiʿī"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" interpreted it as referring to the case where a man purchases merchandise from another"","" and they have not yet separated"","" when another person comes and offers him the same merchandise or something better for a lower price"","" thereby causing the sale of his companion to be annulled. The option (al-khiyār) exists before the separation"","" and this constitutes corruption (fasād)"","" and he has disobeyed Allah if he was aware of the hadith. And the sale in this case is binding.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2057.]"""""
"10898","(10893) al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said in the book al-Risālah: And it has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Let none of you bid over the bid of his brother (lā yasūmu aḥadukum ʿalā sawm akhīh).\"" If this is established—and I do not recall it as firmly established—then it is like the prohibition: \""Let none of you propose over the proposal of his brother"","" nor bid over his bid"",""\"" when the seller is pleased and gives permission for the sale before the actual sale takes place. If the sale is concluded"","" then it is binding. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold by public auction (bāʿa fī man yazīd)"","" and selling by public auction is a man bidding over the bid of his brother. However"","" the seller was not pleased with the first bid until he sought a higher offer.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us. Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us. al-Rabīʿ narrated to us from al-Shāfiʿī"","" and he mentioned it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The hadith of bidding (al-sawm) has been established through various chains.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"10899","(10894) Among them is what ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us. Tamtām narrated to us. ʿAffān narrated to us. Shuʿbah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us. Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us. Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us. My father narrated to us. Shuʿbah narrated to me from ʿAdī ibn Thābit from Abū Ḥāzim from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man should bid over the bid of his brother, and he mentioned the rest of the wordings that have preceded in the chapter on al-Taṣriyah (concealing defects in livestock).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿArʿarah from Shuʿbah. Then he said: Muʿādh and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad followed him (in narrating it) from Shuʿbah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2577.]"
"10900","(10895) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥām al-Muzakkī and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī said: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us. Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us. Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: Shuʿbah narrated to us from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nAnd Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ that he forbade a man to bid over the bid of his brother and to propose over the proposal of his brother.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith from Shuʿbah from both of them.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1515.]"
"10901","(10896) It was narrated by Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A Muslim shall not outbid another Muslim.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"","" Abū Bakr"","" narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr and others.\n\nSome of them narrated it from Shuʿbah"","" from al-Alāʾ: \""He forbade a man from outbidding his brother"",""\"" and some of them said: \""He forbade a man from selling against the sale of his brother.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1515]"""""
"10902","(10897) Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān al-Naysābūrī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid narrated to us; Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A man shall not propose marriage over the proposal of his brother"","" nor shall he outbid him. A woman shall not be married alongside her paternal aunt"","" nor alongside her maternal aunt. And a woman shall not ask for the divorce of her sister so as to take what is in her vessel; rather"","" let her marry"","" for she shall have only that which Allah has decreed for her.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn Ḥassān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10903","(10898) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us; Kathīr ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walīd ibn Rabāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \None of you shall outbid his brother"","" nor shall he propose over his proposal.\""\n\nAl-Awzāʿī narrated it with this wording from Abī Kathīr"","" from Abū Hurayrah. And it was also reported from him: \""A man shall not outbid his brother.\""\n\nThis is a single ḥadīth"","" and the narrators differed in its wording"","" because the one who narrated it with one of these three terms—al-bayʿ (sale)"","" al-sawm (outbidding)"","" and al-istiyām (bidding)—did not mention alongside it anything from the other two terms"","" except in a shādh (irregular) narration mentioned by Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"","" from Sufyān"","" from al-Zuhrī"","" from Saʿīd"","" from Abū Hurayrah"","" in which he mentioned the terms al-bayʿ and al-sawm together. Most narrators did not mention the term al-sawm from Ibn ʿUyaynah in it. It may be that the meaning of what Ibn al-Musayyab narrated from Abū Hurayrah is as others explained it from al-sawm and al-istiyām"","" or the narration of Ibn al-Musayyab may be given precedence over the narration of others"","" for he was the most precise and the most learned among them. Alongside him from the companions of Abū Hurayrah were ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj"","" Abū Saʿīd the freedman of ʿĀmir ibn Kurayz"","" and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb in some narrations from al-ʿAlāʾ from him. And his narration agrees with the narration of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the one before it.]"""""
"10904","(10899) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and others informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Lahīʿah and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shumāsah al-Mahrī, that he heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir upon the minbar saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The believer is the brother of the believer. It is not permissible for a believer to sell against the sale of his brother until he withdraws"","" nor to propose over his proposal until he withdraws.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1414]"""""
"10905","(10900) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us by dictation; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not engage in najash (artificial bidding)"","" nor shall a townsman sell on behalf of a bedouin"","" nor shall a man sell against the sale of his brother"","" nor shall he propose over the proposal of his brother.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr"","" both from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2033]"""""
"10906","(10901) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not intercept the caravans for trade"","" nor shall some of you sell against the sale of others"","" nor engage in najash (artificial bidding)"","" nor shall a townsman sell on behalf of a bedouin. And do not tie up the udders of camels and sheep. Whoever buys them after that has the choice of two options after milking them: if he is pleased with them"","" he keeps them"","" and if he is displeased with them"","" he returns them along with a ṣāʿ of dates.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. And they both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Abī Ḥāzim"","" from Abū Hurayrah: \""He forbade a Muhājir from selling on behalf of a bedouin.\"" And that has passed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2043]"""""
"10907","(10902) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin.\"" He said: I said: \""What is meant by 'a townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin'?\"" He said: \""Do not be his broker (simsār).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from two other routes from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2055]"""""
"10908","(10903) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn informed us, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, that Anas ibn Mālik said: \We were forbidden that a townsman should sell on behalf of a bedouin.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2053]"""""
"10909","(10904) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abān al-Balkhī narrated to us; Abū Hammām al-Ahwāzī Muḥammad ibn al-Zibriqān narrated to us, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin"","" even if he be his brother or his father.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1523]"""""
"10910","(10905) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us by dictation; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Khaythamah informed us; Abū al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin. Leave the people"","" for some of them are provided for by means of others.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1522]"""""
"10911","(10906) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin.\""\n\nThis hadith"","" with this chain of narration"","" is counted among the unique narrations of al-Shāfiʿī from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what has preceded.]"""""
"10912","(10907) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us from the original of his book: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See what has preceded.]"""""
"10913","(10908) Abū Bakr al-Ardashtānī narrated to us: al-Qāḍī Abū Naṣr Shuʿayb ibn ʿAlī al-Hamadhānī narrated to us therein: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Naṣr al-Rāzī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated it from his father from Ibn ʿUmar. And Mālik ibn Anas has musnads that he did not include in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ, which the eminent among his companions narrated from him outside of al-Muwaṭṭaʾ. And Allah knows best."
"10914","(10909) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The rights of a Muslim over another Muslim are six.\"" It was asked: \""What are they"","" O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""When you meet him"","" greet him with salām; when he invites you"","" accept his invitation; when he seeks your counsel"","" counsel him; when he sneezes and praises Allah"","" say yarḥamuk Allāh to him; when he falls ill"","" visit him; and when he dies"","" follow his funeral procession.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2162]"""""
"10915","(10910) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Hārūn narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlqamah al-Marwazī narrated to us: Abū Ḥamzah al-Sukkari narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Leave the people alone; Allah provides some of them from others. And when one of you seeks counsel from his brother"","" let him counsel him.\""\n\nAnd something to that effect was narrated from Ḥakīm ibn Abī Yazīd from his father from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and it was also said from him from his father from one who heard the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10916","(10911) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāhid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from Sālim al-Makkī that a bedouin narrated to him, saying: \I came to Madīnah with a milking she-camel of mine during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and I stayed with Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUbayd Allāh. I said: 'I have no knowledge of the people of this market; would you sell on my behalf?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that a townsman should sell on behalf of a bedouin. But go to the market"","" and whoever wishes to buy from you"","" consult me so that I may command you or forbid you.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""""
"10917","(10912) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from al-Taymī from Abū ʿUthmān from ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, from the Prophet (ﷺ): \He forbade intercepting the sales caravans.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shayyah"","" and al-Bukhārī also narrated it as has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1518]"""""
"10918","(10913) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik and others informed me from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade intercepting trade caravans until they reach the markets.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik and others from Nāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2057]"
"10919","(10914) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq, Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl, and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar — whose wording it is — said: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade intercepting the caravans and that a townsman should sell on behalf of a bedouin.\"" He said: \""I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: 'What is the meaning of his words: \""A townsman shall not sell on behalf of a bedouin\""?' He said: 'He should not act as a broker for him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad and others"","" and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated previously.]"""""
"10920","(10915) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated, reciting to Mālik, from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not intercept the trade caravans for the purpose of buying.\"" And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith.\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Mālik"","" as has preceded. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2043]"""""
"10921","(10916) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥakīm narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Abū al-Zinād narrated from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not intercept the trading caravans.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: And I have heard in this hadith: \""So whoever intercepts them"","" then the owner of the goods has the option (of annulment) after he arrives at the market.\"" And we take this (ruling)"","" if it is established. And in this there is evidence that when a man intercepts the goods and purchases them"","" the sale is valid; however"","" the owner of the goods has the option after the goods arrive at the market. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its isnād is good.]"""""
"10922","(10917) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Awzāʿī narrated from Ibn Sīrīn.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Zuhayr al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not intercept the trading caravans. So whoever intercepts them and purchases anything from them"","" then the owner has the option when he comes to the market.\"" And in the narration of al-Awzāʿī: \""When he comes to the market"","" he has the option.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1519]"""""
"10923","(10918) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us, Hishām ibn Sulaymān narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Hishām al-Qurdūsī informed me, mentioning it (the hadith), except that he said: \When his master comes to the market"","" he has the option.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""""
"10924","(10919) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us, al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us, Abū Tawbah narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah: that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited intercepting the trading caravans. He said: \So if an interceptor intercepts them"","" then the owner of the goods has the option regarding them when they arrive at the market.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Sunan Abī Dāwūd 3437]"""""
"10925","(10920) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ Abū Tawbah narrated it with its like, except that he added: \So if an intercepting buyer intercepts them and purchases them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""""
"10926","(10921) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ narrated to me, my uncle Juwayriyah ibn Asmāʾ narrated from Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to him that they used to buy food from the trading caravans during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he forbade them from selling it in the place where they had purchased it until they moved it to the food market.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, from Juwayriyah, and he said in its text: \We used to intercept the trading caravans and buy food from them"","" and the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade us from selling it until we brought it to the food market.\""\n\nAnd in this there is evidence for the validity of purchasing from the trading caravans; they were only prohibited from selling it after taking possession of it until they moved it to the food market"","" so that they would not inflate prices upon those who might estimate that it was cheaper in that place. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2048]"""""
"10927","(10922) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited a sale combined with a loan (bayʿ wa salaf), and he prohibited two sales in one transaction (bayʿatayn fī bayʿah), and he prohibited profit from that for which one has not assumed liability. [Ḥasan. Previously cited under number 10880]"
"10928","(10923) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zaydān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd, meaning al-Muḥāribī, narrated to us, Mūsā ibn ʿUmayr narrated from Makhūl, from Abī Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever trusts a believer and then defrauds him"","" his fraud is ribā (usury).\""\n\nMūsā ibn ʿUmayr al-Qurashī — the scholars have spoken regarding him. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī said: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: \""Most of what Mūsā ibn ʿUmayr narrates is such that the trustworthy narrators do not corroborate him upon it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And its meaning has been narrated from Yaʿīsh ibn Hishām al-Qarqasānī from Mālik"","" and there is disagreement regarding its isnād"","" and it is weaker than this. [Bāṭil. Ibn ʿAdī cited it 6716]"""""
"10929","(10924) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to me, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Nasawī al-Faqīh in Dāmighān, from the original of his book, narrated to us, al-Khalīl ibn Aḥmad al-Nasawī dictated it to us by dictation, Khidāsh ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Yaʿīsh ibn Hishām narrated from Mālik, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The fraud of one who is trusted (al-mustarsil) is ribā (usury).\"" [Bāṭil]"""""
"10930","(10925) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Ẓufar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Daqqāq narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Qurashī narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Manbijī narrated to us, Yaʿīsh ibn Hishām al-Qarqasānī narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Anas ibn Mālik, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The fraud of one who is trusted (al-mustarsil) is ribā (usury).\""\n\nAnd from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"","" from his father"","" from ʿAlī"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" who said: \""The fraud of one who is trusted (al-mustarsil) is ribā (usury).\"" [Bāṭil]"""""
"10931","(10926) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us: Burayd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Burdah narrated to us: Abū Burdah narrated to me, saying: I came to al-Madīnah and met ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām. He said: \Come with me to my house"","" so that I may give you to drink from a cup in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drank"","" and you may pray in a mosque in which he prayed.\"" So I went with him"","" and he gave me sawīq to drink and dates to eat"","" and I prayed in his mosque. Then he said to me: \""You are in a land in which ribā is prevalent. Among the forms of ribā is that one of you lends a loan for a fixed term; when the term expires"","" the borrower comes to repay it along with a basket containing a gift. So beware of that basket and what is in it.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb"","" from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6910]"""""
"10932","(10927) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, who said: \I came to al-Madīnah and met ʿAbdullāh ibn Salām. He said to me: 'Will you not come to the house so that I may feed you sawīq and dates?' So we went"","" and he fed us sawīq and dates. Then he said: 'You are in a land in which ribā is prevalent. If a man owes you a debt and then gifts you a bundle of fodder"","" or barley"","" or a bundle of chopped straw"","" do not accept it"","" for that is from ribā.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"","" from Shuʿbah. And it has been narrated to us from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh"","" from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb"","" a story similar to this one regarding the loan and the gift. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3603]"""""
"10933","(10928) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Tamtām Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā al-Azraq narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, who narrated to me: Kulthūm ibn al-Aqmar narrated to me, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: \I said to Ubayy ibn Kaʿb: 'O Abā al-Mundhir"","" I wish to go out for jihād"","" so I will go to al-ʿIrāq and take a loan.' He said: 'You are in a land in which ribā is widespread. If you lend a man a loan and he then gifts you something"","" take your loan and return his gift to him.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 14652]"""""
"10934","(10929) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najīd narrated to us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥammād narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, that Ubayy ibn Kaʿb sent a gift to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb from the produce of his land, and he returned it. Ubayy said: \Why did you return my gift"","" when you know that I have the finest produce among the people of al-Madīnah? Accept from me"","" since you return my gift to me.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) had previously loaned him ten thousand dirhams. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10935","(10930) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: My father narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said regarding a man who was owed twenty dirhams by another man, who began to send him gifts. Every time the debtor sent him a gift, he sold it, until the total value of the gifts reached thirteen dirhams. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Do not take from him except seven dirhams.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10936","(10931) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us: My father narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿAmmār al-Duhnī, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, who said: \We had a neighbour who was a fishmonger (sammāk)"","" and he owed a man fifty dirhams. He used to send him fish as a gift. He came to Ibn ʿAbbās and asked him about that. Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'Offset against your debt the value of what he has gifted you.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10937","(10932) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Yūnus and Khālid narrated to us, from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAbdullāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — that he was asked about a man who borrowed some dirhams from another man, and then the borrower made use of the lender's mount. ʿAbdullāh said: \Whatever benefit he derived from its back is ribā.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: \""He means that it is a loan which brought a benefit (i.e."","" it constitutes ribā).\"" Shaykh Aḥmad said: \""This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAwn"","" from Ibn Sīrīn"","" that a man lent another man some dirhams and stipulated that he could use the back of his horse. This was mentioned to Ibn Masʿūd"","" and he said: \""Whatever benefit he derived from its back is ribā.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10938","(10933) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Munqidh narrated to me: Idrīs ibn Yaḥyā narrated to me, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAyyāsh, who said: Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated to me, from Abī Marzūq al-Tujībī, from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that he said: \Every loan that brings a benefit is a form of ribā.\"" Mawqūf (stopped at the Companion). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10939","(10934) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from ʿUtbah ibn Ḥumayd al-Ḍabbī, from Yazīd ibn Abī Yaḥyā, who said: \I asked Anas ibn Mālik"","" saying: 'O Abā Ḥamzah"","" a man among us lends his brother money"","" and then the borrower gifts him something.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When one of you is granted a loan and the borrower then gifts him a platter"","" let him not accept it"","" or if he loads it onto a riding animal for him"","" let him not ride it"","" unless there was such a practice between them before that.'\""' This is what he said. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2432]"""""
"10940","(10935) Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated it from Ismāʿīl, from ʿUtbah, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, who said: \I asked Anas ibn Mālik.\"" Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated it to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Maʿmarī narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it in similar terms.\n\nAl-Maʿmarī said: Hishām said regarding this ḥadīth: \""It is Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Hunāʾī"","" and I consider this to be an error. This is the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yazīd al-Hunāʾī"","" from Anas.\"" And Shuʿbah and Muḥammad ibn Dīnār narrated it and stopped it (as a mawqūf report)."""""
"10941","(10936) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that he heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar say: \Whoever gives a loan (salaf) shall not stipulate anything except its repayment.\"" Some of the weak narrators raised it (as a marfūʿ hadith) from Nāfiʿ"","" but it is nothing. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10942","(10937) Abū Aḥmad informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Muḥammad narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated that it reached him: A man came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and said, \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" I gave a man a loan and stipulated that he must repay me with something better than what I lent him.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said"","" \""That is ribā (usury).\"" The man said"","" \""Then what do you command me"","" O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" ʿAbdullāh said"","" \""A loan (salaf) is of three types: a loan by which you seek the Countenance of Allah — then you shall have the Countenance of Allah; a loan by which you seek the favour of your companion — then you shall have the favour of your companion; and a loan you give so that you may take something impure in exchange for something pure — and that is ribā.\"" The man said"","" \""Then what do you command me"","" O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān?\"" He said"","" \""I think you should tear up the document. If he gives you the equivalent of what you lent him"","" accept it. If he gives you less than what you lent him and you accept it"","" you shall be rewarded. And if he gives you more than what you lent him"","" his soul being pleased with that"","" then that is gratitude he has shown you"","" and you shall have the reward for the respite you granted him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1362]"""""
"10943","(10938) Al-Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; Ibn Firās informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Daybulī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, who said: A man said to Ibn Masʿūd, \I took a loan from a man on the condition that I lend him the back of my horse to ride.\"" ʿAbdullāh said"","" \""Whatever benefit he derives from it is ribā.\"" (The chain from Ibn Sīrīn to ʿAbdullāh is munqaṭiʿ.) [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1362]"""""
"10944","(10939) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed us; Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us; I heard Abū Salamah narrate from Abū Hurayrah: A man came to demand repayment from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and spoke harshly to him, so his Companions were about to harm him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Leave him"","" for the one who has a right has a right to speak. Buy a camel for him and give it to him.\"" They said"","" \""We find for him a camel of a better age than his.\"" He said"","" \""Buy it and give it to him"","" for the best of you is the one who is best in repayment.\"" Narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"","" and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī in various places"","" Muslim 1601]"""""
"10945","(10940) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us orally; Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Būshanjī Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Farrāʾ Maḥbūb ibn Mūsā informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Ḥamzah al-Zayyāt, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and asked him (for something), so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked on his behalf for half a wasq (of provisions) and gave it to him. Then the man came to demand repayment, so he gave him a full wasq and said, \Half of it is repayment of your debt"","" and half is a gift from me.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10946","(10941) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ informed me; Saʿīd ibn Hānīʾ narrated from al-ʿIrbāḍ ibn Sāriyah al-Sulamī, who said: I sold a young camel to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and I came to demand its price. I said, \O Messenger of Allah"","" give me the price of my young camel.\"" He said"","" \""Yes"","" I shall not give you anything except a Bactrian (bukhtiyyah) camel.\"" Then he repaid me and did so excellently. Then a Bedouin came and said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" give me my young camel.\"" So he repaid him with an aged camel. The Bedouin said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this is better than my young camel.\"" He said"","" \""It is yours. The best of people are those who are best in repayment.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"","" 2/35]"""""
"10947","(10942) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; al-Bāghandī narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā and Thābit — meaning Muḥammad ibn al-Zāhid — and ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā said: Miṣʿar ibn Kidām narrated to us; Muḥārib ibn Dithār narrated; Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) in the mosque at mid-morning and he said to me, \Stand and pray.\"" I owed him a debt"","" so he repaid me and gave me more. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Khallād ibn Yaḥyā and Thābit al-Zāhid. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 423]"""""
"10948","(10943) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated; al-Aʿmash narrated; Sālim — meaning Ibn Abī al-Jaʿd — narrated; Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while I with me was a sick camel, and I was driving it at the rear of the people. He said, \What is the matter with this camel of yours?\"" I said"","" \""It is sick"","" or lame"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He took hold of its tail"","" struck it"","" and said"","" \""Ride it.\"" I saw myself at the front of the people"","" and I was holding it back. When we drew near"","" I wanted to hasten to my family"","" but he said"","" \""Do not come to your family at night.\"" Then he said"","" \""Have you married?\"" I said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""A virgin or a previously married woman?\"" I said"","" \""A previously married woman.\"" He said"","" \""Why not a virgin"","" so that she may play with you and you with her?\"" I said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" my father ʿAbdullāh left young girls"","" and I disliked bringing one like them to join them"","" so I intended to marry a woman of mature understanding.\"" He neither said \""You did wrong\"" nor \""You did well.\"" Then he said to me"","" \""Sell me this camel of yours.\"" I said"","" \""It is yours"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said"","" \""Sell it to me.\"" I said"","" \""It is yours"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" When he insisted"","" I said"","" \""A man owes me a gold ūqiyyah"","" so take it in exchange for that.\"" He said"","" \""Yes"","" travel on it to your family.\"" He sent for Bilāl and said"","" \""Give him a gold ūqiyyah and give him extra.\"" Bilāl gave me an ūqiyyah and added a qīrāṭ of gold. I said"","" \""This qīrāṭ that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me extra shall never leave me.\"" I placed it in a purse"","" and it remained with me until the people of Shām took it on the Day of Ḥarrah. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash — al-Bukhārī by allusion and Muslim by direct narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 715]"""""
"10949","(10944) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakkī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Qays, from Mujāhid, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar borrowed dirhams from a man and then repaid him with dirhams that were better than them. The man said, \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" these are better than the dirhams I lent you.\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said"","" \""I know that"","" but my soul was pleased to do so.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"","" 1360]"""""
"10950","(10945) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated from Abū ʿUmays, from Ibn Juʿdubah, from ʿUbayd — who is Ibn al-Sabbāq — from Zaynab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me fifty wasqs of dates from Khaybar and twenty wasqs of barley. She said: Then ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī came to me and said, \Would you like me to give you your wealth from Khaybar here in Madīnah"","" so that I may measure it out for you according to the measure of Khaybar?\"" She said"","" \""Not until I ask about that.\"" She mentioned that to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" and he said"","" \""Do not do that"","" for how can you guarantee what is between the two?\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Gharazah. In the narration of Ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"","" she said: \""Then ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAdī came to me during the caliphate of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" We have narrated from Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he disliked that. It has also been narrated in a marfūʿ ḥadīth"","" but it is ḍaʿīf"","" so I have not mentioned it due to its weakness. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"","" 21028]"""""
"10951","(10946) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Hushaym informed us; Khālid informed us from Ibn Sīrīn: that he did not see any harm in *safātij* (bills of exchange) when conducted on the basis of recognized good practice. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"10952","(10947) He said: and Hushaym narrated to us; al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh informed us; from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ: that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr used to take dirhams from people in Makkah and then write to Muṣʿab ibn al-Zubayr in ʿIrāq, and they would receive payment from him. Ibn ʿAbbās was asked about that, and he saw no harm in it. It was said to him: \What if they receive something better than their dirhams?\"" He said: \""There is no harm"","" so long as they receive the equivalent weight of their dirhams.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated regarding this from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). If this is authentically established from him and from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"","" then what they intended — and Allah knows best — is that this is when it is done without a prior stipulation. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10953","(10948) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād and Muḥammad ibn al-Khaṭṭāb ibn ʿUmar both said: Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Sufyān narrated to us; from Salamah ibn Kuhayl; from Abū Salamah; from Abū Hurayrah who said: A man was owed a camel of a certain age by the Prophet (ﷺ). He came to demand it, so he (ﷺ) said: \Give it to him.\"" They searched but could not find one of that age except one of a higher age. He (ﷺ) said: \""Give it to him.\"" The man said: \""You have given me my due in full — may Allah give you your due in full.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The best among you are those who are most excellent in repayment of debts.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2182]"""""
"10954","(10949) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us; Abū Kurayb informed us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; from ʿAlī ibn Ṣāliḥ; from Salamah ibn Kuhayl; from Abū Salamah; from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) borrowed a camel of a certain age and gave him one of a greater age. He (ﷺ) said: \The best among you are those most excellent in repayment of debts.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding.]"""""
"10955","(10950) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs ibn Salamah al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Zayd, who is Ibn Aslam, informed me; from ʿAṭāʾ; from Abū Rāfiʿ: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) borrowed a young camel from a man. Then some camels came to the Prophet (ﷺ). Abū Rāfiʿ said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded me to repay the man his young camel. I searched among the camels but found nothing except a four-year-old male camel. I mentioned that to the Prophet (ﷺ), and he said: \Give it to him"","" for the best of Allah's servants are those most excellent in repayment.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1600]"""""
"10956","(10951) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Hārūn ibn Sulaymān informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; from Sufyān; from Manṣūr; from Sālim; from Abū al-Dardāʾ who said: That I lend out two dinars twice is more beloved to me than that I give them in charity, because I lend them and they return to me, and then I give them in charity, so I receive the reward of both.\n\nIt has been narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: \That I lend twice is more beloved to me than that I give it once.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated regarding this from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"","" and it has been narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd that he said: \""That I lend twice is more beloved to me than that I give in charity once.\"" And it has been narrated from him as a *marfūʿ* (elevated) narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"10957","(10952) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Jurjānī in Ḥalab informed us; Hāshim ibn al-Qāsim informed us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us; from Sulaym ibn Yasīr; from Qays ibn Rūmī; from Sulaymān ibn Udhunān; from ʿAlqamah; from ʿAbdullāh who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever lends silver twice is as if he gave it in charity once.\""\n\nThis is how Sulaym ibn Yasīr al-Nakhaʿī"","" Abū al-Ṣabāḥ al-Kūfī"","" narrated it. Al-Bukhārī said: \""He is not strong (in narration).\""\n\nAnd al-Ḥakam"","" Abū Isḥāq"","" Isrāʾīl"","" and others narrated it from Sulaym ibn Udhunān"","" from ʿAlqamah"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd"","" as his own statement. And Dalham ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated it from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Kindī"","" from ʿAlqamah"","" from ʿAbdullāh.\n\nAnd Manṣūr narrated it from Ibrāhīm"","" from ʿAlqamah: \""It used to be said thus.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another chain from Ibn Masʿūd as a *marfūʿ* narration"","" but its elevation (*rafʿ*) is weak. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2430]"""""
"10958","(10953) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad, meaning Ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to me; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to me — and I was the one who asked him; Muʿtamir narrated to me. He said: I recited it to Fuḍayl ibn Miṣrābah, from Abū Ḥarīz, that Ibrāhīm narrated to him: that al-Aswad ibn Yazīd used to borrow from a mawlā of the Nakhaʿ who was a merchant. When his stipend came, he would repay him. His stipend came, and al-Aswad said to him: \If you wish"","" you may defer it from us"","" for there are other obligations upon us in this stipend.\"" The merchant said: \""I will not do so.\"" So al-Aswad paid him five hundred dirhams in cash. When the merchant received them"","" the merchant said to him: \""Here"","" take them.\"" Al-Aswad said: \""I asked you for this and you refused.\"" The merchant said: \""I heard you narrate to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: 'Whoever lends something twice"","" it is for him the equivalent of the reward of one of them"","" had he given it in charity.'\""\n\nThis is narrated uniquely by ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥusayn"","" Abū Ḥarīz"","" the judge of Sijistān"","" and he is not strong (in narration). [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān 1155]"""""
"10959","(10954) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Tamtām informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿĀʾishah narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us; from Thābit; from Anas, who elevated it (*rafaʿahu*), saying: \Lending a thing is better than giving it in charity.\""\n\nImām Aḥmad said: \""I found it in the Musnad as a *marfūʿ* narration"","" so I was hesitant about it and said: 'He elevated it (*rafaʿahu*).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"10960","(10955) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl informed me; Thawr ibn Zayd narrated to me; from Abū al-Ghayth; from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes the wealth of people intending to repay it"","" Allah will repay it on his behalf; and whoever takes it intending to destroy it"","" Allah will destroy him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Uwaysī"","" from Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2257]"""""
"10961","(10956) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl al-Dabbās informed me in Makkah: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Zayd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Shabīb narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me, saying: Abū Hurayrah said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If I had gold equal to Mount Uḥud"","" it would not please me that three nights should pass while I still possess any of it"","" except something I set aside for the repayment of a debt.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Shabīb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2259]"""""
"10962","(10957) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Jarīr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us: Hishām narrated to us: Jarīr narrated, from Manṣūr, from Ziyād ibn ʿAmr ibn Hind, from ʿImrān ibn Ḥudhayfah, from Maymūnah: that she used to incur debts. It was said to her: \You take on debts and accumulate them"","" yet you are not in hardship.\"" She said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever incurs a debt while intending to repay it"","" Allah will be with him"","" helping him in that.' So I seek that help.\""\n\nIsḥāq al-Ḥanẓalī narrated something similar from Jarīr"","" and Zāʾidah narrated something similar from Manṣūr. [Ḥasan for something else. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2408]"""""
"10963","(10958) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb al-Ḍabbī and Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāfiẓ both said: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mujabbir narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that she used to incur debts. It was said to her: \What is the matter with you and debt"","" when you have nothing with which to repay it?\"" She said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'There is no servant who has the intention to repay his debt except that he will have from Allah a helper.' So I seek that help.\"" It has also been narrated through another chain from ʿĀʾishah. [Ḥasan for something else. Narrated by al-Ḥākim 2612]"""""
"10964","(10959) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us. He said: I heard Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī say: ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to take on debts. It was said to her: \What is the matter with you and debt?\"" She said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'There is no servant who has the intention to repay his debt except that he will have from Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" a helper.' So I seek that help.\""\n\nThe wording is that of al-Ḥajjāj's ḥadīth. It was also said: from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar. [Ḥasan for something else. Narrated by Aḥmad 6/72]"""""
"10965","(10960) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Mundhir, Abū Bakr al-Qazzāz, narrated to us: Ibn Abī Fudayk narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Sufyān al-Aslamī narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \Indeed"","" Allah"","" the Blessed and Most High"","" is with the debtor until he repays his debt"","" so long as it is not for something that Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" disapproves of.\"" He used to say to one of his freedmen: \""Take a debt for me"","" for I dislike that a night should pass with Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" not being with me"","" because of what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī and others followed him"","" narrating from Ibn Abī Fudayk. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2409]"""""
"10966","(10961) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl and Hishām ibn ʿAmmār both said: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm al-Makhzūmī, from his father, from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Rabīʿah: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) borrowed from him a sum of over ten thousand. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned on the day of Ḥunayn, wealth came to him. He said: \Call Ibn Abī Rabīʿah for me.\"" He said to him: \""Take what you lent. May Allah bless you in your wealth and your offspring. Indeed"","" the repayment of a loan is praise and fulfilment.\"" Hishām said: \""Reward and fulfilment.\"" And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Whoever deceives us is not of us.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2424]"""""
"10967","(10962) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" if I am killed in the cause of Allah"","" will Allah forgive my sins?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""If you are killed in the cause of Allah"","" being patient"","" seeking reward"","" advancing and not retreating"","" Allah will forgive your sins.\"" When he sat down"","" he called him and said: \""What did you say?\"" He repeated it to him. He said: \""Except for debt"","" for Jibrīl"","" peace be upon him"","" has just informed me of that.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" from Yazīd ibn Hārūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1885]"""""
"10968","(10963) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us, from Abī Kathīr, the freedman of Muḥammad ibn Jaḥsh, from Muḥammad ibn Jaḥsh, who said: We were one day sitting in the place of funerals with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He raised his head toward the sky, then placed his palm on his forehead and said: \Glory be to Allah! What severity has been revealed!\"" We fell silent and were filled with fear. The next day I asked him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what is this severity that has been revealed?\"" He said: \""Regarding debt. By the One in whose Hand is my soul"","" if a man is killed in the cause of Allah"","" then is brought back to life"","" then is killed again twice"","" and he has a debt"","" he will not enter Paradise until his debt is repaid on his behalf.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 5/289]"""""
"10969","(10964) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Maʿdān ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Thawbān, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever's soul departs from his body while he is free from three things shall enter Paradise: embezzlement (ghulūl)"","" debt"","" and arrogance.\"" Likewise"","" Hammām"","" Abū ʿAwānah"","" and others narrated it from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2412]"""""
"10970","(10965) ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī narrated us in Makkah: Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ḥaywah informed us: Bakr ibn ʿAmr informed us that Shuʿayb ibn Zurʿah informed him. He said: ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say to his companions: \Do not frighten yourselves.\"" It was said to him: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" and by what do we frighten ourselves?\"" He said: \""By debt.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/154]"""""
"10971","(10966) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed me: Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd narrated to us: Bakr ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Shuʿayb ibn Zurʿah narrated to me that he heard ʿUqbah ibn ʀmir saying: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not frighten souls after their security.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" what is that?\"" He said: \""Debt.\"" [Weak. See its predecessor.]"""""
"10972","(10967) He said: And Bakr ibn ʿAmr narrated to me from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah that Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān said: \Debt reduces the free man to servitude.\""\n\nḤaywah corroborated it from Bakr ibn ʿAmr"","" except that he said \""Jaʿfar ibn Sharḥabīl\"" — and he is Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah ibn Sharḥabīl ibn Ḥasanah. [Weak.]"""""
"10973","(10968) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed me: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: My brother narrated to me from Sulaymān, from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿAtīq, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), informed him: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate in the prayer, saying: \O Allah"","" I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.\"" She said: A person said to him: \""How frequently you seek refuge from debt!\"" He said: \""When a man falls into debt"","" he speaks and lies"","" and he makes a promise and breaks it.\""\n\nThe wording is that of Ibn Sakhṭawayh. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān and from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. Similarly"","" Muslim narrated it from al-Ṣaghānī from Abū al-Yamān. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī (2267).]"""""
"10974","(10969) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) He said: And Abū Bakr informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb and al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashshār both said: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us. Both said: Sharīk narrated to us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: A caravan arrived, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) purchased goods from it and profited several awqiyyahs of gold. He gave it in charity among the orphans of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and said: \I do not purchase that whose price I do not have with me.\""\n\nWakīʿ similarly narrated it from Sharīk"","" and Qutaybah and ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it from Sharīk from Simāk from ʿIkrimah"","" raising it to the Prophet. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3344) and Aḥmad (1/235).]"""""
"10975","(10970) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī both said: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir narrated to us from Ribʿī ibn Ḥirāsh that Ḥudhayfah narrated to them, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The soul of a man from among those who came before you was received by the angels"","" and they said: 'Did you do any good?' He said: 'No.' They said: 'Remember.' He said: 'I used to lend to people and would instruct my young men to grant respite to the one in difficulty and to overlook the one who was well-off.' He said: Allah"","" the Most High"","" said: 'Overlook his faults.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī (1971).]"""""
"10976","(10971) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from Ribʿī ibn Ḥirāsh from Ḥudhayfah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \A man died and it was said to him: 'What did you do?' He said: 'I used to trade with people; I would be lenient in demanding payment and grant respite to the one in difficulty.' He entered Paradise.\"" Abū Masʿūd al-Badrī said: \""And I heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī (2261).]"""""
"10977","(10972) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥājjāj and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And al-Ustādh Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Isfarāyīnī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Jawsqānī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq from Abū Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \A man from among those who came before you was brought to account"","" and nothing good was found for him except that he was a wealthy man who mingled with people and would say to his servants: 'Overlook the one in difficulty.' Allah said to His angels: 'We are more deserving of that; overlook his faults.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of Abū Bakr. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others. [Authentic. Muslim (1561).]"""""
"10978","(10973) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah narrated to him that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \There was a man who used to lend to people. When a debtor fell into hardship"","" he would say to his young man: 'Overlook his debt; perhaps Allah will overlook our faults.' He met Allah"","" and He overlooked his faults.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it through two other chains from al-Zuhrī. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī (1972).]"""""
"10979","(10974) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Ājurī narrated to us: Khālid ibn Khidāsh al-Muhallabī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyūb from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah that Abū Qatādah sought a debtor of his, who hid from him. Then he found him and said: \I am in difficulty.\"" He said: \""By Allah?\"" He said: \""By Allah.\"" Abū Qatādah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Whoever would be pleased that Allah save him from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection"","" let him grant respite to one in difficulty or waive his debt.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Khālid ibn Khidāsh. [Authentic. Muslim (1563).]"""""
"10980","(10975) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ziyād ibn Mihrān al-Simsār narrated to us: Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us: Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Yaʿqūb ibn Mujāhid Abī Ḥazrah from ʿUbādah ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: My father and I went out seeking knowledge among this clan of the Anṣār before they perished. The first person we met was Abū al-Yasar, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and with him was a young servant of his. He had a collection of written sheets with him. Abū al-Yasar was wearing a striped Yemeni cloak, and his young servant was also wearing a striped Yemeni cloak. My father said to him: \O uncle"","" I see on your face a trace of anger.\"" He said: \""Indeed. I was owed a debt by so-and-so al-Ḥarāmī. I went to his family and offered greetings and said: 'Where is he?' They said: 'He is not here.' Then a young son of his came out"","" and I said: 'Where is your father?' He said: 'He heard your voice and hid beneath my mother's howdah.' I said: 'Come out to me"","" for I know where you are.' So he came out"","" and I said: 'What made you hide from me?' He said: 'By Allah"","" I will tell you and not lie to you. I feared that if I spoke to you"","" I would lie to you"","" and if I made you a promise"","" I would break it. You are a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" and by Allah"","" I am in difficulty.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'By Allah?' He said: 'By Allah.' I said: 'By Allah?' He said: 'By Allah.' I said: 'By Allah?' He said: 'By Allah.' He then brought his document and erased it with his hand and said: 'If you find the means to repay"","" then repay me"","" and if not"","" you are absolved.' He then bore witness with the sight of these two eyes\"" — and he placed his two fingers on his eyes — \""and with the hearing of these two ears"","" and my heart retained this\"" — and he pointed to the area of his heart — \""from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" who said: 'Whoever grants respite to one in difficulty or waives his debt"","" Allah will shade him under His Throne.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf. [Authentic. Muslim (3006).]"""""
"10981","(10976) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us; Abū Maʿmar narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah narrated from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from Buraydah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever grants respite to one in financial difficulty"","" then for every day [of respite] he shall receive the reward of charity equal to it.\"" He [Buraydah] said: I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" a charity [reward] for every day?\"" Then I said to him: \""For every day"","" the equivalent of it as charity?\"" He said: \""For every day"","" a charity"","" so long as the debt has not yet become due. And when the debt becomes due"","" and he grants respite after it has become due"","" then for every day he shall receive the equivalent of it as charity.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2418]"""""
"10982","(10977) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us; al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated from Nubayḥ al-ʿAnazī, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Madīnah towards the polytheists to fight them. He [Jābir] mentioned the hadith concerning the killing of his father and the severity of the creditors in pressing for repayment. He said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Call for me so-and-so\"" — the creditor who had been severe upon me in demanding repayment. He said: \""Defer Jābir's father's debt until the coming harvest season.\"" He [the creditor] said: \""I will not do that"",""\"" and he made excuses"","" saying: \""It is the property of orphans.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Where is Jābir?\"" He [Jābir] then mentioned the hadith concerning the settlement of the debt. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 3/397]"""""
"10983","(10978) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me; ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Dimashqī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us; Abū Ghassān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \May Allah have mercy upon a person who is lenient when he sells"","" lenient when he buys"","" and lenient when he demands repayment.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAyyāsh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1970]"""""
"10984","(10979) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us orally; Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Jamīl al-Azdī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān narrated to us. They both said: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ narrated to us; Isrāʾīl ibn Yūnus narrated from Zayd ibn ʬAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Allah forgave a man who was before you: he was easy-going when he sold"","" easy-going when he bought"","" easy-going when he paid"","" and easy-going when he demanded payment.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 1320]"""""
"10985","(10980) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed us from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Jaʿfar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar and ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever seeks a right"","" let him seek it whether it is fulfilled or unfulfilled.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Mājah 2423]"""""
"10986","In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. My Lord, make it easy and assist me, O Generous. May Allah's blessings and peace be upon our master Muḥammad, his family, and his Companions.\n\n(10981) The pious shaykh Abū al-Qāsim Manṣūr ibn ʿAbd al-Munʿim ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Farāwī al-Naysābūrī — may Allah have mercy upon him and upon us — informed us, reciting to him, and he authorized me [to transmit] his audition and his authorizations. He said: Abū al-Maʿālī Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī informed us, and he authorized him [to transmit] his auditions. He said: The Imām and Ḥāfiẓ Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Bayhaqī — may Allah have mercy upon him — informed us. He said: More than one of our shaykhs informed us from Zāhir ibn Ṭāhir. He said: The Imām al-Bayhaqī said: [This is the same chain of narration as the preceding hadith.]"
"10987","(10982) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Qurashī narrated to us; ʿAmmār ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭaybah narrated to us; Yaʿqūb, meaning Abū Yūsuf, narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī, meaning Abū Ayyūb al-Ifrīqī, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever is entrusted with the wealth of an orphan"","" let him trade with it"","" and let him not leave it until charity [obligatory alms] consumes it.\""\n\nWe have narrated it in the Book of Zakāh from al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ"","" from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Mandal ibn ʿAlī"","" from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī"","" from ʿAmr.\n\nThe authentic narration is that of Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim"","" from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"","" from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"","" that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \""Seek [sustenance] through the wealth of orphans"","" lest charity consume it.\""\n\nWe have narrated it through various routes from ʿUmar.\n\nIt has also been narrated through another route as a mursal narration from the Prophet ﷺ."""""
"10988","(10983) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; ʿAbd al-Majīd informed us from Ibn Jurayj, from Yūsuf ibn Māhik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Seek [sustenance] through the wealth of the orphan — or he said: the wealth of orphans — lest charity destroy it or consume it.\"""""""
"10989","(10984) Abū al-Qāsim Hibat Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭabarī al-Faqīh informed us; ʿĪsā ibn ʿAlī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Baghawī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated from ʿAmr, who is Ibn Dīnār, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Sāʾib, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \Seek [sustenance] through the wealth of orphans"","" lest charity consume it.\"""""""
"10990","(10985) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Saʿīd ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAdl informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Dāwūd al-Ḍabbī narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḥuddānī narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, who said: al-Ḥakam ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ narrated to me, saying: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — said to me: \Is there a merchant with you? For I have the wealth of an orphan"","" and zakāh is about to consume it.\"" I said to him: \""Yes.\"" He said: He handed over ten thousand [dirhams] to me. I was absent from him for as long as Allah willed"","" then I returned to him and he said to me: \""What has become of the wealth?\"" I said: \""Here it is; it has reached a hundred thousand.\"" He said: \""Return our wealth to us; we have no need of it [through trade].\"""""""
"10991","(10986) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, and ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq — all of them reporting from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) used to pay the Zakāh on our wealth, even though it was being traded with in al-Baḥrayn."
"10992","(10987) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to borrow the wealth of the orphans under his care, considering it more secure for them than leaving it idle. He said: And he used to pay the Zakāh on their wealth from their own funds."
"10993","(10988) The Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Sālim, from his father, that he had the wealth of two orphans in his custody. He began paying Zakāh on it. I said: O father, why do you not trade with it or invest it in a mudārabah, seeing how quickly it is diminishing? He said: I shall continue to pay Zakāh on it even if nothing remains but a single dirham. He said: Then he purchased a house for the two of them with that wealth. [Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd, Hadith 2764]"
"10994","(10989) The Shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us; Zuhayr narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Ṣilat ibn Zufr, who said: I was sitting with ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd when a man from Hamdān came upon a piebald horse and said: O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, shall I buy this? He said: What is the matter with it? He said: Its owner bequeathed it to me. He said: Do not buy it, and do not borrow from its owner's wealth. [Ibn al-Jaʿd, Hadith 2546. This narration is weak; one of its narrators is a mudallis.]"
"10995","(10990) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr — meaning Ibn Abī Shaybah — said: And Abū al-Walīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; both saying: Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, who said: A woman related to me through my maternal uncle passed away, leaving behind a servant and young children. Saʿīd ibn Jubayr said: There is no harm in the father assuming guardianship over his son's offspring and providing for them.\n\nThe Shaykh Abū al-Walīd said: Our companions said: He may assume guardianship and purchase from his own funds, and it becomes theirs.\n\nHe said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, saying: And Abū Bakr narrated to us, saying: I said to Azhar: Ibn ʿAwn narrated to you from Muḥammad, who said: When a man intends to take control of his child's slave-girl, and he mentioned something similar to that.\n\nHe said: And Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Wakīʿ; Abū Sufyān ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us, saying: I asked al-Ḥasan and Ṭāwūs, and they both said: There is no harm in that.\n\nHe said: And al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr narrated to us; Ibn Idrīs narrated from Mūsā ibn Saʿīd, that his grandmother died in the care of Abū Barzah, and they issued a fatwā to Abū Barzah permitting him to sell some of her slave-girls. He mentioned the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ; its narrators are trustworthy.]"
"10996","(10991) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḁfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {Whoever is wealthy, let him abstain; and whoever is poor, let him consume with kindness} — she said: This verse was revealed concerning the guardian of an orphan's wealth: if he is poor, he may consume from it in a reasonable manner in return for his stewardship over it. [Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī 4575 and Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim 3019]"
"10997","(10992) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated from Hishām, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: It was revealed concerning the guardian of an orphan's wealth who manages it and maintains it — if he is in need, he may consume from it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ibn Numayr, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah."
"10998","(10993) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-ʿUmarī narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Mahdī informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān al-Ḍubaʿī narrated from Abū ʿĀmir al-Khazzāz, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), on what grounds may I strike my orphan? He said: On the same grounds on which you would strike your own child — without shielding your wealth with his wealth, and without enriching yourself from his wealth. This is how he narrated it. The preserved version is: [Ṣaḥīḥ Ibn Ḥibbān 4244 and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam 89. This narration is weak.]"
"10999","(10994) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd and Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from al-Ḥasan al-ʿUranī, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, on what grounds may I strike my orphan? He said: On the same grounds on which you would strike your own child. He said: May I then partake of his wealth? He said: Without amassing wealth thereby, and without shielding your own wealth with his. This is a mursal narration. [It is mursal.]"
"11000","(10995) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, who said: A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said: I have the wealth of orphans in my custody, and he sought permission to partake of it. Ibn ʿAbbās said: Can you not seek out their lost property? He said: Yes. He said: Can you not treat their camels when they are afflicted with mange? He said: Yes. He said: Can you not plaster their watering troughs? He said: Yes. He said: Can you not be present for them on the day they arrive at the water? He said: Yes. He said: Then partake of their provisions — meaning their milk. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq 147, in the Book of Tafsīr; Tafsīr al-Ṭabarī, no. 8631]"
"11001","(10996) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from Ibn ʿAbbās that a man asked him, saying: \I have an orphan under my care; may I drink from the milk?\"" He replied: \""If you search for its lost camel"","" plaster its water trough"","" and treat its scabies"","" then drink — without harming its offspring and without excessive milking.\"" [Muwṭaʾ Imām Mālik no. 937"","" and Muṣannaf Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr no. 571]"""""
"11002","(10997) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us that Jarīr narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The guardian places his hand alongside their hands"","" and he should not wear the turban or anything above it.\"" [Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr no. 570]"""""
"11003","(10998) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us that Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to us that al-Ashjaʿī narrated from Sufyān from al-Suddī from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \He may consume the orphan's wealth with his fingers"","" and nothing beyond that.\"""""""
"11004","(10999) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Narsī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me that Sulaymān al-Shaybānī narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: *\And whoever is rich"","" let him abstain; and whoever is poor"","" let him consume in a fair manner.\""*"""""
"11005","(11000) \If he is poor"","" let him place his hand alongside their hands and eat"","" but he should not clothe himself with a turban or anything above it from their wealth.\"""""""
"11006","(11001) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Barāʾ, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāẓ, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: \I consider myself in relation to the wealth of Allah as the guardian of an orphan considers himself in relation to the orphan's wealth. If I am in need"","" I take from it; when I become affluent"","" I return it; and when I am free of need"","" I abstain.\"" [Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr no. 788"","" and Tafsīr Ibn Kathīr 2/218]"""""
"11007","(11002) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us that Warqāʾ narrated from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His words: *\And whoever is poor"","" let him consume in a fair manner"",""\""* he said: \""The guardian of the orphan may consume from the orphan's wealth his sustenance"","" wear from it what covers him"","" drink the surplus of the milk"","" and ride the surplus of the mounts. If he becomes affluent"","" he repays; and if he remains in hardship"","" he is in a state of permissibility.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿUbaydah"","" Mujāhid"","" Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"","" and Abū al-ʿĀliyah that they said: \""He must repay it.\"" And it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ: \""He need not repay it.\"" [This narration is weak.]"""""
"11008","(11003) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us that Isrāʾīl narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When the verse *'And do not approach the orphan's wealth except in the best manner'* was revealed"","" they separated their wealth from the wealth of the orphans. Food began to spoil and meat began to rot. They complained of this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" so Allah"","" the Most High"","" revealed: *'Say: To set their affairs right is better"","" and if you mix with them"","" they are your brothers.'* He said: So they mixed with them.\"" [Musnad Aḥmad"","" hadith 3002; Sunan al-Nasāʾī"","" hadith 3669]"""""
"11009","(11004) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us that al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Abū Wahb from Sulaymān ibn Mūsā that Nāfiʿ narrated to him from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"","" the wealth belongs to the slave and the debt is upon him"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And whoever pollinates a date palm and then sells it after its pollination"","" the fruit belongs to him"","" unless the buyer stipulates otherwise.\""\n\nAnd if this is authentic"","" then what is meant — and Allah knows best — is the slave who has been given permission to trade"","" when he has wealth in his possession and a debt is attached to it; the master takes his wealth and pays his debt from it. [Musnad Aḥmad 3/309; Sunan al-Nasāʾī"","" hadith 4964]"""""
"11010","(11005) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī informed us that Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father from the jurists among the Tābiʿūn of the people of Madīnah, who said: \They used to say: The debt of a slave is upon his own responsibility"","" and whatever he takes from the people's wealth other than a debt — such as something he steals"","" wealth he usurps"","" or a camel he slaughters — all of that is in the position of a wound he inflicts. Either his master must pay the blood money on his behalf"","" or he must surrender his slave.\"""""""
"11011","(11006) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — in the latter's final sessions — informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām — both of them said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, he said: I read before Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from Abū Masʿūd al-Anṣārī, that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog, the hire of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2237, 2282]"
"11012","(11007) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd informed us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah informed us, he said: I heard my father — he had purchased a slave cupper — so he went to the cupping vessels and broke them and said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of blood, the price of a dog, the hire of a prostitute, and cursed the consumer of ribā and the one who pays it, the tattooer and the one tattooed, and the image-maker.\n\nal-Bukhārī extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Shuʿbah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2238, 2086]"
"11013","(11008) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr and Abū al-Azhar and Ḥamdān al-Sulamī — all of them said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Qāriẓ, from al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd, from Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The earnings of a cupper are vile"","" the earnings of a prostitute are vile"","" and the price of a dog is vile.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1568 and Ibn Ḥibbān 5152]"""""
"11014","(11009) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Danūqā informed us: Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr informed us, from ʿAbd al-Karīm, from Qays ibn Ḥabṭar, from Ibn ʿAbbās, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of wine, the hire of a prostitute, and the price of a dog, and he said: \When someone comes seeking the price of a dog"","" fill his hand with dust.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in al-Sunan from Abū Tawbah from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr"","" in an abridged form.\n\n[Musnad Aḥmad 2351"","" Ḥadīth 2094 and Sunan Abī Dāwūd 2482]"""""
"11015","(11010) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Maʿrūf ibn Suwayd al-Judhāmī informed me that ʿAlayy ibn Rabbāh al-Lakhmī informed them that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The price of a dog is not permissible"","" nor the fee of a soothsayer"","" nor the hire of a prostitute.\""\n\n[Ibn Wahb included it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ 13]"""""
"11016","(11011) As for the ḥadīth which Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī, informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Mālik al-Ḍabbī informed us: Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān informed us: Muʾammal informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us: Qays informed us, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Abū Hurayrah: he prohibited the hire of a prostitute, the stud fee of a stallion, the price of a cat, and the price of a dog except a hunting dog. Thus did Qays ibn Saʿd narrate it from ʿAṭāʾ from him through this chain, though the narration of Ḥammād from Qays is subject to scrutiny.\n\nAnd al-Walīd ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rabbāḥ and al-Muthannā ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated from ʿAṭāʾ from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ: \Three things — all of them are suḥt (unlawful earnings).\"" And they mentioned the earnings of a cupper"","" the hire of a prostitute"","" and the price of a dog except a vicious dog. And al-Walīd and al-Muthannā are both weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\n[The narration mentioned contains al-Walīd and al-Muthannā"","" both of whom are weak.]"""""
"11017","(11012) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Abū Yazīd al-Qurashī informed us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth informed us: Ḥammād informed us: Abū al-Zubayr informed us, from Jābir, he said: The price of a dog and a cat was prohibited, except a hunting dog.\n\nThus did ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrate it. And likewise Suwayd ibn ʿAmr narrated from Ḥammād, then he said: and Ḥammād did not mention \from the Prophet ﷺ.\"" And ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated from Ḥammād with uncertainty regarding the mention of the Prophet ﷺ in it. And al-Haytham ibn Jamīl narrated from Ḥammād and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited — and al-Ḥasan ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir from the Prophet ﷺ"","" and it is not strong.\n\nThe authentic aḥādīth from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the prohibition of the price of a dog are free of this exception. The exception appears only in the authentic aḥādīth concerning the prohibition of keeping dogs. Perhaps those narrators — who are below the rank of the Ṣaḥābah and the Tābiʿūn — were confused in the ḥadīth of prohibition of the price. And Allah knows best.\n\n[The narration is weak (ḍaʿīf).]"""""
"11018","(11013) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ granted me permission to narrate his narration from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās, from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Shāfiʿī, from one who used to debate with him on this issue, he said: One of our companions informed us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas that ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — fined a man twenty camels as the price of a dog he had killed. Al-Shāfiʿī said: I said to him: Tell me, had this been established from ʿUthmān, would you not have done anything in your argumentation against something established from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when what is established from ʿUthmān contradicts it? He said: Mention it. I said: A trustworthy authority informed us from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan, he said: I heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān delivering a sermon, and he was commanding the killing of dogs. Al-Shāfiʿī said: How could he command the killing of that for which he fined whoever killed it its price?\n\nThe Shaykh said: What has been narrated from ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with him — regarding the compensation for a dog is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ). It has also been narrated through another chain from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī that he mentioned it from ʿUthmān in a story he narrated, and it is also disconnected. And it has been narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ.\n\n[The narration is weak. ʿImrān's hearing from ʿUthmān is not established.]"
"11019","(11014) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, that he ruled regarding a hunting dog killed by a man at forty dirhams, and he ruled regarding a herding dog at a sheep. This is mawqūf (ending at the Companion). And Ibn Jurayj — they do not consider his hearing from ʿAmr to be established. Al-Bukhārī — may Allah have mercy on him — said: He did not hear it.\n\n[The narration is weak. Ibn Jurayj is a mudallis (concealer of defects) in its chain.]"
"11020","(11015) The Shaykh said: Ismāʿīl ibn Jastās narrated it — and he is not well-known — from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, he said: It was ruled regarding a hunting dog at forty dirhams; regarding a sheep dog, a sheep from the flock; regarding a crop dog, a faraq (a large measure) of food; and regarding a house dog, a faraq of dust is due upon the one who killed it — that he must give it — and it is due upon the owner of the dog to accept it, along with a reduction from the compensation.\n\nAbū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khayrūyah informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, from Ismāʿīl, and he mentioned it.\n\n[The narration is weak.]"
"11021","(11016) Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī — informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī — informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris — narrated to us, al-Bukhārī — narrated to us, Qutaybah — narrated to us, Hushaym — narrated to us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Ismāʿīl — that is, ibn Jastās — that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ruled regarding a hunting dog that its penalty was forty dirhams.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: This ḥadīth has not been corroborated.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: The authentic narration from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr is contrary to this."
"11022","(11017) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-ʿAdl — informed me, my grandfather Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn Zurārah — narrated to us, Hushaym — narrated to us, Ḥuṣayn, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: He (the Prophet ﷺ) prohibited the price of a dog, the fee of a prostitute, the wage of a soothsayer, and the earnings of a cupper. [Mustadrak al-Ḥākim]"
"11023","(11018) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us, al-Shāfiʿī — informed us, Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs."
"11024","(11019) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī — informed me, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām al-Warrāq — narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, who said: I read before Mālik, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Muttafaq ʿalayh]"
"11025","(11020) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq — informed us, Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ commanded the killing of dogs in al-Madīnah. He was informed of a woman who had a dog on the outskirts of al-Madīnah, so he sent to her, and it was killed. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq, ḥadīth 19610; its chain is ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11026","(11021) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us, al-Shāfiʿī — informed us, Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh — informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad — both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — narrated to us, and he said: I read before Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" except a dog for livestock or a hunting dog"","" two qīrāṭs will be deducted from his deeds every day.\"" And in the narration of Yaḥyā: \""a hunting dog.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""""
"11027","(11022) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us orally, Abū Saʿīd — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī — informed us in Makkah, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" except a dog for livestock"","" two qīrāṭs will be deducted from his reward every day.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" from Sufyān"","" and he said: \""except a dog for hunting or livestock.\"" [Muttafaq ʿalayh]"""""
"11028","(11023) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed him, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Shaybah — narrated to us, Sufyān, and he mentioned it."
"11029","(11024) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī — informed us in Khurāsān, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh — al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān, and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān, and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Sukkari — in al-ʿIrāq, all of them said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah — narrated to us, Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah, from ʿUmar ibn Ḥamzah al-ʿUmarī — informed us, Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever takes a dog"","" except a dog for livestock or a hunting dog"","" one qīrāṭ will be deducted from his deeds every day.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd"","" from Marwān"","" and he said: \""two qīrāṭs.\"" And he also narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar"","" from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah"","" from Sālim"","" and he said: \""one qīrāṭ.\"" Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar contradicted him"","" narrating it from Ibn Abī Ḥarmalah"","" and he said: \""two qīrāṭs.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim]"""""
"11030","(11025) And Abū Naṣr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh — informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us, Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid — narrated to us, Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us, Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān, who said: I heard Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" except a hunting dog for game or a dog for livestock"","" two qīrāṭs will be deducted from his reward every day.\"""""""
"11031","(11026) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Wakīʿ reported from Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān, from — and he mentioned it similarly, and added: Sālim said that Abū Hurayrah used to say: \Or a dog of the farm (kalb al-ḥarth)"",""\"" and he was a man of farming.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Agreed upon]"""""
"11032","(11027) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us that Sufyān reported from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: I went with Ibn ʿUmar to Banī Muʿāwiyah, and dogs barked at us. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" except a dog for hunting or for livestock"","" two qīrāṭ will be deducted from his reward every day.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through another chain from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār. [Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim 1574]"""""
"11033","(11028) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us by dictation, that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd reported from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded the killing of dogs, except a dog for livestock or for hunting. It was said to Ibn ʿUmar: \Indeed"","" Abū Hurayrah says: 'Or a dog of the farm (kalb al-zarʿ).'\"" He said: \""Indeed"","" Abū Hurayrah had farmland.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" from Ḥammād ibn Zayd. And Abū al-Ḥakam ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Ibn ʿUmar the mention of the farm dog"","" as though he took it from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the farm dog"","" and from the Prophet (ﷺ) himself regarding the dog of livestock and hunting."""""
"11034","(11029) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā both said: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Shuʿbah reported from Qatādah, from Abī al-Ḥakam, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar narrate from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" except a dog for farming"","" or for sheep"","" or for hunting"","" one qīrāṭ will be deducted from his reward every day.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim]"""""
"11035","(11030) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us that Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Hammām reported from Qatādah, from Abī al-Ḥakam al-Bajalī, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a dog other than a dog for farming or for livestock"","" one qīrāṭ will be deducted from his deeds every day.\"" I said to Ibn ʿUmar: \""If there is a dog in a house and I dislike it?\"" He said: \""The burden falls upon the owner of the house who possesses it.\""\n\n[Musnad Aḥmad 4798 and al-Awhām lil-Khaṭīb 2352; the narration is weak.]"""""
"11036","(11031) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr, Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Khabbāb al-Tinnīsī in Tinnīs, and Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī Abū ʿUthmān in Ḥimṣ all said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us that al-Awzāʿī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me that Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated to me that Abū Hurayrah narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Tamtām narrated to us that Mūsā narrated to us that Hammām reported from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr that Abū Salamah narrated to him from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a dog"","" one qīrāṭ will be deducted from his deeds every day"","" except a dog for farming or for livestock.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Awzāʿī: \""Whoever keeps (iqtanā)…\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl"","" and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq from al-Awzāʿī. And Maʿmar narrated it from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah"","" and he said: \""Except a dog for hunting"","" or farming"","" or livestock.\"" And Yūnus narrated it from al-Zuhrī from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Abū Hurayrah"","" and he said in the hadith: \""Not a dog for hunting"","" nor for livestock"","" nor for land"",""\"" and he said: \""Two qīrāṭ every day.\"" Both narrations have preceded in the book of Purification. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 2322"","" Muslim 1575]"""""
"11037","(11032) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī both said: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Marwazī and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I read to Mālik from Yazīd ibn Khuṣayfah that al-Sāʾib ibn Yazīd informed him that he heard Sufyān ibn Abī Zuhayr — and he was a man from Shanūʾah, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Whoever keeps a dog that is of no benefit to him for farming or for livestock"","" one qīrāṭ will be deducted from his deeds every day.\"" He (al-Sāʾib) said: \""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" by the Lord of this mosque.\"" The wording is from the hadith of Abū ʿAbdillāh from Abū ʿAbdillāh ibn Yaʿqūb.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 2323"","" Muslim 1567]"""""
"11038","(11033) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that Shuʿbah reported from Abī al-Tayyāḥ from Muṭarrif, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal, that the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded the killing of dogs, then he said: \What concern have I with dogs?\"" Then he gave concession regarding the dog of livestock and the dog of hunting.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim 280]"""""
"11039","(11034) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sābiq narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān reported from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to kill the dogs, so we killed them, to the extent that if a Bedouin woman came with her dog, we would kill it. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Were it not that dogs are one of the nations (ummah min al-umam)"","" I would not wish to annihilate them"","" but I would have commanded their killing. However"","" kill from among them every jet-black dog (aswad bahīm) with two white spots (over its eyes).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim 1572]"""""
"11040","(11035) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj informed me that Abī al-Zubayr informed him that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us to kill the dogs, to the extent that a woman would come from the desert with her dog and we would kill it. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade us from killing them and said: \Confine yourselves to killing the jet-black dog with two spots (nuqṭatayn)"","" for it is a devil (shayṭān).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim]"""""
"11041","(11036) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad both said: Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Aʿyan narrated to us: Maʿqil narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, who said: I asked Jābir about the price of a dog and a cat, and he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) rebuked against that. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Salamah ibn Shabīb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1569]"
"11042","(11037) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad al-Rāzī in Rayy informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dabarī informed us from ʿAbd al-Razzāq from ʿUmar ibn Zayd al-Ṣanʿānī, who informed me: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the eating of the cat and the eating of its price. Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal from ʿAbd al-Razzāq with his chain of narration, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade the price of the cat. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq 8748, and al-Mujam al-Awsaṭ 4529]"
"11043","(11038) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥātim al-ʿAdl in Marw narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Hārūn al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Kūfī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us — all of them from al-Aʿmash from Abū Sufyān from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the price of the dog and the cat.\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from a group of narrators from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus. And this is a ṣaḥīḥ hadith according to the condition of Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj, but not that of al-Bukhārī, for al-Bukhārī does not use as evidence the narration of Abū al-Zubayr nor the narration of Abū Sufyān. Perhaps Muslim did not include it in the Ṣaḥīḥ because Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated it from al-Aʿmash, saying: Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh said, and then he mentioned it. Then al-Aʿmash said: I think Abū Sufyān mentioned it. Thus al-Aʿmash was uncertain about the continuity of the hadith, and so the narration of Abū Sufyān thereby became weak.\n\nSome of the people of knowledge interpreted this as referring to the cat when it has become wild and it is not possible to take possession of it. And among them are those who claimed that this was at the beginning of Islam when it was ruled to be impure; then when it was ruled that its leftover water was pure, its price became permissible. There is no clear evidence for either of these two positions. And Allah knows best."
"11044","(11039) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: There is no harm in the price of the cat. The Shaykh said: When the hadith is established and its abrogation is not established, the statement of ʿAṭāʾ does not enter into it."
"11045","(11040) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, and Abū al-Ḥasan ibn al-Muʾammal informed us: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us. Both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Muslim.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Sulaymān, who is al-Aʿmash, from Abū al-Ḍuḥā, who is Muslim, from Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah, who said: When the last verses of Sūrat al-Baqarah were revealed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out and recited them to us and said: \Trading in wine has been made impermissible.\""\n\nThe wording is that of Shuʿbah's hadith. And in the narration of Yaʿlā: \""The verses at the end of Sūrat al-Baqarah concerning ribā"",""\"" and he said: \""He recited them to the people and prohibited trading in wine.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from various routes from al-Aʿmash"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2226 and Muslim 1580]"""""
"11046","(11041) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb ibn Abī al-Ashras narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Sāmī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Iyās al-Jurayrī narrated from Abū Naḍrah from Abū Saʿīd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivering a sermon in al-Madīnah, and he said: \O people"","" I see that Allah"","" exalted be His mention"","" has expressed displeasure with wine"","" and perhaps Allah will send down a command concerning it. So whoever has anything of it"","" let him sell it and benefit from it.\"" He said: It was only a short time before he said: \""Indeed"","" Allah has forbidden wine. So whoever reaches this verse and has anything of it"","" let him neither drink it nor sell it.\"" The people then poured out whatever they had of it into the streets of al-Madīnah and spilled it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1578]"""""
"11047","(11042) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Mālik ibn Anas and others narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Waʿlah al-Sabāʾī, one of the people of Egypt, that he asked ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās about what is pressed from grapes. Ibn ʿAbbās said: A man presented the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with a skin of wine. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \Did you not know that Allah has forbidden it?\"" He said: No. Then he whispered to a man. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""What did you whisper to him?\"" He said: \""I told him to sell it.\"" He said: \""Indeed"","" the One who has forbidden its drinking has forbidden its selling.\"" He then opened the two skins until what was in them was gone. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1579]"""""
"11048","(11043) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā, Abū Bakr, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: Muḥammad informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Waʿlah from Ibn ʿAbbās from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), a similar narration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb with both chains of narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11049","(11044) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: ʿUmar said: \Indeed"","" Samurah ibn Jundub sold wine. May Allah fight Samurah! Did he not know that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Allah has cursed the Jews; fats were made unlawful for them"","" so they melted them down and sold them.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī Shaybah and others"","" all from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2223"","" Muslim 1582]"""""
"11050","(11045) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ghāfiqī, one of the people of Egypt, and a client of ours called Abū Ṭuʿmah, that both of them went out from Egypt as pilgrims and sat with Ibn ʿUmar, and the story was mentioned. Ibn ʿUmar said: \I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Allah has cursed wine"","" the one who drinks it"","" the one who pours it"","" the one who sells it"","" the one who buys it"","" the one who presses it"","" the one who has it pressed"","" the one who carries it"","" the one for whom it is carried"","" and the one who consumes its price.'\"" [Naṣb al-Rāyah 4/263]"""""
"11051","(11046) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffār narrated to us: al-Asfati, meaning al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl, narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Ṭu'mah ibn 'Amr al-Ju'fi narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Bayān narrated from 'Urwah ibn al-Mughīrah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever sells wine"","" let him [also] slaughter the pigs.\"" [This narration is weak (ḍa'īf).]"""""
"11052","(11047) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffār narrated to us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth — (ḥ) — and Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: 'Abd Allāh ibn Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Layth, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from 'Aṭā' ibn Abī Rabbāḥ, from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh, that he heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ saying during the Year of the Conquest (Fatḥ), while he was in Makkah: \Indeed"","" Allāh and His Messenger have forbidden the sale of wine (khamr)"","" carrion (maytah)"","" pork (khinzīr)"","" and idols (aṣnām).\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allāh"","" what do you say about the fat of carrion? With it ships are caulked"","" with it skins are greased"","" and with it people light their lamps.\"" He ﷺ said: \""No"","" it is forbidden (ḥarām).\"" Then the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \""May Allāh fight the Jews! When Allāh forbade them [the consumption of] their fat"","" they melted it down"","" then sold it and consumed its price.\"" The wording is that of Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). Reported by al-Bukhārī and Muslim together in their Ṣaḥīḥ collections"","" no. 1581"","" from Qutaybah.]"""""
"11053","(11048) Abu 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abu al-Ḥusayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tamīm al-Qanṭarī narrated to us: Abu Qilābah narrated to us: Abu 'Āṣim narrated to us: 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far — (ḥ) — and Abu 'Abd Allāh informed us: Abu al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Abu 'Āṣim, from 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far, narrated to me: Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb said: 'Aṭā' ibn Abī Rabbāḥ wrote to me that he heard Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh saying: \I heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ during the Year of the Conquest saying…\"" — and he mentioned it with the same meaning"","" except that he said: \""Then a man said to him: 'What do you say about the fat of carrion"","" O Messenger of Allāh?' He ﷺ said: 'May Allāh fight [them].'\"" — and he did not mention what was between the two. [Reported by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ"","" from Muhammad ibn al-Muthannā. And al-Bukhārī extracted it"","" saying: \""And Abu 'Āṣim mentioned"","" and he cited its chain of narration.\""]"""""
"11054","(11049) Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: 'Abd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Mu'āwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Wahhāb ibn Bukht, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-A'raj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \Indeed"","" Allāh — exalted is His praise — has forbidden wine (khamr) and its price"","" and has forbidden carrion (maytah) and its price"","" and has forbidden pork (khinzīr) and its price.\"" [Abū Dāwūd"","" no. 3485.]"""""
"11055","(11050) Abu Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abu Manṣūr al-'Abbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Ismā'īl ibn 'Ayyāsh narrated to us, from Ḥabīb ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: \Al-suḥt (that which is forbidden) is: a bribe (rishwah) given to a judge; the dowry (mahr) of a prostitute (baghī); the price of a dog; the price of a monkey; the price of a pig; the price of wine (khamr); the price of carrion (maytah); the price of blood; the stud fee of a stallion ('asb al-faḥl); the wage of a professional mourner (nā'ihah); the wage of a singer (mughanniyah); the wage of a soothsayer (kāhin); the wage of a magician (sāḥir); the wage of a physiognomist (qā'if); the price of the skins of predatory animals; the price of the skins of carrion — but if they are tanned"","" there is no harm; the price of images and statues (ṣuwar al-tamāthīl); the gift given for intercession (shafā'ah); and the payment for military service (ja'īlah al-ghazw).\"" [This narration is disconnected (munqaṭi') between Ḥabīb ibn Ṣāliḥ and Ibn 'Abbās"","" and it is stopped (mawqūf). Reported by Sa'id ibn Manṣūr"","" no. 745.]"""""
"11056","(11051) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffār narrated to us: Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us: Khālid al-Ḥadhā' narrated to us: Barakah narrated to us, from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ sitting at the Corner (al-Rukn). He raised his gaze toward the heavens"","" laughed"","" and said: 'May Allāh curse the Jews' — three times — 'Indeed"","" Allāh forbade them [the consumption of] fats"","" so they sold them and consumed their prices. Indeed"","" when Allāh forbids a people from eating a thing"","" He forbids them from its price.'\"" He (the narrator) said: \""And Ismā'īl narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Wuhibb narrated to us: Khālid al-Ḥadhā' narrated to us: Barakah"","" Abū al-Walīd"","" narrated to us"","" from Ibn 'Abbās"","" that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ was sitting behind the Maqām (of Ibrāhīm)"","" raised his gaze toward the heavens"","" and said…\"" — and he mentioned it with the same meaning. [Reported by Abū Dāwūd in the Sunan"","" from Musaddad. Musnad Aḥmad 1/247"","" and Sunan Abī Dāwūd"","" no. 3488.]"""""
"11057","(11052) Abu 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abu al-Ḥasan ibn Maḥmūd al-Marwazī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn 'Ali al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Ibn Dāwūd narrated to us, from Muṭī' al-Ghazzāl, from al-Sha'bī, from Ibn 'Umar, from 'Umar — may Allāh be pleased with him — who said: \Trade (tijārah) is not permissible in anything whose consumption and drinking is not permissible.\"" [This narration is weak (ḍa'īf).]"""""
"11058","(11053) Abu 'Amr al-Adīb narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Ismā'īlī narrated to us: Ibn Abī Ḥassān al-Anmāṭī narrated to us: Hishām ibn 'Ammār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym said: \I heard Ismā'īl ibn Umayyah narrating from Sa'id ibn Abī Sa'id"","" from Abū Hurayrah"","" who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said — meaning: 'Your Lord"","" exalted is His majesty"","" says: There are three [types of people] against whom I shall be a disputant on the Day of Resurrection"","" and whomever I dispute shall be defeated: a man to whom I gave [a pledge] and then he betrayed it; a man who sold a free person and consumed his price; and a man who hired a worker"","" took his full due"","" but did not give him his wages.'\"" [Reported by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ"","" from Bishr ibn Marḥūm"","" from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym. Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī"","" no. 2227.]"""""
"11059","(11054) Al-Nufaylī also narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym, and said: \From his father"","" from Abū Hurayrah.\"" Abu al-Qāsim 'Abd al-Khāliq ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Khāliq informed us: Abu Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Mu'ammal narrated to us: Al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Nufaylī narrated to us"","" from Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym"","" and he mentioned it. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ).]"""""
"11060","(11055) Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us: Abu Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah narrated to us: 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Bakr ibn Muḍar narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Zaḥr narrated to us: 'Ali ibn Yazīd narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Abū Umāmah narrated to us, from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ, who said: \Do not buy female singers (mughanniyāt)"","" nor sell them"","" nor teach them. There is no good in trade in them"","" and their price is forbidden (ḥarām).\"" Regarding matters like this"","" the verse was revealed: {And of the people is he who buys idle talk (lahw al-ḥadīth)} [Sūrah Luqmān"","" 31:6]. And with its meaning"","" a group narrated from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Zaḥr"","" and with its meaning"","" al-Faraj ibn Faḍālah narrated from 'Ali ibn Yazīd. Abū 'Īsā said: \""I asked al-Bukhārī about the chain of this hadith"","" and he said: 'Ali ibn Yazīd is a narrator whose hadith is abandoned (dhāhib al-ḥadīth)"","" while 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Zaḥr and al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān have been declared trustworthy (thiqah).'\"" The Shaykh — may Allāh have mercy on him — said: \""And it has been narrated from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym"","" from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Sābit"","" from 'Ā'ishah"","" but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). And it has been narrated from Layth"","" going back to the first chain"","" in which Layth made an error.\"" [This narration is weak (ḍa'īf). See al-Ṣaḥīḥah"","" no. 2922.]"""""
"11061","(11056) Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — 'Abdullāh ibn Ahmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me — my father narrated to us — Wakī' narrated to me — Khālid al-Ṣaffār, who heard it from 'Ubaydullāh ibn Zaḥr — from 'Alī ibn Yazīd — from al-Qāsim ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān — from Abū Umāmah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The sale of singing girls is unlawful"","" and their purchase is unlawful"","" and trading in them is unlawful"","" and consuming their prices is ḥarām.\""\n\nIn the narration of Bakr ibn Muḍar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" he said: \""Do not sell singing girls"","" nor purchase them"","" nor teach them"","" and there is no good in trading in them"","" and their price is ḥarām.\""\n\nRegarding this very ḥadīth"","" the verse was revealed: {And of the people is he who buys the diversion of speech…} until {those — for them is a humiliating punishment.} [Luqmān: 6]"""""
"11062","(11057) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — 'Alī ibn Ḥamshādh al-'Adl narrated to us — Bishr ibn Mūsá narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Dīnār said: I heard Abū al-Minhāl saying: I heard Iyās ibn 'Abd al-Muzanī — and he saw a man selling water — saying: \Do not sell water"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the sale of water.\""\n\nAl-Shāfi'ī"","" may Allah have mercy upon him"","" mentioned this report from Sufyān in the Sunan of Ḥarmalah and then said: The meaning of this ḥadīth is that water be sold in the place where Allah created it — that is"","" a man comes to a desert well belonging to him to water his livestock"","" and there is surplus water beyond what his livestock needs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the owner of the water from selling that surplus and forbade him from withholding it. Then he continued speaking until he said: If a man carries water upon his back"","" there is no harm in selling it to another"","" for he owns what he has carried.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And Yaḥyá ibn Ādam narrated it from Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah"","" and in the ḥadīth he said: \""…for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the sale of surplus water.\"" [Musnad 'Abd al-Razzāq"","" no. 14495; Musnad al-Ḥumaydī"","" no. 836]"""""
"11063","(11058) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr narrated to us — Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn 'Affān narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Ādam narrated to us — Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah from — and he mentioned it, but did not say \and he saw a man selling water.\""\n\nLikewise"","" Dāwūd ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-'Aṭṭār narrated it from 'Amr ibn Dīnār: \""He forbade the sale of surplus water.\""\n\nAnd Ibn Jurayj narrated it from 'Amr ibn Dīnār that Abū al-Minhāl informed him that Iyās ibn 'Abd said to the people: \""Do not sell surplus water"","" for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of water.\""\n\nAbū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Ibn Jurayj mentioned it. And upon this is based the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn 'Abdullāh al-Anṣārī."""""
"11064","(11059) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us — 'Uthmān ibn 'Umar narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj — (ḥ) and Abū al-Walīd informed me — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Wakī' narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the sale of surplus water.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nLikewise"","" Yaḥyá al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 1565]"""""
"11065","(11060) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Tamīm al-Qanṭarī al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us — Abū Qilābah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us — Abū 'Āṣim informed us — Ibn Jurayj from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir: \that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the sale of water"","" and the striking of camels for payment"","" and that a man should sell his land and its water.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: His statement in this ḥadīth — \""and that a man should sell his land and its water\"" — he intended"","" and Allah knows best"","" that he rents it out along with the water for cultivation in exchange for some of what it produces. For Rūḥ ibn 'Ubādah narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"","" and in the ḥadīth he said: \""…and the sale of water and land to be cultivated.\"" And with the same meaning"","" Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated it from Abū 'Āṣim"","" and Bayāḍ said: \""The whiteness (i.e."","" the produce) of the land.\"""""""
"11066","(11061) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn 'Alī al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī narrated to us — Abū 'Abdullāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn 'Uthmān al-Nasawī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn 'Uthmān al-Baṣrī narrated to us — Abū 'Āṣim informed us — Ibn Jurayj informed me — Ziyād ibn Sa'd informed me — that Hilāl ibn Usāmah informed him — that Abū Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān informed him — that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Surplus water must not be sold so that pasture may be sold by means of it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn 'Uthmān al-Nawfalī al-Baṣrī"","" with the wording of sale in this narration"","" and in it is evidence for the correctness of the interpretation of al-Shāfi'ī"","" may Allah have mercy upon him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim"","" 1566]"""""
"11067","(11062) Abū 'Abdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris said — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn 'Affān narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Ādam narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn 'Ayāsh narrated to us — from Shu'ayb ibn Shu'ayb, the brother of 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb — from his brother 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb — from Sālim, the freedman of 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr, who said: \They gave me thirty thousand for the surplus water of his land at al-Waḥṭ.\"" So I wrote to 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr"","" and he wrote back to me: \""Do not sell it"","" but establish your watering place"","" then give water to the nearest and then the nearest"","" for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the sale of surplus water.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""""
"11068","(11063) Abū Sa'īd ibn Abī 'Amr narrated to us — Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī narrated to us — Yaḥyá ibn Ādam narrated to us — Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us — from Ibn Jurayj — from 'Aṭā': \He was asked about selling water in water-skins. He said: 'This is different — a man draws it and carries it. There is no harm in it"","" for it is not like the surplus water that flows away into the ground.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its narrators are trustworthy (thiqāt) and its chain is connected (muttaṣil)]"""""
"11069","(11064) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan said — Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Anas ibn 'Iyāḍ narrated to us — from Bukayr ibn Mismaar — from Ziyād, the freedman of Sa'd — that he asked 'Abdullāh ibn 'Abbās and Marwān al-Ḥakam about selling copies of the Qur'ān for trade therein. They said: \We do not see that it should be made a commodity of trade. But whatever you have produced by your own hands"","" there is no harm in it.\""\n\nIbn Wahb said"","" and Mālik said to me regarding the sale and purchase of copies of the Qur'ān: \""There is no harm in it.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11070","(11065) 'Alī ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn 'Abdullāh ibn Bazī' narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn al-'Alā' narrated to us — Ja'far ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Alī from his father — from 'Alī ibn al-Ḥusayn — from Ibn 'Abbās, who said: \Copies of the Qur'ān used not to be sold. Rather"","" a man would bring his parchment to the Prophet ﷺ"","" and a man would stand and seek reward and write"","" then another would stand and write"","" until the copy of the Qur'ān was completed.\"" [Irwā' al-Ghalīl"","" 1385]"""""
"11071","(11066) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrūwī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: Layth informed us, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Purchase the muṣḥaf"","" but do not sell it.\"" [Weak. Al-Majmūʿ by al-Nawawī"","" 2429]"""""
"11072","(11067) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Abū Bishr informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, the like of it, as his (Ibn ʿAbbās's) statement. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr, 3962]"
"11073","(11068) He said: And Saʿīd narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Zakarīyāʾ informed us, from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: Ibn ʿUmar said: \I wish that the hands of those who sell the maṣāḥif would be cut off.\"" [Sunan Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"","" no. 120]"""""
"11074","(11069) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Jābir, from Sālim, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar used to pass by the sellers of maṣāḥif and say: 'What a wretched trade!'\"""""""
"11075","(11070) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrūwī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Iyās al-Jurayrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaqīq, who said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to dislike the selling of maṣāḥif.\"" [Kitāb al-Umm"","" 1767]"""""
"11076","(11071) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ informed us, who said: al-Shāfiʿī said, from Ibn ʿUlayyah, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — that he disliked the buying and selling of maṣāḥif.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \They — meaning some of the Iraqis — do not say this; they see no harm in selling and buying them. And among the people are those who see no harm in buying them"","" but we dislike their sale.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This dislike (karāhah) is of the category of Tanzīh (disliked but not forbidden)"","" out of reverence for the muṣḥaf"","" lest it be debased by being sold or made a commodity of trade.\n\nAnd it is narrated from Ibn Masʿūd that he permitted it"","" but its chain of narration is weak. And the statement of Ibn ʿAbbās — 'Purchase the muṣḥaf and do not sell it' — if it is authentically reported from him"","" it indicates that selling it is permissible (jāʾiz) while being disliked (makrūh). And Allah knows best.\"""""""
"11077","(11072) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Ḥafṣ al-Tūmanī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṭufāwī informed us, from Layth, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \He (Ibn Masʿūd) permitted the selling of maṣāḥif.\"" Abū Aḥmad said: \""I did not write this except from ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAbbās through this chain of narration.\"" The Shaykh said: \""This chain of narration is weak.\"" [Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil]"""""
"11078","(11073) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Bishr informed us: Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir informed us: Saʿīd said: \I spoke to Maṭar al-Warrāq about the selling of maṣāḥif"","" and he said: 'Do you forbid me from selling maṣāḥif"","" when the great scholar — or he said"","" the great jurist — of this ummah"","" al-Ḥasan and al-Shaʿbī"","" saw no harm in it?'\"" [Al-Maʿrifah wa al-Tārīkh"","" 312]"""""
"11079","(11074) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrūwī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Hushaym informed us: Yūnus informed us, from al-Ḥasan, that he used to see no harm in the selling and buying of maṣāḥif.\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Dāwūd informed us, from al-Shaʿbī, that he was asked about that, and he said: \He is only seeking the price of its paper and the wage of its transcription.\""\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-ʿAmmī informed us: Mālik ibn Dīnār informed us"","" saying: \""Jābir ibn Zayd came to me while I was writing"","" and I said: 'What do you think of my craft"","" O Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ?' He said: 'How excellent is your craft! You are transcribing the Book of Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" from page to page"","" from verse to verse"","" and from word to word. This is ḥalāl — there is no harm in it.'\""\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad informed us: Mālik ibn Dīnār informed us"","" that ʿIkrimah sold a muṣḥaf of his"","" and that al-Ḥasan used to see no harm in it."""""
"11080","(11075) Abū al-Qāsim Hibat Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭabarī informed us in Baghdad: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān ibn Naḍlah informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī informed us, from Dāwūd ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Tammār, from his father, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I shall certainly meet Allah"","" Mighty and Majestic"","" before I give anyone the wealth of another without his goodwill. Indeed"","" sale is only by mutual consent.\"" [Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr"","" and Sunan Ibn Mājah"","" 2185"","" and Ibn Ḥibbān"","" 4967]"""""
"11081","(11076) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Hushaym informed us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Rustum informed us; a shaykh from Banī Tamīm informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib addressed us with a sermon — or he said: ʿAlī said: \There shall come upon the people a biting era in which the wealthy man shall bite his hands over what he possesses"","" though he has not been commanded to do so.\"" Allah"","" exalted be His praise"","" said: {And do not forget graciousness among you} [al-Baqarah: 237]. In it"","" the wicked shall be elevated"","" the virtuous shall be humiliated"","" and the compelled shall be made to sell — whereas the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the sale of the compelled"","" the sale of uncertainty (gharar)"","" and the sale of fruit before it has ripened.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11082","(11077) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ḥāmid ibn Shuʿayb informed us; Surayj ibn Yūnus informed us; Hushaym informed us, from Abū ʿĀmir al-Muzanī; a shaykh from Banī Tamīm informed us, saying: ʿAlī addressed us with a sermon and said: \There shall come upon the people an era in which the wicked shall be given precedence over the virtuous"","" and the compelled shall be made to sell — whereas the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade the sale of the compelled"","" the sale of uncertainty (gharar)"","" and the sale of fruit before it ripens.\""\n\nThis Abū ʿĀmir is Ṣāliḥ ibn Rustum al-Khazzāṣ al-Baṣrī. It has been narrated through various chains from ʿAlī and Ibn ʿUmar"","" all of which are not strong. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11083","(11078) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Khurrādh informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān informed us, from Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿUmar, from Muṭarrif, from Bashīr ibn Muslim, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let no man ride the sea except one who is a warrior (ghāzī)"","" a performer of ʿumrah"","" or a pilgrim (ḥājj)"","" for beneath the sea is fire"","" and beneath the fire is sea"","" and beneath the sea is fire. And let not the property of a Muslim be purchased under compulsion (ḍaghtah).\"" [Weak]"""""
"11084","(11079) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Haytham al-Shaʿrānī and Aḥmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadī both said: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Zakarīyāʾ informed us, from Muṭarrif, from Bashīh Abū ʿAbdullāh, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let none ride the sea except a pilgrim"","" a performer of ʿumrah"","" or a warrior in the cause of Allah"","" for beneath the sea is fire"","" and beneath the fire is sea.\"" And he said: \""Let nothing be purchased from one under the compulsion of authority (sulṭān).\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Shaʿrānī.\n\nIt has also been said that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated with this chain from Bishr Abū ʿAbdullāh"","" from Bashīr ibn Muslim"","" from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr. [Weak]"""""
"11085","(11080) The shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us; Sharīk informed us, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Sharīḥ, who said: \Marriage and sale are not valid over one who is under compulsion (muḍṭahad).\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"","" no. 2156]"""""
"11086","(11081) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq informed us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir informed us, from Shuʿbah, from Qatādah, from Abū Ḥassān al-Aʿraj, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I bear witness that a salaf transaction (a loan with a stipulated term) is something which Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has made lawful and permitted. He recited this verse: {O you who believe"","" when you contract a debt for a specified term"","" write it down} [al-Baqarah: 282].\"" [Musnad al-Shāfiʿī"","" no. 1391]"""""
"11087","(11082) He said: And Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū Ḥudhayfah informed us, from Sufyān, from Abū Ḥayyān, from a man, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding this verse: {O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a specified term} — he said: \It refers to wheat in a known measure.\"""""""
"11088","(11083) Abū Zakarīyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Manīʿī informed us; ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad informed us; Sufyān informed us, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Kathīr, from Abū al-Minhāl, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) arrived in Madīnah while the people were engaging in salaf transactions in dates for two or three years. He said: 'Whoever makes a salaf transaction in dates"","" let him do so in a known measure"","" a known weight"","" and for a known term.'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAmr al-Nāqid. In the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"","" it is: \""two years and three"",""\"" and he said: \""for a known term\"" — without the conjunction (wāw). In the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \""and a known term.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""I memorized it as I have described from Sufyān many times"","" and the one I trust informed me from Sufyān that he said: 'Everything I said"","" he said regarding the term: for a known term.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ṣadaqah"","" Qutaybah"","" and ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī. And Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAmr al-Nāqid"","" all of them from Sufyān"","" and they said: \""for a known term.\""\n\nAnd likewise Sufyān al-Thawrī said it"","" from Ibn Abī Najīḥ. [Agreed upon]"""""
"11089","(11084) Abū Zakarīyāʾ ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: He heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \I see no harm in a salaf transaction involving silver"","" whether it is in cash (naqd) or on credit.\"" [Musnad al-Shāfiʿī"","" no. 617]"""""
"11090","(11085) He said: And Saʿīd informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, that Ibn ʿUmar used to permit it."
"11091","(11086) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Nāʿif from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar that he said: There is no harm in a man advancing payment (salaf) for specified food at a known price for a stipulated term, provided it is not in crops whose ripeness has not yet appeared or fruit whose ripeness has not yet appeared.\n\nThe Shaykh said: By this he means—and Allah knows best—that he should not advance payment for specific crops by their very identity or specific fruit by their very identity, for that is not permissible, because the sale of specific fruits still on the trees is only permissible once ripeness has appeared in them."
"11092","(11087) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb from Qatāda from Abī Ḥassān al-Aʿraj from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: I bear witness that a salaf (forward sale) guaranteed for a stipulated term has been made lawful by Allah in His Book and He has given permission for it. Then he recited: \O you who believe"","" when you contract a debt for a stipulated term"","" write it down.\"" [al-Baqarah: 282]"""""
"11093","(11088) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Musaddad informed us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated, saying: We discussed before Ibrāhīm the matter of pledging (rahn) and the guarantor (qabīl) in salam (forward sale). So Ibrāhīm said: Al-Aswad narrated to us from ʿĀʾishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) purchased food from a Jew on deferred payment and pledged his coat of mail as security. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq from al-Makhzūmī from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. (T) And it has been narrated to us from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās that he saw no harm in a pledge (rahn) and a guarantor (qabīl) in a salaf (forward sale). [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī, Muslim 1603]"
"11094","(11089) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Ibn Jurayj informed me that ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed him from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar that he saw no harm in a pledge (rahn) and a guarantor (ḥamīl) accompanying a salaf (forward sale)."
"11095","(11090) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyābī narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Sulaymān informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzayma narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us. They both said: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Kathīr from Abī al-Minhāl from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Madīnah while the people were engaging in forward sales (salaf) for fruits for two and three years. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Engage in forward sales for fruits by a known measure for a known term.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym. The ḥadīth of al-Firyābī is similar"","" except that he said: \""By a known measure and a known weight for a known term.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"","" and he said: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd said: Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ"","" and he said: \""By a known measure and a known weight.\"" Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī from Sufyān al-Thawrī."""""
"11096","(11091) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar informed us, Shuʿba informed us.\n\n(H) And Ibn Kathīr narrated to us, Shuʿba informed me, Muḥammad or ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mujāld said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād and Abū Burda differed regarding salaf, so they sent me to Ibn Abī Awfā. I asked him, and he said: \We used to engage in forward sales (salaf) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" Abū Bakr"","" and ʿUmar"","" in wheat"","" barley"","" dates"","" and raisins.\"" Ibn Kathīr added: \""To a people who did not have it in their possession.\"" Then they both agreed"","" so I asked Ibn Abza"","" and he said the same.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 2243]"""""
"11097","(11092) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Ḥasan, that is Ibn Sufyān, narrated to us, Ḥibbān ibn Mūsā informed us, ʿAbdullāh, that is Ibn al-Mubārak, informed us, Sufyān narrated from al-Shaybānī from Muḥammad ibn Abī Mujāld who said: Abū Burda and ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaddād sent me to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abza and ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā. I asked them both about salaf, and they said: \We used to obtain war spoils with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" and the Nabateans of Shām would come to us"","" so we would engage in forward sales with them in wheat"","" barley"","" and oil for a stipulated term.\"" It was asked: \""Did they have crops"","" or did they not have crops?\"" He said: \""We did not ask them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from Ibn al-Mubārak. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 2243]"""""
"11098","(11093) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiya narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd.\n\n(H) And Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that he saw no harm in a man selling something on deferred payment when he did not have its original (i.e., the goods) in his possession."
"11099","(11094) And al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Saʿīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, the same as it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11100","(11095) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us.\n\n(H) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us, Khālid ibn Makhlad, that is al-Qaṭawānī, narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmayr narrated to us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwa narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) purchased a camel from a Bedouin in exchange for a wasq of ʿajwa dates. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked his household for dates but did not find any, so he mentioned that to the Bedouin. The Bedouin cried out: \What treachery!\"" The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Nay"","" you"","" O enemy of Allah"","" are the treacherous one!\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Leave him"","" for the one who has a right has a claim to speak.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a message to Khawla bint Ḥakīm and dispatched the Bedouin with the messenger"","" saying: \""Tell her: I purchased this camel from this Bedouin in exchange for a wasq of ʿajwa dates"","" but I did not find them at my household"","" so advance (as salaf) a wasq of ʿajwa dates to this Bedouin on my behalf.\"" When the Bedouin received his due"","" he returned to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \""Have you received it?\"" He said: \""Yes"","" and you fulfilled and gave generously.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Those are the best of people—those who fulfill their obligations and give generously.\"" In the narration of Abū al-Azhar: Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmayr"","" a client of Banī Asad"","" narrated to me; Hishām ibn ʿUrwa narrated to me.\n\nThis ḥadīth has also been narrated in an abridged form from Ḥammād ibn Salama from Hishām ibn ʿUrwa. [Musnad Aḥmad 6/268"","" 26780]"""""
"11101","(11096) Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed us, orally: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated to us: from Jam'i ibn Shaddad, from Tariq ibn 'Abd Allah al-Muharibi, who said:\n\n\I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) pass by the market of Dhi al-Majaz while I was engaged in a transaction of mine. He passed by wearing a red garment (hullah hamra')"","" and I heard him say: 'O people"","" say: There is no god but Allah"","" and you will prosper.' And a man was following him"","" pelting him with stones"","" his ankles bleeding"","" while he was saying: 'O people"","" do not obey this one"","" for he is a liar.' I said: 'Who is this?' It was said: 'This is a young man from the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib.' I said: 'Then who is this one pelting him with stones?' It was said: 'His uncle"","" 'Abd al-'Uzza — Abu Lahab ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib.'\n\nWhen Allah made Islam prevail"","" we set out from al-Rabadhah"","" and with us was a woman of ours"","" until we encamped near Madinah. While we were sitting"","" a man came to us wearing two garments. He greeted us and said: 'Where are you people from?' We said: 'From al-Rabadhah"","" and we have with us a red camel.' He said: 'Will you sell me the camel?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'For how much?' We said: 'For such-and-such a measure (sa') of dates.' He said: 'I have taken it.' And he did not insist on exacting the full measure. He took hold of the camel's halter and led it away until it disappeared behind the walls of Madinah. Some of us said to others: 'Do you know the man?' None of us knew him. The people reproached one another"","" saying: 'You give your camel to someone you do not know!' The woman among us said: 'Do not reproach one another"","" for we have seen the face of a man who will never betray you. I have seen nothing more resembling the moon on the night of the full moon than his face.'\n\nWhen evening came"","" a man came to us and said: 'Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Are you the ones who came from al-Rabadhah?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to you. He commands you to eat of these dates until you are satisfied"","" and to measure until you receive your full due.' So we ate of the dates until we were satisfied"","" and we measured until we received our full due.\n\nThe next morning we arrived in Madinah"","" and lo"","" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing"","" addressing the people from the pulpit. I heard him say: 'The hand of the giver is the upper hand. Begin with those whom you support: your mother"","" your father"","" your sister"","" your brother"","" and then the nearest"","" the nearest.' Then a man from the Ansar said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" these are the Banu Tha'labah ibn Yarbu'"","" who killed so-and-so during the Jahiliyyah. Avenge our blood for us.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his hands until I could see the whiteness of his armpits"","" and he said: 'A mother shall not be made to suffer on account of her child. A mother shall not be made to suffer on account of her child.' And he mentioned the hadith.\""\n\n(T) It was also narrated by Abu Janab al-Kalbi from Jam'i ibn Shaddad. [Sahih. Ibn Khuzaymah no. 195"","" Sahih Ibn Hibban 6562]"""""
"11102","(11097) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — among the last narrators they said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik informed us.\n\n(And) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us: Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hasan al-Faqih — narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us in al-Basrah: 'Abd Allah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi', who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) borrowed a young camel (bakr). Then camels from the charity (sadaqah) came to him"","" and he commanded me to repay the man his young camel. I said: 'I did not find among the camels anything except a choice (khiyar) four-year-old camel (rubi'iyyan).' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Give it to him"","" for the best of people are those who are most excellent in repayment.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb from Malik. [Sahih Muslim 1600]"""""
"11103","(11098) Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya — informed us: Abu Sahl — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Nahwi — narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said:\n\n\A man was owed a camel of a certain age by the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He came to demand it"","" and the Prophet said: 'Give it to him.' They searched but found only a camel of an age greater than the one owed. He said: 'Give it to him.' The man said: 'You have given me my full due — may Allah give you your full due.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'The best of you are those who are most excellent in repayment.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Sufyan.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \""This is a firmly established hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"","" and I act according to it. In it is the fact that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) guaranteed a camel by description. In this is evidence that it is permissible to guarantee an entire animal by description.\"" [Sahih. Al-Bukhari and Muslim 1601]"""""
"11104","(11099) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajaniyy informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali, that:\n\n\'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) sold a camel of his called 'Usayfir for twenty camels"","" to be delivered at a fixed term.\"""""""
"11105","(11100) He said: And Malik narrated to us from Nafi', that:\n\n\'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar purchased a riding camel for four she-camels"","" guaranteed by him"","" to be delivered to its owner in al-Rabadhah.\"""""""
"11106","(11101) He said: And Malik narrated to us: He asked Ibn Shihab about the sale of animals — two for one — to a deferred term. He said: \There is no harm in that.\"""""""
"11107","(11102) He said: And Malik narrated to us from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that:\n\n\He used to say: 'There is no usury (riba) in animals.'\"""""""
"11108","(11103) And Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamirawayh narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: 'Ubaydah — meaning Ibn Humayd — narrated to us from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas, that:\n\n\He used to see no harm in a salam (forward sale) in animals.\"""""""
"11109","(11104) He said: And Sa'id narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Yunus narrated to us from al-Hasan, that:\n\n\He used to see no harm in a salam (forward sale) in animals"","" provided the age was known and the term was fixed.\"""""""
"11110","(11105) He said: And Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us from 'Ammar al-Duhni, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Mas'ud, that:\n\n\He disapproved of a salam (forward sale) in animals.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Hammad from Ibrahim from Ibn Mas'ud."""""
"11111","(11106) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us — Saʿīd narrated from Abū Maʿshar, from Ibrāhīm, that Ibn Masʿūd did not see any harm in salam (forward sale) in all things for a specified term, except in animals."
"11112","(11107) And in what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās, from al-Rabīʿ, from al-Shāfiʿī: that one of those who spoke with him on this issue said to him, \We only disliked salam in animals because Ibn Masʿūd disliked it.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said"","" \""This narration from him is munqaṭiʿ (discontinued). And al-Shaʿbī"","" who is greater than the one who narrated the dislike from him"","" claims that he only entered into a salam for a specific stud camel"","" and this is disliked (makrūh) among us and among everyone — this is the sale of malāqiḥ (pregnant camels) and maḍāmīn (the offspring in their wombs)"","" or both.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: Al-Shāfiʿī means by the narration of the one who narrated from Ibn Masʿūd as discontinued in the matter of dislike the narration of Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī. As for the narration of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn Masʿūd"","" it is also discontinued"","" for Saʿīd ibn Jubayr did not meet Ibn Masʿūd. It has also been narrated from him from Ḥudhayfah.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And I said to Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan: 'You informed me from Abū Yūsuf"","" from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib"","" from Abū al-Bakhtarī"","" that some cousins of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān came to a valley and did something to a man's camels — they cut off the milk of his camels and killed his young ones. So the man came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān while Ibn Masʿūd was with him"","" and he was pleased with the ruling of Ibn Masʿūd. He ruled that the man be given camels like his camels and young ones like his young ones. ʿUthmān carried this out.' Thus it is narrated from Ibn Masʿūd that he adjudicated in the case of an animal with a similar animal as a debt"","" because when he gave the ruling in al-Madīnah and the man was given the animals in his valley"","" it was a debt. And you wish to narrate from ʿUthmān that he agreed with his opinion"","" while you narrate from al-Masʿūdī"","" from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" who said: 'A salam was made for ʿAbd Allāh regarding some slave-girls"","" one of whose masters was Abū Ziyādah or Abū Zāʾidah"","" our mawlā.' And you narrate from Ibn ʿAbbās that he permitted salam in animals"","" and from another man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAl-Shaykh said: And it has been narrated from ʿUmar that he mentioned among the categories of ribā (usury) salam made in age (i.e."","" specifying the age of animals). Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar said: al-Masʿūdī informed us from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said — and he mentioned it — and this is munqaṭiʿ (discontinued)."""""
"11113","(11108) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī narrated to us — Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Shaqīq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let no woman sleep with another woman and then describe her to her husband as though he were looking at her.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash. [Bukhārī 5240"","" 5241]"""""
"11114","(11109) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us — Sufyān and Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kathīr, from Abū al-Minhāl, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ came to al-Madīnah while the people were entering into salam contracts in dates for two or three years. He said: 'Whoever enters into a salam in dates"","" let him do so with a known measure"","" a known weight"","" and a known term.'\"" Al-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Sufyān"","" and from ʿAmr ibn Zurārah and others from Ismāʿīl. And we have narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he prohibited the sale of al-kāliʾ bi-l-kāliʾ (deferred debt for deferred debt)"","" and from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: \""I see no harm in salam when silver (wariq) is paid in cash for something.\"""""""
"11115","(11110) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Shuʿbah said: ʿAmr informed me from Abū al-Bakhtarī, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿUmar about salam in palm trees. He said: 'The sale of palm trees has been prohibited until their fruit shows signs of ripening.' So I asked Ibn ʿAbbās. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the sale of palm trees until one may eat from them or they may be eaten"","" and until they may be weighed.'\"" Shuʿbah said: \""I said to a man in the gathering"","" 'What is meant by weighing?' He said"","" 'Until they may be estimated (yuḥzar).'\"" Al-Bukhārī recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1537]"""""
"11116","(11111) And it was narrated from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār, from Ghundar, from Shuʿbah, except that in the narration of Ibn ʿUmar he said: \ʿUmar prohibited the sale of fruit until it ripens"","" and he prohibited the sale of silver for gold on credit (nasaʾan) with immediate payment (bi-nājiz).\"" And in the explanation he said: \""I asked"","" 'What is meant by weighing?' A man who was with him said"","" 'Until it may be estimated (yuḥzar).'\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated both of them. And Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār without the narration of Ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2250 and Muslim 1537]"""""
"11117","(11112) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq, who said: \I heard a man from the people of Najrān say: 'I asked Ibn ʿUmar about salam in palm trees.' He said: 'As for salam in palm trees"","" a man entered into a salam for another man's palm trees"","" but they did not bear fruit that year. He mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ"","" who said: \""Why do you consume his wealth?\"" So he commanded him to return it to him. Then he prohibited salam in palm trees until their fruit shows signs of ripening.'\"""""""
"11118","(11113) Abū Saʿid al-Mālinī narrated to us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from a man from Najrān, from Ibn ʿUmar, that a man entered into a salam with another man for palm trees, but they did not produce anything that year. They brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \Why do you consider his wealth lawful for yourself? Return it to him.\"" Then he said: \""Do not enter into salam for palm trees until their fruit shows signs of ripening.\"""""""
"11119","(11114) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Sarī narrated to us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ḥamzah ibn Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām said: \When Allah intended guidance for Zayd ibn Saʿnah\"" — and he mentioned the ḥadīth until he said: \""Zayd ibn Saʿnah said: 'O Muḥammad"","" would you sell me known quantities of dates for a known term from the garden of Banī Fulān?' He said: 'No"","" O Jew"","" but I will sell you known quantities of dates for such and such a term"","" but I will not specify the garden of Banī Fulān.' I said: 'Yes.' So he made a sale with me. I opened my purse and gave him eighty dinārs for known quantities of dates for such and such a term.'\"""""""
"11120","(11115) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us — Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \There is no salam tied to the time of the stipend (al-ʿaṭāʾ)"","" nor to the time of harvest (al-ḥaṣād)"","" nor to the time of threshing (al-undur)"","" nor to the time of pressing (al-ʿaṣīr). Rather"","" set for it a fixed term.\"""""""
"11121","(11116) 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Najjār al-Muqri' informed us in Kūfah; he said: Abū Ja'far ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; he said: al-Qāḍī Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; he said: Qabīṣah narrated from Sufyān — meaning al-Thawrī — from 'Abd al-Karīm from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): He (Ibn 'Abbās) disliked salam (forward sale) being stipulated until the time of harvest, or until the grain fully ripens, or until it is gathered into the threshing floor. However, he said: \Specify it by a named month (i.e."","" a definite term).\"""""""
"11122","(11117) And 'Abd al-Wāḥid informed us; he said: Ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; he said: Ibrāhīm narrated to us; he said: Qabīṣah narrated from Sufyān.\n\n(Ḥ) And 'Abd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdād; he said: Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; he said: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; he said: 'Abd al-Razzāq informed us; he said: al-Thawrī narrated from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Nubayḥ from Abū Sa'īd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Salam (forward sale) — however its price is determined — constitutes ribā (usury). However"","" (it is permissible with) a known measure (of weight/volume) to a known term"","" and increase (the quantity) as much as you are able.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of 'Abd al-Razzāq: \""Advance payment (as-salaf) in a known measure to a known term"","" and increase in it as much as you are able.\"""""""
"11123","(11118) Abū al-Fatḥ al-'Umarī, the Shaykh, informed us; he said: 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us; he said: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us; he said: 'Alī ibn al-Ja'd informed us; he said: Shu'bah narrated from Anas ibn Sīrīn, who said: I heard Abū 'Ubaydah narrating from his father: He (his father) used to prohibit the sale of food at the price of the threshing floor (i.e., at the unharvested crop's estimated price)."
"11124","(11119) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; he said: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — Abū al-Shaykh — informed us; he said: 'Abd Allāh ibn Bundār ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḍabbī narrated to us; he said: Abū 'Abd Allāh Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; he said: al-Nu'mān ibn 'Abd al-Salām narrated from Ibn Jurayj from 'Amr ibn Dīnār from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both): He ('Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar) used to dislike that a person purchase (something) and say, \I will pay you when I am in ease (i.e."","" when funds become available to me).\"""""""
"11125","(11120) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; he said: Abū 'Abd Allāh ibn Ya'qūb informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb informed us; he said: Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us; he said: Kulaib ibn Wā'il narrated, saying: I said to Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): \A man owed me some dirhams"","" so I went to him to collect the debt. He said"","" 'I do not have (the money) with me"","" but record it against me as food (payment) until the harvest.' He (Ibn 'Umar) said: 'That is not permissible (lā yaṣluḥ).'\"""""""
"11126","(11121) As for the ḥadīth which Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us — he said: 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far narrated to us; he said: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; he said: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; he said: Shu'bah narrated from 'Umārah ibn Abī Ḥafṣah from 'Ikrimah, who said: 'Ā'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \A merchant arrived with merchandise. I said"","" 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" if only you were to set aside these two coarse garments of yours and send to so-and-so the merchant so that he might sell you two garments"","" to be paid for when ease (of funds) comes to you.' So the Prophet (ﷺ) sent (word) to him: 'Send me two garments"","" to be paid for when ease (of funds) comes to me.' He said"","" 'Muḥammad wishes to take my property.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'By Allah"","" they know well that I am the most trustworthy of them in fulfilling trusts and the most God-fearing of them before Allah.' And similar to this.\""\n\nThis (incident) is understood to mean that he (the Prophet ﷺ) proposed the sale to be paid for at the time of ease"","" but did not actually contract a binding sale upon that basis. And even if he had agreed to that"","" it would have been more appropriate for him (the Prophet ﷺ) to stipulate a definite time"","" or to contract the sale in absolute terms and then settle it whenever ease came. And Allah knows best."""""
"11127","(11122) Abū 'Amr al-Adīb informed us; he said: Abū Bakr al-Ismā'īlī informed us; he said: al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawārib narrated to us; he said: 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us; he said: Sulaymān al-Shaybānī informed us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Mujālad narrated, saying: Abū Burdah and 'Abd Allāh ibn Shaddād sent me to 'Abd Allāh ibn Abī Awfā to ask him: \Did you used to engage in salam (forward sale) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in wheat"","" barley"","" and raisins?\"" So I asked him"","" and he said: \""We used to engage in salam with the Nabataeans of Shām in wheat"","" barley"","" and raisins"","" in a known measure to a known term.\"" I said: \""Was it with those who had cultivated land?\"" He said: \""We did not ask them about that.\"" He (Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Mujālad) said: \""Then they sent me to 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā"","" and they said: 'Ask him: Did the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to engage in salam during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in wheat"","" barley"","" and raisins?'\"" He said: \""The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to engage in salam in wheat"","" barley"","" and raisins with the Nabataeans of Shām"","" in a known measure to a known term"","" and they did not ask them"","" 'Do you have a cultivated crop or not?'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl from 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī"","" and he said: \""oil\"" instead of \""raisins.\"" And Shu'bah narrated it from Ibn Abī Mujālad"","" and he said: \""and raisins or dates"",""\"" expressing doubt regarding raisins and dates. And Zā'idah narrated it from al-Shaybānī from Muḥammad ibn Abī Mujālad"","" and he said: \""and dates and raisins.\"" [Narrated by al-Bukhārī]"""""
"11128","(11123) Abū Ḥāziim al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; they both said: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; he said: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; he said: Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; he said: Hushaym narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding salam (forward sale) in coarse cotton cloth (al-karābīs): He said: \If it is a known measure to a known term"","" then there is no harm in it.\"""""""
"11129","(11124) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; he said: Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us; he said: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from 'Aṭā' (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \There is no harm in engaging in salam (forward sale) in meat.\"""""""
"11130","(11125) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; he said: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; he said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; he said: Shaybān narrated from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr from 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakrah from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought bread and oil"","" and he said: 'By Allah"","" O stomach"","" you shall subsist upon bread and oil as long as ghee is sold by the awqiyyah (plural of ūqiyyah).'\"" [Narrated by Ibn Sa'īd"","" 3/314]"""""
"11131","(11126) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi informed us: Abu Usamah narrated from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \The similitude of a righteous companion and an evil companion is like that of a musk-carrier and a bellows-blower. The musk-carrier will either give you a gift"","" or you may purchase from him"","" or you will find from him a pleasant fragrance. As for the bellows-blower"","" he will either burn your garments"","" or you will find from him a foul odour.\"" [Reported by al-Bukhari and Muslim in their Sahih from Abu Kuraib"","" from Abu Usamamah.]"""""
"11132","(11127) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated — (H) and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us: Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abadi informed us: Musaddad informed us: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Umm Kulthum. Ibn Wahb in his narration said: Umm Kulthum bint Abi Salamah said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah"","" may Allah be pleased with her"","" he said to her: 'I have sent some awqiyyahs of musk and a suit of garments as a gift to the Negus"","" but I think he has died"","" and I believe the gift I sent to him will be returned. If it is returned to me"","" then it shall be yours — or yours (all of you).' And it was as he said: the Negus died"","" and when the gift was returned to him"","" he gave each of his wives an awqiyyah of that musk"","" and he gave the remainder to Umm Salamah"","" and he gave her the suit of garments.\"" In the narration of Musaddad: \""It will be returned to me"","" and if it is returned to me"","" I think he said: 'I shall divide it among you"","" or it shall be yours.'\"" He said: \""And it was as he said.\"" [Weak: Tabaqat Ibn Sa'd 8/96]"""""
"11133","(11128) Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Nazif al-Misri in Makkah informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Kharuf al-Madinii through dictation informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn Sahl al-Marwazi informed us: Yahya ibn Ma'in informed us — (H) and Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-'Abbas Muhammad al-Dawri informed us: Yahya ibn Ma'in informed us: Hafs ibn Ghayath narrated from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever grants a Muslim a respite (in a sale)"","" Allah will pardon his slip.\"" In the narration of al-Misri: \""Whoever grants a remorseful person a respite"","" Allah will pardon him.\"""""""
"11134","(11129) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sam informed us: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi informed us: Malik ibn Anas narrated from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever grants a remorseful person a respite"","" Allah"","" the Most High"","" will pardon him on the Day of Resurrection.\"""""""
"11135","(11130) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran informed us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz through dictation in Makkah informed us: Ishaq al-Farwi narrated it with a similar meaning. He said: And Abu al-Hasan al-Misri informed us: Abu al-'Abbas 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi informed us: Malik narrated from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever grants a Muslim a respite regarding his slip"","" Allah"","" the Most High"","" will grant him a respite on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Abu al-'Abbas said: \""Ishaq used to narrate this hadith from Malik from Sumayy"","" but he narrated it to us from the original of his book from Suhayl.\"" The sheikh said: \""This matn is other than the matn of the hadith of Sumayy"","" and Allah knows best.\"" And it has been narrated from Muhammad ibn Wasi'"","" from Abu Salih."""""
"11136","(11131) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Adami in Makkah informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani al-Busi informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated from Ma'mar, from Muhammad ibn Wasi', from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever grants a remorseful person a respite"","" Allah will grant him a respite on the Day of Resurrection.\"" And he mentioned the hadith."""""
"11137","(11132) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Asad informed us: Sufyan narrated from Salamah ibn Musa, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \If you have made a salam (forward contract)"","" there is no harm in taking some of your salam and some of your principal — that is the recognised practice.\"" And Jabir al-Ju'fi narrated from Nafi'"","" from Ibn 'Umar"","" with the meaning of the statement of Ibn 'Abbas. And the well-known narration from Ibn 'Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with them both"","" is that he disliked that. And we have received the narration from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah and 'Amr ibn Dinar with the meaning of the statement of Ibn 'Abbas. [Reported by Ibn 'Uyaynah"","" Part 41]"""""
"11138","(11133) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khayruwayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Shahab narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he disliked that a sale should be made and then returned, along with the dirhams being returned. In this there is an indication that an iqalah (cancellation of a sale) is a dissolution (faskh), and it is not valid except with the return of the principal. As for al-tawliyyah (selling at cost), it is a sale. Al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Sirin and 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah said this, and likewise al-sharikah (partnership) with us is not permissible in salam before taking possession, in light of the prohibition that has been transmitted against selling food before taking possession."
"11139","(11134) Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani informed us: Rabi' ibn 'Ulayyah narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah, from Hanzalah ibn Qays, from Abu al-Yasar, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever would love that Allah shade him on the Day when there shall be no shade"","" let him grant respite to one in difficulty"","" or remit his debt.\"" [Musnad Ahmad 15095"","" Muslim 3014]"""""
"11140","(11135) Abu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khayruwayh informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us: Sufyan narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar: that Ibn 'Abbas saw no harm in saying: \I shall hasten payment to you"","" and you shall remit some of my debt.\"" And a musnad hadith has been narrated concerning this"","" but in its chain there is weakness. [Ibn Abi Shaybah 22226]"""""
"11141","(11136) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Jawharī in Baghdād informed me; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Madanī narrated to us. [Weak]"
"11142","(11137) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh informed me; Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ Jazarah narrated to us; al-Ḥakam ibn Mūsā Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — and this is his wording — both said: Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī al-Makkī narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Yazīd ibn Rukānah, from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \When the Prophet ﷺ commanded the expulsion of Banī al-Naḍīr from al-Madīnah"","" some of them came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" you have commanded their expulsion"","" yet they have outstanding debts owed by people that have not yet become due.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Remit and expedite"",""' or he said: 'And hasten [the settlement of] your debts.'\"" Al-Wāqidī narrated it in his Sīrah from the nephew of al-Zuhrī"","" from al-Zuhrī"","" from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr. [Al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ"","" 817]"""""
"11143","(11138) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us, from Abū al-Zinād, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, the mawlā of al-Saffāḥ, who said: \I sold cloth to the people of the market on deferred payment"","" then I intended to travel to al-Kūfah. They proposed to me that I reduce their debt and they would pay me immediately. I asked Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him) about that"","" and he said: 'I do not permit you to consume this nor to feed it to others.'\"" [Muwaṭṭaʾ Imām Mālik"","" 1351]"""""
"11144","(11139) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Mālik informed us, from ʿUthmān ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn Khaldah, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh, that Ibn ʿUmar was asked about a man who had a debt owed to him by another man at a fixed term, and the creditor would reduce the debt in exchange for the debtor paying it early. Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) disapproved of that and forbade it. [Muwaṭṭaʾ Imām Mālik, 1352]"
"11145","(11140) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abū al-Minḥāl, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): A man owed me a debt and said to me"","" 'Pay me early and I will reduce your debt for you.' He forbade me from that and said: 'The Commander of the Faithful — meaning ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) — forbade us from selling cash for credit.'\"" A musnad ḥadīth has been narrated on this matter"","" though its chain contains weakness. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 14359]"""""
"11146","(11141) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abū al-Minḥāl, who said: \I asked Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him): A man owed me a debt and said to me"","" 'Pay me early and I will reduce your debt for you.' He forbade me from that and said: 'The Commander of the Faithful — meaning ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) — forbade us from selling cash for credit.'\"" A musnad ḥadīth has been narrated on this matter"","" though its chain contains weakness. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 14359]"""""
"11147","(11142) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAwn, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to dislike this expression: 'I have been entrusted with such-and-such,' and he would say: 'Indeed, trust (al-Islām) belongs to Allah, the Lord of the Worlds.'\ [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" 14115]"""""
"11148","(11143) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Murādī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; Sulaymān — meaning Ibn Bilāl — informed me; al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to me, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" set prices for us.\"" He said: \""Rather"","" supplicate to Allah.\"" Then another man came to him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" set prices.\"" He said: \""Rather"","" it is Allah who raises and lowers [prices]. Indeed"","" I hope to meet Allah with no one having any claim of injustice against me.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in Kitāb al-Sunan from Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān al-Dimashqī"","" from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl. It was also narrated by Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar from al-ʿAlāʾ. [Musnad Aḥmad"","" 8243"","" 8635]"""""
"11149","(11144) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Shabīb al-Fāmī, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī from his original copy, all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl and ʿAffān ibn Muslim both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Thābit, and from Ḥumayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" prices rose. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" prices have become high; set prices for us.' He said: 'Indeed"","" Allah is the One who sets prices"","" the One who withholds"","" the One who extends"","" the Provider. Indeed"","" I hope to meet my Lord with none of you seeking from me any injustice regarding blood or property.'\"" [Musnad Aḥmad"","" 2863"","" 14103]"""""
"11150","(11145) Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Wakīl al-Muḥammadābādī informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated it with a similar wording, except that he said: \Indeed"","" Allah — Mighty and Majestic — is the Creator"","" the One who withholds"","" the One who extends"","" the Provider"","" and the One who sets prices.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in al-Sunan from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"","" from ʿAffān. It has also been narrated on this topic from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet ﷺ. As for the athar which…"""""
"11151","(11146) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Mālik informed me from Yūnus ibn Yūsuf from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah while he was selling raisins in the market. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \Either you raise the price"","" or you remove yourself from our market.\"" This is the abridged version. Its complete narration is found in what al-Shāfiʿī transmitted from al-Dāwardī from Dāwūd ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Tammār from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad from ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him: that he passed by Ḥāṭib at the market of al-Muṣallā"","" and before him were two baskets filled with raisins. He asked him about their price"","" and he priced them at two mudd per dirham. ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said to him: \""I have been informed of a caravan arriving from al-Ṭāʾif carrying raisins"","" and they will base their pricing on yours. Either you raise your price"","" or take your raisins home and sell them however you wish.\"" When ʿUmar returned"","" he reflected upon himself"","" then came to Ḥāṭib at his house and said to him: \""What I said was not a firm command nor a binding ruling from me; it was merely something I intended for the welfare of the people of the city. So sell wherever you wish and however you wish.\"" This is among what Abū Nuʿaym wrote to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Ḥasan al-Isfarāyīnī informed us that Abū ʿAwanah informed them"","" saying: al-Muzanī narrated to us"","" and al-Shāfiʿī narrated it."""""
"11152","(11147) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ, the son of the daughter of Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, informed us: my grandfather narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from Yaḥyā, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib used to narrate that Maʿmar said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever hoards is a transgressor.\"" A man said to Saʿīd: \""But you hoard!\"" Saʿīd replied: \""Maʿmar"","" who used to narrate this hadith"","" also used to hoard.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Muslim 1605]"""""
"11153","(11148) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn informed us: Khālid informed us from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from Maʿmar ibn Abī Maʿmar, one of Banī ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb, who said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \None hoards except a transgressor.\"" I said to Saʿīd: \""But you hoard.\"" He said: \""And Maʿmar used to hoard as well.\"" The wording is that of the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. In the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān"","" the phrase \""one of Banī ʿAdī ibn Kaʿb\"" is absent"","" and at the end he added: ʿAmr said: \""Saʿīd used to hoard oil.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ"","" saying: our companions narrated to me from ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn. The Sheikh"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" said: \""There is a detailed discussion of hoarding mentioned in the books of jurisprudence"","" and my understanding regarding both of them is that they did not hoard in the prohibited manner. And it has been narrated from Abū Umāmah that the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" forbade the hoarding of food.\"""""""
"11154","(11149) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Ghassīlī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād al-Narsī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever hoards intending thereby to inflate prices upon the Muslims is a transgressor"","" and the covenant of Allah is absolved from him.\"" [Narrated by al-Ḥākim]"""""
"11155","(11150) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Zayd ibn Abī Laylā Abū al-Muʿallā al-ʿAdawī narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Ḥasan say: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ziyād entered upon Maʿqil ibn Yasār, and Maʿqil ibn Yasār said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Whoever interferes in any of the prices of the Muslims in order to inflate them against them"","" it is a right upon Allah to cast him into the greatest part of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated it from Zayd"","" adding in it: \""his head foremost.\"" [Musnad al-Ṭayālisī 970]"""""
"11156","(11151) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn Sālim ibn Thawbān from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The one who brings goods to the market is provided for"","" and the hoarder is cursed.\"" ʿAlī ibn Sālim is alone in narrating this from ʿAlī ibn Zayd. Al-Bukhārī said: \""He is not followed up in his hadith.\"""""""
"11157","(11152) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Rabīʿah from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb went out to the market and saw people hoarding with the surplus of their gold. ʿUmar said: \No"","" by the grace of Allah! Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" brings us provision until it arrives at our market"","" whereupon certain people stand and hoard it with the surplus of their gold"","" withholding it from the widows and the poor. When the importers bring goods"","" they sell according to their own terms of manipulation. But whatever importer brings goods"","" carrying them upon the pillar of his liver through winter and summer until he arrives at our market—he is a guest of ʿUmar. Let him sell however Allah wills and hold back however Allah wills.\"" Mālik mentioned it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ as a mursal narration from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"","" may Allah be pleased with him."""""
"11158","(11153) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū Badr Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us: Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us: Ziyād ibn Khaythamah narrated to us from Saʿīd al-Ṭāʾī from ʿAṭiyyah from Abū Saʿīd, who said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When you enter into a salam (forward sale) in something"","" do not transfer it to other than it.\"" In the narration of al-Rūdhbārī: \""Whoever enters into a salam in something"","" let him not transfer it to other than it.\"" Reliance is placed upon the hadith prohibiting the sale of food before taking full possession of it. However"","" ʿAṭiyyah al-ʿAwfī is not used as a basis for legal argument."""""
"11159","(11154) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us from Ḥuṣayn from Muḥammad ibn Zayd ibn Khulaydah, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar about salam (forward sale). I said: \We enter into salam and say: 'If we are given wheat"","" then at such-and-such a price"","" and if we are given dates"","" then at such-and-such a price.'\"" He said: \""Make your salam in each category with a known quantity of silver. If he gives you that"","" [well and good]; otherwise"","" take back your principal and do not exchange it for another commodity.\"" [Musnad Ibn Abī Shaybah 21400]"""""
"11160","(11155) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Abū Hurayrah: that he entered upon Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam while he was in Madīnah, and Marwān had permitted the sale of ṣukūk (promissory notes) with deferred terms before they were fully taken into possession. Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: \You have permitted usury! Food is sold before it is taken into full possession.\"" And he bore witness"","" saying: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah"","" peace and blessings be upon him"","" say: 'Whoever purchases food"","" let him not sell it until he has taken full possession of it.'\"" So Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam reversed that sale. [Muslim 1528]"""""
"11161","(11156) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me, al-Ḍaḥḥāk narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, from Abū Hurayrah that he said to Marwān: \You have permitted the sale of ṣikāk (promissory notes/letters of credit)"","" whereas the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited the sale of food before it is taken into possession.\"" Marwān then delivered a sermon and prohibited their sale. Sulaymān ibn Yasār said: \""I saw the guards seizing them from the hands of the people.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm."""""
"11162","(11157) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād ibn Jaʿfar, that Ibn ʿUmar purchased something and the measure was heaped up for him. Ibn ʿUmar said: \Move your hand and do not hold it over the top; for I am only entitled to what the measure takes.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11163","(11158) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \No pressing down"","" no filling up"","" and no shaking.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11164","(11159) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The measure (mikyāl) is the measure of the people of Madīnah"","" and the weight (wazn) is the weight of the people of Makkah.\"" [Abū Dāwūd 3340"","" al-Nasāʾī 4/224]"""""
"11165","(11160) ʿAlī narrated to us, Sulaymān narrated to us, Ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Sulaymān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd al-Narsī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us. Both said: Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ḥanẓalah, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The measure (mikyāl) is the measure of the people of Makkah"","" and the scale (mīzān) is the scale of the people of Madīnah.\"" Sulaymān said: \""Thus did Abū Aḥmad narrate it"","" reporting it from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" and he contradicted Abū Nuʿaym in the wording of the hadith. The correct narration is what Abū Nuʿaym reported"","" both in chain and wording.\"""""""
"11166","(11161) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris, and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us. They said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak, from Thawr ibn Yazīd, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Measure your food"","" and you will be blessed.\"" Al-Walīd ibn Muslim and Yaḥyya ibn Ḥamzah also narrated it from Thawr ibn Yazīd"","" and they said: \""You will be blessed therein.\"" [Musnad Aḥmad 4145"","" 23904]"""""
"11167","(11162) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥassān al-Anmāṭī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, al-Walīd narrated to us, Thawr narrated. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr narrated to us, al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, al-Manīʿī narrated to us, Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim narrated to us, Yaḥyya ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Thawr ibn Yazīd, and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā, from al-Walīd ibn Muslim."
"11168","(11163) Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī also narrated it. He said: Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us from Thawr ibn Yazīd, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Miqdām. Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us, al-Manīʿī narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11169","(11164) Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd also narrated it from Baḥīr ibn Saʿd, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Measure your food"","" and you will be blessed therein.\"" Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī narrated it to us in Baghdād"","" Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us"","" ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Bazzāz narrated to us"","" ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us"","" Baqiyyah narrated"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11170","(11165) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Yazīd al-Naḥwī narrated that ʿIkrimah narrated to him from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) arrived in Madīnah, the people were the most dishonest in measure. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \Woe to those who give less [than due]\"" (al-Muṭaffifīn"","" 83:1). Thereafter they improved their measuring. [Ibn Mājah 2223]"""""
"11171","(11166) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Raḥabī narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O company of merchants"","" you have been entrusted with a matter in which the preceding nations were destroyed — namely"","" the measure and the scale.\"" Abū ʿAlī Ḥanash narrated it as a raised (marfūʿ) hadith"","" while others narrated it as a stopped (mawqūf) hadith from Ibn ʿAbbās through another chain."""""
"11172","(11167) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Sālim, meaning Ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, who said: I heard Kurayb say: Ibn ʿAbbās said: \O company of non-Arabs"","" Allah has entrusted you with two matters by which the generations before you were destroyed — the measure and the scale.\"""""""
"11173","(11168) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Muḥārib ibn Dithār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) purchased a camel from me and gave me extra (overpaid). Those dirhams remained with me until they were lost on the day of al-Ḥarrah. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2097 and Muslim 715]"
"11174","(11169) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, meaning al-Muqriʾ, said: I heard Sufyān al-Thawrī narrate from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Suwayd ibn Qays, who said: I and Makhrafah al-ʿAbdī brought cloth from Baḥrayn or Hajar. When we were at Minā, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us and purchased a pair of trousers from me. He said: There was a weigher there who weighed for a fee. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) paid him the price and then said to him: \Weigh and give extra (make it overweight).\"" Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ likewise narrated it from Simāk. [Musnad Aḥmad 4/352]"""""
"11175","(11170) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Qays narrated it, except that he said: \Cloth from Hajar. I sold the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) a pair of trousers"","" and there was a weigher there who weighed for a fee. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Weigh and give extra (make it overweight).'\"" Shuʿbah contradicted them both."""""
"11176","(11171) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk, who said: I heard Abū Ṣafwān Mālik ibn ʿUmayr say: I sold the Prophet (ﷺ) a pair of trousers before the Hijrah for three dirhams. He weighed for me and gave extra (overpaid)."
"11177","(11172) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar and Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm, both close in meaning, said: Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Abī Ṣafwān ibn ʿUmayrah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Makkah before he emigrated, and I sold him a pair of trousers. He weighed and gave extra (overpaid). Abū Dāwūd said: Qays narrated it as Sufyān said. The position of Sufyān is the correct one. Abū Dāwūd said: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Shuʿbah, who said: \Sufyān was more precise (aḥfaẓ) than me.\"""""""
"11178","(11173) Abū Manṣūr al-Baghdādī the jurist, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān, Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah, and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣaffār informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Najīd narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Kajjī narrated to us: al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Faḍāʾ narrated from his father, from ʿAlqamah ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade breaking the lawful currency of the Muslims circulating among them, except in the case of necessity — that a dirham be broken to make silver, or a dīnār be broken to make gold."
"11179","(11174) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān the trustworthy narrator in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Khālid, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from Ḥudhayfah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a house and does not purchase another house with its price"","" no blessing will be in it or in anything from its price.\"" [al-Ṣaḥīḥah 2327]"""""
"11180","(11175) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn Ḥātim narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us: Abū Ḥamzah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, from his brother Saʿīd ibn Ḥurayth, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a house or property and does not spend its price on something similar"","" no blessing will be in it.\"" [al-Ṣaḥīḥah 2327]"""""
"11181","(11176) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādhī narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Ḥanafī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir narrated to me: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr narrated from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth from his brother Saʿīd ibn Ḥurayth, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever sells a house or property should know that it is likely that no blessing will remain in its price unless he invests it in something similar.\"""""""
"11182","(11177) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān al-Ghulābī narrated to me: A shaykh from Banī Tamīm narrated that Ibn ʿUyaynah said regarding the interpretation of this hadith — \Whoever sells a house and does not purchase another house from its price"","" no blessing will be in its price\"" — Sufyān said: \""Indeed"","" Allah says: {And He blessed therein and determined therein its sustenance} [al-Fussilat 41:10]. He says: So when one departs from the blessing and does not reinvest it in something similar"","" no blessing will be for him.\"""""""
"11183","(11178) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed me: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn informed me that ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān informed him from Usāmah ibn Zayd, who said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" will you stay in your house in Makkah?\"" He said: \""Has ʿAqīl left us any house or houses?\"" He (the narrator) said: \""ʿAqīl and Ṭālib inherited Abū Ṭālib"","" but neither Jaʿfar nor ʿAlī inherited him"","" because the two of them were Muslims"","" while ʿAqīl and Ṭālib were disbelievers. For this reason"","" ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāab (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: 'A believer does not inherit from a disbeliever.'\"" The wording is from the hadith of Abū ʿAmr. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aṣbagh from Ibn Wahb"","" and narrated by Muslim from Ḥarmalah and others. (Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1588"","" and Muslim 1351)]"""""
"11184","(11179) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: ʿAffān narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Thābit al-Bunānī from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rābiḥ from Abū Hurayrah regarding the story of the conquest of Makkah. He said: \Abū Sufyān came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"","" the green pastures of Quraysh have been destroyed; there is no Quraysh after today.' He said: 'Whoever enters the house of Abū Sufyān is safe"","" and whoever lays down his weapons is safe"","" and whoever closes his door is safe.'\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ḥammād ibn Salamah and Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah from Thābit. And Sulaymān's version adds: \""So the people went to the house of Abū Sufyān"","" and the people closed their doors.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1780]"""""
"11185","(11180) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bundār al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: al-Nuʿmān ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Farrūkh, the mawlā of Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥārith, who said: \Nāfiʿ ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥārith purchased the house of the prison from Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah for ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — if he approved of it or disliked it. Nāfiʿ gave Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah four hundred.\"" Ibn ʿUyaynah said: \""It is the prison of the people today in Makkah.\"" And it is narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that he was asked about renting the houses of Makkah"","" and he said: \""There is no harm in renting"","" just as there is no harm in buying. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) purchased a house from Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah for four thousand dirhams.\"""""""
"11186","(11181) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us: Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān said: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah said: \ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr used to establish residences in Makkah in a manner that no one else among the people would establish. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) bequeathed to him her chamber"","" and he purchased the chamber of Sawdah.\"""""""
"11187","(11182) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī informed us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal ibn Ghassān al-Ghulābī narrated to me: al-Zubayrī narrated: \Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām sold the house of al-Nadwah to Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān for one hundred thousand. ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr said: 'O Abū Khālid"","" you have sold the legacy of Quraysh and its most precious possession.' He said: 'Far from it"","" O son of my brother! The noble virtues have passed away. There is no nobility today except through Islam.' Then he said: 'Bear witness that these dirhams are in the cause of Allah"","" the Blessed and Most High.'\"""""""
"11188","(11183) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us in Baghdad: al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir narrated from his father from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bābāh from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Makkah is a place of resting; its plots shall not be sold and its houses shall not be rented.\"" Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir is weak (ḍaʿīf)"","" and his father is not strong (qawī). There is disagreement upon him; it has been narrated from him in this manner"","" and it has also been narrated from him from his father from Mujāhid from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr"","" raised (marfūʿ)"","" with part of its meaning."""""
"11189","(11184) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh and Abū Jaʿfar ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, both saying: Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah al-Sukkārī narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn al-Ḥakam al-ʿUranī narrated to us: Abū Ḥanīfah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Ziyād from Abū Najīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Makkah is sacred"","" and selling its plots is forbidden"","" and renting its houses is forbidden.\"" It has been narrated in this manner as marfūʿ (raised to the Prophet)"","" but its being raised is an error. The correct view is that it is mawqūf (stopped at the companion). Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī told me this from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī."""""
"11190","(11185) Hibbat Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭabarī al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Fārisī informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Amawī narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to us: Abū Najīḥ narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr that he said: \Indeed"","" one who consumes the rent of the houses of Makkah only consumes fire in his belly.\"" And likewise Muḥammad ibn Rabīʿah narrated it from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Ziyād with this wording"","" as mawqūf (stopped) upon ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr."""""
"11191","(11186) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān, from ʿAlqama ibn Naḍla al-Kinānī, who said: The houses of Makkah were called al-Sawāʾib, and their residential quarters were not sold during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), nor during the time of Abū Bakr, nor during the time of ʿUmar. Whoever was in need would reside in them, and whoever was without need would provide accommodation for others. This narration is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected).\n\nAnd in it is information about their generous custom of providing accommodation from their homes when they had no need for it. And the one who was most knowledgeable about the affairs of Makkah informed about the practice of inheritance and sale therein. And Allah knows best."
"11192","(11187) Abū Dāwūd narrated in al-Marāsīl from Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqama, from Ibn Abī Ḥusayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The best of merchandise is most deserving of having its price inquired about.\"" [Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl"","" 166]"""""
"11193","(11188) And from Abū Tawba, from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) passed by a Bedouin who was selling something and said: \You should adhere to the first price offered"","" for profits accompany leniency (samāḥ).\"" [Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl"","" 167]"""""
"11194","(11189) And from Qutayba and Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾida, from Abū Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī, from Khālid, meaning Ibn Abī Mālik, who said: I sold some merchandise to Muḥammad ibn Saʿd, and he said: \Give me your hand"","" so that I may shake it gently (in agreement)"","" for the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'Blessing lies in mutual leniency (al-mumāsaḥa).'\"" Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us of all of that; Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us; and Abū Dāwūd narrated it. [Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl"","" 8]"""""
"11195","(11190) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn al-Muʾammal informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-ʿAbadī informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) purchased food from a Jew on credit and pledged an iron coat of mail as security.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad, from Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd, and he (al-Bukhārī) and Muslim narrated it from another chain from al-Aʿmash. [Muslim, 1603]"
"11196","(11191) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; al-Daqqīqī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; al-Thawrī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from ʿĀʾisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away while his coat of mail was pledged with a Jew for thirty ṣāʿ of barley. Yazīd did not mention \with a Jew.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr."""""
"11197","(11192) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādhī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us; Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from ʿIkrima, from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed away while his coat of mail was pledged with a Jew for thirty ṣāʿ of barley — food he had taken for his family. [Musnad Aḥmad, 3399]"
"11198","(11193) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū Muslim al-Kajjī narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatāda, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: I walked to the Prophet (peace be upon him) with barley bread and rancid fat, and he had indeed pledged his coat of mail for barley. I heard him say: \The family of Muhammad have not had"","" by morning or by evening"","" more than one ṣāʿ.\"" And at that time they comprised nine households.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm"","" and he narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥawshab"","" from Asbāṭ Abī al-Yasʿ al-Baṣrī"","" from Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"","" and he added therein: \""in Madīnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī"","" 2069]"""""
"11199","(11194) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatāda, from Anas: that he walked to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with barley bread and rancid fat. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had pledged a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madīnah, and he had taken barley from him for his family. I heard him say one morning: \The family of Muhammad do not have a ṣāʿ of dates nor a ṣāʿ of barley.\"" And he had nine wives at that time.\n\nShaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated it from Qatāda and included in it his statement: \""in Madīnah.\"""""""
"11200","(11195) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdād; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Qatāda, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) was invited to barley bread and rancid fat. I heard him say one morning: \By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad"","" the family of Muhammad do not have a ṣāʿ of grain nor a ṣāʿ of dates.\"" And he had nine wives at that time. He had pledged a coat of mail of his with a Jew in Madīnah"","" and he had taken a ṣāʿ from him"","" for he did not find enough to suffice him — or he said: to redeem it."""""
"11201","(11196) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl and others narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pawned his armour with Abū al-Shaḥm al-Yahūdī, a man from Banī Ẓafar, for [a measure of] barley. This chain is discontinuous (munqaṭiʿ), and what precedes it suffices."
"11202","(11197) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us.\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from al-Suddī, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about wine being made into vinegar. He said: \No.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. And in the narration of Qabīṣah"","" he said: from Abū Hubayrah — and Abū Hubayrah is Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād — and he said in its text: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) was asked about wine being made into vinegar"","" and he disapproved of it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim 1983]"""""
"11203","(11198) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, from al-Suddī, from Abū Hubayrah, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while there were orphans in his care, and he had wine at the time when wine was prohibited. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" shall I make it into vinegar?\"" He said: \""No.\"" So he poured it out until the valley flowed with it.\nWakīʿ narrated it from Sufyān"","" and he mentioned that Abū Ṭalḥah asked him about orphans who inherited wine. He said: \""Pour it out.\"" He said: \""Shall I not make it into vinegar?\"" He said: \""No.\"""""""
"11204","(11199) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated, from al-Suddī, from Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: There were orphans under my father's care. He purchased wine, and when the prohibition of wine was revealed, he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said: \Shall I make it into vinegar?\"" He said: \""No.\"" So he poured it out. His statement \""under my father's care\"" refers to the care of Abū Ṭalḥah"","" who was the husband of his mother."""""
"11205","(11200) Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣrūyah ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khanb narrated to us in Bukhārā: Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Abū Janāb narrated, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: A man had the property of orphans in his care. He used to buy for them worn-out and damaged goods, repair them, and sell them. He purchased wine and placed it in jars. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed the prohibition of wine. He came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and asked him about it. He said: \Pour it out.\"" Then he asked him again"","" and he said: \""Pour it out.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" they have no other wealth.\"" He said: \""Pour it out.\"" So he poured it out."""""
"11206","(11201) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʤAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to me, from Ibn Shihāb, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb was brought a cooked preparation at al-Jābiyah, which was being cooked and was thick like concentrated date juice. He said: \There is indeed in this a drink from which one has been forbidden. Let not the vinegar of wine that has gone bad be drunk until Allah makes its corruption manifest; at that point the vinegar becomes pure. And there is no harm for a person to purchase vinegar that he finds with the People of the Book"","" so long as he does not know that they deliberately caused it to spoil after it had become wine.\"" His statement \""has gone bad\"" (ufsidat) means it was treated. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī up to his statement \""the vinegar becomes pure.\""]"""""
"11207","(11202) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd al-Rāzī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bakkār narrated to us: Farj ibn Faḍālah narrated, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Tanning renders the dead animal permissible"","" just as vinegar renders wine permissible.\"" Farj said"","" meaning that when wine changes and becomes vinegar"","" it becomes permissible. Farj ibn Faḍālah is alone in narrating this from Yaḥyā"","" and he is weak (ḍaʿīf). He narrates from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd a number of aḥādīth that are not corroborated. Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said this"","" as narrated from him by Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith. According to this explanation"","" the disagreement is resolved"","" except that the ḥadīth is weak."""""
"11208","(11203) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dihqān narrated to us in Kūfah: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghurzah narrated to us: Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Mughīrah — and he is Ibn Ziyād — narrated, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A household shall never be in need of condiments in which there is vinegar. And the best of your vinegars is the vinegar of your wine.\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh said: This ḥadīth is feeble (wāhin)"","" and al-Mughīrah ibn Ziyād is a narrator of rejected reports.\nThe Shaykh said: The people of the Ḥijāz call grape vinegar \""vinegar of wine"",""\"" and this is what is intended by the report"","" if the report is authentic"","" Allah willing"","" or [it refers to] wine that turned into vinegar by itself. And likewise what…"""""
"11209","(11204) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated, from Umm Khidāsh, that she saw ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) using the vinegar of wine as a condiment.\nIt is also narrated from Musarbal al-ʿAbadī, from his mother, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said: \There is no harm in the vinegar of wine.\"" However"","" its chain is unknown (majhūl)."""""
"11210","(11205) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Narsī narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Zakariyyā narrated, from al-Shaʿbī, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The back [of a mount] may be ridden at its expense when it is pledged as security"","" and the milk of a she-camel may be drunk when it is pledged as security. The one who drinks [the milk] and the one who rides [the mount] are responsible for its maintenance.\"""""""
"11211","(11206) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Kūfī informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Zakariyyā narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: \The back (of a pledged animal) is to be ridden at the expense of the one who holds it in pledge"","" and the milk of a milch animal is to be drunk when it is pledged; and upon the one who rides it and drinks its milk is the expense (of its maintenance).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym.\n\nLikewise"","" Ibn al-Mubārak and Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān narrated it from Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah. And Hushaym and Sufyān ibn Ḥabīb narrated it from Zakariyyā"","" and they added in its text: \""al-murtahin\"" (the pledge-holder). This addition is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). In the narration of Yaʿqūb al-Dawraqī from Hushaym"","" he said: \""When an animal is pledged"","" then upon the one who pledged it is its fodder"","" and the milk of the milch animal is to be drunk"","" and upon the one who drinks and rides is its expense.\"""""""
"11212","(11207) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us in Baghdād, al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mujashshir informed us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pledged animal is to be milked and ridden.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm"","" and he said: 'Indeed"","" they used to dislike benefiting from the pledged animal in any way.'\"" Likewise"","" it was narrated from Abū ʿAwanah from al-Aʿmash"","" raised (marfūʿ) to the Prophet."""""
"11213","(11208) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā informed us, Shaybān — meaning Ibn Farūkh — informed us, Abū ʿAwanah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The pledged animal is to be ridden and milked.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm"","" and he disliked benefiting from it in any way.\"" The group narrated it from al-Aʿmash"","" as a statement of Abū Hurayrah (mawqūf)."""""
"11214","(11209) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid informed us. And Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī informed us in Kūfah, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us, both saying: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī informed us, Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash. And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Tamtām informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash. And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah who said: \The pledged animal is to be ridden and milked.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""It is as though the statement of Abū Hurayrah — and Allah knows best — means that whoever pledges an animal that yields milk and can be ridden"","" the pledgor (al-rāhin) should not be prevented from its milk and its back"","" for he has custody of it; thus it is milked and ridden as it was before the pledge. The benefits of the pledge belong to the pledgor (al-rāhin)"","" and the pledge-holder (al-murtahin) has no share in them.\"""""""
"11215","(11210) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Fudayk narrated from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pledge should not be withheld from its owner who pledged it; its gain is his and its loss is upon him.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""Its gain means its increase"","" and its loss means its destruction and decrease.\"""""""
"11216","(11211) He (al-Shāfiʿī) said: \And al-Shāfiʿī informed us"","" al-Thiqah (the trustworthy narrator) informed us"","" from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Unaysah"","" from Ibn Shihāb"","" from Ibn al-Musayyab"","" from Abū Hurayrah"","" from the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" the same or similar in meaning"","" without contradicting it.\"""""""
"11217","(11212) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated from Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ and Yūnus, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn who said: \A man came to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd and said: 'I lent a man five hundred dirhams"","" and he pledged a horse with me"","" and I rode it — or I had someone ride it.' He said: 'Whatever you obtained from its back is ribā (usury).'\"""""""
"11218","(11213) And from Sufyān, who said: \Zakariyyā narrated to me from al-Shaʿbī that he said regarding a man who took a slave-girl in pledge and she suckled a child for him: 'He must pay the owner of the slave-girl the value of the milk for the suckling.'\"""""""
"11219","(11214) And from Sufyān, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from al-Shaʿbī who said: \No benefit is to be derived from the pledged property in any way.\"""""""
"11220","(11215) And from Sufyān, from Jābir, from a man called Ibrāhīm, who said: \Shurayḥ was asked about a man who took a cow in pledge and drank from its milk. He said: 'That is the drinking of ribā (usury).'\"""""""
"11221","(11216) And with this isnad, from Sufyan: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from ʿAmr ibn Dinar, who said: Muʿadh ibn Jabal used to say regarding a palm tree that is pledged as security, if fruit then emerges upon it, it [the fruit] belongs to the pledged security. This is munqatiʿ [disconnected], and likewise is the hadith of Ibn Sirin."
"11222","(11217) And in what Abū ʿAbd Allah the Hafiz permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbas, from al-Rabiʿ, from al-Shafiʿi, who said: Mufarraj ibn Mazin narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from ibn Tawus, from his father, that Muʿadh ibn Jabal gave a ruling regarding a person who pledged a fruit-bearing palm tree: the mortgagor shall count its dates as part of the principal. He [al-Shafiʿi] said: And Sufyan ibn ʿUyaynah mentioned something similar to it. Al-Shafiʿi said: And I consider Mufarraj to be correct. He said: In the hadith is [a reference to] the year in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the pilgrimage."
"11223","(11218) Abū ʿAbd Allah the Hafiz informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbas Muhammad ibn Yaʿqub narrated to us: al-Rabiʿ ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafiʿi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ismaʿil ibn Abī Fudayk informed us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Ibn Shihab, from Saʿid ibn al-Musayyib, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The pledged security shall not be withheld from its owner; he who pledged it to him — its gain is his and its loss is upon him.\""\n\nAnd likewise did Sufyan al-Thawri narrate it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"","" and he said in its matn: \""The pledged security belongs to the one who pledged it; its gain is his and its loss is upon him.\"" And Ismaʿil ibn ʿAyyash narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb and connected it."""""
"11224","(11219) Abū ʿAbd Allah the Hafiz informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbas Muhammad ibn Yaʿqub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn ʿAwf ibn Sufyan al-Taʾi narrated to us: ʿUthman ibn Saʿid ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated to us: Ismaʿil ibn ʿAyyash narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from al-Zuhri, from Saʿid ibn al-Musayyib, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The pledged security shall not be withheld from its owner; its gain is his and its loss is upon him.\"" And it has been narrated from Ziyad ibn Saʿd from al-Zuhri"","" connected [mawsulan]."""""
"11225","(11220) Abū ʿAbd Allah the Hafiz informed us: Abū al-Walid al-Faqih narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Talib and Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sāʿid both narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿImran al-ʿAbidi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Saʿd, from al-Zuhri, from Saʿid ibn al-Musayyib, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The pledged security shall not be withheld; its gain is his and its loss is upon him.\"""""""
"11226","(11221) Abū ʿAbd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abū Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us, saying: ʿAli ibn ʿUmar the Hafiz informed us: Abū Muhammad ibn Sāʿid narrated to us — and he mentioned it. ʿAli said: \Ziyad ibn Saʿd is among the reliable huffaz"","" and this is a hasan"","" connected isnad.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Others have narrated it from Sufyan"","" from Ziyad"","" as a mursal [disconnected] tradition"","" and that is the preserved version. And Abū ʿAmr al-Awzaʿi and Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī narrated it from al-Zuhri"","" from Ibn al-Musayyib"","" as mursal"","" except that they attributed the statement \""its gain is his and its loss is upon him\"" to the words of Ibn al-Musayyib. And Allah knows best."""""
"11227","(11222) Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Abū al-Husayn al-Fasawi narrated to us: Abū ʿAli al-Luʾluʾi narrated to us: Abū Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Hisab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Thawr narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The pledged security shall not be withheld.\"" I said to him: \""Have you considered your statement 'the pledged security shall not be withheld' — does a man say"","" 'If I do not come to you with your wealth"","" then this pledged security is yours'?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He [the narrator] said: \""And it reached me afterwards that he said: 'If it is destroyed"","" the right of this [creditor] does not vanish; rather"","" the loss falls upon the one who held the security. Its gain is his and its loss is upon him.'\"""""""
"11228","(11223) Abū Hazim the Hafiz informed us: Abū al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn ʿUbayd Allah al-Hanafi in Harat informed us: al-Husayn ibn Idris ibn Khurram al-Ansari informed us: Muhammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawarib informed us: Hassan ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm al-Tustari, from ʿAmr ibn Dinar, who said: Abī Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The pledged security is for what is in it.\"" Abū Hazim said: Hassan ibn Ibrāhīm al-Kirmānī is the sole narrator of this. The Shaykh said: And it is munqatiʿ [disconnected] between ʿAmr ibn Dinar and Abī Hurayrah."""""
"11229","(11224) Abū Saʿd al-Malini informed us: Abū Ahmad ibn ʿAdi the Hafiz informed us: Zakariyya al-Saji said: I heard Ismaʿil ibn Abī ʿAbbad al-Dhariʿ saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The pledged security is for what is in it.\"" Abū Ahmad said: And Abū ʿAbbad — his name is Umayyah"","" a Basran — thus said Zakariyya al-Saji.\n\nThe Shaykh said: It has been said"","" \""Ismaʿil ibn Abī Umayyah al-Dhariʿ"",""\"" and it has been said regarding him"","" from Saʿid ibn Rashid"","" from Humayd"","" from Anas"","" marfūʿan [with a raised chain]. Abū al-Hasan al-Dāraqutnī said: \""This Ismaʿil fabricates hadith"","" and this is not correct.\"" Abū ʿAbd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abū Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us of that from him. And the fundamental principle in this chapter is a mursal hadith"","" and it contains the weakness that it contains."""""
"11230","(11225) Abū Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us: Abū al-Husayn al-Fasawi narrated to us: Abū ʿAli al-Luʾluʾi narrated to us: Abū Dawud narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-ʿAlaʾ narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak informed us, from Musʿab ibn Thabit, who said: I heard ʿAtaʾ relating that a man pledged a horse, and it perished while in his possession. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the mortgagee: \His right has been lost.\""\n\nAnd al-Shafiʿi"","" may Allah have mercy upon him"","" has sufficed us in clarifying the weakness of this hadith"","" and that is in what Abū ʿAbd Allah the Hafiz permitted me to narrate from him"","" that Abū al-ʿAbbas informed them"","" saying: Al-Rabiʿ informed us: Al-Shafiʿi informed us: Ibrāhīm narrated to us"","" from Musʿab ibn Thabit"","" from ʿAtaʾ"","" who said: \""Al-Hasan claimed such and such"","" and then related this statement.\"" Ibrāhīm said: \""ʿAtaʾ used to be astonished at what al-Hasan narrated.\"" Al-Shafiʿi said: \""And more than one informed me"","" from Musʿab"","" from ʿAtaʾ"","" from al-Hasan"","" and someone I trust informed me that a man among the people of knowledge narrated it from Musʿab"","" from ʿAtaʾ"","" from the Prophet ﷺ"","" and was silent regarding al-Hasan. I said to him: 'The companions of Musʿab narrate it from ʿAtaʾ from al-Hasan.' He said: 'Yes"","" thus he narrated to us"","" but ʿAtaʾ is more sound in my view as mursal than al-Hasan as mursal.'\""\n\nAl-Shafiʿi said: \""And that which indicates the weakness of this [tradition] with ʿAtaʾ — if he narrated it — is that ʿAtaʾ used to give a fatwa contrary to it"","" and would say regarding it the opposite of this. All of it [his position] is that what is apparent of its destruction constitutes an amanah [trust]"","" and what is hidden of its destruction — they shall share the surplus. And this is the more established narration from him. And it has been narrated from him that they shall share [the surplus] absolutely. And we have not doubted in it"","" so we do not doubt that ʿAtaʾ"","" if Allah wills"","" does not narrate it from the Prophet ﷺ as a confirmed [tradition] with him"","" and yet holds a view contrary to it — though I do not know anyone who narrates this from ʿAtaʾ and raises it [to the Prophet] except Musʿab. And that which was narrated from ʿAtaʾ raising it is consistent with the statement of Shurayh: 'The pledged security is for what is in it.' And it may be that the horse is worth more than what is owed"","" or equal to it or less"","" and it was not reported that he asked about the value of the horse.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And that has been narrated from other than him"","" from ʿAtaʾ"","" raising it — \""The pledged security is for what is in it.\"" [Daʿīf]"""""
"11231","(11226) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Muhammad — informed us; Abu al-Husayn al-Fasawi narrated to us; Abu Ali al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us; al-Walid informed us; Abu 'Amr informed us from 'Ata': that a man pledged a horse as security (rahn), and the horse died. The Prophet ﷺ said: \The pledge is for what is in it (i.e."","" the pledge stands for what it covers).\""\n\nIt was also narrated with these same words but without the story by Zam'ah ibn Salih from Ibn Tawus from his father"","" as a mursal narration. Zam'ah is not strong (in hadith). Al-Shafi'i"","" may Allah have mercy on him"","" mentioned that he relied in this issue upon the mursal of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib rather than others"","" because his mursal narrations are more authentic than the mursal narrations of others"","" and also because it has been narrated as a musnad (connected) narration as well. And Allah knows best."""""
"11232","(11227) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us. He said: I heard my uncle, Abu 'Abd Allah, meaning Ahmad ibn Hanbal, say: \The mursal narrations of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib are sound (sahih); we do not see any mursal narrations more authentic than his. As for al-Hasan and 'Ata"","" their mursal narrations are not of that calibre; they are the weakest of mursal narrations"","" because they used to take from everyone.\"""""""
"11233","(11228) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih both informed us; they said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us; Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us; Abu 'Asim narrated to us from Abu al-'Awwam; Matar narrated to us from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said regarding a man who pledges something as security (rahn) and it is lost: \If the pledge is worth less than the debt"","" the remainder of the claim is due upon him (the pledgor); and if it is worth more"","" then the one holding it is a trustee (amin).\""\n\nThis is not well-known from 'Umar. The narrations differ on this matter from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib"","" and it has been narrated from him:"""""
"11234","(11229) As Abu al-Qasim — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Shabban al-'Attar in Baghdad — informed us; 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Qatadah from Khilas from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If there is an excess in the pledge (i.e."","" its value exceeds the debt)"","" and it is destroyed by a calamity"","" then the pledge stands for what is in it. But if no calamity befalls it"","" then the excess must be returned.\""\n\nWhatever Khilas narrated from 'Ali"","" he took it from a written page (sahifah)"","" as Yahya ibn Ma'in and other huffaz have stated. It has also been narrated from 'Ali"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" in absolute terms: \""They shall mutually return the excess.\"""""""
"11235","(11230) 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Shabban informed us; 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated from Mansur from al-Hakam from 'Ali regarding the pledge: if it is destroyed, \they shall mutually return the excess.\"""""""
"11236","(11231) He said: And 'Abd al-Baqi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from al-Hajjaj from al-Hakam from 'Ali who said regarding the pledge: \They shall return the surplus and the deficiency.\"" This is munqati' (disconnected)"","" because al-Hakam ibn 'Utbah did not meet 'Ali. And it has also been narrated from al-Hajjaj through another weak chain as a musnad (connected) narration."""""
"11237","(11232) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Ma'mar ibn Sulayman narrated from al-Hajjaj from al-Sha'bi from al-Harith from 'Ali who said: \If the pledge is worth more than the loan"","" or the loan is worth more than the pledge"","" and then it is destroyed"","" they shall mutually return the excess.\"""""""
"11238","(11233) And from al-Hajjaj from 'Ata' who said: \It used to be said: 'They shall mutually return the excess between them.'\"" Al-Harith al-A'war"","" al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah"","" and Ma'mar ibn Sulayman are not relied upon as authoritative (in hadith). And it has been narrated through a third chain from 'Ali. [Da'if (Weak)]"""""
"11239","(11234) 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad ibn Shabban in Baghdad informed us; 'Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' narrated to us; Hamid ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah narrated from 'Ali ibn Salih from 'Abd al-A'la from Ibn al-Hanafiyyah from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If the pledge is of lesser value"","" the excess is returned; and if it is of greater value"","" it stands for what is in it.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: The narration from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" that \""they shall mutually return the excess\"" is more authentic than the narration of 'Abd al-A'la. And we have seen your companions (i.e."","" the scholars) weaken the narration of 'Abd al-A'la — which has no opposing narration — severely. So how much more so when it is opposed by one who is closer to authenticity and more deserving of it than him? This is the speech regarding what Abu 'Abd Allah permitted me to narrate from him"","" from Abu al-'Abbas"","" from al-Rabi'"","" from al-Shafi'i."""""
"11240","(11235) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — recited to him — Abu Bakr informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the son of the daughter of al-'Abbas ibn Hamzah, narrated to us; Harun ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-Rukhi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us. He said: I asked Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan about 'Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, and he said: \You know and you reject.\"" Yahya said: I asked Sufyan"","" meaning al-Thawri"","" about the narrations of 'Abd al-A'la from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah"","" and he declared them weak."""""
"11241","(11236) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abī Ḥaṣīn, from Shurayḥ, who said: \The pledges are gone with what is in them.\"""""""
"11242","(11237) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed me; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: I heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pledge shall not be withheld (lā yaghlaq al-rahn).\""\n\nThus the owner of the pledge is prevented from transacting with the one to whom he pledged it until he transacts with someone else. Thus I found it in my book"","" and its correct meaning"","" as I understand it"","" is that \""the pledge being withheld\"" means that the owner of the pledge is prevented from transacting with the one who holds the pledge. He said: \""The pledge shall not be withheld"",""\"" meaning the owner of the pledge shall not be prevented from dealing with the mortgagee. And Allah knows best."""""
"11243","(11238) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Isrāʾīl narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿĀmir ibn Masʿūd al-Qurashī narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pledge shall not be withheld.\"" A man had mortgaged a house in Madīnah for a fixed term. When the term expired"","" the one who took the mortgage said: \""It is mine.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The pledge shall not be withheld.\"" This is a mursal hadith."""""
"11244","(11239) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān al-Bazzāz narrated in Baghdād; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Dāwūd al-Ḍabbī narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Maʿmar, who said: I said to al-Zuhrī, \O Abū Bakr"","" what is the meaning of his statement"","" 'The pledge shall not be withheld'?\"" He said: He means: \""If I do not redeem it by such-and-such a date"","" then it is yours.\"""""""
"11245","(11240) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik ibn Anas narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Abī Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man who becomes bankrupt"","" and another man finds his property in his exact form with him"","" then he (the owner) has the greatest right to it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2402"","" and Muslim 1559]"""""
"11246","(11241) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed him that Abī Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām informed him that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever finds his property in its exact form with a man or a person who has become bankrupt"","" then he has the greatest right to it over others.\"""""""
"11247","(11242) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us; Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm narrated it with the same meaning, except that he said \with a man\"" without any doubt. al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. Muslim also narrated it from the hadith of Hushaym"","" al-Layth ibn Saʿd"","" Ḥammād ibn Zayd"","" Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"","" ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī"","" Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"","" and Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth — all of them from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Anṣārī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11248","(11243) In his narration from al-Layth ibn Saʿd in this hadith: \Any person who becomes bankrupt"","" and then a man finds his merchandise in its exact form"","" then he has the greater right to it over others.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to me; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Idrīs al-Anṣārī in Harāt and ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Yaḥyā Abū Sahl both said: Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"","" and he mentioned it"","" saying \""from"","" from.\"" Sufyān al-Thawrī also narrated it explicitly from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd regarding the purchaser of the merchandise. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11249","(11244) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; al-Firyābī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Abī Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When a man purchases merchandise and then becomes bankrupt"","" and it is still with him in its exact form"","" then he (the original owner) has the greater right to it over the creditors.\"" The Shaykh said: In my book it occurred to me as \""from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"","" from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm"",""\"" and that is an error."""""
"11250","(11245) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Bayān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abī Bakr ibn ʿAmr, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, and he mentioned it, saying: \Whoever purchases merchandise and then becomes bankrupt"","" then its owner has the greater right to it.\""\n\nSimilarly"","" ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ghazī narrated it from al-Firyābī"","" from Sufyān"","" from Yaḥyā. And similarly"","" Zayd ibn Abī al-Zarqāʾ narrated it from Sufyān"","" from Yaḥyā. [Ibn Khuzaymah]"""""
"11251","(11246) Yazīd ibn al-Hādī narrated it on the authority of Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm with his chain of narration. He said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any man who finds his specific commodity with a man who has become insolvent"","" then he has greater right to it than anyone else.\""\n\nAbū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣrūyah al-Kushmayhanīy informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Khunb informed us; Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us; Saʿīd"","" meaning Ibn Abī Maryam"","" informed us; Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd informed me; Ibn al-Hādī informed me; Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm informed me — and he mentioned it. Likewise"","" Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it on the authority of Ibn al-Hādī."""""
"11252","(11247) ʿAlīy ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣriyy informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yazīd informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlīy ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us; Ibn Abī Maryam informed us; Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd informed me; Yazīd ibn al-Hādī informed me; Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ibn Milḥān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us; Layth informed us, on the authority of Ibn al-Hādī, on the authority of Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm — and he mentioned it, except that in the ḥadīth of Layth he said: \from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nAnd ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Ḥusayn narrated it explicitly on the authority of Abū Bakr ibn Ḥazm in the context of sale. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11253","(11248) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlīy ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzīy informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad said: Ibn Abī ʿUmar informed us; Hishām ibn Sulaymān informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj; Ibn Abī Ḥusayn informed me that Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm informed him that ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed him, on the authority of the ḥadīth of Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, on the authority of the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ), regarding the man who becomes insolvent: if his commodity is found with him and it has not been altered, then it belongs to the one who sold it to him.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Ibn Abī ʿUmar."
"11254","(11249) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Rajāʾ al-Adīb said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghāniyy informed us; Abū Salamah al-Khuʿāʿiyy informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamiyy, and Abū Naṣr Manṣūr ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Mufassir al-Muqrīʾ said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūriyy informed us; Abū Salamah al-Khuʿāʿiyy informed us, on the authority of Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, on the authority of Khuthaym ibn ʿIrāk, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a man becomes insolvent and a man finds his commodity with him"","" then he has greater right to it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Ḥajjāj ibn al-Shāʿir"","" on the authority of Abū Salamah Manṣūr ibn Salamah al-Khuʿāʿiyy. [Narrated by Muslim]"""""
"11255","(11250) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miṣriyy informed us; Sulaymān ibn Shuʿayb al-Kaysāniyy informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād al-Raṣāṣiyy informed us; Shuʿbah informed me; Qatādah informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us; Shuʿbah informed us. Qatādah informed me, on the authority of al-Naḍr ibn Anas, on the authority of Bashīr ibn Nahīk, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a man becomes insolvent and a man finds his specific commodity with him"","" then he has greater right to it.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā. Muslim extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ghundar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdiyy"","" on the authority of Shuʿbah."""""
"11256","(11251) Hishām al-Dastawāʾiyy narrated it on the authority of Qatādah, and he said in its text: \A man finds his specific commodity with him"","" then he has greater right to it than the creditors.\""\n\nAbū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us; Abū Khaythamah informed us; Muʿādh ibn Hishām informed us"","" on the authority of his father"","" and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ on the authority of Abū Khaythamah."""""
"11257","(11252) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawiyy informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhliyy and Abū al-Azhar said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us, on the authority of Ayyūb, on the authority of ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, on the authority of Hishām ibn Yaḥyā, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a man becomes insolvent and the seller finds his specific commodity with him"","" then he has greater right to it than the creditors.\"""""""
"11258","(11253) Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl informed us; my grandfather Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; ʿAlīy ibn Ḥujr informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah informed us that he heard Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib say: \A freed slave of Umm Ḥabībah"","" the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" became insolvent. The matter was disputed and brought before ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUthmān ruled that whoever had already received anything of his right before the insolvency became manifest"","" then it is his; and whoever found his specific commodity"","" then it is his.\"""""""
"11259","(11254) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisiyy informed us; Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed me; Abū al-Muʿtamir informed me, on the authority of ʿUmar ibn Khaldah, who said: \We came to Abū Hurayrah concerning a companion of ours who had been afflicted"","" i.e."","" had become insolvent"","" and a man had found his specific commodity with him.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""This is the matter regarding which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a ruling: that whoever becomes insolvent or dies"","" and a man finds his specific commodity with him"","" then he has greater right to it"","" unless the man leaves behind sufficient [wealth] to discharge his debts.\""\n\nLikewise"","" Shabābah ibn Sawwār and ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlīy and others narrated it on the authority of Ibn Abī Dhiʾb"","" and they said: \""unless its owner leaves behind sufficient [wealth] to discharge his debts.\""\n\n[Musnad al-Ṭayālisī 2497]"""""
"11260","(11255) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿiyy said: \Among what we read upon Mālik"","" on the authority of Ibn Shihāb"","" who was informed by Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith"","" i.e."","" Ibn Hishām"","" that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Any man who sells a commodity and the one who purchased it becomes insolvent"","" and the seller has not received anything of its price"","" and he finds it in its specific form"","" then he has greater right to it. And if the buyer dies"","" then the owner of the commodity is equal to the creditors.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿiyy said: \""The one I take as more worthy for me"","" i.e."","" the ḥadīth of Ibn Khaldah"","" is because what I take is a connected narration in which the Prophet (ﷺ) combined death and insolvency"","" whereas the ḥadīth of Ibn Shihāb is disconnected. Even if no one contradicted it"","" it would not be something that the scholars of ḥadīth would establish as authentic"","" and even if there were no proof for abandoning it except this alone"","" it would be incumbent upon one who knows ḥadīth to abandon it on two grounds. Alongside this"","" Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrates his ḥadīth on the authority of Abū Hurayrah"","" and it does not contain what Ibn Shihāb narrated from him as a mursal narration"","" if he narrated it all"","" and I do not know from whom he narrated it. Perhaps he narrated the first part of the ḥadīth and gave his own opinion for the latter part. And it is found in the ḥadīth of Abū Bakr"","" on the authority of Abū Hurayrah"","" on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" that he concluded the statement with: 'then he has greater right to it.' It is most likely that what is beyond this is a statement of Abū Bakr"","" not a narration.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated it on the authority of al-Zubaydiyy"","" on the authority of al-Zuhrīy"","" as a connected narration"","" but it is not authentic.\""\n\n[Muwṭaʾ Imām Mālik 2686]"""""
"11261","(11256) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Firās al-Mālikī in Makkah informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār, meaning al-Khabāʾirī, narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from al-Zubaydī, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Any man who sells a commodity and finds it intact with a man who has become insolvent"","" having received nothing of its price"","" then it belongs to him (the seller). But if he has paid part of its price"","" then what remains is on par with the other creditors.\""\n\nAl-Rūdhabārī added in his narration: \""And any person who dies and in his possession is another person's property in its exact form"","" whether he has taken payment from it or not"","" then he is on par with the other creditors.\"""""""
"11262","(11257) And Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Isḥāq narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Khabāʾirī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from al-Zuhrī, and he mentioned it similarly, without the story of death (halāk). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11263","(11258) And al-Yamān ibn ʿAdī narrated it from al-Zubaydī, from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, and it is weak. Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Simnānī narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us: al-Yamān ibn ʿAdī narrated to me: al-Zubaydī narrated, and he mentioned it with the meaning of the ḥadīth of Ismāʿīl in the text, differing in the isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ, through other than this isnād]"
"11264","(11259) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh is confused in ḥadīth, and this is not established from al-Zuhrī; rather it is mursal. And al-Yamān ibn ʿAdī contradicted him in its isnād, and al-Yamān ibn ʿAdī is weak. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11265","(11260) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī narrated to us: Sulaymān al-Shādhakūnī narrated to us: Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Nawqānī narrated to us therein, and Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Mufassir in Naysābūr said: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Fahd al-Baṣrī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ placed a restriction on the property of Muʿādh ibn Jabal and sold it for a debt that he owed."
"11266","(11261) And Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us by dictation: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Hishām ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from his father, who said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, was a young man, forbearing and generous, among the best of his people's youth. He would never hold on to anything. He continued to incur debts until all his property was consumed by debt. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and spoke to his creditors. Had they forgiven anyone for the sake of another, they would have forgiven Muʿādh for the sake of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold his property until Muʿādh stood with nothing remaining.\n\nThus did Hishām ibn Yūsuf al-Ṣanʿānī narrate it from Maʿmar. And ʿAbd al-Razzāq contradicted him in its isnād, for he narrated it as follows:"
"11267","(11262) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, who said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, was a handsome, generous young man, among the best of his people's youth. He would not be asked for anything but that he would give it, until a debt was incurred against him that consumed all his property. He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to speak to his creditors on his behalf, and he did so, but they waived nothing for him. Had anyone been forgiven at the request of another, Muʿādh would have been forgiven at the request of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: The Prophet ﷺ called him, and he did not leave until he sold his property and distributed it among his creditors. He said: So Muʿādh, may Allah be pleased with him, stood with no property.\n\nAnd thus did ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak narrate it from Maʿmar, without saying \from his father"",""\"" and he said: from al-Zuhrī"","" from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik"","" who said: Muʿādh was… and he mentioned it. And it was narrated through two weak chains from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh regarding the story of Muʿādh."""""
"11268","(11263) And Abū Jaʿfar al-Mustamlī narrated to us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, from Ismāʿīl ibn Rajāʾ, from Abī Mijlaz, that two young men of Juhaynah shared a slave. One of them freed his share, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ detained him until he sold some sheep of his for that purpose. This is mursal."
"11269","(11264) And Abū Manṣūr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Dāmghānī in Bayhaq informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Abū Yaʿqūb Isḥāq ibn Khālawayh al-Bābṣīrī narrated to us: Sahl ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: Two men of Juhaynah shared a slave. One of them freed him, so the Prophet ﷺ held him liable for him. He had nearly two hundred sheep, so he sold them and gave their price to his partner. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah is weak.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abī Mijlaz, mursal, and this is more likely."
"11270","(11265) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Najayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Dulāf, from his father, that a man from Juhaynah used to purchase riding camels, overpaying for them, and then travel swiftly, outpacing the pilgrims. He became insolvent, and his matter was raised to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, who said: \To proceed: O people"","" the poor wretch—the poor wretch of Juhaynah—was content with his religion and trustworthiness being said: 'He outpaced the pilgrims.' But he incurred debts recklessly and awoke burdened by them. So whoever has a claim of debt against him"","" let us come in the morning"","" and we will divide his property among his creditors. And beware of debt"","" for its beginning is worry and its end is war.\"" [Weak]"""""
"11271","(11266) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm, from Ayyūb, who said: I was informed that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu) issued a similar ruling and said: \We shall divide his wealth among them in shares.\"""""""
"11272","(11267) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us, from his father.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad narrated to us — Abū Thābit narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from his father, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \The soul of the believer remains suspended by his debt until it is discharged on his behalf.\"" [Musnad al-Shāfiʿī 1645]"""""
"11273","(11268) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār in Baghdād informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — both saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us — Sufyān al-Thawrī informed us — my father informed me, from al-Shaʿbī — Simʿān ibn Mushannaj narrated to me, from Samurah: that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) prayed over a funeral, and when he had given the final salām, he asked: \Is there anyone from the family of so-and-so here?\"" He repeated this several times. A man then stood up"","" dragging his lower garment from the back of the assembly. The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said to him: \""Did I not call your name only for some good? Verily"","" so-and-so — one of their men — is constrained by his debt. If you could see his family and those who are concerned for his affair"","" they would rise and settle his debt.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of the Baghdādī. It has also been reported regarding the settlement of debt upon the deceased from Ibn ʿUmar in a marfūʿ chain"","" and from Zayd ibn Thābit in a mawqūf chain"","" and both of them are ḍaʿīf."""""
"11274","(11269) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdan informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibn Milḥān narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — al-Layth.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ashajj, from ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Saʿd, from Abī Saʿīd, who said: A man was afflicted during the era of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) regarding fruit he had purchased, and his debt became excessive. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \Give charity on his behalf.\"" So the people gave charity on his behalf"","" but it did not suffice to discharge his debt. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) then said: \""Take what you find"","" and you are entitled to nothing beyond that.\"" Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"","" from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim 1556]"""""
"11275","(11270) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Kaʿb informed me that Muʿādh ibn Jabal — who was one of the men of his people, Banū Salamah — had his debt become excessive during the era of the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), and the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) did not increase anything for his creditors except that he distributed his wealth among them. [Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl 172]"
"11276","(11271) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn al-Jahm al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us — al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faraj narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar narrated to me — ʿĪsā ibn al-Nuʿmān narrated to me, from Muʿādh ibn Rifāʿah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal was among the most handsome of people in countenance, the best of them in character, and the most generous of them in hand. He incurred a heavy debt, and his creditors pursued him until he was absent from them for days, remaining in his house, until his creditors sought the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) to summon him. So he sent for him, calling him, and he came with his creditors. They said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" take for us our due from him.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \""May Allah have mercy upon the one who gives charity on his behalf.\"" He said: So some people gave charity on his behalf"","" while others refused and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" take for us our due from him.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \""Be patient with them"","" O Muʿādh.\"" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) separated his wealth and gave it to his creditors"","" and they divided it among themselves"","" receiving five-sevenths of their rights. They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" sell him to us.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \""Leave him"","" for you have no claim against him.\"" Al-Wāqidī is alone in some of its wordings."""""
"11277","(11272) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥasan al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated to us — Ḥajjāj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj — ʿAmr ibn Dīnār informed me, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) sold a free man who had become bankrupt in his debt. Others besides him narrated it from Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad with a doubt in its isnād."
"11278","(11273) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Jarrāḥ narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Ḥajjāj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abī Saʿīd or Abī Saʿd, that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) sold a free man who had become bankrupt."
"11279","(11274) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdan informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us — Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us — Ḥammād ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us, from Qatādah, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, that Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated to him: A man came to al-Madīnah and mentioned that wealth was coming to him, so people gave him much wealth on credit. He consumed it, and the man was seized and found to have no wealth. The Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) ordered that he be sold. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)."
"11280","(11275) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī narrated to us — both saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Dīnār narrated to us — Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, who said: I saw an old man in al-Iskandarīyah called Surraq. I said to him: \What is this name?\"" He said: \""A name given to me by the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam)"","" and I shall never abandon it.\"" I said: \""Why did he name you that?\"" He said: \""I came to al-Madīnah and told them that my wealth was coming"","" so they entered into transactions with me. I consumed their wealth"","" and they brought me before the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam)"","" who said: 'You are Surraq (a thief)!' Then he sold me for four camels.\"" The creditors said to the one who purchased me: \""What will you do with him?\"" He said: \""I shall free him.\"" They said: \""We are not more desirous of reward than you.\"" So they freed me among them"","" and my name remained.\n\nA similar meaning was narrated by ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿAbdullāh"","" the two sons of Zayd ibn Aslam"","" from their father"","" completing the narration regarding his purchase from a Bedouin"","" a she-camel"","" and his consumption of its price. Muslim ibn Khālid al-Zanjī narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam"","" from Ibn al-Baylamānī"","" from Surraq. Imām Aḥmad said: And our shaykh — al-Ḥākim — narrated it in al-Mustadrak from what we had not read to him"","" from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAttāb al-ʿAbadī"","" from Abū Qilābah"","" from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad"","" from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"","" from Zayd ibn Aslam"","" from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī"","" who said: I saw an old man in al-Iskandarīyah"","" and he mentioned a narration completing the ḥadīth of Ibn Bashshār.\n\nThe crux of the ḥadīth of Surraq rests upon these narrators"","" and none of them are strong: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbdillāh and the two sons of Zayd. Even if the ḥadīth is from Zayd from Ibn al-Baylamānī"","" then Ibn al-Baylamānī is ḍaʿīf in ḥadīth"","" and there is a consensus of the scholars regarding his opposition (khilāf)"","" and they do not unanimously abandon a well-established narration as evidence of his weakness — or its abrogation"","" if it is established. And success is through Allah."""""
"11281","(11276) And in what Abū Dāwūd narrated in his *Marāsīl* from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd, from Muḥammad ibn Thawr, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, who said: \During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" there were debts upon men"","" and we do not know of any free man being sold for a debt.\"" Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us"","" Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us"","" Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us"","" and Abū Dāwūd narrated it."""""
"11282","(11277) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Mūsā ibn al-Sāʾib, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A man has the greatest right over his own property when he finds it"","" and the buyer should pursue the one who sold it to him.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it from ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn with the same meaning. [Musnad Aḥmad 5/13"","" Abū Dāwūd 3531]"""""
"11283","(11278) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Zayd ibn ʿUqbah, from his father, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If one of you loses his property or it is stolen from him and he finds it in the possession of a man"","" identifiable as his"","" then he has the greater right to it"","" and the buyer should return to the seller for the price.\"" [Musnad Aḥmad 4/222"","" Ibn Mājah 2331]"""""
"11284","(11279) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, al-Firyābī narrated to us, Sufyān informed us, from Wabr ibn Abī Dulaylah, from Fulān ibn Fulān, from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The delay of one who is able (to pay) renders his honour (i.e."","" speaking against him) permissible and his punishment permissible.\"" Sufyān said: \""His honour being permissible means that one may say: 'He has wronged me regarding my right"",""' and his punishment being permissible means that he may be imprisoned.\"" This Fulān ibn Fulān is Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maymūn ibn Musaykah. [Musnad Aḥmad 4/222"","" Abū Dāwūd 3628]"""""
"11285","(11280) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us, al-Ḍaḥḥāk Abū ʿĀṣim informed us, Wabr ibn Abī Dulaylah informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh—\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah both informed us, saying: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us, Abū Muslim al-Kajjī—who is Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh—narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Wabr ibn Abī Dulaylah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maymūn, from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The delay of one who is able (to pay) renders his honour permissible and his punishment permissible.\"""""""
"11286","(11281) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Nufaylī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak informed us, from Wabr ibn Abī Dulaylah, from Muḥammad ibn Maymūn, and he mentioned it. Ibn al-Mubārak said: \His honour being permissible means that severity may be used against him"","" and his punishment being permissible means that he may be detained.\""\n\nAbū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us"","" Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us"","" Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us"","" ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us"","" Maʿmar informed us"","" from Hammām ibn Munabbih"","" who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us"","" and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"","" the delay of the wealthy is an injustice"","" and if one of you is referred to a man of means"","" let him follow (that reference).\"" Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Maʿmar."""""
"11287","(11282) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī al-Ḍuḥā, from Masrūq, from Khabbāb, who said: \I was a blacksmith in the Jāhiliyyah"","" and al-ʿĀṣ ibn Wāʾil owed me some dirhams. I went to him to demand payment"","" and he said: 'I will not repay you until you disbelieve in Muḥammad.' I said: 'By Allah"","" I will not disbelieve until Allah causes you to die and then resurrects you.' He said: 'Then leave me until I die and am resurrected"","" and I will be given wealth and children"","" and I will repay you.' Then the verse was revealed: *'Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our signs and said"","" \""I will surely be given wealth and children\""?'*\"" [Sūrah Maryam 77]\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Isḥāq from Wahb ibn Jarīr"","" and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2091"","" Muslim 2795]"""""
"11288","(11283) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrating in Minā from Abū Hurayrah that a Bedouin demanded repayment of a debt that was owed to him from the Prophet ﷺ, and he spoke harshly to him. The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ were about to harm him, but the Prophet ﷺ said: \Leave him"","" for the one who is owed a right has a right to speak.\"" Then he said: \""Repay him.\"" They said: \""We can only find a camel better than his.\"" He said: \""Buy it and give it to him"","" for the best of you is the best in repayment.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their *Ṣaḥīḥ* from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2305"","" Muslim 1601]"""""
"11289","(11284) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Sarī narrated to us, al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥamzah ibn Yūsuf ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Salām said: \When Allah intended to guide Zayd ibn Saʿnah"","" Zayd said: 'There is nothing of the signs of prophethood that I did not recognize in the face of Muḥammad ﷺ when I looked at him"","" except two that I had not yet experienced from him: His forbearance overcomes his ignorance (i.e."","" his anger)"","" and the severity of ignorance shown towards him only increases his forbearance.' Then he mentioned the ḥadīth regarding his transaction with the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nZayd ibn Saʿnah said: \""When two or three days remained before the appointed time"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out for the funeral of a man from the Anṣār"","" and with him were Abū Bakr"","" ʿUmar"","" and ʿUthmān"","" along with a group of his Companions"","" may Allah be pleased with them. When he had prayed over the funeral and approached a wall to sit by it"","" I came to him and looked at him with a harsh face. Then I grabbed the collar of his shirt and his cloak and said: 'Pay me my due"","" O Muḥammad! By Allah"","" I have known you"","" the Banū ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"","" to be tardy in repayment. I have had experience of your dealings.' I looked at ʿUmar"","" and his eyes were spinning in his face like a revolving celestial sphere. Then he glared at me and said: 'O Jew! Are you doing this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? By the One Who sent him with the truth"","" were it not that I fear missing his (appointed time)"","" I would strike your neck with my sword.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was looking at ʿUmar"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" with calmness"","" composure"","" and a smile. Then he said: 'O ʿUmar"","" he and I were in need of something other than this from you: that you command me to pay well and that you command him to demand well. Take him"","" O ʿUmar"","" and pay him his due"","" and give him twenty additional ṣāʿs of dates in return for what you frightened him with.'\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth regarding his acceptance of Islam."""""
"11290","(11285) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Jaʿfar—meaning Ibn Rabīʿah—informed us, from al-Aʿraj, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī informed me from Kaʿb ibn Mālik that he had a sum of money owed to him by ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ḥadrad al-Aslamī. He met him and held on to him, and they spoke until their voices were raised. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by them and said: \O Kaʿb!\"" And he gestured with his hand as if to say: \""Half.\"" So he took half of what was owed and left half. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it"","" saying: al-Layth said"","" and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 457"","" Muslim 1558]"""""
"11291","(11286) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Asad narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Hirmās ibn Ḥabīb, a man from the people of the desert, narrated from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a debtor of mine, and he said to me: \Hold on to him.\"" Then he said to me: \""O brother of Banī Tamīm"","" what do you intend to do with your captive?\"""""""
"11292","(11287) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq al-Harawī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sāmī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Hirmās ibn Ḥabīb al-ʿAnbarī narrated from his father, from his grandfather: He brought a debtor to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \Hold on to him.\"" Then he met him after that and said: \""What has become of your captive"","" O brother of Banī al-ʿAnbar?\"""""""
"11293","(11288) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Wārah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Sābiq narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Abī Qays narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā, from his brother, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, who said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque while Ubayy ibn Kaʿb was holding fast to a man. He prayed, fulfilled his need, and then came out, and there he was still holding fast to him. He said: \Even now"","" O Ubayy? Even now"","" O Ubayy? Whoever seeks his brother's debt"","" let him seek it with full forbearance or without full forbearance.\"" When he heard that"","" he released him and followed him. He said: \""O Prophet of Allah"","" you said just now: 'Whoever seeks his brother's debt"","" let him seek it with full forbearance or without full forbearance.'\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""O Prophet of Allah"","" what is al-ʿafāf (forbearance)?\"" He said: \""Not reviling him"","" not being harsh upon him"","" not being obscene toward him"","" and not harming him.\"" He said: \""Full forbearance or without full forbearance?\"" He said: \""Fully exacting his right or leaving some of it.\"""""""
"11294","(11289) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl ibn Baḥr narrated to us; Abū al-Ṭāhir Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us. Both said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed me, from Ayyūb, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father: He was seeking a man for a debt, and the man hid from him. He said: \What compelled you to do this?\"" He said: \""Hardship.\"" So he made him swear an oath to that effect"","" and he swore. Then he called for his document and gave it to him"","" and he said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever shows leniency to one in difficulty or forgives his debt"","" Allah will relieve him of the distresses of the Day of Resurrection.'\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṣāliḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1563]"""""
"11295","(11290) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū Muḥammad Dalaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, and from Abū al-Zinād, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah and others: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭābb, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to make the insolvent person swear by Allah that he did not possess anything with which to repay, neither in property nor in cash—or he said, in ready money—and that if he were to find something from a source of which they were unaware, he would surely repay it. Then they would release him."
"11296","(11291) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādhī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah, from his father, from his grandfather: The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion for a part of the day, then released him. [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq 15313]"
"11297","(11292) Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Saqaṭī narrated to us in Makkah; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Abū Jaʿfar: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Detention is only until the matter becomes clear to the Imam. Whatever detention occurs after that is injustice.\"""""""
"11298","(11293) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated from Sufyān; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ narrated: I sold goods to a man, and when I had sold them to him, I learned that he was insolvent. So I brought him before Shurayḥ and said: \Take a guarantor for me from him.\"" Shurayḥ said: \""Your property is where you placed it.\"" He refused to take a guarantor for me. I said: \""Then I have stipulated that if my soul desires it"","" I have a greater right to it.\"" Shurayḥ said: \""You have acknowledged the sale; produce evidence for your condition.\"" [Muṣannaf ʿAbd al-Razzāq 14295]"""""
"11299","(11294) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Yazīd ibn Hurmuz: Najdah wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās asking him: \When does the orphanhood of the orphan end?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās wrote back to him: \""You have written to me asking when the orphanhood of the orphan ends. By my life"","" a man's beard may grow while he is still weak in taking for himself and weak in giving from it. So when he takes for himself from the good that people take"","" orphanhood has departed from him.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1812]"""""
"11300","(11295) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hārūn ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Yazīd ibn Hurmuz, who said: Najdah al-Ḥarūrī wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās, and he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: He said to Yazīd: \Write to him: 'You have asked me about the orphan—when does the name of orphanhood cease from him? Indeed"","" the name of orphanhood does not cease from him until he reaches maturity and sound judgment is discerned from him.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar."""""
"11301","(11296) And it was narrated from Qays ibn Sa'd from Yazid ibn Hurumaz from Ibn Abbas, who said: \As for what you asked regarding the termination of a minor's orphanhood"","" then when he reaches puberty and sound discretion is discerned in him"","" his orphanhood has ceased. So hand over his property to him.\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz — it was reported to us by Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim — Ahmad ibn Salama narrated to us — Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us — Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim reported to us — my father narrated to me"","" he said: I heard Qays"","" and he mentioned it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih]"""""
"11302","(11297) It was reported to us by Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari in Baghdad — it was reported to us by Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar — Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiya narrated from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar —\n\n(And) it was reported to us by Abu Abd al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri', both of them said: Al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) presented me for battle on the day of Uhud"","" and I was fourteen years of age"","" but he did not permit me. Then on the day of the Trench"","" when I was fifteen years of age"","" he granted me permission. I came to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz"","" and Umar was then the Caliph. I narrated this hadith to him and he said: 'Indeed"","" this is the demarcation between the young and the old.' And he wrote to his governors: 'Impose the obligation of military service upon those who have reached fifteen years of age"","" and whoever is below that"","" attach him to his family.'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ubayd. Both al-Bukhari and Muslim extracted it from the hadith of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar. [Sahih. al-Bukhari 2664"","" Muslim 1868]"""""
"11303","(11298) It was reported to us by Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz — Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quraysh informed me — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan reported to us — Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Ubayd Allah mentioned the hadith with its like, except that he said: \And He presented me on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen years of age"","" and He granted me permission.\"" Nafi' said: \""I came to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz and mentioned it to him"",""\"" except that he said: \""And whoever is below that age"","" place him among the dependents.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr"","" and al-Bukhari extracted it from two other chains from Ubayd Allah."""""
"11304","(11299) And Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, and he added therein at his statement \but he did not permit me\"": \""and he did not consider me to have reached maturity.\""\n\nIt was reported to me by the noble Abu al-Fath al-Umari — Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh reported to us — Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj mentioned it with its addition and its meaning"","" except that he did not mention \""among the dependents.\"" Ibn Sa'id said regarding this hadith: \""There is a rare word in it"","" which is his statement: 'and he did not consider me to have reached maturity.'\"""""""
"11305","(11300) It was reported to us by Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Adib — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Isma'ili reported to us — al-Mani'i reported to us — Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us — Abdullah ibn Idris and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: \I was presented before the Prophet (peace be upon him) on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years of age"","" and he considered me too young. Then I was presented before him in the year of the Trench when I was fifteen years of age"","" and he granted me permission.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Abi Shayba. And thus did Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi say from Ubayd Allah: \""He considered me too young and returned me with the boys.\"""""""
"11306","(11301) It was reported to us by Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz — Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim reported to us — Ahmad ibn Salama reported to us — Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar both said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us — Ubayd Allah narrated from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) presented me on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years of age"","" and he considered me too young and returned me with the boys. Then on the day of the Trench"","" he presented me when I was fifteen years of age"","" and he granted me permission.\"" Ubayd Allah said: \""And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: 'Permit those who have reached fifteen years of age for military service.'\"" Ubayd Allah said: \""I do not think Nafi' narrated this to anyone other than him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna.\n\nAnd in the hadith of Hammad ibn Zayd from Ubayd Allah from Nafi' from Ibn Umar: \""That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) accepted Ibn Umar and Rafi' ibn Khadij on the day of the Trench"","" and both of them were fifteen years of age.\"" Ishaq narrated it from Rawh from him."""""
"11307","(11302) It was reported to us by Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Sukkari in Baghdad — it was reported to us by Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar — Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiya narrated from Abu Ma'shar from Nafi' from Ibn Umar, who said: \I was presented before the Prophet (peace be upon him) on the day of Badr when I was thirteen years of age"","" and he did not permit me to fight. And I was presented before him on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years of age"","" and he did not permit me to fight. And I was presented before him on the day of the Trench when I was fifteen years of age"","" and he permitted me to fight.\"""""""
"11308","(11303) It was reported to us by Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan al-Adl in Baghdad — Abu Amr ibn al-Sammak reported to us — Hanbal ibn Ishaq ibn Hanbal narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated from Musa ibn Uqba from Ibn Shihab, who said: \These are the military campaigns of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in which he fought: the battle of Badr in the month of Ramadan in the year two; then he fought on the day of Uhud in Shawwal of the year three; then he fought on the day of the Trench"","" which is the day of the Confederates"","" and against Banu Qurayza in Shawwal of the year four; then he fought against Banu al-Mustaliq and Banu Lihyan in Sha'ban of the year five; then he fought on the day of Khaybar in the year six; then he fought on the day of the Conquest in Ramadan of the year eight; and he fought on the day of Hunayn and besieged the people of Ta'if in Shawwal of the year eight.\"" And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith.\n\n[Sahih. al-Bukhari 4026]"""""
"11309","(11304) It was reported to us by Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad — Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us — Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me — Hassan ibn Abdullah narrated from Ibn Luha'ita — Abu al-Aswad narrated from Urwa, who said: \This is the mention of the military campaigns of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in which he fought.\""\n\nYa'qub said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated from Musa from Ibn Shihab"","" who said: \""This is the mention of the military campaigns of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in which he fought"",""\"" and he mentioned it with the same narration as Hanbal."""""
"11310","(11305) It was reported to us by Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal reported to us — al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyib reported to us — Ahmad ibn Hanbal reported to us — Musa ibn Dawud narrated, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas say: \Badr took place a year and a half after the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in Madinah"","" and Uhud was one year after that"","" and the Trench in the year four"","" and Banu al-Mustaliq in the year five"","" and Khaybar in the year six"","" and Hudaybiyyah in the year of Khaybar"","" and the Conquest in the year eight"","" and Banu Qurayza in the year of the Trench.\"""""""
"11311","(11306) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: The Battle of Uḥud took place in Shawwāl of the third year. And through this chain of narration from Ibn Isḥāq, he said: The Battle of al-Khandaq took place in Shawwāl of the fifth year.\n\nThe Sheikh said: The statement of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, and then al-Zuhrī, in the narration of Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from him, and then Mālik ibn Anas regarding the Battle of al-Khandaq — that it occurred in the fourth year — is more deserving of correctness than the statement of one who said it occurred in the fifth year, because of the agreement of their statement with the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar, given the continuous chain of the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar and its established authenticity, and the disconnected nature of the statement of others. Some of the people of knowledge have reconciled between their statements by saying that Uḥud occurred two and a half years after the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Madīnah, and al-Khandaq occurred four and a half years after his arrival. Whoever said \the fourth year\"" meant after the completion of four years and before the completion of the fifth"","" and whoever said \""the fifth year\"" meant after the completion of four years and the entry into the fifth year. As for the statement of Ibn ʿUmar regarding the day of Uḥud — \""I was fourteen years of age; I had entered into the fourteenth\"" — and his statement regarding the day of al-Khandaq — \""I was fifteen years of age; I had completed it and exceeded it\"" — he did not transmit the excess because he understood from the indication of the circumstance and the ruling being attached to fifteen years without the excess. And Allah knows best. This method is"","" in my view"","" the most authentic. In the account of al-Khandaq in the Maghāzī of Abī al-Aswad from ʿUrwah"","" and the Maghāzī of Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"","" it is stated that there were two years between Uḥud and al-Khandaq. And Allah knows best."""""
"11312","(11307) As for what Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Ṭāyikānī narrated from Abī al-Muqātil al-Samarqandī from ʿAwf from Khilās from Abū Hurayrah, marfūʿ: \The pen is raised from three: from the boy until he experiences wet dreams. If he does not experience wet dreams until he reaches eighteen years of age…\"" — this is among what Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of: Aḥmad ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Zāhid informed me: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd al-Tūyakī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Ṭāyikānī narrated to us"","" and he mentioned it within a long fabricated ḥadīth. And this Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim was well known for fabricating aḥādīth. We seek refuge in Allah from being forsaken.\n\nAnd Qatādah narrated from Anas"","" marfūʿ: \""When the boy reaches fifteen years of age"","" the prescribed punishments are enforced upon him.\"" Its chain of narration is weak"","" and it is recorded in al-Khilāfiyyāt with its chain."""""
"11313","(11308) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from Abī al-Ḍuḥā from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The pen is raised from three: from the sleeper until he awakens"","" from the boy until he experiences wet dreams"","" and from the insane person until he regains consciousness.\""\n\nAnd we have received it from the ḥadīth of Wahayb from Khālid al-Ḍadhāʾ"","" and from the ḥadīth of Abī Ẓabyān from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) from ʿAlī"","" both marfūʿ and mawqūf"","" and from the ḥadīth of Abī Ẓabyān from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" marfūʿ."""""
"11314","(11309) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Madanī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us from his father from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ruqaysh, that he heard elders from Banī ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf and from his maternal uncle ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Aḥmad say: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \There is no orphanhood after puberty"","" and there is no fasting of a day until the night.\""\n\nAnd this has been narrated through another chain from ʿAlī and from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh"","" marfūʿ."""""
"11315","(11310) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī informed us in it: Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Sumayʿ narrated to us: Abū Rāzin narrated to us, who said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \When a woman experiences wet dreams"","" that which is obligatory upon her mothers in terms of covering becomes obligatory upon her.\"""""""
"11316","(11311) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Barṭī al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatādah from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Ṣafiyyah bint al-Ḥārith from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted except with a head covering (khimār).\"""""""
"11317","(11312) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ayyūb from Muḥammad, that ʿĀʾishah came down to Ṣafiyyah Umm Ṭalḥah al-Ṭalaḥāt and saw her daughters. She said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered while there was a young girl in my chamber. He threw his garment to me and said: 'Divide it into two pieces; give this one half and the girl who is with Umm Salamah half"","" for I see that she has menstruated"",""' or he said"","" 'I see that they both have menstruated.'\"""""""
"11318","(11313) The jurist Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shurayḥ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Sharīk narrated to us from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Zurʿah from Māhān al-Ḥanafī from Umm Salamah, who said: \When the young girl menstruates"","" that which is obligatory upon her mother in terms of covering becomes obligatory upon her.\"" [Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"","" 2150]"""""
"11319","(11314) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from Abī Umāmah from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: When Banū Qurayẓah submitted to the judgment of Saʿd (may Allah be pleased with him), the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for him, and he was nearby. He came riding a donkey, and when he drew near, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Stand up to receive your master.\"" He came and sat before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" who said: \""These people have submitted to your judgment.\"" He said: \""I judge regarding them that the fighters be killed and the offspring be taken as captives.\"" He said: \""You have judged among them with the judgment of Allah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and others"","" and Muslim narrated it through two other chains from Shuʿbah.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3043]"""""
"11320","(11315) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Saqqāʾ and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ both informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us: Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr narrated to me: ʿAṭiyyah al-Qurazī narrated to me, who said: \I was among the captives of Qurayẓah. They would examine us: whoever had grown pubic hair was killed"","" and whoever had not grown pubic hair was not killed. I was among those who had not grown pubic hair.\"""""""
"11321","(11316) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī informed us; al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from ʿAṭiyyah al-Quraẓī, who said: I was presented before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the day of Qurayẓah, and they were doubtful regarding me. The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that I be examined as to whether pubic hair had grown. They looked at me and found that pubic hair had not grown, so he released me and placed me among the captives."
"11322","(11317) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr; ʿAṭiyyah al-Quraẓī narrated to me, saying: We were presented before the Prophet (ﷺ) at the time of Qurayẓah. Whoever among us had reached puberty or whose pubic hair had grown was executed. He said: They looked at me, and my pubic hair had not grown, so I was left alone."
"11323","(11318) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam al-Miṣrī informed us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Jurayj and Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed me from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid; ʿAṭiyyah — a man from Banī Qurayẓah — informed him that the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stripped him on the day of Qurayẓah, and when they did not see that the razor had passed over his pubic hair — meaning his pubic hair had not grown — they spared him from execution. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh."
"11324","(11319) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Khaṭmī informed us from ʿUmarah ibn Khuzaymah from Kathīr ibn al-Sāʾib, who narrated to me: The sons of Qurayẓah informed me that they were presented before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time of Qurayẓah. Whoever among them had reached puberty or whose pubic hair had grown was executed, and whoever had not reached puberty or whose pubic hair had not grown was left alone."
"11325","(11320) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us; Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, who said: A young boy was brought to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) who had falsely accused a girl of zinā in his poetry. He said: \Examine him.\"" He was found not to have grown pubic hair"","" so the ḥadd punishment was averted from him. Abū ʿUbayd (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Some narrate this from ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). Abū ʿUbayd said: His statement \""ibtahar\"" (he falsely accused) means that he slandered her with himself"","" claiming \""I did such-and-such with her"",""\"" while lying. If he had actually done it"","" that would be called \""ibtiyār.\"""""""
"11326","(11321) Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us; Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ayyūb ibn Mūsā narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, who said: Ibn Abī al-Ṣaʿbah was brought to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) after he had confessed in his poetry to having committed zinā with a woman. He said: \Examine his lower garment area.\"" They looked and found that hair had not grown. He said: \""Had the hair grown"","" I would have had the ḥadd punishment carried out on him.\"" And from Sufyān"","" Abū Ḥuṣayn narrated to us from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr"","" who said: A young boy was brought to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) who had committed theft. He said: \""Examine his lower garment area.\"" They looked and found that hair had not grown"","" so he did not have his hand cut off."""""
"11327","(11322) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Jawwāb narrated to us; ʿAmmār — that is, ibn Ruzayq — narrated to us from Ashʿath ibn Sawwār from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Ḥafṣ from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: When a boy incurs a ḥadd punishment and there is doubt as to whether he has experienced nocturnal emission or not, his pubic hair should be examined."
"11328","(11323) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of the Most High: \And test the orphans until they reach the age of marriage; if then you find sound judgment in them"","" release their property to them\"" (al-Nisāʾ: 6). He said: Allah"","" Blessed and Exalted"","" says: \""Test the orphans at the time of puberty. If you discern sound judgment in them regarding their affairs and the proper management of their wealth"","" then release their property to them and have witnesses over them.\"""""""
"11329","(11324) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Hishām informed us from al-Ḥasan, who said: \Sound judgment\"" means righteousness in religion and the safeguarding of one's wealth."""""
"11330","(11325) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī both informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf narrated to us from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān regarding His words: \And test the orphans\"" — meaning the guardians and executors. He says: \""Test them when they reach the age of marriage; if then you find sound judgment in them\"" (al-Nisāʾ: 6) — that is"","" inclination toward religion and the proper management of their wealth — \""then release their property to them\"" (al-Nisāʾ: 6)."""""
"11331","(11326) It was narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān, who reported to us Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār, who reported to us ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk, who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us al-Layth from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, that Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith informed him: She had freed a female slave of hers without seeking the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was her day on which he would visit her, she said: \Are you aware"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" that I have freed my slave-girl so-and-so?\"" He said: \""Did you do so?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Had you given her to your maternal uncles"","" it would have been greater in reward for you.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"","" and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Ibn Bukayr."""""
"11332","(11327) It was narrated to us Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad, who reported to us Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz, who narrated to us Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām, who narrated to us Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad.\n\n(Ḥ) And it was narrated to us Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who reported to us Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Anmāṭī, who narrated to us Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh, who narrated to us Ḥajjāj, who said: Ibn Jurayj informed me that Ibn Abī Mulaikah informed him that ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr informed him from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr: She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \O Prophet of Allah"","" I have nothing except what al-Zubayr brings to me. Is there any sin upon me if I set aside some of what he brings?\"" He said: \""Set aside what you can"","" and do not keep count"","" lest Allah keep count against you.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim from Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh and others"","" and it was narrated by al-Bukhārī from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm and others from Ḥajjāj."""""
"11333","(11328) It was narrated to us Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān, who reported to us Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd, who narrated to us Ibn Milḥān, who narrated to us Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, who narrated to us al-Layth.\n\n(Ḥ) And it was narrated to us Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who reported to us Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm, who narrated to us Aḥmad ibn Salamah, who narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd, who narrated to us al-Layth from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \O Muslim women"","" let no neighbour belittle a gift to her neighbour"","" even if it be a sheep's hoof.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"","" and it was narrated by al-Bukhārī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from al-Layth."""""
"11334","(11329) It was narrated to us Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān, who reported to us Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd, who narrated to us Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq, who narrated to us Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, who narrated to us Shuʿbah from Ayyūb from ʿAṭāʾ.\n\n(Ḥ) And Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, who narrated to us Ḥammād ibn Zayd from Ayyūb, who said: I heard ʿAṭāʾ say: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās say: \I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ\"" — or ʿAṭāʾ said: \""I bear witness concerning Ibn ʿAbbās\"" — that he said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon after the prayer on the day of ʿĪd"","" then he came to the women"","" thinking that they had not heard him"","" and Bilāl was with him. He exhorted them and commanded them to give charity. So the woman would cast her ring and her earring"","" and Bilāl would collect them in the fold of his garment.\"" This is the wording of Ḥammād's narration. In the narration of Shuʿbah it is: \""He went out on the day of Fiṭr and prayed two rakʿahs"","" then delivered a sermon"","" then came to the women and commanded them to give charity"","" and Bilāl was with him"","" so they began casting [their jewellery].\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Shuʿbah"","" close to the wording of Ḥammād"","" and it was narrated by Muslim from Abū al-Rabīʿ from Ḥammād."""""
"11335","(11330) It was narrated to us Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, who reported to us Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Harawī, who narrated to us Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh, who narrated to us Abū ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr, who reported to us Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman's gift from her wealth is not permissible when her husband has authority over her (i.e."","" in marriage).\"""""""
"11336","(11331) And it was narrated to us Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak, who reported to us ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar, who narrated to us Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb, who narrated to us Abū Dāwūd from Ḥammād, who narrated to us Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When a man has authority over a woman"","" her gift is not permissible except with his permission.\"""""""
"11337","(11332) It was narrated to us Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who narrated to us ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh, who narrated to us Hishām ibn ʿAlī and Muḥammad ibn Ghālib, who both said: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, who narrated to us Ḥammād from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind and Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman has no authority over her wealth when her husband has authority over her (i.e."","" in marriage).\"" It was narrated by Abū Dāwūd from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl."""""
"11338","(11333) And it was narrated to us Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī, who reported to us Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah, who narrated to us Abū Dāwūd, who narrated to us Abū Kāmil, who narrated to us Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith, who narrated to us Ḥusayn from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, that his father informed him from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman's gift is not permissible except with the permission of her husband.\"""""""
"11339","(11334) It was narrated to us Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, who narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm, who narrated to us al-Rabīʿ, who said: al-Shāfiʿī said — referring to this hadith: \We heard it"","" but it is not established with a sound chain"","" so it is incumbent upon us to speak about it. The Qurʾān indicates the contrary"","" then the Sunnah"","" then the narrations (āthār)"","" then reason.\"" And he said in Mukhtaṣar al-Buwayṭī and al-Rabīʿ: \""It is possible that this pertains to what is recommended"","" just as it is said that she may not fast a voluntary fast while her husband is present except with his permission; yet if she does so"","" her fast is valid. And if she goes out without his permission and sells"","" it is valid. And Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her) freed a slave-girl before informing the Prophet ﷺ"","" and he did not censure her for that. This"","" along with other evidence"","" indicates that the statement of the Prophet ﷺ — if he indeed said it — was a matter of etiquette and recommendation for her.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The chain of this hadith going back to ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is sound. Whoever establishes the hadiths of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is bound to establish this one"","" except that the hadiths that preceded it in this chapter have sounder chains"","" and in them"","" as well as in the verses of the Qurʾān that al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) cited as evidence"","" there is indication of the validity of her disposal of her own wealth without the husband's involvement. Thus"","" the hadith of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is interpreted as pertaining to etiquette and recommendation"","" as he indicated in the book of al-Buwayṭī. And with Allah lies success."""""
"11340","(11335) It was narrated to us Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who reported to us Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl, who narrated to us Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ, who said: I heard ʿAlī ibn ʿUthmān say: Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Ṭalaḥī narrated to me from al-Zubayr ibn al-Madīnī, their judge, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar purchased a piece of land for six hundred thousand dirhams. ʿAlī and ʿUthmān considered placing a restriction (ḥajr) on him. He said: \I met al-Zubayr and he said: 'No one has ever made a cheaper purchase than the one you have made.' Then ʿAbdullāh mentioned the restriction to him. He said: 'If I had wealth"","" I would be your partner.' He said: 'Then I will lend you half the wealth.' He said: 'Then I am your partner.' He said: \""Then ʿAlī and ʿUthmān came to them while they were negotiating. He said: 'What are you negotiating about?' They mentioned the restriction on ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar. He said: 'Would you place a restriction on a man whose partner I am?' They said: 'No"","" by my life.' He said: 'I am his partner.' So they left him alone.\"""""""
"11341","(11336) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal say: ʿAmr al-Nāqid narrated to us: Abū Yūsuf al-Qāḍī Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar came to al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām and said: \I have purchased such-and-such"","" and ʿAlī intends to come to the Commander of the Faithful"","" ʿUthmān — meaning — so that he may ask him to impose a restriction (ḥajr) upon me regarding it.\"" Al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I am your partner in the sale.\"" Then he went to ʿUthmān and mentioned that to him. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""How can I impose a restriction upon a man in a sale in which al-Zubayr is a partner?\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) would not seek the restriction except that he considered it valid; and al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him)"","" had the restriction been invalid"","" would have said: \""No restriction may be imposed upon a free"","" adult person.\"" Likewise ʿUthmān — rather"","" all of them recognized the validity of restriction according to the ḥadīth of your companion."""""
"11342","(11337) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdād: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān narrated to us: Shuʿayb narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Ḥajjāj ibn Abī Manīʿ narrated from his grandfather, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿAwf ibn al-Ḥārith ibn al-Ṭufayl — who was the maternal nephew of ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), through her mother — narrated that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was informed that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr said, regarding a gift or a charitable grant that ʿĀʾishah had given: \By Allah"","" ʿĀʾishah must desist"","" or I shall surely impose a restriction upon her.\"" She said: \""Did he say this?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""It is a vow upon me to Allah that I shall never speak to Ibn al-Zubayr again.\"" When the estrangement from her grew prolonged"","" Ibn al-Zubayr sought intercession with her. She said: \""By Allah"","" I shall never intercede for anyone regarding him"","" and I shall never expiate the vow that I have made.\"" When this became too much for Ibn al-Zubayr"","" he spoke to al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad ibn ʿAbd Yaghūth"","" both of whom were from Banū Zuhrah"","" and said to them: \""I adjure you by Allah"","" take me in to ʿĀʾishah"","" for it is not permissible for her to vow to sever ties with me.\"" So al-Miswar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān came with Ibn al-Zubayr"","" wrapping him in their cloaks"","" until they sought permission to enter upon ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). They said: \""Peace be upon you"","" and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. May we enter?\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Enter.\"" They said: \""All of us?\"" She said: \""Yes"","" enter"","" all of you"",""\"" not knowing that Ibn al-Zubayr was with them. When they entered"","" Ibn al-Zubayr went behind the curtain"","" embraced ʿĀʾishah"","" and began adjuring her and weeping. Al-Miswar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān also began adjuring her to speak to him and accept his apology"","" saying: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade what you know of estrangement"","" and it is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three nights.\"" When they persisted in reminding and urging her"","" she began reminding them and weeping"","" saying: \""I have made a vow"","" and a vow is a serious matter.\"" They continued with her until she spoke to Ibn al-Zubayr. Then she expiated her vow by freeing forty slaves. Thereafter"","" whenever she remembered that vow after having freed the forty slaves"","" she would weep until her tears soaked her head-cover.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. The Sheikh said: Here is ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) — she does not deny the validity of restriction (ḥajr)"","" and Ibn al-Zubayr considered it valid. Restriction was well known in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"","" and no rejection of it has been narrated from him. This is indicated by what follows."""""
"11343","(11338) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us: Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to engage in trade, but there was a weakness in his mental capacity. His family came to the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: \O Prophet of Allah"","" impose a restriction upon so-and-so"","" for he engages in trade while there is a weakness in his mental capacity.\"" The Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) called him and forbade him from trading. The man said: \""O Prophet of Allah"","" I cannot bear to abstain from trading.\"" He (peace be upon him) said: \""If you will not abandon trading"","" then say: 'Take it"","" take it"",""' and there shall be no deception.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Rūdhbārī. In the narration of Ibn Bushrān: \""A man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to engage in trade"",""\"" and the rest is the same.\n\nIt is as though the Prophet (peace be upon him)"","" when he saw him"","" did not consider him deserving of restriction"","" and his leaving him without imposing restriction is evidence of the permissibility of restriction."""""
"11344","(11339) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Raffāʾ al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bushr narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father, from the jurists of Madīnah, that they used to say: \The spendthrift (safīh) under guardianship and the slave — their divorce is valid"","" and their manumission is invalid"","" except that the spendthrift may free his mother of a child (umm walad) if he wishes.\"""""""
"11345","(11340) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from al-Shaʿbī, from Warrād, the freedman of al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: \Allah has forbidden you to disobey your mothers"","" to bury your daughters alive"","" and to withhold what is due. And He has disliked for you three things: idle talk"","" excessive questioning"","" and squandering wealth.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah"","" from Jarīr"","" and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm."""""
"11346","(11341) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Faḍl al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sūqah narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Thaqafī, from Warrād, who said: Al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah wrote to Muʿāwiyah — and Warrād claimed that he wrote it with his own hand — \I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Allah has forbidden three things and prohibited three things: disobedience to mothers"","" burying daughters alive"","" and withholding what is due and making unjust demands. And He has prohibited three things: idle talk"","" squandering wealth"","" and persistent begging.'\"""""""
"11347","(11342) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us: Ayyūb ibn Muḥammad al-Wazzān narrated to us: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sūqah narrated it with its meaning, but he did not mention \and Warrād claimed that he wrote it with his own hand.\"" Muḥammad said: ʿAbd al-Malik informed me that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr was asked about squandering wealth (iḍāʿat al-māl). He said: \""It is that a man is given provision by Allah and he places it in what Allah has forbidden for him.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Shaʿbī"","" from Warrād"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar"","" from Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah."""""
"11348","(11343) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Shujāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated from Zuhayr, that Abū Isḥāq narrated to them from Abī al-ʿUbaydayn, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \Spending in other than what is right is squandering (tabdhīr).\"""""""
"11349","(11344) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: It was read to Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir while I heard: Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us: Kathīr ibn Zayd narrated from al-Walīd ibn Rabbāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Reconciliation (ṣulḥ) is permissible among Muslims.\"""""""
"11350","(11345) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Daqqāq narrated to us in Baghdād: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik, from his father, that he demanded repayment of a debt owed to him by Ibn Abī Ḥadrad in the mosque, and their voices rose until the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) heard them. He came out and lifted the curtain of his chamber and said: \O Kaʿb"","" remit this much of your debt\"" — and he gestured"","" meaning half. He said: \""Yes.\"" So he (Kaʿb) paid the remainder.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Musnadī"","" from ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar."""""
"11351","(11346) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā b. Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad b. al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr b. Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus b. Yazīd informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, who said: ʿAbd Allāh b. Kaʿb b. Mālik narrated to me that Kaʿb b. Mālik informed him: that he demanded repayment of a debt owed to him by Ibn Abī Ḥadrad in the mosque during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Their voices rose until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) heard them while he was in his house. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to them until he lifted the curtain of his chamber and called out, \O Kaʿb!\"" He said"","" \""Here I am"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He gestured to him with his hand"","" saying"","" \""Remit half of your debt.\"" Kaʿb said"","" \""I have done so"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" \""Rise and pay it (the remainder).\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad"","" who is Ibn Ṣāliḥ"","" and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah"","" both of them on the authority of Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11352","(11347) Abū Zakariyyā b. Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr b. al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: Baḥr b. Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to me: Yūnus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ibn Mālik narrated to me that Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh informed him: that his father was killed as a martyr on the day of Uḥud and he was in debt. The creditors became severe in demanding their rights. Jābir said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and spoke to him"","" and he asked them to accept the fruit of my garden and to absolve my father (of the remainder)"","" but they refused. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not give them my garden"","" nor did he break it up for them"","" but he said"","" 'I shall come to you in the morning.' He came to us when morning arrived and walked among the palm trees and invoked blessing upon their fruit. I harvested them and paid the creditors their dues"","" and there still remained some of the fruit for us. I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him of that. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to ʿUmar"","" who was sitting there"","" 'Listen"","" O ʿUmar"","" to what he is saying.' ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"","" 'Did we not already know that you are His Messenger? By Allah"","" you are indeed the Messenger of Allah.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī 2601]"""""
"11353","(11348) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Ḥalīm al-Marwazī narrated to me: Abū al-Muwajjah informed me: ʿAbdān informed me: ʿAbd Allāh informed me: Yūnus b. Yazīd informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ibn Kaʿb b. Mālik narrated to me that Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh informed him, and he mentioned it similarly, adding in his narration: He said, \And (regarding) Abū Lubābah"","" an orphan under his care had a dispute with him concerning a palm tree"","" and the judgment was given in favour of Abū Lubābah. The boy wept"","" so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abū Lubābah"","" 'Give him your palm tree.' He said"","" 'No.' He said"","" 'Give it to him"","" and you shall have a cluster in Paradise.' He said"","" 'No.' Ibn al-Daḥdāḥah heard of this and said to Abū Lubābah"","" 'Will you sell me that cluster of yours in exchange for my garden?' He said"","" 'Yes.' Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said"","" 'The palm tree that you wished to give to the orphan—if I give it to him"","" shall I have a cluster in Paradise?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" 'Yes.' Then Ibn al-Daḥdāḥah was killed as a martyr on the day of Uḥud"","" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"","" 'How many a hanging cluster there is for Ibn al-Daḥdāḥah in Paradise!'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān"","" without the story of Abū Lubābah. It appears that al-Zuhrī mentioned the story of Abū Lubābah as a mursal narration.\n\nIt was also narrated by Shuʿayb b. Abī Ḥamzah"","" on the authority of al-Zuhrī"","" on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab"","" on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" as a mursal narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11354","(11349) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh b. Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād: Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Jaʿfar b. Muḥammad b. al-Azhar narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal b. Ghassān al-Ghulābī narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Sharīk narrated, on the authority of Abī Isḥāq, who said: A man was owed one thousand five hundred dirhams by another man. They refused to pay him until the five hundred was waived. He wrote a document and acquitted him (of the five hundred), then he demanded the five hundred from him. They took their dispute to Sharīḥ. He said to the witnesses, \Did he place the five hundred in his hand?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" So he ordered him to return it.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""We also do not permit the waiving (of debt) if it is conditional.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11355","(11350) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās b. Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Manṣūr b. Salamah Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl narrated, on the authority of Kathīr b. Zayd, on the authority of al-Walīd b. Rabāḥ, on the authority of Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Reconciliation is permissible among Muslims.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11356","(11351) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr b. Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Marwān b. Muḥammad narrated to us: Sulaymān b. Bilāl—or ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad; Abū Dāwūd was uncertain—on the authority of Kathīr b. Zayd, and he mentioned it similarly, adding: \Except a reconciliation that makes lawful what is unlawful"","" or makes unlawful what is lawful.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11357","(11352) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: al-Ḥusayn b. al-Ḥasan b. Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us: Abū Yaḥyā b. Abī Masarrat narrated to us: Ibn Zabalah narrated to us: Kathīr b. ʿAbd Allāh narrated, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Reconciliation is permissible among Muslims"","" except a reconciliation that makes unlawful what is lawful"","" or makes lawful what is unlawful.\""\n\nAbū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī likewise narrated it on the authority of Kathīr b. ʿAbd Allāh. The reliance is upon his narration"","" for Muḥammad b. al-Ḥasan b. Zabalah is weak beyond measure. The narration of Kathīr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr b. ʿAwf al-Muzanī"","" when combined with what precedes it"","" is strengthened. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""""
"11358","(11353) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid b. Bilāl narrated to us: Yaḥyā b. al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated, on the authority of Idrīs al-Awdī, who said: Saʿīd b. Abī Burdah brought out a document to us and said, \This is the letter of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) to Abū Mūsā"",""\"" and he mentioned it"","" and in it was: \""Reconciliation is permissible among people"","" except a reconciliation that makes lawful what is unlawful"","" or makes unlawful what is lawful.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11359","(11354) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl b. Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad b. Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd b. Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Dāwūd b. Abī Hind narrated, on the authority of ʿAṭāʾ, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, that he saw no harm in al-mukhārajah (mutual withdrawal) in matters of inheritance. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"11360","(11355) He said: And Saʿīd b. Manṣūr narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated, on the authority of ʿUmar b. Abī Salamah, on the authority of his father, who said: The wife of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān was reconciled concerning her share of one-quarter of the one-eighth for eighty thousand.\n\nThis is understood to mean that she was aware of the amount of her share.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Shaʿbī, on the authority of Sharīḥ, that he said: \Any woman who is reconciled concerning her one-eighth and is not informed of what her husband has left—that is entirely suspicion.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11361","(11356) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī; Sālim informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, when a man owed him gold or silver, would give him the choice at the time of repayment, saying: \Which of the two types is more preferable to you?\"" Then he would repay it according to the prevailing exchange rate of the people"","" or he would exchange it and take possession of it. When the man accepted that"","" ʿAbdullāh saw no harm in it. [Ḥasan]"""""
"11362","(11357) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāyinī informed us there; Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Khālid al-Marwazī informed us in Baghdād; Khalaf ibn Hishām informed us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ informed us from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khāld from al-Shaʿbī from Saʿīd, the freed slave of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, who said: I owed Ibn ʿUmar some dirhams, so I went to him to demand payment. He said: \When my stipend comes"","" I will pay you.\"" He said: Then his stipend came — a hundred dinars. He said: So I went to him"","" and he said to his young servant: \""Take these dinars to the market; when a price is established for them"","" give him his dirhams in exchange. And if he prefers that you sell them for dirhams"","" then sell them and give him his dirhams.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11363","(11358) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī informed me; my grandfather informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us; Mālik informed me from al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \Whoever has committed a wrong against his brother should seek his forgiveness for it"","" for there shall be neither dinars nor dirhams there. Before anything else"","" his brother's rights shall be taken from his good deeds. And if he has no good deeds"","" the evil deeds of his brother shall be cast upon him.\""\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways. [Ṣaḥīḥ — al-Bukhārī 2449"","" 6534]"""""
"11364","(11359) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb informed us; Usāmah ibn Zayd informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Rāfiʿ, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, informed us from Umm Salamah, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when two men from the Anṣār came disputing over matters that had long since lapsed and become obsolete. The Prophet ﷺ said: \I judge between you only in that which no revelation has been sent down to me. Whomever I rule in favour of by virtue of an argument I perceive"","" and he thereby wrongfully seizes a portion of his brother's wealth"","" he shall come bearing it as a yoke around his neck on the Day of Resurrection.\"" The two men wept"","" and each one said: \""My right belongs to him"","" O Messenger of Allah — take it!\"" He said: \""No. But go"","" draw lots"","" and intend good. Then let each of you absolve his companion.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11365","(11360) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Misʿar informed us from Azhar from Muḥārib, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Send back the disputing parties so that they may reconcile"","" for the adjudication of judgment breeds rancour among the people.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11366","(11361) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us; Maʿrif ibn Wāṣil informed us; Muḥārib ibn Dithār, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Send back the disputing parties"","" perhaps they may reconcile"","" for reconciliation is more conducive to truthfulness and further removed from enmity.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11367","(11362) He said: And Yaḥyā informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us from ʿAlī ibn Badhīmah al-Jazarī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Send back the disputing parties when there is kinship between them"","" for the adjudication of judgment begets hatred among them.\"" These narrations from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) are munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11368","(11363) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Mūsā ibn ʿUbaydah informed us from Yaʿqūb ibn Zayd that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) went out on a Friday, and a water spout belonging to al-ʿAbbās poured down upon him. He ordered it to be removed, so it was removed. Al-ʿAbbās said: \You have removed my water spout! By Allah"","" the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself placed it where it was with his own hand.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By Allah"","" you shall place it back with your own hand"","" and there shall be no ladder for you except ʿUmar.\"" So al-ʿAbbās placed his feet upon ʿUmar's shoulders and restored it to its place. It has also been narrated through two other chains from ʿUmar and al-ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11369","(11364) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Musayyib informed us; Abū ʿUmayr ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Naḥḥās informed us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us; Shuʿayb al-Khurāsānī informed us from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī from Saʿīb ibn al-Musayyib that when ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to expand the Mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the expansion encroached upon the house of al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. He then narrated a story in which he mentioned the account of the water spout with the same meaning.\nIt was also narrated by ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father from his grandfather from ʿUmar with the same meaning. And it was narrated by Ibn ʿUyaynah from Abū Hārūn al-Madanī in a disconnected form, abridged, with part of its meaning. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"11370","(11365) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Muqriʾ informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl informed us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us; Saʿīd informed us from Qatādah from Khilās from Abī Rāfiʿ from Abū Hurayrah that two men brought a dispute to the Prophet ﷺ over some merchandise, neither of them having any proof. The Prophet ﷺ said: \Draw lots upon the oath"","" whether one likes it or dislikes it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11371","(11366) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Burdah, from his father, from Abū Mūsā, who said: Two men brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning a matter for which neither of them had any proof. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged between them by dividing it equally in half."
"11372","(11367) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated from — and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \He divided it between them equally in half.\"""""""
"11373","(11368) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyāṭī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sulaymān ibn Abī al-Jūn al-ʿAnasī narrated to us; Daththim ibn Qurān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Anṣārī narrated from Ḥudhayfah, who said: A people disputed among themselves over enclosures between them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, and I judged in favour of the one in whose direction the fastenings of the ropes were found. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: \You have judged correctly.\"" This ḥadīth is narrated uniquely by Daththim ibn Qurān al-Yamāmī"","" and he is weak (ḍaʿīf). There is disagreement regarding its isnād; it has been narrated in this manner and also from two other chains. [Weak]"""""
"11374","(11369) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh both informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Manīʿ narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us. Both said: Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Daththim ibn Qurān narrated to us; ʿUqayl ibn Dīnār, the mawlā of Jāriyah ibn Ẓafar, narrated from Jāriyah ibn Ẓafar, that a house belonged to two brothers. They erected a partition wall in the middle of it. Then they both died, and each left descendants. The descendants of each claimed the partition wall for themselves to the exclusion of the other. The two sets of descendants brought their dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, who sent Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān, may Allah be pleased with him, to judge between them. He judged the partition wall in favour of the one in whose direction the fastenings of the ropes were found. Then he returned and informed the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \You have judged correctly.\"" Daththim said — or he said: \""You have done well.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Dāwūd ibn Rushayd. [Weak]"""""
"11375","(11370) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; ʿUmar ibn Sinān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ādam ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Salamah ibn al-Ḥasan al-Kūfī narrated from Daththim ibn Qurān, from Nimrān ibn Jāriyah ibn Ẓafar, from his father, who said: A people came disputing to the Prophet ﷺ over a hut. He sent Ḥudhayfah with them, and he judged the hut in favour of the one in whose direction the ropes were found. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \You have done well.\"" And thus narrated Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh from Daththim. These are three different narrations of disagreement regarding Daththim ibn Qurān's isnād."""""
"11376","(11371) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: \Daththim ibn Qurān is weak (ḍaʿīf).\"" The Shaykh said: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn counted him"","" in the narration of Ibn Abī Maryam from him"","" among those whose ḥadīth should not be written from the people of al-Yamāmah. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal also weakened him and said: \""His ḥadīth should not be written.\"""""""
"11377","(11372) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn al-Najjār informed us in Kūfah; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Ḥammād narrated from Asbāṭ, from Simāk, from a man from the people of Baṣrah, that a people disputed over a hut of theirs and brought their case to ʿAlī. He judged between them: \Let it be seen which of them is closer to the ropes"","" for he is more entitled to it.\"" This narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous). And al-Walīd ibn Abī Thawr narrated it from Simāk"","" from Ḥanash"","" from ʿAlī"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" but it is not strong. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11378","(11373) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib informed us; ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn Maslamah, narrated from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \None of you should prevent his neighbour from fixing a wooden beam in his wall.\"" Then Abū Hurayrah would say: \""Why do I see you turning away from it? By Allah"","" I shall certainly cast it upon your shoulders.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Narrated by al-Bukhārī 2463"","" Muslim 1609]"""""
"11379","(11374) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūṣuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz, that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \None of you should prevent his neighbour from placing a wooden beam upon his wall.\"" Then Abū Hurayrah would say: \""Why do I see you turning away from it? By Allah"","" I shall certainly cast it upon your shoulders.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11380","(11375) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Zuhrī say: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj say: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you seeks his neighbour's permission to fix his wooden beam in his wall"","" he should not prevent him.\"" When he narrated this to them"","" they lowered their heads. He said: \""Why do I find you turning away? By Allah"","" I shall certainly cast it upon your shoulders.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Khaythamah from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11381","(11376) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let none of you prevent his neighbour from placing a beam in his wall.\"" Then Abū Hurayrah said: \""Why do I see you turning away from it? By Allah"","" I shall certainly cast it upon your backs.\"" [Its chain of narration is ṣaḥīḥ (authentic).]"""""
"11382","(11377) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Jannād narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Wuhaib narrated to us, from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from ʿIkrimah, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited drinking directly from the mouth of a water-skin and prohibited any one of you from preventing his neighbour from placing a beam upon his wall. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (5627) and Muslim (609).]"
"11383","(11378) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \It is not for a neighbour to prevent his neighbour from placing his beams upon his wall.\"" This chain of narration is ṣaḥīḥ (authentic).\n\nSufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"","" Ḥammād ibn Zayd"","" and Ḥammād ibn Salamah also narrated it from Ayyūb with the same meaning. Al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of Sufyān. He also extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrīt"","" from ʿIkrimah"","" from Abū Hurayrah. In the narration of al-Zubayr"","" it reads: \""whether he wishes or refuses.\"" However"","" Simāk ibn Ḥarb and Jābir al-Juʿfī contradicted them"","" narrating it from ʿIkrimah"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"11384","(11379) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: Sharīk narrated to us: Simāk narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you asks his neighbour to support his rafters upon his wall"","" let him not prevent him.\"" [Its chain of narration is munkar (denounced).]"""""
"11385","(11380) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you differ regarding a road"","" make it seven cubits wide"","" and whoever builds a structure"","" let him support it upon his neighbour's wall.\"" [Its chain of narration is munkar (denounced).]"""""
"11386","(11381) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkārī narrated to us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from Jābir, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Let none of you prevent his neighbour from placing his beam upon his wall"","" and when you differ regarding a path"","" make it seven cubits wide.\""\n\n(T) It was also narrated by Ibn Lahīʿah"","" from Abū al-Aswad"","" from ʿIkrimah"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" regarding the gutter. Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl narrated it from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn"","" from ʿIkrimah"","" from Ibn ʿAbbās"","" regarding both matters. The narration of Ayyūb"","" Khālid"","" and al-Zubayr is more authentic"","" and Allah knows best. [Its chain of narration is munkar (denounced).]"""""
"11387","(11382) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Balkhī narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, that Hishām ibn Yaḥyā informed him that ʿIkrimah ibn Salamah ibn Rabīʿah informed him that two brothers from Banī al-Mughīrah met Jāmiʿ ibn Yazīd al-Anṣārī, who said: \I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded that a neighbour should not prevent his neighbour from driving beams into his wall.\"" The one who had sworn the oath said: \""O my brother"","" I know that the ruling has been decided in your favour against me"","" and I have taken an oath. So place a pillar apart from my walls.\"" The other did so and drove his beams into the pillar. Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAmr said: \""I myself witnessed that.\""\n\n(T) al-ʿAbbābs also narrated it from Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad"","" from Ibn Jurayj"","" with the same meaning"","" in a more complete form. It is recorded at the end of the book Iḥyāʾ al-Mawāt. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""""
"11388","(11383) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me by way of ijāzah, that Abū al-Ḥayn ibn Ṣubayḥ informed them, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shīrūyah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī informed us: Rūḥ narrated to us: Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq al-Makkī narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿdah, who said: A man in Madīnah intended to place his beam upon his companion's wall without his permission, so he prevented him. Then whomever you wish from the Anṣār narrated from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he prohibited him from preventing it, so he was compelled to allow it. [Ḥasan.]"
"11389","(11384) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan, Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Rāʾī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī, from his father, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There shall be no harming nor reciprocal harming. Whoever harms"","" Allah will harm him"","" and whoever causes hardship"","" Allah will cause hardship upon him.\"" ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad is the only one who narrated it from al-Dārawardī. [Its chain of narration is munkar (denounced).]"""""
"11390","(11385) Mālik ibn Anas narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There shall be no harming nor reciprocal harming"",""\"" as a mursal narration. Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us"","" and he mentioned it."""""
"11391","(11386) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us — Abū al-Aḥraz Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Jamīl al-Azdī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — from Muḥammad ibn Ḥabbān — from Lu'lu'ah — from Abī Ṣirmah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever causes harm"","" Allah shall cause him harm"","" and whoever makes things difficult"","" Allah shall make things difficult for him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11392","(11387) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us — Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, they both said — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — he said: I read aloud to Mālik — from Abī al-Zinād — from al-Aʿraj — from Abī Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The deferral of a debt by a wealthy person is an injustice (ẓulm)"","" and if any of you is referred to a wealthy person for payment"","" let him accept the reference.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"","" and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Bukhārī 2287"","" Muslim 1546]"""""
"11393","(11388) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation — Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbaydullāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bālūwayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Faqīh informed us — Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Akhr narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar informed us — from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"","" among injustices is the deferral of a debt by a wealthy person"","" and if any of you is referred to a wealthy person for payment"","" let him accept the reference.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"","" and al-Bukhārī reported it through another chain from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11394","(11389) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us — Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from his father — from al-Aʿraj — from Abū Hurayrah — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The deferral of a debt by a wealthy person is an injustice"","" and if any of you is referred to a wealthy person for payment"","" let him accept the reference.\"" Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabāḥ al-Dūlabī also narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād with the wording reported by Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11395","(11390) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl al-Sāmirī in Baghdad narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah al-ʿAbadī narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from Yūnus.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḍarawī al-Harawī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The deferral of a debt by a wealthy person is an injustice"","" and if you are referred to a wealthy person for payment"","" then accept it"","" and do not engage in two sales within a single sale.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11396","(11391) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Qustānī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to me — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Shuʿbah informed me — Khulayd ibn Jaʿfar informed me, saying: I heard Abū Iyās narrate from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, who said: \There is no liability upon the wealth of a Muslim\"" — meaning a ḥawālah (transfer of debt). And others narrated from Shuʿbah unconditionally: \""There is no liability in it\"" — meaning a ḥawālah.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said"","" in the narration of al-Muzanī in al-Jāmiʿ al-Kabīr: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan used as evidence the statement of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān regarding the ḥawālah or al-kafālah (surety): \""The owner of the debt shall return; there is no liability upon the wealth of a Muslim.\"" I asked him about this ḥadīth"","" and he claimed it was from an unknown man from a known man"","" disconnected from ʿUthmān. Thus"","" according to his own principle"","" it is invalid on two grounds. Even if it were authentically reported from ʿUthmān"","" it would not constitute proof"","" because it is unknown whether he said this regarding the ḥawālah or the kafālah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: The unknown man in this report is Khulayd ibn Jaʿfar"","" and Khulayd is a Baṣran from whom Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī did not use as evidence in al-Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj did narrate his ḥadīth which he narrates along with al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyān from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd regarding musk and other matters. And Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj"","" when he narrated from him"","" would praise him. And Allah knows best. The \""known man\"" intended here is Abū Iyās Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah al-Muzanī"","" and he is disconnected (munqaṭiʿ)"","" as stated"","" for Abū Iyās belongs to the third generation of the Tābiʿūn of the people of Basra"","" and he did not meet ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"","" nor was he alive during his era."""""
"11397","(11392) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated — from Sharḥbīl ibn Muslim — from Abī Umāmah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Al-Zaʿīm (the guarantor) is liable (ghārim).\""\n\nAl-Muzanī said: \""Al-Zaʿīm in the language means al-Kafīl (the surety).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: We have narrated it from Qatādah from al-Suddī. [Ḥasan]"""""
"11398","(11393) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb informed me — Abū Hānī al-Khawlānī narrated to me — from ʿAmr ibn Mālik, who heard Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \I am a guarantor (zaʿīm)"","" and the guarantor is the one who assumes liability (ḥamīl) for the one who believed in me"","" submitted (aslama)"","" and emigrated (hājar) — for him is a house in the outskirts of Paradise.\"" [Ḥasan]"""""
"11399","(11394) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in another place — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed me — Abū Hānī informed me — from ʿAmr ibn Mālik al-Janbī, who heard Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \I am a guarantor"","" and the guarantor is the one who assumes liability — for the one who believed in me"","" submitted"","" and strove in the cause of Allah — for him is a house in the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise. And I am a guarantor for the one who believed in me"","" submitted"","" and emigrated — for him is a house in the outskirts of Paradise"","" a house in the middle of Paradise"","" and a house in the highest chambers of Paradise. Whoever does that and leaves no path for good un sought and no escape from evil un attempted"","" he shall die wherever he wishes to die.\""\n\nAl-Muzanī mentioned here the ḥadīth of Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī regarding al-ḍamān (surety)"","" and the chain of Abī Saʿīd's ḥadīth is ḍaʿīf. Therefore"","" the more appropriate course for us is to present what [Ḥasan]"""""
"11400","(11395) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us — Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd narrated — from Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought the body of a man from the Anṣār so that he might pray over him. He asked: \Does he have any debt upon him?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He asked: \""Did he leave anything behind?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So he prayed over him. Then another body was brought. He asked: \""Does he have any debt upon him?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He asked: \""Did he leave anything behind?\"" They said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Pray over your companion.\"" Abū Qatādah"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" said: \""The debt is upon me"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over him.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm"","" completing it thus. [Bukhārī 2297"","" Muslim 1619]"""""
"11401","(11396) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī — informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Nājiyah — narrated to us; Abū Mūsā — narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān — from Yazīd ibn Abī ʿUbayd, who said: Salamah ibn al-Akwāʿ — narrated to us, who said:\n\nI was with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral was brought. They said, \O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over him.\"" He said"","" \""Did he leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Did he leave anything [of value]?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" So he prayed over him. Then another funeral was brought. They said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over her.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave anything?\"" They said"","" \""Three dīnārs.\"" He said"","" \""Three small coins.\"" Then a third funeral was brought. They said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over him.\"" He said"","" \""Did he leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Did he leave anything?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Pray over your companion.\"" A man from the Anṣār"","" known as Abū Qatādah"","" said"","" \""Pray over him"","" and his debt is upon me.\"" So he prayed over him.\n\nThis is according to the narration of Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd. In the narration of Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm"","" regarding the second funeral"","" they said"","" \""Three dīnārs"",""\"" and he prayed over her. [Ṣaḥīḥ]\n\n---"""""
"11402","(11397) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥassān al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq — informed us; Maʿmar — from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray over anyone who had a debt. A deceased person was brought, and he said, \Does he have a debt?\"" They said"","" \""Yes"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" two dīnārs.\"" He said"","" \""Pray over your companion.\"" Abū Qatādah said"","" \""They are upon me"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So he prayed over him. Then when Allah granted victory to His Messenger ﷺ"","" he said"","" \""I am closer to every believer than his own self. Whoever leaves a debt"","" it is upon me"","" and whoever leaves wealth"","" it is for his heirs.\""\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad referenced it as 22963"","" 14205"","" 14206.]\n\n---"""""
"11403","(11398) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf — informed him; Abū ʿAlī — al-Ḥasan ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Jawharī al-Baghdādī — narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī — narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn — narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Walīd al-Waṣṣāfī — from ʬAṭiyyah ibn Saʿd al-ʿAwfī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a funeral to pray over. He turned to us and said, \Does your companion have a debt?\"" They said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Did he leave anything to cover it?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Pray over your companion.\"" ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) said"","" \""His debt is upon me"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" So he stepped forward"","" prayed over him"","" and said"","" \""May Allah reward you well"","" O ʿAlī"","" for you have freed your brother's burden. No Muslim frees his brother's burden except that Allah will free his burden on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nʿAbadah ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated it from Abū Nuʿaym — al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn — more completely"","" and in it he said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" he is free from his debt"","" and I am the guarantor for what is upon him.\""\n\nZāfir ibn Sulaymān narrated it from al-Waṣṣāfī"","" and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" I am the guarantor of his debt.\""\n\nThe ḥadīth revolves around ʿUbaydullāh al-Waṣṣāfī"","" and he is very weak. It has also been narrated from another chain from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib with a weak isnād. [Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""""
"11404","(11399) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Ṭāhir — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādhī — narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Zubaydī al-Ḥimṣī — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh — from ʬAṭāʾ ibn ʿAjlan, from Abū Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, who said:\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a funeral, he would not ask about any of the man's deeds except that he would ask about his debt. If it was said, \He has a debt"",""\"" he would refrain from praying over him. If it was said"","" \""He has no debt"",""\"" he would pray over him. A funeral was brought"","" and when he stood"","" he asked his companions"","" \""Does your companion have any debt?\"" They said"","" \""He has two dīnārs of debt.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away and said"","" \""Pray over your companion.\"" ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" they are upon me; he is free from them.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward"","" prayed over him"","" and then said"","" \""O ʿAlī"","" may Allah reward you well. Allah will free your burden as you freed your brother's burden. There is no deceased person who dies with a debt except that he is mortgaged by his debt. Whoever frees the burden of a deceased person"","" Allah will free his burden on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nSome of them said"","" \""Is this specific to ʿAlī"","" or is it general for all Muslims?\"" He said"","" \""No"","" rather it is general for all Muslims.\""\n\nʬAṭāʾ ibn ʿAjlan is weak. The narrations regarding Abū Qatādah assuming the debt of the deceased are more authentic. And Allah knows best.\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of the ḥamālah (surety) which al-Muzanī cited as evidence… [Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""""
"11405","(11400) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us; Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Baḥtarī — narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr — narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah — from Hārūn ibn Riʾāb, from Kinānah ibn Nuʿaym, from Qabīṣah ibn al-Mukhāriq, who said:\n\nI came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him regarding a surety (ḥamālah). He said, \Asking (for charity) has been made impermissible except in three cases: a man who takes on a surety — asking is permissible for him until he fulfills it"","" then he should refrain; a man whom a calamity befalls that destroys his wealth — asking is permissible for him until he attains a means of livelihood or sufficiency in living"","" then he should refrain; and a man who is afflicted by need or poverty"","" until three men of wisdom from his people testify — then asking becomes permissible for him. Beyond that"","" asking is unlawful (suḥt).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd"","" from Hārūn ibn Riʾāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1044.]\n\n---"""""
"11406","(11401) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār — informed me; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī — narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī — narrated to us; Zāʾidah — from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, who said: Jābir said:\n\nA man died. We washed him, embalmed him, and shrouded him. Then we brought him to the Prophet ﷺ so that he might pray over him. He took a few steps and then said, \Does he have a debt?\"" We said"","" \""Yes"","" two dīnārs.\"" He turned away. Abū Qatādah assumed the two dīnārs. We came to him"","" and Abū Qatādah said"","" \""The two dīnārs are upon me.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"","" \""The right of the creditor is established"","" and the deceased is free from them.\"" He said"","" \""Yes.\"" So he prayed over him. Then he said to him a day later"","" \""What happened to the two dīnārs?\"" He said"","" \""He only died yesterday.\"" He returned to him the next day and said"","" \""I have paid them.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"","" \""Now you have cooled his skin for him.\""\n\nIn this narration is the indication that upon repayment"","" his skin was cooled for him"","" and his statement"","" \""The right of the creditor is established"","" and the deceased is free from them\"" — if Ibn ʿAqīl preserved it accurately"","" then what is meant by it"","" and Allah knows best"","" is that the creditor has the right to demand repayment from you alone"","" if he wishes"","" just as he would have the right to demand it from you alone if you owed him something from another source"","" and the deceased is free from it. The creditor has the right to demand it from you alone"","" if he wishes. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""""
"11407","(11402) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī — (ḥ) and ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah and Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah — both said: narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad — from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that:\n\nA man was owed ten dīnārs by a debtor. He said to him, \By Allah"","" I have nothing with which to repay you today.\"" The creditor said"","" \""By Allah"","" I will not leave you until you give me [what you owe] or bring me a guarantor who will assume it on your behalf.\"" The debtor said"","" \""By Allah"","" I have nothing with which to repay"","" and I cannot find anyone to assume it on my behalf.\"" So he dragged him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and the debtor said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this man has seized me. I asked him to grant me respite for one month"","" but he refused until I repay him or bring him a guarantor. I said"","" 'By Allah"","" I cannot find a guarantor"","" and I have nothing with which to repay today.'\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the creditor"","" \""Can you not grant him respite for one more month?\"" He said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Then I will assume it on his behalf.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assumed the debt on his behalf. The man went away and returned with the amount he had promised. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him"","" \""Where did you get this gold?\"" He said"","" \""From a mine.\"" He said"","" \""Go"","" we have no need of it. There is no good in it.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repaid it on his behalf.\n\nIn this is an indication that the right remained upon the debtor's obligation even after the assumption of the guarantee"","" until he confirmed the period of respite. Then the Prophet ﷺ voluntarily repaid it on his behalf and refrained from dealing with the mine's wealth. And Allah knows best.\n\nWe have narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said"","" \""The soul of the believer is suspended by his debt until it is repaid on his behalf.\"" [Ḥasan]\n\n---"""""
"11408","(11403) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Qumāsh — narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl — Abū ʿImrān al-Jabalī — narrated to us; Maʿn ibn ʿĪsā al-Qazzāz — from al-Ḥārith ibn al-Malik ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Iyās al-Laythī, from al-Qāsim ibn Yazīd ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Qusayṭ, from his father, from ʬAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while he was suffering from a severe fever, his head bound. He said, \Take my hand"","" O Faḍl.\"" So I took his hand until he sat upon the pulpit. Then he said — and he mentioned the ḥadīth until he said — \""Whoever I have taken money from"","" this is my wealth; let him take from it.\"" A man stood and said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" I have three dirhams with you.\"" He said"","" \""As for me"","" I do not call a speaker a liar"","" nor do I ask for an oath regarding what is owed to you.\"" He said"","" \""Do you not remember that a beggar passed by you and you ordered me"","" so I gave him three dirhams?\"" He said"","" \""Give them"","" O Faḍl.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]\n\n---"""""
"11409","(11404) Abū ʿAmr — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Adīb — informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī — informed us; al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā — narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Shuʿjāʿ and Yūsuf — both said: narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim — from Yazīd, that is, Ibn Abī ʿUbayd, from Salamah, that is, Ibn al-Akwāʿ, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a funeral. They said, \O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over her.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave anything?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" So he prayed over him. Then another funeral was brought. They said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over her.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""Yes\"" — or they said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave anything?\"" They said"","" \""Three dīnārs.\"" He said"","" \""Three small coins\"" — and he gestured with his hand. Then another funeral was brought. It was said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" pray over her.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave any debt?\"" They said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Did she leave anything?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Pray over your companion.\"" Abū Qatādah said"","" \""O Prophet of Allah"","" his debt is upon me.\"" So he prayed over him.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ in an abridged form from Abū ʿĀṣim. [Bukhārī 2295.]\n\n---"""""
"11410","(11405) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān — narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr — narrated to us; Zāʾidah — from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, who said: Jābir said:\n\nA man died. We washed him, embalmed him, and shrouded him. Then we brought him to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him, \Will you pray over him?\"" He stood"","" took a few steps"","" and then said"","" \""Does he have a debt?\"" It was said"","" \""Two dīnārs.\"" He turned away. Abū Qatādah assumed them. We came to him"","" and Abū Qatādah said"","" \""The two dīnārs are upon me.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"","" \""The right of the creditor is established"","" and the deceased is free from them.\"" He said"","" \""Yes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over him. Then he said to him a day later"","" \""What happened to the two dīnārs?\"" He said"","" \""He only died yesterday.\"" He returned to him the next day and said"","" \""I have paid them.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"","" \""Now you have cooled his skin for him.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""""
"11411","(11406) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Dawud al-Munadi narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Isa ibn Sadaqah said: I, my father, and the imam of the quarter entered upon Anas ibn Malik and they said, \Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"","" that Allah may benefit us thereby.\"" He said: A man had died"","" and the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came. We said"","" \""O Messenger of Allah"","" will you pray over him?\"" He said"","" \""Does he have a debt upon him?\"" We said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Will one of you guarantee his debt so that I may pray over him?\"" They said"","" \""No.\"" He said"","" \""Then what benefit would it be to you if I were to pray over a man who is held as a pledge in his grave until Allah resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection and takes account of him?\"" And Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated it from 'Isa"","" inserting between him and Anas ibn Malik 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Umayyah. [Da'if]"""""
"11412","(11407) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdān informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: 'Isa ibn Sadaqah narrated from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Umayyah, who said: I witnessed Anas ibn Malik saying, \All praise is to Allah"","" Who has withheld the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission.\"" A man said to him"","" \""O Abu Hamzah"","" would you not narrate to us a hadith"","" perhaps Allah will benefit us thereby?\"" He said"","" \""Whoever among you is able to die without having any debt upon him"","" let him do so"","" for I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a bier of a man was brought to him so that he might pray over him. He said"","" 'Does he have a debt upon him?' They said"","" 'Yes.' He said"","" 'What benefit would it be to him if I were to pray over a man whose soul is held as a pledge in his grave"","" his soul not ascending to Allah? Were a man to guarantee his debt"","" I would stand and pray over him"","" for my prayer would benefit him.'\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11413","(11408) Abu Bakr al-Farisi informed us: Ibrahim ibn Allah al-Isfahani narrated to us: Abu Ahmad ibn Faris said: Al-Bukhari said: Abu al-Walid said, \He is da'if\"" — meaning 'Isa ibn Sadaqah — \""and 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa contradicted them both"","" saying"","" 'Sadaqah ibn 'Isa"",""' and he agreed with Yunus in mentioning his hearing from Anas.\"" [Sahih]"""""
"11414","(11409) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us: Abu Ja'far ibn Duham al-Shaybani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated from Sadaqah ibn 'Isa, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bier of a man to pray over him. He said, \Does he have a debt upon him?\"" They said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""If you guarantee his debt"","" I shall pray over him.\"" Al-Bukhari said"","" and Abu Dawud said: Sadaqah — Abu Muhriz — heard Anas. [Sahih]"""""
"11415","(11410) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu al-Fadl, al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub al-'Adl, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-'Abdi narrated to us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid — (h) and Abu 'Abd Allah informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, the hafiz, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid — informed me: 'Amir al-Sha'bi narrated from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day, and when he turned around, he said, \Is there anyone from the sons of so-and-so here?\"" The people fell silent"","" and whenever he began with something"","" they would fall silent. Then he said again"","" \""Is there anyone from the sons of so-and-so here?\"" A man said"","" \""This is so-and-so.\"" He said"","" \""Verily"","" your companion has been detained at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owed.\"" A man said"","" \""His debt is upon me"",""\"" and he settled it. (t) And with its meaning"","" a group narrated from al-Sha'bi"","" and Sa'id ibn Masruq al-Thawri narrated from al-Sha'bi from Sam'anan ibn Mushannaj from Samurah"","" and its mention has already passed in the Book of Bankruptcy. [Da'if]"""""
"11416","(11411) Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-'Attar informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan al-'Amiri narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from Abi Salamah from Abi Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The soul of the believer is suspended by his debt until it is settled on his behalf.\"" [Ahmad 4402"","" 9677]"""""
"11417","(11412) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Ibn Kathir — (h) and he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Al-Firyabi — (h) and he said: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym said: They said: Sufyan narrated from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah from his father from Abi Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The soul of the believer is suspended so long as there is a debt upon him.\"" [Munkar al-Isnad]"""""
"11418","(11413) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq said: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus informed us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to me: Al-Layth ibn Sa'd — (h) and Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: Abu Bakr al-Marwazi informed us: 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Al-Layth narrated to me: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated from al-A'raj from Abi Hurayrah from the Messenger of Allah (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He mentioned that a man from the Children of Israel asked some of the Children of Israel to lend him a thousand dinars. He said, \Bring me witnesses that I may attest them for you.\"" He said"","" \""Allah is sufficient as a witness.\"" He said"","" \""Then bring me a guarantor.\"" He said"","" \""Allah is sufficient as a guarantor.\"" He said"","" \""Then he lent them to him for a specified term.\"" He went out to sea and attended to his need"","" then sought a vessel to set out for the term he had set"","" but found no vessel. He took a piece of wood and hollowed it out"","" placed the dinars in it along with a note from him to his companion"","" then sealed its opening. He came to it at the sea and said"","" \""O Allah"","" You know that I borrowed from so-and-so a thousand dinars"","" and he asked me for a guarantor"","" and I said"","" 'Allah is sufficient as a guarantor"",""' and he was satisfied with You. And he asked me for witnesses"","" and I said"","" 'Allah is sufficient as a witness"",""' and he was satisfied with You. I have striven to find a vessel by which I may send to him what is his"","" but I found no vessel. I entrust them to You.\"" He cast it into the sea until it entered it"","" then turned away"","" while he was in that state seeking a vessel to set out to his land. The man who had lent him came out hoping that a vessel might have arrived with his money"","" and there he was with the piece of wood. He took it for his people as firewood. When he split it"","" he found the money and the note. Then the man came and brought him a thousand dinars and said"","" \""By Allah"","" I have been striving to find a vessel to come to you with your money"","" but I found no vessel before the one in which I arrived.\"" He said"","" \""Had you sent me anything?\"" He said"","" \""Yes.\"" He said"","" \""Then Allah"","" the Almighty and Majestic"","" has delivered on your behalf. Depart with a thousand dinars"","" guided aright.\"" Al-Bukhari extracted it in the Sahih and said"","" \""And Al-Layth said.\"" [Sahih. Ahmad extracted it 1/2348"","" 8571]"""""
"11419","(11414) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn 'Irak ibn Malik narrated from his father from his grandfather from Abi Hurayrah: That the Prophet (may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) detained a man on suspicion, and on another occasion he took a guarantor from the accused as a precaution and for verification. Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym is da'if."
"11420","(11415) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir informed us: My grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur, narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Yahya ibn Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated from Abi Ishaq from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, who said: I prayed the morning prayer with 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, and he mentioned the story of Ibn al-Nawwahah and their companions, and their testimony for Musaylimah the Liar regarding the message, and that 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud — may Allah be pleased with him — ordered the killing of Ibn al-Nawwahah. Then he consulted the people about those men, and Jarir and al-Ash'ath stood and said, \Ask them to repent and take their tribesmen as guarantors.\"" So he asked them to repent"","" and they repented"","" and their tribesmen acted as their guarantors. Al-Bukhari mentioned it in the translation without an isnad. Al-Bukhari said"","" and Abu al-Zinad said from Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn 'Amr al-Aslami from his father: That 'Umar — may Allah be pleased with him — sent him as a collector of charity"","" and a man had intercourse with his wife's slave-girl. Hamzah took guarantors from the man until he came to 'Umar"","" and 'Umar had already flogged him a hundred lashes. He accepted their testimony and excused him on account of his ignorance. [Sahih. Ahmad 1/384 2"","" 3642]"""""
"11421","(11416) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us that al-Sarrāj narrated to us that Yaʿqūb al-Dawraqī narrated from Hushaym from Muṭarrif from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \The testimony of a man against the testimony of another man is not accepted in a prescribed punishment (ḥadd)"","" nor is surety (kafālah) valid in a prescribed punishment.\"" And we have also narrated it from Shurayḥ"","" Masrūq"","" and Ibrāhīm. A ḥadīth has been narrated on this subject with a weak chain. [Weak]"""""
"11422","(11417) Abū Manṣūr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Dāmaghānī and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Khasrūjirdī both informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ṣaffār al-Baghdādī narrated to us that Abū Hammām al-Walīd ibn Shujaʿ narrated to us that Baqiyyah narrated to me that Abū Muḥammad al-Kulāʿī narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAnbasah al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us that Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Baqiyyah narrated from ʿUmar al-Dimashqī, who narrated to me that ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no surety (kafālah) in a prescribed punishment (ḥadd).\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: ʿUmar ibn Abī ʿUmar al-Dimashqī is a narrator of rejected ḥadīth from reliable authorities. The Shaykh said: Baqiyyah is alone in narrating it from Abū Muḥammad ʿUmar ibn Abī ʿUmar"","" and he is among the unknown teachers of Baqiyyah"","" and his narrations are rejected. And Allāh knows best. [Weak]"""""
"11423","(11418) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us that Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated from Sulaymān al-Shaybānī, who said: I heard Ḥabīb — who used to bring disputants before Shurayḥ — say: \A man brought a son of Shurayḥ before Shurayḥ. He had stood surety for a man who owed a debt"","" so Shurayḥ detained him. When night fell"","" he said: 'Go to ʿAbdillāh with bedding and food.' And his son was named ʿAbdillāh.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11424","(11419) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān narrated to us that Muʿādh narrated from Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj from al-Ḥakam and Ḥammād that they both said regarding a man who stood surety for another man and then that man died: \One of them said: 'He (the surety) is liable for the dirhams.' The other said: 'Nothing is upon him.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11425","(11420) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us that Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Jurayj narrated from ʬāʾ from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh and from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) arrived on the morning of the fourth of Dhū al-Ḥijjah"","" uttering the talbiyah for Ḥajj"","" with nothing mixed with it. When we arrived"","" he commanded us"","" so we made it an ʿUmrah"","" by making our women lawful for us. The talk about this spread.\""\n\nʿAṭāʾ said: Jābir said: \""One of us would go to Minā while his semen was dripping from his private part.\"" Jābir said: \""This reached the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"","" so he stood as an addresser and said: 'It has reached me that certain people are saying such-and-such. By Allāh"","" I am more God-fearing than them. Had I known beforehand what I came to know afterwards"","" I would not have brought the sacrificial animal"","" and had I not had the sacrificial animal with me"","" I would have exited the iḥrām.'\""\n\nThen Surāqah ibn Mālik ibn Juʿshum (may Allāh be pleased with him) stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allāh"","" is it for us specifically or forever?\"" He said: \""No"","" rather forever.\""\n\nThen ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allāh be pleased with him) came. One of them (the narrators) says: \""He said: 'Labbayka with that by which the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) entered iḥrām"",""' and the other said: 'Labbayka with the Ḥajj of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ).'\"" So the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) commanded him to remain in his iḥrām and included him in the sacrificial offering.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān. [Bukhārī 1564"","" Muslim 1240]"""""
"11426","(11421) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī and Abū al-Faḍl al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn Qūhyār both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Abī al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: \We sacrificed at al-Ḥudaybiyah seventy camels"","" one camel for seven (persons).\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Share in the sacrificial offering (hadī).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ as mentioned previously in the Book of Ḥajj. [Bukhārī 3560"","" Muslim 1318]"""""
"11427","(11422) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥayyān ibn Mulāʿib and Muḥammad ibn Ghālib ibn Ḥarb both said: ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us that Wuhib narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated from Mujāhid from al-Sāʾib ibn Abī al-Sāʾib that he was a partner of the Prophet (ﷺ) in the early days of Islam in trade. On the day of the Conquest (of Makkah), he said: \Welcome to my brother and my partner! You neither quarreled nor disputed.\""\n[Aḥmad 3095"","" Abū Dāwūd 4836]"""""
"11428","(11423) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Yaḥyā narrated from Sufyān, who narrated to me that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Muhājir narrated from Mujāhid from Qāʾid al-Sāʾib from al-Sāʾib, who said: \I came to the Prophet (ﷺ)"","" and they began praising me and mentioning me. The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: 'I know him best among you.' I said: 'You have spoken the truth — may my father and mother be sacrificed for you — you were my partner. What an excellent partner you were! You neither quarreled nor disputed.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11429","(11424) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Shabīb al-Maʿmarī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sulayman al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated to us that Abū Hammām Muḥammad ibn al-Zibriqān narrated to us that Abū Ḥayyān al-Taymī narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said: \Allāh"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" says: 'I am the third of the two partners"","" so long as neither of them betrays his companion. When he betrays"","" I withdraw from between them.'\"" [Munkar al-Isnād]"""""
"11430","(11425) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Miṣṣīṣī narrated with this same chain from Abū Hurayrah, who raised it (as a marfūʿ narration), saying: \Indeed"","" Allāh"","" the Most High"","" says…\"" and he mentioned it. [Munkar]"""""
"11431","(11426) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Baghdādī narrated to us therein; Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī narrated to us in Makkah; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarra narrated to us; al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū ʿUqayl narrated to me from his grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām, who had met the Prophet ﷺ. His mother Zaynab bint Ḥumayd took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" take his pledge of allegiance.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""He is young.\"" And he passed his hand over his head and supplicated for him. And he used to offer a single sheep as a sacrifice on behalf of his entire household.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj and ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf"","" from Ibn Wahb"","" from Saʿīd"","" from Zuhrah ibn Maʿbad — and he is Abū ʿUqayl — up to his words \""and supplicated for him.\"" Then he added from Zuhrah ibn Maʿbad: \""His grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām used to take him out to the market to buy provisions"","" and Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn al-Zubayr would meet him and say to him: 'Include us"","" for the Prophet ﷺ has supplicated for you with blessing.' So he would include them"","" and perhaps he would obtain a camel as it was and send it to the household.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 7210]"""""
"11432","(11427) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī narrated to me; Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb narrated to us from Abī ʿUqayl: \His grandfather ʿAbdullāh ibn Hishām used to take him out"",""\"" and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11433","(11428) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ḥafarī narrated to us from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Abī Isḥāq, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: \I"","" ʿAmmār ibn Yāsir"","" and Saʿd shared in what we obtained on the day of Badr. Neither I nor ʿAmmār brought anything"","" while Saʿd brought two captives.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3388]"""""
"11434","(11429) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Khalaf al-Marwazī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim and Sufyān ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us from Kathīr ibn Zayd, from al-Walīd ibn Rabāḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions.\"" He said: And Sufyān added in his narration: \""…that which is in accordance with the truth among them.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated this with its addition from the ḥadīth of Khuṣayf from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah"","" and from ʿAṭāʾ from Anas ibn Mālik"","" marfūʿ (elevated to the Prophet).\n\n[Ḥasan]"""""
"11435","(11430) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Khuzaym al-Qazzāz narrated to us; Hishām ibn Khālid narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from Kathīh ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Muzanī, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions"","" except a condition that renders ḥalāl as ḥarām or a condition that renders ḥarām as ḥalāl.\""\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""""
"11436","(11431) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Abū ʿĪsā al-Khutlī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad al-Ādharamī narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd likewise Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated it from Kathīr ibn ʿAbdullāh.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"
"11437","(11432) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; my paternal uncle narrated to us; my father narrated to me from Ibn Isḥāq, from Abī Nuʿaym Wahb ibn Kaysān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, that he heard him narrating, saying: \I intended to go to Khaybar"","" so I came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him and said: 'I intend to go to Khaybar.' He said: 'When you come to my agent"","" take from him fifteen wasqs of dates. And if he demands a sign from you"","" place your hand on his collarbone.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd 3632]"""""
"11438","(11433) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to me; my father narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me from Sufyān al-Thawrī, from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me"","" so I stood over the sacrificial camels. He commanded me"","" so I distributed their meat. Then he commanded me"","" so I distributed their coverings and their skins.\""\n\n[Bukhārī 1940"","" Muslim 1317]"""""
"11439","(11434) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sayyār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to me; Ibn Abī Najīḥ narrated to me, and he mentioned something similar to it, except that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed me over the sacrificial camels.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"","" and Muslim extracted it from another chain from Ibn Abī Najīḥ.\n\nAnd we have narrated in the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah"","" in the story of the man who demanded from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a camel that was owed to him: \""Buy him a camel and give it to him.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh"","" in the story of the sale of his camel to the Prophet ﷺ: \""O Bilāl"","" pay him and give him more.\"" So he gave him four dīnārs and added a qīrāṭ for him.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11440","(11435) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us; Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī narrated to us; Abū Tawbah narrated to me; Muʿāwiyah ibn Salām narrated to me from Zayd ibn Salām that he heard Abā Salām narrate to me; ʿAbdullāh al-Hawzanī, meaning Abū ʿĀmir al-Hawzanī, said: \I met Bilāl"","" the muʾadhdhin of the Prophet ﷺ"","" in Ḥalab"","" and I said: 'O Bilāl"","" tell me how the expenditure of the Prophet ﷺ was.' He said: 'He had nothing"","" except that I was the one entrusted with that from the time Allah sent him until he passed away. When a Muslim man came to him and he saw him naked"","" he would command me"","" and I would go and borrow"","" and I would buy a cloak and something else"","" and I would clothe him and feed him"","" until one of the polytheists confronted me and said: \""O Bilāl"","" indeed I have ample means"","" so do not borrow from anyone but me.\"" So I did that. Then one day"","" when I had performed ablution and stood to give the adhān for the prayer"","" the polytheist appeared among a group of merchants. When he saw me"","" he said: \""O Ḥabashī!\"" I said: \""Here I am"","" at your service!\"" He turned to me with a stern face and spoke harsh words. He said: \""Do you know how many days remain between you and the month?\"" I said: \""It is near.\"" He said: \""There are only four nights between you and it. I will take from you what you owe me"","" for I did not give you what I gave you out of respect for you or for the sake of your companion"","" but rather I gave it to you so that you would become my slave"","" and I would return you to herding sheep as you were before that.\"" He pressed me as such people press others. I went away"","" and then I gave the adhān for the prayer until I had prayed ʿIshāʾ. The Prophet ﷺ returned to his family"","" and I sought permission to enter upon him"","" and he granted me permission. I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" may my father and mother be sacrificed for you"","" indeed the polytheist whom I mentioned to you — that I used to borrow from him — has said such and such. You have nothing with which to pay my debt"","" nor do I have anything"","" and he will expose me. Grant me permission to go to some of those tribes who have accepted Islam"","" until Allah provides for His Messenger ﷺ what will pay my debt.\"" So I went out until I reached my house. I placed my sword"","" my quiver"","" my spear"","" and my sandals by my head"","" and I turned my face toward the horizon. Whenever I dozed off"","" I would wake up. When I sensed the night upon me"","" I slept until the first light of dawn broke. I intended to set out when a man came running"","" calling: \""O Bilāl"","" answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!\"" So I went until I came to him"","" and there were four mounts laden with their burdens. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and sought permission"","" and the Prophet ﷺ said to me: \""Rejoice"","" for Allah has come with the settlement of your debt.\"" I praised Allah. He said: \""Did you not pass by the four halted mounts?\"" I said: \""Yes"","" O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Then their necks and what is upon them belong to you. Upon them are garments and food that the chief of Fadak sent as a gift to him. Take them to yourself and pay your debt.\"" He said: \""So I did that. I unloaded their burdens"","" then I tied them securely. Then I proceeded to give the adhān for the Fajr prayer. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prayed"","" I went to al-Baqīʿ and placed my fingers in my ears and called out"","" saying: 'Whoever is owed a debt by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" let him come.' I continued selling and paying"","" and presenting and paying"","" until no debt remained upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the face of the earth"","" until two awqiyyahs or one and a half awqiyyahs remained with me. Then I went to the mosque"","" and most of the day had passed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque alone. I greeted him"","" and he said to me: 'What happened to what was in your custody?' I said: 'Allah has settled everything that was upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; nothing remains.' He said: 'Did anything remain?' I said: 'Yes"","" two dīnārs.' He said: 'See that you relieve me of them"","" for I will not enter upon any of my family until you relieve me of them.' No one came to us"","" so he spent the night in the mosque until morning. He remained in the mosque the second day until the latter part of the day"","" when two riders came. I went to them and clothed them and fed them. When he prayed ʿIshāʾ"","" he called me and said: 'What happened to what was in your custody?' I said: 'Allah has relieved you of it.' He said 'Allāhu Akbar' and praised Allah"","" out of fear that death might overtake him while that was still with him. Then I followed him until he came to his wives. He greeted each woman individually until he came to his resting place.' This is what you asked me about.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11441","(11436) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Bushayr ibn Yasār, the freedman of the Anṣār, from Sahl ibn Abī Ḥathmah and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj, that both of them narrated to him — or both of them narrated — that ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl and Muḥayyiṣah ibn Masʿūd came to Khaybar on some errand and separated among the palm trees. ʿAbdullāh ibn Sahl was killed. His brother ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahl and his two cousins Muḥayyiṣah and Ḥuwayyiṣah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and mentioned the matter of their companion. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who was the closer in relation, began to speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Let the eldest speak first.\""\n\nYaḥyā said: \""Al-kubr means that the eldest should begin the speech.\"" So they both spoke regarding the matter of their companion"","" and he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"","" and Muslim narrated it from al-Qawārīrī from Ḥammād.\n[Bukhārī 6142"","" Muslim 1669]"""""
"11442","(11437) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah say: I heard Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq say: Abū Kurayb narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Idrīs narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from Jahm ibn Abī al-Jahm, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) used to dislike disputation. Whenever he had a dispute, he would appoint ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṍālib as his representative in it. When ʿAqīl grew old, he appointed me.\n[Weak]"
"11443","(11438) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, from a man of the people of Madīnah called Jahm, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he appointed ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar to represent him in disputes, and he said: \Indeed"","" disputes lead to destruction (quḥam).\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Abū al-Ziyād said: \""Al-quḥam refers to places of destruction.\""\n[Weak]"""""
"11444","(11439) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us — and I think it was — from al-Zuhrī, from Ḥabīb, the freedman of ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abī Murāwiḥ, from Abū Dharr, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and asked him, saying: \O Messenger of Allah"","" which deed is best?\"" He said: \""Faith in Allah and striving in the cause of Allah.\"" He asked: \""Which act of emancipation is best?\"" He said: \""That which is most valued by its owner.\"" He said: \""What if I cannot do that?\"" He said: \""Then help the craftsman or make something for the one who cannot do it himself.\"" He said: \""What if I am unable to do that?\"" He said: \""Then keep people from your harm"","" for it is a charity that you give on yourself.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"","" and they both narrated it from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father.\n[Bukhārī 2518"","" Muslim 84]"""""
"11445","(11440) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us; Abū Badr Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Mihrān narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Abī al-Bakhtarī, from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" the wealthy have taken all the reward.\"" He said: \""Do you not pray"","" fast"","" and strive?\"" I said: \""Yes"","" and they do as we do — they pray"","" fast"","" strive"","" and give charity"","" while we do not give charity.\"" He said: \""In you there are many acts of charity. Indeed"","" your speaking on behalf of the mute to convey his need is charity; your hearing on behalf of the deaf to convey his need is charity; your guiding the blind to the path is charity; your using your strength to help the weak is charity; your removing harm from the road is charity; and your intimate relations with your family is charity.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" does one of us fulfill his desire and still receive reward?\"" He said: \""What do you think — if he were to fulfill it unlawfully"","" would there be sin upon him?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Do you then account for evil but not account for good?\""\n\nWe have narrated this through other chains from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him).\n[Bukhārī 843"","" Muslim 595]"""""
"11446","(11441) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us from ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Yaḥyā ibn Rāshid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever intercedes to prevent one of the prescribed punishments of Allah has indeed opposed Allah in His dominion. Whoever dies while owing debt"","" there will be no dinār or dirham there"","" but rather good deeds and bad deeds. Whoever disputes in falsehood while knowing it remains in the displeasure of Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" until he desists. And whoever says about a believer that which is not in him is held back in the mire of corruption until he retracts what he said.\"""""""
"11447","(11442) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly, except for his words: \Whoever dies while owing debt.\"""""""
"11448","(11443) Abū ʿAlī informed us; Abū Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Yūnus narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd al-ʿUmarī narrated to us; al-Muthannā ibn Yazīd narrated to me from Maṭar al-Warrāq, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), with the same meaning. He added: \And whoever assists in a dispute with injustice incurs the wrath of Allah.\"""""""
"11449","(11444) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ibrāhīm al-Hāshimī informed us in Baghdād; ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us; Abū Qilābah ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Rajāʾ Abū Yaḥyā, the dealer in miscellaneous goods, said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrate from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Abī Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever walks with a people"","" giving the impression that he is a witness when he is not a witness"","" he is a false witness. Whoever assists in a dispute without knowledge remains in the displeasure of Allah until he desists. And fighting a believer is disbelief"","" and reviling him is sinfulness (fusūq).\"""""""
"11450","(11445) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us from Ibn al-Mubārak, from Dāwūd ibn Abī al-Furāt, from Muḥammad ibn Zayd, who said: ʿUmar passed judgment regarding a slave woman whose master had gone on a campaign and ordered a man to sell her. Then her master decided to emancipation her and bore witness to that. The slave girl had already been sold. They calculated and found that her emancipation had occurred before her sale. So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that her emancipation be upheld, her price be returned, and her dower be taken on account of what had been consummated with her.\n[Sound (Ḥasan)]"
"11451","(11446) He said: And Abū al-Walīd informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, from Ḥibbān, from Ibn al-Mubārak, and he mentioned something similar to it, and he said therein: 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Azīz (may Allah be pleased with him) rendered the judgment. [Ḥasan]"
"11452","(11447) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-'Abbās — 'Abd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw — informed me; al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Nāfi' ibn 'Umar informed us; from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who said: I wrote to Ibn 'Abbās concerning two women who used to stitch leather, and in the house there were people who engaged in idle talk. One of them came out with her hand gushing blood and said: \This one has struck me"",""\"" while the other denied it. He said: So Ibn 'Abbās wrote to me: \""Indeed"","" the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made"","" and he said: 'Were people to be granted [what they claim] based on their claims alone"","" people would claim the blood and wealth of others.'\"" He said: \""Summon her and recite over her: 'Indeed"","" those who exchange the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price — they will have no share in the Hereafter"","" and Allah will not speak to them"","" nor will He look at them on the Day of Resurrection"","" nor will He purify them"","" and for them is a painful punishment.'\"" He said: So he recited it over them"","" and she confessed. When this reached him"","" he was pleased.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nu'aym and others"","" from Nāfi' ibn 'Umar. [Bukhārī 4552]"""""
"11453","(11448) Abū al-Qāsim — 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdad — informed us; Abū al-Qāsim — Ḥabīb ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Dāwūd al-Qazzāz — narrated to us; Abū Bakr — 'Umar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn 'Umar ibn Yazīd al-Sadūsī — narrated to us; 'Āṣim ibn 'Alī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Dhi'b narrated to us; from al-Maqburī; from Abū Hurayrah; from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever has committed a wrong against his brother"","" whether concerning his honour or his wealth"","" let him seek his brother's forgiveness for it before a time comes when there will be neither dīnār nor dirham. If he has righteous deeds"","" they will be taken from him in proportion to the wrong he committed"","" and if he has no righteous deeds"","" the evil deeds of his companion will be taken and placed upon him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"","" from Ibn Abī Dhi'b. [Bukhārī 6534]"""""
"11454","(11449) Abū Muḥammad — 'Abd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn 'Abd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdad — informed us; Ismā'īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; 'Abbās ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Tarqafī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ya'lā narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ghaylān narrated, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulaymān ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: Mā'iz ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" purify me.\"" He said: \""Woe to you! Go back"","" seek forgiveness from Allah"","" and repent to Him.\"" He went back not far"","" then came again and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" purify me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""Go back"","" seek forgiveness from Allah"","" and repent to Him.\"" He went back not far"","" then came again and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" purify me.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said the same to him. When it was the fourth time"","" the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""From what shall I purify you?\"" He said: \""From zinā (adultery/fornication).\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) asked: \""Is he insane?\"" He was informed that he was not insane. He said: \""Has he drunk wine?\"" A man stood up and sniffed him but found no smell of wine from him. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Are you a muhṣan (married)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered regarding him"","" and he was stoned. The people were divided into two groups concerning him. One group said: \""Mā'iz is destroyed upon the worst of his deeds; his sin has encompassed him.\"" And another group said: \""There is no repentance better than the repentance of Mā'iz"","" who came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"","" placed his hand in his hand"","" and then said: 'Kill me with stones.'\"" He said: They remained in that state for two or three days. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) came to them while they were sitting. He greeted them"","" then sat down and said: \""Seek forgiveness for Mā'iz ibn Mālik.\"" He said: They said: \""May Allah forgive Mā'iz ibn Mālik.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""He has repented with a repentance so vast that were it divided among an entire nation"","" it would suffice them.\"" He said: Then a woman from Ghāmid"","" from the Azd"","" came and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" purify me.\"" He said: \""Woe to you! Go back"","" seek forgiveness from Allah"","" and repent to Him.\"" She said: \""Perhaps you intend to turn me back as you turned back Mā'iz ibn Mālik.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" She said: \""I am pregnant from zinā.\"" He said: \""Are you a muhṣan (married)?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then we will not stone you until you deliver what is in your womb.\"" He said: A man from the Anṣār acted as her guarantor until she delivered. Then she came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \""The Ghāmidī woman has delivered.\"" He said: \""Then we will not stone her and leave her infant child with no one to nurse him.\"" A man from the Anṣār stood up and said: \""I will take responsibility for his nursing"","" O Prophet of Allah.\"" So he stoned her.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb"","" from Yaḥyā ibn Ya'lā ibn al-Ḥārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1695]"""""
"11455","(11450) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-'Abbās — Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb — informed us; al-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfi'ī informed us; Mālik informed, from al-Zuhrī, from 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Utbah, from Abū Hurayrah, and from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī: that they both informed him regarding the story of the two men who brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he ordered Unays al-Aslamī to go to the other woman, and if she confessed, to stone her. So she confessed, and he stoned her.\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Mālik, and both he and Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Layth and others, from al-Zuhrī. [Bukhārī 6828, Muslim 1698]"
"11456","(11451) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; 'Affān narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Qatādah narrated, from Anas: that a slave-girl was found with her head crushed between two stones. She was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) and it was said: \Who did this to you? Was it so-and-so? Was it so-and-so?\"" — until the Jew was named. She indicated with her head. The Jew was summoned and he confessed. The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered regarding him"","" and his head was crushed between two stones.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Hammām ibn Yaḥyā. [Bukhārī 2413"","" Muslim 1672]"""""
"11457","(11452) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Sa'īd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Ibn 'Awn narrated, from Ibrāhīm: that a man confessed before Sharīḥ, then went and denied it. Sharīḥ said to him: \Your maternal aunt's sister's son has testified against you.\"" He said: And Ibn Sīrīn narrated that Sharīḥ said to him: \""Your maternal aunt's sister's son has testified against you.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Sa'd 6/136]"""""
"11458","(11453) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Mūsā both said: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī and Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl both said: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad, from 'Ā'ishah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The pen is lifted from three: from the child until he reaches puberty"","" from the insane person until he regains his senses"","" and from the sleeper until he awakens.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""""
"11459","(11454) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Sa'īd — Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb al-Thaqafī — informed me; Abū al-'Abbās ibn al-Ṣaqr al-Sukkarī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated, from Mālik ibn Anas, from Nāfi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \My nation has been relieved of [accountability for] error"","" forgetfulness"","" and that which they are coerced to do.\""\n\nAnd likewise 'Umar ibn Sa'īd al-Manbajī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā. What is preserved from al-Walīd ibn Muslim is from al-Awzā'ī"","" from 'Aṭā'"","" from Ibn 'Abbās"","" and from al-Walīd"","" from Ibn Lahī'ah"","" from Mūsā ibn Wardān"","" from 'Uqbah ibn 'Āmir — both of them from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Munkar]"""""
"11460","(11455) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-'Alawī — informed us; Abū al-Qāsim — 'Ubayd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bālūyah al-Muzakkī — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzāq informed us; Ma'mar informed, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to us. He said: And Abū al-Qāsim (ﷺ) said: \Allah"","" the Mighty and Majestic"","" has ninety-nine names — one hundred minus one. Whoever enumerates them will enter Paradise. He is Witr (Odd) and loves the witr (odd).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfi'"","" from 'Abd al-Razzāq"","" and both he and al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-A'raj"","" from Abū Hurayrah. [Bukhārī 2736"","" Muslim 2677]"""""
"11461","(11456) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us from Sufyān from Layth from Ṭāwūs, who said: If the sick person makes an acknowledgment (iqrār) in favour of an heir or a non-heir, it is valid.\n\nAnd it has reached me from Abū Yaḥyā al-Sājī that he said: It has been narrated from al-Ḥasan, ʿAṭāʾ, and ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz that his acknowledgment is valid.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And al-Ḥasan said: The most deserving moment in which a man is to be considered truthful is the last day of this world and the first day of the Hereafter. Al-Bukhārī said: And Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj bequeathed that al-Fazāriyyah should not be uncovered from what her door had been locked upon. He said: And some people said: His acknowledgment is not valid on account of the suspicion (sūʾ al-ẓann) directed at the heirs. Yet the Prophet ﷺ said: \Beware of suspicion"","" for suspicion is the most false of speech.\"" And the property of the Muslims is not lawful (to take). Due to the saying of the Prophet ﷺ: \""The sign of the hypocrite is that when he is entrusted with something"","" he betrays.\"" And Allah"","" the Most High"","" said: \""Indeed"","" Allah commands you to render trusts to their rightful owners\"" (al-Nisāʾ 4:58) — and He did not specify an heir or other than him. [Weak]"""""
"11462","(11457) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of suspicion"","" for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy upon one another"","" do not search for one another's faults"","" do not compete with one another in worldly matters"","" do not envy one another"","" do not harbour hatred for one another"","" and do not turn your backs on one another. And be"","" O servants of Allah"","" brothers.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Bukhārī 1413"","" Muslim 1544]"""""
"11463","(11458) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Nāfiʿ ibn Mālik ibn Abī ʿĀmir, Abū Suhayl, narrated from his father from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The signs of the hypocrite are three: when he speaks"","" he lies; when he is entrusted"","" he betrays; and when he makes a promise"","" he breaks it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Rabīʿ"","" and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah and others from Ismāʿīl. [Bukhārī 33"","" Muslim 59]"""""
"11464","(11459) As for what Nūḥ ibn Darrāj narrated from Abān ibn Taghlib from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \There is no bequest (waṣiyyah) for an heir"","" nor an acknowledgment of a debt.\"" Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated it to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Ashʿath ibn Shaddād"","" who is al-Khurāsānī"","" narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Nūḥ ibn Darrāj narrated it"","" and he mentioned Jābir. Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: He narrated it to me in another place and did not mention Jābir. The Shaykh said: And ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr narrated it from Nūḥ"","" and he did not mention Jābir; thus it is munqaṭiʿ (discontinued)"","" and its narrator is weak — one cannot use such a narration as a proof."""""
"11465","(11460) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us. He said: I heard al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: Nūḥ ibn Darrāj is a liar, a wicked man. He served as a judge for several years while he was blind, and he did not inform the people that he was blind, due to his wickedness. He said in another place: for three years. And he did not know what ḥadīth was, nor did he have any competence in anything. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"11466","(11461) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that al-Sarrāj narrated to us that Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us from Hushaym from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from Ibn Sīrīn from Shurayḥ: that he used not to permit that (i.e., a bequest) for an heir. [Weak]"
"11467","(11462) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Ḥafṣ and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb said: Shuʿbah narrated to us from al-Ḥakam from Shurayḥ, who said: Two men testified before him — one of them testified to one thousand three hundred, and the other testified to one thousand. So he (Shurayḥ) judged against him for one thousand. He said: \Do you pass judgment against me when their two testimonies have differed?\"" He said: \""It has been settled at one thousand.\"" Sulaymān said: \""Indeed"","" they have both agreed upon one thousand.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11468","(11463) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Qurqubī narrated to us in Hamadhān: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: al-Ḥakam ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us: Shuʿayb narrated to us from al-Zuhrī. He informed me that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers, said: ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ had enjoined upon his brother Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ to take the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah. ʿUtbāh said: \He is my son.\"" When the Prophet ﷺ arrived at the time of the Conquest (of Makkah)"","" Saʿd took the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah also came along with him. Saʿd said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this is the son of my brother; he enjoined upon me that he is his son.\"" ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this is my brother"","" the son of Zamʿah"","" and he was born on his (my father's) bed.\"" The Prophet ﷺ looked at the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah and saw that he was the most resembling of people to ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""He is yours"","" O ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah"","" because he was born on his father's bed.\"" And the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Veil yourself from him"","" O Sawdah bint Zamʿah"",""\"" on account of what he saw of his resemblance to ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. And Sawdah bint Zamʿah was the wife of the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān al-Ḥakam ibn Nāfiʿ. [Bukhārī 2053"","" Muslim 1457]"""""
"11469","(11464) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us from al-Zuhrī from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: al-Zuhrī narrated to me: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard ʿĀʾishah say: Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ and ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah disputed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Saʿd said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" my brother ʿUtbah enjoined upon me"","" saying: 'When you arrive in Makkah"","" look for the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah and take him"","" for he is my son.'\"" And ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" he is my brother and the son of my father's slave-girl"","" and he was born on my father's bed.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a clear resemblance to ʿUtbah and said: \""He is yours"","" O ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah. The child belongs to the bed (al-walad lil-firāsh). And veil yourself from him"","" O Sawdah.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Ḥumaydī.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad"","" and Muslim narrated it from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and others"","" all of them from Ibn ʿUyaynah. And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and Musaddad ibn Musarhad said: Sufyān narrated to us — and he mentioned the ḥadīth with its meaning. Musaddad ibn Musarhad added in his ḥadīth: \""He is your brother"","" O ʿAbd.\"" And this is a preserved addition. Yūnus ibn Yazīd also narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11470","(11465) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣabīḥ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Wahb narrated to us: my uncle narrated to me: Yūnus narrated to me from Ibn Shihāb: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah said: ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ enjoined upon his brother Saʿd to take the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah. ʿUtbah said: \He is my son.\"" When the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Makkah at the time of the Conquest"","" Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ took the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah also came along with him. Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ said: \""This is the son of my brother; his father enjoined upon me.\"" ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"","" this is my brother"","" born on his (my father's) bed.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the son of the slave-girl of Zamʿah and saw that he was the most resembling of people to ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""He is yours; he is your brother"","" O ʿAbd ibn Zamʿah"","" because he was born on his (father's) bed.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Veil yourself from him"","" O Sawdah"",""\"" on account of the resemblance to ʿUtbah ibn Abī Waqqāṣ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ and said: And al-Layth said: Yūnus narrated to me"","" and he mentioned it with its meaning and included this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""""
"11471","(11466) And as for the one who informed us — Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' — he informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, that Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr, from 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: Zam'ah had a slave-girl with whom he had relations, and a man used to follow her, suspected [of being involved] with her. Then Zam'ah died while the slave-girl was pregnant, and she bore a boy who resembled the man who had been suspected concerning her. So Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about that. He said: \As for the inheritance"","" it is his. And as for you"","" observe hijab from him"","" for he is not a brother for you.\"" The isnad of this hadith does not rival the isnad of the first hadith"","" because the first hadith is narrated by transmitters who are well-known for their memorization"","" jurisprudence"","" and trustworthiness"","" and 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) relates that story as though she had witnessed it herself. As for the second hadith"","" among its transmitters is one who was attributed to poor memory in his later years — namely Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid — and among them is one whose hadith is not established by any corroborating cause — namely Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr. And it has been reported in other than this hadith from Mujahid"","" from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr"","" or al-Zubayr ibn Yusuf"","" a mawla of the family of al-Zubayr"","" and 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr"","" as though he did not witness the story due to his youth. The narration of one who witnessed it"","" together with all those in its isnad who are reliable"","" trustworthy huffaz well-known for jurisprudence and probity"","" is more deserving of being adopted. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it may be said that the meaning of his statement \""if he said it"","" then he is not a brother for you\"" is [that he is not a brother] in terms of resemblance"","" even though by the ruling of the firāsh (bed) he is a brother. Thus there is no contradiction with his statement \""He is your brother"","" O 'Abd"",""\"" for he linked him to the firāsh when he assigned the inheritance to him. And with Allah lies success. [Da'if]"""""
"11472","(11467) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, that Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us, that 'Affan narrated to us, that Abu 'Awanah narrated from 'Asim, from Shaqiq, who said: 'Abd Allah said: \Every act of kindness (ma'ruf) is a charity (sadaqah).\"" And we used to count ma'ruf"","" in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"","" as the cooking pot (qidr)"","" the bucket (dalw)"","" and the like thereof. [Hasan. Abu Dawud 1657]"""""
"11473","(11468) And Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdān informed us that Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, that Isma'il ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, that Qutaybah narrated to us, that Abu 'Awanah narrated — mentioning it similarly, except that he said: \And we used to count al-ma'un in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) as the cooking pot and the bucket.\"" And thus Abu Dawud narrated it in the book of al-Sunan from Qutaybah. [Hasan]"""""
"11474","(11469) And 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahawayh al-'Askari narrated to us, that Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us, that Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, that Shu'bah narrated from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazar, from Ibn Mas'ud, regarding His statement (al-ma'un): \It is the withholding of the spoon (fa's)"","" the bucket"","" and the cooking pot"","" and the like thereof.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"11475","(11470) Abu al-Qasim Zayd ibn Abi Hashim al-'Alawi in Kufah informed us that Abu Ja'far ibn Duham narrated to us, that Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah informed us, that Waki' narrated from al-A'mash, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding {wa yamna'una al-ma'un}: \It is the lending of useful items ('ariyyat al-mata').\"" [Hasan]"""""
"11476","(11471) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, that Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, that Waki' narrated from Bassam, from 'Ikrimah, who said: \Al-ma'un is the spoon"","" the cooking pot"","" and the bucket.\"" I said: \""Then woe to the one who withholds this?\"" He said: \""No. Rather"","" woe to the one who gathers them — woe to the one who shows off in his prayer and is heedless of it"","" and woe to the one who withholds this.\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11477","(11472) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us, that Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, that Adam narrated to us, that Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: \There was a state of fear in Madinah"","" so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) borrowed a horse from Abu Talhah called al-Mandub"","" and he rode it. When he returned"","" he said: 'We did not see anything [to fear]"","" and indeed we found it [the horse] to be like a sea [in its abundance and excellence].'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Adam"","" and Muslim reported it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Bukhari 2627"","" Muslim 2307]"""""
"11478","(11473) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us that Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh al-'Adl narrated to us, that Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us, that Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, that 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ayman narrated to me that his father said: \I entered upon 'A'ishah and with her was a slave-girl of hers upon which was a cotton garment worth five dirhams. She said: 'Raise your gaze to my slave-girl and look at her"","" for it displeases me that she should wear it in the house"","" though I had a garment during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) such that no woman in Madinah would adorn herself without sending to me to borrow it.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from my father [i.e."","" Abu Nu'aym]. [Bukhari 2628]"""""
"11479","(11474) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us that 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, that Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, that Abu Dawud narrated to us, that Isma'il ibn Iyyash narrated to us, that Sharahbil ibn Muslim al-Khawlami heard Abu Umamah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The debt is to be repaid"","" the borrowed item is to be returned"","" the animal taken for milking is to be given back"","" and the guarantor (al-za'im) is liable.\"" [Hasan]"""""
"11480","(11475) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us that Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Faqih in Bukhara informed us that Salih ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us, that Ishaq ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi narrated to us, that Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Khalid al-Hadha', from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) borrowed armour and weapons from Safwan ibn Umayyah during the Battle of Hunayn. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"","" is it a loan to be returned?\"" He said: \""A loan to be returned ('ariyyah mu'addah).\"" [Da'if]"""""
"11481","(11476) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us, they said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi informed us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid informed me, my father informed me, Ibn Jabir from Sulayman ibn Musa, that he informed him, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, that he informed him, regarding the interpretation of the loaned, restored property (al-'ariyya al-mu'addah): A people had in their possession properties taken as spoils from the polytheists. They said, \Islam has secured for us what we hold of the polytheists' spoils.\"" This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"","" and he said"","" \""Islam does not secure for you that which is not rightfully yours. The loaned property must be restored.\"" So the people returned what they held of those properties. 'Ali said: This is a mursal hadith"","" and no proof is established by it. [Da'if]"""""
"11482","(11477) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us verbally and in recitation, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi in recitation, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar informed us, Yunus ibn Bukayr from Ibn Ishaq, 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn Qatada informed me, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir, from his father Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out toward Hunayn, and he mentioned the hadith, and in it: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Safwan ibn Umayya and asked him for a hundred coats of mail and their requisite equipment. He said, \By force"","" O Muhammad?\"" He said"","" \""Rather"","" as a guaranteed loan until we return them to you.\"" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went forth on his expedition. [Da'if — al-Hakim 2301]"""""
"11483","(11478) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf al-'Adl informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Sharik from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Umayya ibn Safwan ibn Umayya, from his father: That the Prophet ﷺ borrowed coats of mail from him on the Day of Hunayn. He said, \By force"","" O Muhammad?\"" He said"","" \""No"","" rather as a guaranteed loan.\""\n\nAnd Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated it from 'Abd al-'Aziz from Ibn Abi Mulayka from Umayya ibn Safwan from his father. [Da'if]"""""
